nt of the door bother me because they are constantly in the way.", "tl": "Die Fahrräder vor der Tür stören mich, weil sie ständig im Weg sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Excuse me, can we move to the side? I think that we are in the way here.", "tl": "Entschuldigung, können wir an den Rand gehen? Ich glaube, dass wir hier im Weg sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Can you please push away the chairs that are in the way?", "tl": "Kannst du bitte die Stühle wegschieben, die im Weg sind?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I cannot work well in the kitchen when other people are in my way.", "tl": "Ich kann in der Küche nicht gut arbeiten, wenn mir andere Leute im Weg sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The cars cannot drive past because the trash cans are in the way.", "tl": "Die Autos können nicht vorbeifahren, weil die Mülltonnen im Weg sind."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3583, "expression_id": 3609, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "noch nicht ausgereift", "english_gloss": "not yet fully developed", "youtube_id": "L_XsIklyXb8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new app is useful, but some features are not yet fully developed.", "tl": "Die neue App ist zwar nützlich, aber einige Funktionen sind noch nicht ausgereift."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Your idea for the project is good, but the concept is not yet fully developed.", "tl": "Deine Idee für das Projekt ist gut, aber das Konzept ist noch nicht ausgereift."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Electric cars are becoming more and more popular, but the battery technology is not yet fully developed.", "tl": "Elektroautos werden immer beliebter, aber die Batterietechnologie ist noch nicht ausgereift."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We cannot make a decision yet because the plan is not yet fully developed.", "tl": "Wir können noch keine Entscheidung treffen, weil der Plan noch nicht ausgereift ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The story of the book is exciting, but the characters are not yet fully developed.", "tl": "Die Geschichte des Buches ist spannend, aber die Charaktere sind noch nicht ausgereift."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Unfortunately, the new system for online exams is not yet fully developed.", "tl": "Das neue System für die Online-Prüfungen ist leider noch nicht ausgereift."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3582, "expression_id": 3608, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "zu dem Design stehen", "english_gloss": "to have an opinion on the design", "youtube_id": "L_XsIklyXb8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I don't know yet how I should feel about the design of the new logo.", "tl": "Ich weiß noch nicht, wie ich zu dem Design des neuen Logos stehen soll."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "What is your opinion on the design of our new living room?", "tl": "Wie stehst du zu dem Design unseres neuen Wohnzimmers?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "What was your opinion back then on the design of the first version of the app?", "tl": "Wie standest du damals zu dem Design der ersten App-Version?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "As a team, we must stand united behind the design of our product.", "tl": "Wir müssen als Team geschlossen zu dem Design unseres Produkts stehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "No matter what the others say, she firmly stands by the design of her own website.", "tl": "Egal was die anderen sagen, sie steht fest zu dem Design ihrer eigenen Website."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I would be interested to know how the boss feels about the new design of the packaging.", "tl": "Mich würde interessieren, wie der Chef zu dem neuen Design der Verpackung steht."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3581, "expression_id": 3607, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auslegen", "english_gloss": "to interpret / construe", "youtube_id": "aFba3ZYADyg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Please don't misinterpret my words, I didn't mean to offend you.", "tl": "Bitte lege meine Worte nicht falsch aus, ich wollte dich nicht beleidigen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss interpreted the rules very generously in this case.", "tl": "Der Chef hat die Regeln in diesem Fall sehr großzügig ausgelegt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "One can interpret his silence as both agreement and rejection.", "tl": "Man kann sein Schweigen sowohl als Zustimmung als auch als Ablehnung auslegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't know exactly how I should interpret his sudden reaction.", "tl": "Ich weiß nicht genau, wie ich seine plötzliche Reaktion auslegen soll."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This sentence in the contract can be interpreted in different ways.", "tl": "Diesen Satz im Vertrag kann man auf verschiedene Weisen auslegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She was afraid that her politeness would be interpreted as weakness.", "tl": "Sie hatte Angst, dass man ihre Höflichkeit als Schwäche auslegen würde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3580, "expression_id": 3606, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Stellung genommen hat", "english_gloss": "made a statement / took a stand", "youtube_id": "aFba3ZYADyg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The mayor made a statement yesterday regarding the allegations.", "tl": "Der Bürgermeister hat gestern zu den Vorwürfen Stellung genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The company has not yet taken a stand on the customers' complaints.", "tl": "Die Firma hat noch nicht zu den Beschwerden der Kunden Stellung genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It is surprising that the actor made a statement about the rumors so quickly.", "tl": "Es ist überraschend, dass der Schauspieler so schnell zu den Gerüchten Stellung genommen hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The boss has finally taken a stand on our proposals for the new project.", "tl": "Der Chef hat endlich zu unseren Vorschlägen für das neue Projekt Stellung genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The minister took a stand on the new tax reform during the press conference.", "tl": "Die Ministerin hat in der Pressekonferenz zu der neuen Steuerreform Stellung genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I think it's good that she made a statement about the misunderstanding instead of ignoring it.", "tl": "Ich finde es gut, dass sie zu dem Missverständnis Stellung genommen hat, anstatt es zu ignorieren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3579, "expression_id": 3605, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen", "english_gloss": "cannot be entirely dismissed", "youtube_id": "aFba3ZYADyg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Your criticism of the new project plan cannot be entirely dismissed.", "tl": "Deine Kritik an dem neuen Projektplan ist nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The concern that it might rain over the weekend cannot be entirely dismissed.", "tl": "Die Sorge, dass es am Wochenende regnen könnte, ist nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The argument that we should do more sports in our daily lives cannot be entirely dismissed.", "tl": "Das Argument, dass wir im Alltag mehr Sport treiben sollten, ist nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His concerns about the high costs of the trip cannot be entirely dismissed.", "tl": "Seine Bedenken wegen der hohen Kosten der Reise sind nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The warning that cell phones disrupt our concentration cannot be entirely dismissed.", "tl": "Die Warnung, dass Handys unsere Konzentration stören, ist nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The assumption that we would have gotten lost without GPS cannot be entirely dismissed.", "tl": "Die Vermutung, dass wir uns ohne GPS verlaufen hätten, ist nicht ganz von der Hand zu weisen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3578, "expression_id": 3604, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Fahrt aufgenommen hat", "english_gloss": "gained momentum / picked up speed", "youtube_id": "aFba3ZYADyg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new project has finally gained momentum after we received the budget.", "tl": "Das neue Projekt hat endlich Fahrt aufgenommen, nachdem wir das Budget bekommen haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The country's economy quickly picked up speed again after the crisis.", "tl": "Die Wirtschaft des Landes hat nach der Krise schnell wieder Fahrt aufgenommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I am glad that the discussion about environmental protection has now really gained momentum.", "tl": "Ich bin froh, dass die Diskussion über den Umweltschutz jetzt richtig Fahrt aufgenommen hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His career as an actor only really picked up speed last year.", "tl": "Seine Karriere als Schauspieler hat erst im letzten Jahr so richtig Fahrt aufgenommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The sale of electric cars has gained significant momentum in recent months.", "tl": "Der Verkauf von Elektroautos hat in den letzten Monaten stark Fahrt aufgenommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The party only really got going late in the evening when the music got better.", "tl": "Die Party hat erst spät am Abend Fahrt aufgenommen, als die Musik besser wurde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3577, "expression_id": 3603, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ausharren", "english_gloss": "to hold out / persevere", "youtube_id": "aFba3ZYADyg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Despite the heavy rain, the fans had to wait it out for hours in front of the hall.", "tl": "Trotz des starken Regens mussten die Fans stundenlang vor der Halle ausharren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I know work is stressful right now, but we just have to hold out for now.", "tl": "Ich weiß, dass die Arbeit im Moment stressig ist, aber wir müssen jetzt einfach ausharren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The mountain climbers had to hold out in a small cave all night until help arrived.", "tl": "Die Bergsteiger mussten die ganze Nacht in einer kleinen Höhle ausharren, bis Hilfe kam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We should wait it out here under the roof until the thunderstorm is over.", "tl": "Wir sollten hier unter dem Dach ausharren, bis das Gewitter vorbei ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She patiently waited it out in the long queue to get a ticket.", "tl": "Sie hat geduldig in der langen Schlange ausgeharrt, um ein Ticket zu bekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The protesters continue to hold out on the street despite the cold.", "tl": "Die Demonstranten harren trotz der Kälte weiterhin auf der Straße aus."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3576, "expression_id": 3602, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf einmal", "english_gloss": "suddenly / all at once", "youtube_id": "aFba3ZYADyg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Suddenly it started to rain, even though the sky was just blue a moment ago.", "tl": "Auf einmal fing es an zu regnen, obwohl der Himmel eben noch blau war."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My laptop suddenly turned off and I hadn't saved my work.", "tl": "Mein Laptop ging auf einmal aus und ich hatte meine Arbeit nicht gespeichert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She was always very nice to me, but all of a sudden she doesn't greet me anymore.", "tl": "Sie war immer sehr nett zu mir, aber auf einmal grüßt sie mich nicht mehr."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "During the walk, he suddenly got a severe headache.", "tl": "Während des Spaziergangs hatte er auf einmal starke Kopfschmerzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why do all the bills always have to come all at once?", "tl": "Warum müssen alle Rechnungen immer auf einmal kommen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It was very quiet in the house when suddenly a loud noise came from the kitchen.", "tl": "Es war ganz leise im Haus, als auf einmal ein lautes Geräusch aus der Küche kam."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3575, "expression_id": 3601, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "a medias", "english_gloss": "halfway", "youtube_id": "gkxFHpfHyI0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I don't like to leave books half-read, so I will finish it tonight.", "tl": "No me gusta dejar los libros a medias, así que lo terminaré esta noche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Since the apartment belongs to both of us, we split the rent fifty-fifty.", "tl": "Como el piso es de los dos, pagamos el alquiler a medias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I only heard half of the story because I arrived late to the meeting.", "tl": "Solo me enteré de la historia a medias porque llegué tarde a la reunión."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you are going to do the job halfway, it's better that you don't do it at all.", "tl": "Si vas a hacer el trabajo a medias, es mejor que no lo hagas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We had to leave the movie half-watched because the power went out.", "tl": "Tuvimos que dejar la película a medias porque se cortó la luz."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My brother and I bought this car together to save money.", "tl": "Mi hermano y yo compramos este coche a medias para ahorrar dinero."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3574, "expression_id": 3600, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "No es justo", "english_gloss": "it's not fair", "youtube_id": "gkxFHpfHyI0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It's not fair that I have to clean the whole kitchen while you watch TV.", "tl": "No es justo que yo tenga que limpiar toda la cocina mientras tú miras la televisión."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I studied all night for the exam, so it's not fair that I got a bad grade.", "tl": "Estudié toda la noche para el examen, así que no es justo que haya sacado una mala nota."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's not fair! You changed the rules of the game halfway through.", "tl": "¡No es justo! Cambiaste las reglas del juego a mitad de la partida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It's not fair that she earns less money doing the same job as her colleagues.", "tl": "No es justo que ella gane menos dinero haciendo el mismo trabajo que sus compañeros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I know you are angry, but it's not fair to blame your brother for what happened.", "tl": "Sé que estás enfadado, pero no es justo culpar a tu hermano por lo que pasó."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Sometimes life is not fair, but we have to keep going despite the difficulties.", "tl": "A veces la vida no es justa, pero tenemos que seguir adelante a pesar de las dificultades."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3573, "expression_id": 3599, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "fuera de aire", "english_gloss": "off the air", "youtube_id": "gkxFHpfHyI0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The radio show went off the air due to a technical problem.", "tl": "El programa de radio se quedó fuera del aire por un problema técnico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The host told us the truth when we were already off the air.", "tl": "El presentador nos contó la verdad cuando ya estábamos fuera del aire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we don't get more sponsors, the channel will go off the air next month.", "tl": "Si no conseguimos más patrocinadores, el canal quedará fuera del aire el próximo mes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She prefers to talk about her private life off the air.", "tl": "Ella prefiere hablar de su vida privada fuera del aire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the storm, the local station was off the air for several hours.", "tl": "Durante la tormenta, la estación local estuvo fuera del aire por varias horas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Be careful with what you say, we are not off the air yet.", "tl": "Ten cuidado con lo que dices, todavía no estamos fuera del aire."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3572, "expression_id": 3598, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "agotaron todas las instancias", "english_gloss": "exhausted all avenues", "youtube_id": "gkxFHpfHyI0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The lawyers exhausted all legal avenues before accepting the judge's decision.", "tl": "Los abogados agotaron todas las instancias legales antes de aceptar la decisión del juez."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We tried to resolve the problem with the company, but since we exhausted all avenues, we had to file a complaint.", "tl": "Intentamos resolver el problema con la empresa, pero como agotamos todas las instancias, tuvimos que hacer una denuncia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The student exhausted all avenues to appeal his grade, but did not manage to change it.", "tl": "El estudiante agotó todas las instancias para apelar su calificación, pero no logró cambiarla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Before going on strike, the workers exhausted all avenues of dialogue with the management.", "tl": "Antes de ir a la huelga, los trabajadores agotaron todas las instancias de diálogo con la directiva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We have exhausted all administrative avenues to get the insurance to cover the treatment.", "tl": "Hemos agotado todas las instancias administrativas para que el seguro cubra el tratamiento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She did not want to sell her parents' house and exhausted all possible avenues to prevent it.", "tl": "Ella no quería vender la casa de sus padres y agotó todas las instancias posibles para evitarlo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3571, "expression_id": 3597, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Was macht das mit Ihnen?", "english_gloss": "How does that affect you?", "youtube_id": "l70CciyyCd4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You have been working for three weeks without a break now. How does that affect you?", "tl": "Sie arbeiten jetzt seit drei Wochen ohne Pause. Was macht das mit Ihnen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When you see this terrible news on television, what does that do to you?", "tl": "Wenn Sie diese schrecklichen Nachrichten im Fernsehen sehen, was macht das mit Ihnen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You left your homeland ten years ago. How does it affect you today when you return?", "tl": "Sie haben Ihre Heimat vor zehn Jahren verlassen. Was macht das heute mit Ihnen, wenn Sie zurückkehren?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Your boss criticized your work in front of all your colleagues. How does that affect you?", "tl": "Ihr Chef hat Ihre Arbeit vor allen Kollegen kritisiert. Was macht das mit Ihnen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Suddenly you are in the spotlight and everyone knows your name. What does that do to you?", "tl": "Plötzlich stehen Sie im Rampenlicht und jeder kennt Ihren Namen. Was macht das mit Ihnen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You are spending a week alone in the forest without a cell phone. How does that affect you?", "tl": "Sie verbringen eine Woche allein im Wald ohne Handy. Was macht das mit Ihnen?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3570, "expression_id": 3596, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "damit rechnen", "english_gloss": "to expect / count on something", "youtube_id": "l70CciyyCd4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I didn't expect you to come today already.", "tl": "Ich habe nicht damit gerechnet, dass du heute schon kommst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss fully expects us to finish the project on time.", "tl": "Der Chef rechnet fest damit, dass wir das Projekt rechtzeitig fertigstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That was a big surprise, nobody had expected it.", "tl": "Das war eine große Überraschung, niemand hatte damit gerechnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Do you expect prices to fall again next year?", "tl": "Rechnest du damit, dass die Preise im nächsten Jahr wieder sinken?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "There is often traffic on Friday evening, so you should expect that.", "tl": "Am Freitagabend gibt es oft Stau, du solltest also damit rechnen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I have a good feeling after the interview and fully expect to get the job.", "tl": "Ich habe ein gutes Gefühl nach dem Gespräch und rechne fest damit, den Job zu bekommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3569, "expression_id": 3595, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "von bis sein", "english_gloss": "to range from one extreme to another", "youtube_id": "l70CciyyCd4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The weather in April is unpredictable; it can range from sunny to stormy.", "tl": "Das Wetter im April ist unberechenbar; es kann von sonnig bis stürmisch sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The spectators' reactions ranged from enthusiastic to totally disappointed.", "tl": "Die Reaktionen der Zuschauer waren von begeistert bis total enttäuscht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "His tasks in the new company range from making coffee to important negotiations.", "tl": "Seine Aufgaben in der neuen Firma sind von Kaffeekochen bis hin zu wichtigen Verhandlungen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The prices for a hotel room in this city range from very cheap to extremely expensive.", "tl": "Die Preise für ein Hotelzimmer in dieser Stadt sind von sehr günstig bis extrem teuer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "His mood can range from super cheerful to completely annoyed in a single day.", "tl": "Seine Laune kann an einem einzigen Tag von super gelaunt bis völlig genervt sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The quality of the submitted work ranged from absolutely outstanding to useless.", "tl": "Die Qualität der eingereichten Arbeiten war von absolut hervorragend bis unbrauchbar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3568, "expression_id": 3594, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "In der Regel", "english_gloss": "as a rule / usually", "youtube_id": "l70CciyyCd4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Usually, I work from Monday to Friday, but on Wednesday I work from home.", "tl": "In der Regel arbeite ich von Montag bis Freitag, aber am Mittwoch bleibe ich im Homeoffice."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In the summer, the weather here is usually very warm and sunny.", "tl": "Im Sommer ist das Wetter hier in der Regel sehr warm und sonnig."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The trains usually arrive on time, but today there is a delay.", "tl": "Die Züge kommen in der Regel pünktlich an, aber heute gibt es eine Verspätung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "An adult usually needs seven to eight hours of sleep per night.", "tl": "Ein Erwachsener braucht in der Regel sieben bis acht Stunden Schlaf pro Nacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Delivery usually takes two to three business days.", "tl": "Die Lieferung dauert in der Regel zwei bis drei Werktage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "As a rule, cell phones may not be used during class.", "tl": "In der Regel dürfen Handys während des Unterrichts nicht benutzt werden."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3567, "expression_id": 3593, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "débat de fond", "english_gloss": "substantive debate", "youtube_id": "2jw51BodXYE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Voters are waiting for a real substantive debate on national education.", "tl": "Les électeurs attendent un vrai débat de fond sur l'éducation nationale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Instead of arguing over details, journalists should start a substantive debate.", "tl": "Au lieu de se disputer sur des détails, les journalistes devraient lancer un débat de fond."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Tomorrow's meeting will be an opportunity to have a substantive debate on the future of our company.", "tl": "La réunion de demain sera l'occasion d'avoir un débat de fond sur l'avenir de notre entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The ecological transition requires a substantive debate and not just simple political promises.", "tl": "La transition écologique nécessite un débat de fond et non de simples promesses politiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "At university, we try to encourage a substantive debate on new technologies.", "tl": "À l'université, nous essayons d'encourager un débat de fond sur les nouvelles technologies."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is time to conduct a substantive debate on the use of artificial intelligence in medicine.", "tl": "Il est temps de mener un débat de fond sur l'utilisation de l'intelligence artificielle dans la médecine."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3566, "expression_id": 3592, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en flagrant délit", "english_gloss": "red-handed", "youtube_id": "2jw51BodXYE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The thief was arrested red-handed while trying to open the car.", "tl": "Le voleur a été arrêté en flagrant délit alors qu'il essayait d'ouvrir la voiture."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The teacher caught two students red-handed cheating during the exam.", "tl": "Le professeur a surpris deux élèves en flagrant délit de triche pendant l'examen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I caught my cat red-handed on the kitchen table, eating the fish.", "tl": "J'ai attrapé mon chat en flagrant délit sur la table de la cuisine, en train de manger le poisson."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His boss caught him red-handed watching videos instead of working.", "tl": "Son patron l'a surpris en flagrant délit en train de regarder des vidéos au lieu de travailler."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She caught him red-handed lying, and he couldn't deny the facts.", "tl": "Elle l'a pris en flagrant délit de mensonge, et il n'a pas pu nier les faits."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The children were caught red-handed emptying the cookie jar before dinner.", "tl": "Les enfants ont été pris en flagrant délit alors qu'ils vidaient la boîte de biscuits avant le dîner."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3565, "expression_id": 3591, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à la base", "english_gloss": "basically / originally", "youtube_id": "2jw51BodXYE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Originally, we were supposed to go on vacation to Spain, but we changed our minds.", "tl": "À la base, on devait partir en vacances en Espagne, mais on a changé d'avis."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Originally, I studied law, but today I am a developer.", "tl": "À la base, j'ai fait des études de droit, mais aujourd'hui je suis développeur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's a very simple recipe: basically, you just need potatoes and cheese.", "tl": "C'est une recette très simple : à la base, il faut juste des pommes de terre et du fromage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't worry, basically it was just a simple misunderstanding.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, à la base ce n'était qu'un simple malentendu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This project was originally created to help students find accommodation.", "tl": "Ce projet a été créé à la base pour aider les étudiants à trouver un logement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He seems a bit cold, but basically, he is a very kind person.", "tl": "Il a l'air un peu froid, mais à la base, c'est quelqu'un de très gentil."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3564, "expression_id": 3590, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "prennent cette ampleur-là", "english_gloss": "to grow in scale", "youtube_id": "2jw51BodXYE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I didn't think the rumors on the internet would grow to that scale so quickly.", "tl": "Je ne pensais pas que les rumeurs sur internet prennent cette ampleur-là si rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is rare for simple neighborhood protests to grow to that scale.", "tl": "Il est rare que de simples manifestations de quartier prennent cette ampleur-là."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Nobody expected the discussions about the budget to grow to that scale.", "tl": "Personne ne s'attendait à ce que les discussions sur le budget prennent cette ampleur-là."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If this small conflict grows to that scale, we will have to call the police.", "tl": "Si ce petit conflit prend cette ampleur-là, il faudra appeler la police."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The association's project started modestly, but it quickly grew to that scale.", "tl": "Le projet de l'association a commencé modestement, mais il a vite pris cette ampleur-là."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When economic crises grow to that scale, governments must intervene.", "tl": "Quand les crises économiques prennent cette ampleur-là, les gouvernements doivent intervenir."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3563, "expression_id": 3589, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "au fil du temps", "english_gloss": "over time", "youtube_id": "2jw51BodXYE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our friendship has grown stronger over time.", "tl": "Notre amitié s'est renforcée au fil du temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You learn to manage your stress better over time.", "tl": "On apprend à mieux gérer son stress au fil du temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "His musical tastes have changed a lot over time.", "tl": "Ses goûts musicaux ont beaucoup changé au fil du temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This old neighborhood has become very modern over time.", "tl": "Ce vieux quartier est devenu très moderne au fil du temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Over time, I got into the habit of waking up early.", "tl": "Au fil du temps, j'ai pris l'habitude de me lever tôt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Technologies have improved over time.", "tl": "Les technologies se sont améliorées au fil du temps."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3562, "expression_id": 3588, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "partis en fumée", "english_gloss": "gone up in smoke", "youtube_id": "2jw51BodXYE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "All of her savings for the year went up in smoke because of that bad decision.", "tl": "Toutes ses économies de l'année sont parties en fumée à cause de cette mauvaise décision."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Unfortunately, the old downtown restaurant went up in smoke in last night's fire.", "tl": "Malheureusement, le vieux restaurant du centre-ville est parti en fumée dans l'incendie de la nuit dernière."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "All our efforts to organize this surprise party went up in smoke when he found out the secret.", "tl": "Tous nos efforts pour organiser cette fête surprise sont partis en fumée quand il a découvert le secret."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They worked for months on this project, but everything went up in smoke in an instant.", "tl": "Ils ont travaillé pendant des mois sur ce projet, mais tout est parti en fumée en un instant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I invested in this company, but my shares went up in smoke after the financial crisis.", "tl": "J'ai investi dans cette entreprise, mais mes actions sont parties en fumée après la crise financière."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "His beautiful promises of change quickly went up in smoke after the elections.", "tl": "Ses belles promesses de changement sont vite parties en fumée après les élections."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3561, "expression_id": 3587, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "coup de cœur", "english_gloss": "impulse buy / favorite", "youtube_id": "mid23nt6K0E", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As soon as I visited this apartment, I fell in love with it.", "tl": "Dès que j'ai visité cet appartement, j'ai eu un vrai coup de cœur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I didn't need a new jacket, but this one was an impulse buy.", "tl": "Je n'avais pas besoin d'une nouvelle veste, mais celle-ci a été un coup de cœur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This novel is the booksellers' top favorite this week.", "tl": "Ce roman est le grand coup de cœur des libraires cette semaine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our trip to Italy was a real favorite for the whole family.", "tl": "Notre voyage en Italie a été un véritable coup de cœur pour toute la famille."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I heard this song on the radio and instantly fell in love with it.", "tl": "J'ai écouté cette chanson à la radio et j'ai eu un coup de cœur immédiat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I bought this painting on impulse, without thinking too much.", "tl": "J'ai acheté ce tableau sur un coup de cœur, sans trop réfléchir."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3560, "expression_id": 3586, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire appel de", "english_gloss": "to appeal (a decision)", "youtube_id": "mid23nt6K0E", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My lawyer thinks we should appeal this decision.", "tl": "Mon avocat pense que nous devrions faire appel de cette décision."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The company decided to appeal the judgment delivered last week.", "tl": "L'entreprise a décidé de faire appel du jugement rendu la semaine dernière."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The tennis player is going to appeal his suspension before the committee.", "tl": "Le joueur de tennis va faire appel de sa suspension devant le comité."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If the court rejects our request, we will appeal the verdict.", "tl": "Si le tribunal rejette notre demande, nous ferons appel du verdict."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They immediately appealed the mayor's decision regarding the construction work.", "tl": "Ils ont immédiatement fait appel de la décision du maire concernant les travaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Every citizen has the right to appeal a judgment they consider unfair.", "tl": "Chaque citoyen a le droit de faire appel d'un jugement qu'il estime injuste."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3559, "expression_id": 3585, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "mise en œuvre", "english_gloss": "implemented / put into practice", "youtube_id": "mid23nt6K0E", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The director approved the project, but its implementation will take several months.", "tl": "Le directeur a validé le projet, mais sa mise en œuvre prendra plusieurs mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "These new security measures will be implemented starting next week.", "tl": "Ces nouvelles mesures de sécurité seront mises en œuvre dès la semaine prochaine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's an excellent idea, but its practical implementation looks difficult.", "tl": "C'est une excellente idée, mais sa mise en œuvre pratique s'annonce difficile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The city hall has implemented a plan to reduce waste in the city.", "tl": "La mairie a mis en œuvre un plan pour réduire les déchets dans la ville."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Teachers are asking for more resources for the implementation of this reform.", "tl": "Les enseignants demandent plus de ressources pour la mise en œuvre de cette réforme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The new software was successfully implemented in all departments.", "tl": "Le nouveau logiciel a été mis en œuvre avec succès dans tous les services."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3558, "expression_id": 3584, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à mauvais escient", "english_gloss": "wrongly / inappropriately", "youtube_id": "mid23nt6K0E", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You shouldn't share your personal data; it could be used inappropriately.", "tl": "Il ne faut pas partager vos données personnelles, elles pourraient être utilisées à mauvais escient."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Antibiotics are sometimes prescribed inappropriately for simple colds.", "tl": "Les antibiotiques sont parfois prescrits à mauvais escient pour de simples rhumes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The government spent the taxpayers' money unwisely.", "tl": "Le gouvernement a dépensé l'argent des contribuables à mauvais escient."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The director uses his power wrongly to influence his employees.", "tl": "Le directeur utilise son pouvoir à mauvais escient pour influencer ses employés."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You used this word incorrectly in your essay.", "tl": "Tu as employé ce mot à mauvais escient dans ta rédaction."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you waste your energy unwisely, you will be tired before the end of the day.", "tl": "Si tu gâches ton énergie à mauvais escient, tu seras fatigué avant la fin de la journée."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3557, "expression_id": 3583, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus", "english_gloss": "are looking into this more and more", "youtube_id": "mid23nt6K0E", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Scientists around the world are looking into this more and more to find a solution.", "tl": "Les scientifiques du monde entier se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus pour trouver une solution."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our marketing teams are looking into this more and more in order to attract new customers.", "tl": "Nos équipes marketing se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus afin d'attirer de nouveaux clients."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Governments are looking into this more and more to regulate artificial intelligence.", "tl": "Les gouvernements se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus pour réguler l'intelligence artificielle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Schools in the region are looking into this more and more to improve student well-being.", "tl": "Les écoles de la région se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus pour améliorer le bien-être des élèves."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Cybersecurity experts are looking into this more and more since the last cyberattack.", "tl": "Les experts en sécurité informatique se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus depuis la dernière cyberattaque."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Doctors are looking into this more and more to understand the effects of stress on health.", "tl": "Les médecins se penchent de plus en plus là-dessus pour comprendre les effets du stress sur la santé."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3556, "expression_id": 3582, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "carretera y manta", "english_gloss": "to hit the road", "youtube_id": "m1VWmsG1QgY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "On Friday afternoon, as soon as we leave work, we'll hit the road towards the beach.", "tl": "El viernes por la tarde, en cuanto salgamos de trabajar, cogemos carretera y manta hacia la playa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I was so tired of the routine that I decided to hit the road and spend the weekend in the mountains.", "tl": "Estaba tan cansado de la rutina que decidí coger carretera y manta y pasar el fin de semana en la montaña."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you need to disconnect from everything, the best thing you can do is hit the road for a few days.", "tl": "Si necesitas desconectar de todo, lo mejor que puedes hacer es coger carretera y manta unos días."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We already have the suitcases ready in the car, so let's hit the road!", "tl": "Ya tenemos las maletas listas en el coche, así que ¡carretera y manta!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My partner and I didn't plan anything; we just hit the road and stopped wherever we liked.", "tl": "Mi pareja y yo no planeamos nada; simplemente cogimos carretera y manta y paramos donde nos gustó."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Tomorrow we will get up early, hit the road, and we'll be there before noon.", "tl": "Mañana nos levantaremos temprano, cogeremos carretera y manta, y antes del mediodía estaremos allí."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3555, "expression_id": 3581, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "sin techo", "english_gloss": "homeless", "youtube_id": "m1VWmsG1QgY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "During the winter, this organization helps homeless people by offering them hot food.", "tl": "Durante el invierno, esta organización ayuda a las personas sin techo ofreciéndoles comida caliente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The city government is building new shelters for the homeless.", "tl": "El gobierno de la ciudad está construyendo nuevos refugios para los sin techo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Yesterday I spoke with a homeless man who lives near my office and he told me his story.", "tl": "Ayer hablé con un hombre sin techo que vive cerca de mi oficina y me contó su historia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Due to the economic crisis, many families were left homeless overnight.", "tl": "Debido a la crisis económica, muchas familias se quedaron sin techo de la noche a la mañana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We collect warm clothes to donate them to the homeless in the neighborhood.", "tl": "Recogemos ropa de abrigo para donarla a los sin techo del barrio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The number of homeless people has increased in big cities this year.", "tl": "El número de personas sin techo ha aumentado en las grandes ciudades este año."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3554, "expression_id": 3580, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "al raso", "english_gloss": "in the open air", "youtube_id": "m1VWmsG1QgY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We decided not to bring a tent and to sleep in the open air to see the stars.", "tl": "Decidimos no llevar tienda de campaña y dormir al raso para ver las estrellas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't leave the tools out in the open because they will rust with the rain.", "tl": "No dejes las herramientas al raso porque se van a oxidar con la lluvia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The festival concert was held in the open air and the temperature was perfect.", "tl": "El concierto del festival se celebró al raso y la temperatura era perfecta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After the earthquake, many families had to spend the night in the open air.", "tl": "Después del terremoto, muchas familias tuvieron que pasar la noche al raso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "These plants can't stand the cold; if you leave them out in the open in winter, they will die.", "tl": "Estas plantas no aguantan el frío; si las dejas al raso en invierno, se morirán."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My grandfather always told me how he used to sleep under the open sky when he worked in the fields.", "tl": "Mi abuelo siempre me contaba cómo dormía al raso cuando trabajaba en el campo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3553, "expression_id": 3579, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "darle un uso", "english_gloss": "to put to use", "youtube_id": "srQo6Cpv6TY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you don't use that old computer anymore, you should put it to use or give it away.", "tl": "Si ya no usas ese ordenador viejo, deberías darle un uso o regalarlo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We have an empty room at home and we want to put it to practical use.", "tl": "Tenemos una habitación vacía en casa y queremos darle un uso práctico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I finally put to use the coffee maker you gave me for my birthday.", "tl": "Por fin le di un uso a la cafetera que me regalaste por mi cumpleaños."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't throw away those cardboard boxes; I'm sure we can put them to use to organize the closet.", "tl": "No tires esas cajas de cartón; seguro que podemos darles un uso para ordenar el armario."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I bought these tools last year, but I still haven't put them to use.", "tl": "Compré estas herramientas el año pasado, pero todavía no les he dado un uso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you don't know what to do with that broken table, you can put it to a new use as a plant stand.", "tl": "Si no sabes qué hacer con esa mesa rota, puedes darle un nuevo uso como soporte para plantas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3552, "expression_id": 3578, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "apostar por", "english_gloss": "to bet on / to opt for", "youtube_id": "srQo6Cpv6TY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our company is opting for remote work to improve productivity.", "tl": "Nuestra empresa apuesta por el teletrabajo para mejorar la productividad."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I have always preferred to support public education.", "tl": "Siempre he preferido apostar por la educación pública."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Although it was risky, we decided to bet on our love and move in together.", "tl": "Aunque era arriesgado, decidimos apostar por nuestro amor y mudarnos juntos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is important to support local businesses to help the neighborhood's economy.", "tl": "Es importante apostar por el comercio local para ayudar a la economía del barrio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you want to be successful, you have to bet on your own ideas.", "tl": "Si quieres tener éxito, tienes que apostar por tus propias ideas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The coach is going to bet on the young players this season.", "tl": "El entrenador va a apostar por los jugadores jóvenes esta temporada."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3551, "expression_id": 3577, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "ir más allá", "english_gloss": "to go further", "youtube_id": "srQo6Cpv6TY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you want to improve at your job, you must go beyond your daily duties.", "tl": "Si quieres mejorar en tu trabajo, debes ir más allá de tus obligaciones diarias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I don't want this problem to go any further than this office.", "tl": "No quiero que este problema vaya más allá de esta oficina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The director always asks us to go further to provide good service.", "tl": "El director siempre nos pide ir más allá para dar un buen servicio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "With this new technology, science has gone beyond what we thought possible.", "tl": "Con esta nueva tecnología, la ciencia ha ido más allá de lo que creíamos posible."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "His words go beyond a simple apology; he really wants to change.", "tl": "Sus palabras van más allá de una simple disculpa; realmente quiere cambiar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I would like to go further in my career and take on new responsibilities.", "tl": "Me gustaría ir más allá en mi carrera y asumir nuevas responsabilidades."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3550, "expression_id": 3576, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "por detrás de", "english_gloss": "behind / second to", "youtube_id": "srQo6Cpv6TY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The cat went behind the television and pulled the cable.", "tl": "El gato pasó por detrás de la televisión y tiró el cable."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In terms of technological innovation, our country is still behind its neighbors.", "tl": "En cuanto a innovación tecnológica, nuestro país sigue por detrás de sus vecinos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you walk behind the church, you will see a very beautiful park.", "tl": "Si caminas por detrás de la iglesia, verás un parque muy bonito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Despite his efforts, the runner finished behind the race leader.", "tl": "A pesar de sus esfuerzos, el corredor terminó por detrás del líder de la carrera."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The thief entered the store behind the counter while the clerk wasn't looking.", "tl": "El ladrón entró a la tienda por detrás del mostrador mientras el dependiente no miraba."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In the satisfaction survey, our customer service fell behind the competition.", "tl": "En la encuesta de satisfacción, nuestro servicio al cliente quedó por detrás de la competencia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3549, "expression_id": 3575, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "no fue hasta que", "english_gloss": "it was not until", "youtube_id": "srQo6Cpv6TY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It wasn't until I turned thirty that I decided to change careers.", "tl": "No fue hasta que cumplí los treinta que decidí cambiar de carrera."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It wasn't until we arrived at the hotel that we realized the mistake in the reservation.", "tl": "No fue hasta que llegamos al hotel que nos dimos cuenta del error en la reserva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It wasn't until he got sick that he started to watch his diet.", "tl": "No fue hasta que se enfermó que empezó a cuidar su alimentación."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It wasn't until it stopped raining that we were able to go for a walk in the park.", "tl": "No fue hasta que paró de llover que pudimos salir a caminar por el parque."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It wasn't until I read her message that I understood what had really happened.", "tl": "No fue hasta que leí su mensaje que entendí lo que realmente había pasado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It wasn't until we finished the project that we could rest over the weekend.", "tl": "No fue hasta que terminamos el proyecto que pudimos descansar el fin de semana."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3548, "expression_id": 3574, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "puiser", "english_gloss": "to draw from / derive", "youtube_id": "7VN6Nl6myak", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The writer likes to draw his inspiration from his childhood memories.", "tl": "L'écrivain aime puiser son inspiration dans ses souvenirs d'enfance."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At the end of the marathon, she had to draw on her last remaining strength to finish.", "tl": "À la fin du marathon, elle a dû puiser dans ses dernières forces pour finir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "For his presentation, he went to draw information from old history books.", "tl": "Pour son exposé, il est allé puiser des informations dans de vieux livres d'histoire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We had to draw from our savings to repair the car.", "tl": "Nous avons dû puiser dans nos économies pour réparer la voiture."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In the past, the villagers had to draw water from the public well.", "tl": "Autrefois, les habitants du village devaient puiser l'eau au puits public."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This artist draws her ideas from popular culture and cinema.", "tl": "Cette artiste puise ses idées dans la culture populaire et le cinéma."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3547, "expression_id": 3573, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tourne autour de", "english_gloss": "revolves around", "youtube_id": "7VN6Nl6myak", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Everyone knows that the Earth revolves around the Sun.", "tl": "Tout le monde sait que la Terre tourne autour du Soleil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Stop thinking the world revolves around you!", "tl": "Arrête de croire que le monde tourne autour de toi !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The whole meeting this morning revolved around next year's budget.", "tl": "Toute la réunion de ce matin a tourné autour du budget de l'année prochaine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Their family life revolves mainly around the children's sports activities.", "tl": "Leur vie de famille tourne principalement autour des activités sportives des enfants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The plot of this detective novel revolves around a mysterious disappearance.", "tl": "L'intrigue de ce roman policier tourne autour d'une mystérieuse disparition."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "All of her thoughts revolve around her upcoming trip to Italy.", "tl": "Toutes ses pensées tournent autour de son prochain voyage en Italie."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3546, "expression_id": 3572, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "nous fait le plaisir d'être", "english_gloss": "does us the pleasure of being", "youtube_id": "7VN6Nl6myak", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Tonight, the famous writer does us the pleasure of being among us to present his new book.", "tl": "Ce soir, le célèbre écrivain nous fait le plaisir d'être parmi nous pour présenter son nouveau livre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My parents did us the pleasure of being present at our wedding last weekend.", "tl": "Mes parents nous ont fait le plaisir d'être présents à notre mariage le week-end dernier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I hope the director will do us the pleasure of being there for the inauguration of the new offices.", "tl": "J'espère que le directeur nous fera le plaisir d'être là pour l'inauguration des nouveaux bureaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Today, two great chefs do us the pleasure of being on our TV set.", "tl": "Aujourd'hui, deux grands chefs cuisiniers nous font le plaisir d'être sur notre plateau de télévision."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you are free on Saturday, would you do us the pleasure of being our guide in the city?", "tl": "Si tu es libre samedi, est-ce que tu nous ferais le plaisir d'être notre guide dans la ville ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our former colleague did us the pleasure of being by the office this morning to say hello to us.", "tl": "Notre ancienne collègue nous a fait le plaisir d'être de passage au bureau ce matin pour nous dire bonjour."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3545, "expression_id": 3571, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "rien qu'en", "english_gloss": "just in / only in", "youtube_id": "7VN6Nl6myak", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Just thinking about it gives me chills.", "tl": "Rien qu'en y pensant, j'ai des frissons."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Just by looking at his face, I understood that something was wrong.", "tl": "Rien qu'en regardant son visage, j'ai compris que quelque chose n'allait pas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You can improve your French just by listening to podcasts every day.", "tl": "Tu peux améliorer ton français rien qu'en écoutant des podcasts tous les jours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She recognized his voice just by hearing him laugh.", "tl": "Elle a reconnu sa voix rien qu'en l'entendant rire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Just by smelling this scent, I remember my childhood holidays.", "tl": "Rien qu'en sentant cette odeur, je me rappelle mes vacances d'enfance."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We can save a lot of money just by cooking at home.", "tl": "On peut économiser beaucoup d'argent rien qu'en cuisinant à la maison."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3544, "expression_id": 3570, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "un nouveau cap inquiétant a été franchi", "english_gloss": "a worrying new milestone has been reached", "youtube_id": "7VN6Nl6myak", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With this summer's historic drought, a worrying new milestone has been reached.", "tl": "Avec la sécheresse historique de cet été, un nouveau cap inquiétant a été franchi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Experts agree that a worrying new milestone has been reached regarding cyberbullying among young people.", "tl": "Les experts s'accordent à dire qu'un nouveau cap inquiétant a été franchi concernant le cyberharcèlement chez les jeunes"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With the dramatic rise in electricity prices, a worrying new milestone has been reached for small businesses.", "tl": "Avec la hausse spectaculaire des prix de l'électricité, un nouveau cap inquiétant a été franchi pour les petites entrepr"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The number of flu cases is rising so fast that a worrying new milestone was reached this week.", "tl": "Le nombre de cas de grippe augmente si vite qu'un nouveau cap inquiétant a été franchi cette semaine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "After last night's violence during the protest, a worrying new milestone has been reached in the social crisis.", "tl": "Après les violences d'hier soir lors de la manifestation, un nouveau cap inquiétant a été franchi dans la crise sociale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When the school dropout rate exceeded 15%, we realized that a worrying new milestone had been reached.", "tl": "Lorsque le taux de décrochage scolaire a dépassé les 15 %, on a compris qu'un nouveau cap inquiétant avait été franchi."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3543, "expression_id": 3569, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "giocando con il fuoco", "english_gloss": "to play with fire", "youtube_id": "Mepr0UlyAQk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you keep lying to your boss, you are playing with fire.", "tl": "Se continui a mentire al tuo capo, stai giocando con il fuoco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Investing all your savings in that new company means playing with fire.", "tl": "Investire tutti i tuoi risparmi in quella nuova società significa giocare con il fuoco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Marco hasn't paid taxes for years; in my opinion, he is playing with fire.", "tl": "Marco non paga le tasse da anni; secondo me gioca con il fuoco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Guys, don't play that dangerous game, you are playing with fire!", "tl": "Ragazzi, non fate quel gioco pericoloso, state giocando con il fuoco!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "By accepting that job without a written contract, you played with fire.", "tl": "Accettando quel lavoro senza un contratto scritto, hai giocato con il fuoco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you don't study for the final exam, you will be playing with fire.", "tl": "Se non studi per l'esame finale, giocherai con il fuoco."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3542, "expression_id": 3568, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "andare a rintracciare", "english_gloss": "to track down / trace", "youtube_id": "Mepr0UlyAQk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Now I'm going to track down that old invoice you asked me for.", "tl": "Adesso vado a rintracciare quella vecchia fattura che mi hai chiesto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The police went to track down the witness at his house.", "tl": "I carabinieri sono andati a rintracciare il testimone a casa sua."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We need to go track down that old colleague who used to work with us in Milan.", "tl": "Dobbiamo andare a rintracciare quel vecchio collega che lavorava con noi a Milano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Tomorrow we will go track down the source of this technical problem.", "tl": "Domani andremo a rintracciare l'origine di questo problema tecnico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Could you go track down that package that never arrived?", "tl": "Potresti andare a rintracciare quel pacco che non è mai arrivato?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I went to track down my old schoolmates on Facebook.", "tl": "Sono andato a rintracciare i miei vecchi compagni di scuola su Facebook."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3541, "expression_id": 3567, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "dà quasi per scontata", "english_gloss": "to take for granted", "youtube_id": "Mepr0UlyAQk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He takes his health almost for granted, but he should be more careful.", "tl": "Lui dà quasi per scontata la sua salute, ma dovrebbe fare più attenzione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We often take our friends' help almost for granted.", "tl": "Spesso diamo quasi per scontato l'aiuto dei nostri amici."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many young people take it almost for granted that they will find a job right after university.", "tl": "Molti giovani danno quasi per scontato che troveranno un lavoro subito dopo l'università."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't take your girlfriend almost for granted, otherwise you risk losing her.", "tl": "Non dare quasi per scontata la tua ragazza, altrimenti rischi di perderla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You take the luck you have to live here almost for granted.", "tl": "Voi date quasi per scontata la fortuna che avete di vivere qui."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Marco took the promotion almost for granted, and instead they chose another colleague.", "tl": "Marco ha dato quasi per scontata la promozione, e invece hanno scelto un altro collega."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3540, "expression_id": 3566, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "hanno a che fare con", "english_gloss": "to have to do with", "youtube_id": "Mepr0UlyAQk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Today at work I have to deal with a very difficult customer.", "tl": "Oggi al lavoro ho a che fare con un cliente molto difficile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "His excuses have nothing to do with what really happened.", "tl": "Le sue scuse non hanno niente a che fare con quello che è successo veramente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Her new profession has to do with art and design.", "tl": "La sua nuova professione ha a che fare con l'arte e il design."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Right now we are dealing with an emergency situation.", "tl": "In questo momento abbiamo a che fare con una situazione d'emergenza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't like having to do with people who tell lies.", "tl": "Non mi piace avere a che fare con persone che dicono bugie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Have you ever had to deal with a similar problem in the past?", "tl": "Voi avete mai avuto a che fare con un problema simile in passato?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3539, "expression_id": 3565, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "da pior forma", "english_gloss": "the hard way", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I learned the hard way that you shouldn't trust just anyone.", "tl": "Eu aprendi da pior forma que não se deve confiar em qualquer pessoa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He found out the hard way that managing a company is very difficult.", "tl": "Ele descobriu da pior forma que gerir uma empresa é muito difícil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you don't rest now, you will realize the hard way that your body has limits.", "tl": "Se não descansares agora, vais perceber da pior forma que o teu corpo tem limites."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We forgot our umbrellas and found out the hard way that it was going to rain a lot.", "tl": "Nós esquecemo-nos dos guarda-chuvas e descobrimos da pior forma que ia chover imenso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She lost all her work and learned the hard way the importance of saving documents.", "tl": "Ela perdeu todo o seu trabalho e aprendeu da pior forma a importância de guardar os documentos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They realized the hard way that a lack of communication destroys a relationship.", "tl": "Eles perceberam da pior forma que a falta de comunicação destrói uma relação."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3538, "expression_id": 3564, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "meias verdades", "english_gloss": "half-truths", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The politician tried to convince the public with half-truths, but nobody believed him.", "tl": "O político tentou convencer o público com meias verdades, mas ninguém acreditou nele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Instead of telling me the whole truth, you prefer to tell me half-truths.", "tl": "Em vez de me dizer toda a verdade, você prefere me contar meias verdades."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company tried to hide the financial crisis by presenting only half-truths to the employees.", "tl": "A empresa tentou esconder a crise financeira apresentando apenas meias verdades aos funcionários."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't trust him because he always speaks in half-truths to look innocent.", "tl": "Eu não confio nele porque ele sempre fala com meias verdades para parecer inocente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Many news stories on the internet are based on half-truths that confuse people.", "tl": "Muitas notícias na internet são baseadas em meias verdades que confundem as pessoas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Sometimes, half-truths are more dangerous than complete lies.", "tl": "Às vezes, as meias verdades são mais perigosas do que as mentiras completas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3537, "expression_id": 3563, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "a médio prazo", "english_gloss": "in the medium term", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Investing in stocks can be very advantageous in the medium term.", "tl": "Investir em ações pode ser muito vantajoso a médio prazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My goal in the medium term is to get a promotion at work.", "tl": "O meu objetivo a médio prazo é conseguir uma promoção no trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company plans to expand its business to other countries in the medium term.", "tl": "A empresa planeia expandir os seus negócios para outros países a médio prazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Changing eating habits brings excellent results in the medium term.", "tl": "Mudar os hábitos alimentares traz excelentes resultados a médio prazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The government expects these new measures to improve the economy in the medium term.", "tl": "O governo espera que estas novas medidas melhorem a economia a médio prazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Learning a new language is a project that brings results in the medium term.", "tl": "Aprender uma nova língua é um projeto que traz resultados a médio prazo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3536, "expression_id": 3562, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "qual é a do Zema", "english_gloss": "what is someone's deal", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Zema is being very strange today. He didn't speak to anyone in the meeting. What is Zema's deal, anyway?", "tl": "O Zema está muito estranho hoje. Ele não falou com ninguém na reunião. Qual é a do Zema, afinal?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He keeps changing his mind about the project. I really don't understand what Zema's deal is.", "tl": "Ele vive mudando de opinião sobre o projeto. Eu realmente não entendo qual é a do Zema."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Did you see how he looked at us? What's Zema's deal? Is he angry?", "tl": "Você viu como ele olhou para nós? Qual é a do Zema? Será que ele está bravo?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Zema promised to help with the move, but now he's disappeared and isn't answering the phone. What's Zema's deal?", "tl": "O Zema prometeu ajudar na mudança, mas agora sumiu e não atende o telefone. Qual é a do Zema?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I'd like to know what Zema's deal is. One minute he's super friendly, the next he won't even look at me.", "tl": "Queria saber qual é a do Zema. Uma hora ele é super simpático, outra hora nem olha na minha cara."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Man, what's Zema's deal? He said he was going to buy the tickets, but so far nothing.", "tl": "Cara, qual é a do Zema? Ele disse que ia comprar os ingressos, mas até agora nada."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3535, "expression_id": 3561, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "De jeito nenhum", "english_gloss": "no way / by no means", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I can't lend you any more money, no way.", "tl": "Eu não posso te emprestar mais dinheiro, de jeito nenhum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "— Do you think she will accept this proposal? — No way, she is too proud.", "tl": "— Você acha que ela vai aceitar essa proposta? — De jeito nenhum, ela é muito orgulhosa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We cannot go in there without authorization, by no means.", "tl": "Não podemos entrar lá sem autorização, de jeito nenhum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I am not going to travel by plane in this storm, no way!", "tl": "Eu não vou viajar de avião com essa tempestade, de jeito nenhum!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He said he is not going to do the work alone, by any means.", "tl": "Ele disse que não vai fazer o trabalho sozinho de jeito nenhum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Sorry, but I cannot accept this kind of behavior under any circumstances.", "tl": "Desculpe, mas eu não posso aceitar esse tipo de comportamento de jeito nenhum."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3534, "expression_id": 3560, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "Se eu não me engano", "english_gloss": "if I'm not mistaken", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If I'm not mistaken, the meeting starts at two in the afternoon.", "tl": "Se eu não me engano, a reunião começa às duas da tarde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If I'm not mistaken, the nearest supermarket is on that street over there.", "tl": "Se não me engano, o supermercado mais próximo fica naquela rua ali."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If I'm not mistaken, we already know each other from somewhere.", "tl": "Se eu não me engano, nós já nos conhecemos de algum lugar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If I'm not mistaken, her birthday is next week.", "tl": "Se eu não me engano, o aniversário dela é na próxima semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If I'm not mistaken, this blue coat belongs to your brother.", "tl": "Se não me engano, este casaco azul é do teu irmão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If I'm not mistaken, our flight leaves from terminal two.", "tl": "Se eu não me engano, o nosso voo sai do terminal dois."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3533, "expression_id": 3559, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "descolaram", "english_gloss": "to distance or detach oneself", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "They distanced themselves from the main group during the hike to go faster.", "tl": "Eles descolaram do grupo principal durante a caminhada para irem mais depressa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In the polls, the top two candidates pulled away from the others.", "tl": "Nas sondagens, os dois primeiros candidatos descolaram dos outros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They distanced themselves from the initial idea because it was too expensive.", "tl": "Eles descolaram da ideia inicial porque era muito cara."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My friends got away from that party as soon as they could.", "tl": "Os meus amigos descolaram daquela festa assim que puderam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "On the last lap, the two leaders pulled away from the remaining runners.", "tl": "Na última volta, os dois líderes descolaram dos restantes corredores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They broke away from family tradition and opened a modern business.", "tl": "Eles descolaram da tradição familiar e abriram um negócio moderno."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3532, "expression_id": 3558, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "colocando o Renan Santos contra a parede", "english_gloss": "putting someone against the wall", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The journalist is putting Renan Santos against the wall with difficult questions about the debate.", "tl": "O jornalista está colocando o Renan Santos contra a parede com perguntas difíceis sobre o debate."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "During the live interview, they put Renan Santos against the wall so he would explain the plan.", "tl": "Durante a entrevista ao vivo, eles colocaram o Renan Santos contra a parede para ele explicar o plano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If he doesn't give a clear answer today, the public will end up putting Renan Santos against the wall.", "tl": "Se ele não der uma resposta clara hoje, o público vai acabar colocando o Renan Santos contra a parede."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I would like to see the opposition putting Renan Santos against the wall in the next party meeting.", "tl": "Eu gostaria de ver a oposição colocando o Renan Santos contra a parede na próxima reunião do partido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The podcast hosts decided to put Renan Santos against the wall regarding that recent controversy.", "tl": "Os apresentadores do podcast decidiram colocar o Renan Santos contra a parede sobre aquela polêmica recente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He tried to change the subject, but the reporters kept putting Renan Santos against the wall.", "tl": "Ele tentou mudar de assunto, mas os repórteres continuaram colocando o Renan Santos contra a parede."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3531, "expression_id": 3557, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "atropelado", "english_gloss": "overwhelmed or run over (figuratively)", "youtube_id": "Euuc2SxIQlU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I feel completely overwhelmed with so much work this week.", "tl": "Sinto-me completamente atropelada com tanto trabalho esta semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We did everything in a very rushed way and ended up making some mistakes.", "tl": "Fizemos tudo de forma muito atropelada e acabámos por cometer alguns erros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After moving house, I felt overwhelmed by so many changes at the same time.", "tl": "Depois da mudança de casa, senti-me atropelado por tantas novidades ao mesmo tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He speaks in a very rushed way when he is nervous.", "tl": "Ele fala de uma maneira muito atropelada quando está nervoso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My routine is so rushed that I don't even have time to rest.", "tl": "A minha rotina anda tão atropelada que já nem tenho tempo para descansar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The project moved so fast that the team felt overwhelmed by the events.", "tl": "O projeto avançou tão rápido que a equipa se sentiu atropelada pelos acontecimentos."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3530, "expression_id": 3556, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "não serve para nada", "english_gloss": "is good for nothing", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This old phone is good for nothing now; the battery doesn't even last ten minutes.", "tl": "Este telemóvel antigo já não serve para nada, a bateria não dura nem dez minutos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Staying at home complaining is good for nothing; we have to do something to change the situation.", "tl": "Ficar em casa a reclamar não serve para nada, temos de fazer alguma coisa para mudar a situação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "These old keys are useless; we already changed the door lock months ago.", "tl": "Estas chaves velhas não servem para nada, já mudámos a fechadura da porta há meses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "That advice is of no use to me because my situation is completely different.", "tl": "Esse conselho não me serve para nada porque a minha situação é completamente diferente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I tried to read the instruction manual, but it's useless because it is very badly translated.", "tl": "Eu tentei ler o manual de instruções, mas não serve para nada porque está muito mal traduzido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Having very strict rules is good for nothing if nobody respects them in daily life.", "tl": "Ter regras muito estritas não serve para nada se ninguém as respeitar no dia a dia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3529, "expression_id": 3555, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vão ficar sem", "english_gloss": "will go without", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If the children don't eat their soup, they will go without dessert.", "tl": "Se as crianças não comerem a sopa, vão ficar sem sobremesa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you don't buy the tickets now, you will be left without a seat at the concert.", "tl": "Se vocês não comprarem os bilhetes agora, vão ficar sem lugar no concerto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With this train strike, many people will be left without transport to work.", "tl": "Com esta greve de comboios, muitas pessoas vão ficar sem transporte para o trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you don't save the document, you will lose all your work (literally: be left without all the work).", "tl": "Se vocês não guardarem o documento, vão ficar sem o trabalho todo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you don't water the plants this week, they will go without water.", "tl": "Se não regares as plantas esta semana, elas vão ficar sem água."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Hurry up, otherwise you will run out of time to see the museum before it closes.", "tl": "Despechem-se, senão vão ficar sem tempo para ver o museu antes de fechar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3528, "expression_id": 3554, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "não é assim que funciona", "english_gloss": "that's not how it works", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You can't just ignore the rules; that's not how it works.", "tl": "Você não pode simplesmente ignorar as regras; não é assim que funciona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He thinks he can buy my forgiveness, but that's not how it works.", "tl": "Ele acha que pode comprar o meu perdão, mas não é assim que funciona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You want to learn Portuguese in a week? Unfortunately, that's not how it works.", "tl": "Você quer aprender português em uma semana? Infelizmente, não é assim que funciona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I tried to click here to save, but apparently that's not how it works.", "tl": "Eu tentei clicar aqui para salvar, mas pelo visto não é assim que funciona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You can't expect to make money without working; that's not how it works.", "tl": "Você não pode esperar ganhar dinheiro sem trabalhar; não é assim que funciona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Do you want to play video games all day without studying? That's not how it works.", "tl": "Quer jogar videogame o dia todo sem estudar? Não é assim que funciona."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3527, "expression_id": 3553, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de alguma forma", "english_gloss": "somehow / in some way", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I need to solve this computer problem somehow.", "tl": "Eu preciso de resolver este problema no computador de alguma forma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She felt that, somehow, everything was going to work out in the end.", "tl": "Ela sentia que, de alguma forma, tudo ia dar certo no final."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We managed to finish the project on time somehow.", "tl": "Nós conseguimos terminar o projeto a tempo de alguma forma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I think my words hurt him in some way.", "tl": "Acho que as minhas palavras o magoaram de alguma forma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I want to help our group in some way, even if it is with simple tasks.", "tl": "Quero ajudar o nosso grupo de alguma forma, mesmo que seja com tarefas simples."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The cat managed to open the door somehow and escaped into the street.", "tl": "O gato conseguiu abrir a porta de alguma forma e escapou para a rua."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3526, "expression_id": 3552, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de boa fé", "english_gloss": "in good faith", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I bought the car in good faith, without knowing it had engine problems.", "tl": "Eu comprei o carro de boa fé, sem saber que ele tinha problemas no motor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She acted in good faith when she tried to help, but ended up making the situation worse.", "tl": "Ela agiu de boa fé quando tentou ajudar, mas acabou piorando a situação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Both parties signed the contract in good faith, hoping for a long partnership.", "tl": "As duas partes assinaram o contrato de boa fé, esperando uma longa parceria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't be angry, he said that in good faith to protect you.", "tl": "Não fique zangado, ele disse aquilo de boa fé para te proteger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We made the proposal in good faith, but they rejected it immediately.", "tl": "Nós fizemos a proposta de boa fé, mas eles recusaram imediatamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The law protects those who act in good faith in business deals.", "tl": "A lei protege quem age de boa fé em negócios comerciais."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3525, "expression_id": 3551, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vai muito além", "english_gloss": "goes far beyond", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This Portuguese course goes far beyond basic grammar.", "tl": "Este curso de português vai muito além da gramática básica."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Her work at the company goes far beyond what is written in the contract.", "tl": "O trabalho dela na empresa vai muito além do que está escrito no contrato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our friendship goes far beyond just being coworkers.", "tl": "A nossa amizade vai muito além de sermos apenas colegas de trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The impact of technology on society goes far beyond simple communication.", "tl": "O impacto da tecnologia na sociedade vai muito além da simples comunicação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For him, music goes far beyond a simple hobby; it is a passion.", "tl": "Para ele, a música vai muito além de um simples passatempo; é uma paixão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Having a healthy life goes far beyond eating well and exercising.", "tl": "Ter uma vida saudável vai muito além de comer bem e fazer exercício."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3524, "expression_id": 3550, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "correndo contra o tempo", "english_gloss": "racing against time", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We are racing against time to deliver the project before Friday.", "tl": "Estamos correndo contra o tempo para entregar o projeto antes de sexta-feira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She spent the whole night studying, racing against time for today's exam.", "tl": "Ela passou a noite toda estudando, correndo contra o tempo para a prova de hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The doctors are racing against time to save the patient.", "tl": "Os médicos estão correndo contra o tempo para salvar o paciente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The catering hasn't arrived yet and the organizers are racing against time.", "tl": "O buffet ainda não chegou e os organizadores estão correndo contra o tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We left late for the airport and now we are racing against time.", "tl": "Saímos atrasados para o aeroporto e agora estamos correndo contra o tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The construction workers are racing against time to finish the renovation before the rain.", "tl": "Os pedreiros estão correndo contra o tempo para terminar a reforma antes da chuva."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3523, "expression_id": 3549, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "faz sentido", "english_gloss": "makes sense", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "What you are saying makes perfect sense, now I understand your point of view.", "tl": "O que você está dizendo faz todo o sentido, agora eu entendo o seu ponto de vista."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It doesn't make sense to buy a new car if you almost never use it.", "tl": "Não faz sentido comprar um carro novo se você quase nunca o usa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "At that time, their decision made sense, but nowadays things have changed.", "tl": "Naquela época, a decisão deles fazia sentido, mas hoje em dia as coisas mudaram."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It would make sense to accept the job offer if the salary were a bit better.", "tl": "Faria sentido aceitar a proposta de emprego se o salário fosse um pouco melhor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Does it make sense to you that the meeting is postponed to next week?", "tl": "Faz sentido para você que a reunião seja adiada para a próxima semana?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I think it doesn't make sense for us to argue because of such a small problem.", "tl": "Eu acho que não faz sentido a gente discutir por causa de um problema tão pequeno."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3522, "expression_id": 3548, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "contra a vontade", "english_gloss": "against their will", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He went to the party against his will, but in the end he had a lot of fun.", "tl": "Ele foi à festa contra a vontade, mas no final divertiu-se muito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Maria was transferred to another office against her will.", "tl": "A Maria foi transferida para outro escritório contra a sua vontade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't want you to sign this contract against your will.", "tl": "Não quero que assines este contrato contra a tua vontade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The children got up early against their will, as they were still sleepy.", "tl": "As crianças levantaram-se cedo contra a vontade, pois ainda tinham sono."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They sold the old house against their grandparents' will.", "tl": "Eles venderam a casa antiga contra a vontade dos avós."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The doctor said I have to stay in bed, even against my will.", "tl": "O médico disse que tenho de ficar na cama, mesmo contra a minha vontade."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3521, "expression_id": 3547, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "entendeu errado", "english_gloss": "got it wrong / misunderstood", "youtube_id": "O7KFS53bUYA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I'm sorry, I misunderstood the meeting time and arrived late.", "tl": "Desculpe, eu entendi errado o horário da reunião e cheguei atrasado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I think you misunderstood me, I didn't mean to say you did a bad job.", "tl": "Acho que você me entendeu errado, eu não quis dizer que você fez um trabalho ruim."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We misunderstood the project instructions and had to start over.", "tl": "Nós entendemos errado as instruções do projeto e tivemos que começar de novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They misunderstood what the teacher explained in yesterday's class.", "tl": "Eles entenderam errado o que o professor explicou na aula de ontem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Did you misunderstand on purpose or was it just a distraction?", "tl": "Você entendeu errado de propósito ou foi apenas uma distração?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't want you to misunderstand my intention, I just want to help.", "tl": "Não quero que você entenda errado a minha intenção, só quero ajudar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3520, "expression_id": 3546, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dar um zoom", "english_gloss": "to zoom in", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Zoom in on the photo to be able to see his face.", "tl": "Dê um zoom na foto para conseguir ver o rosto dele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I zoomed in on the map, but the street is still very hard to find.", "tl": "Eu dei um zoom no mapa, mas a rua ainda está muito difícil de achar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Can you zoom in on the screen? I can't read the slides.", "tl": "Você pode dar um zoom na tela? Não estou conseguindo ler os slides."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you zoom in on the image, you will notice there is a typo.", "tl": "Se você der um zoom na imagem, vai perceber que há um erro de digitação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I was zooming in on the photo when my phone froze.", "tl": "Eu estava dando um zoom na foto quando o meu celular travou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We need to zoom in on this graph to better analyze the numbers.", "tl": "Nós precisamos dar um zoom neste gráfico para analisar melhor os números."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3519, "expression_id": 3545, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "figura de linguagem", "english_gloss": "figure of speech", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't take what I said literally, it was just a figure of speech.", "tl": "Não leve o que eu disse ao pé da letra, foi apenas uma figura de linguagem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In today's Portuguese class, we learned about different figures of speech.", "tl": "Na aula de português de hoje, nós aprendemos sobre diferentes figuras de linguagem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The writer uses this figure of speech to create a strong image in the reader's mind.", "tl": "O escritor usa essa figura de linguagem para criar uma imagem forte na mente do leitor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I didn't quite understand what you meant; is that some kind of figure of speech?", "tl": "Eu não entendi muito bem o que você quis dizer; isso é alguma figura de linguagem?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Saying that you are 'starving' is a very common figure of speech.", "tl": "Dizer que você está 'morrendo de fome' é uma figura de linguagem muito comum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Avoid using too many figures of speech in work reports so as not to confuse the clients.", "tl": "Evite usar muitas figuras de linguagem em relatórios de trabalho para não confundir os clientes."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3518, "expression_id": 3544, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "me pega", "english_gloss": "strikes me", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sometimes, homesickness hits me by surprise at the end of the day.", "tl": "Às vezes, a saudade de casa me pega de surpresa no fim do dia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I liked the apartment, but the condo fee is what gets me.", "tl": "Eu gostei do apartamento, mas o valor do condomínio é o que me pega."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This question always stumps me during the interview.", "tl": "Essa pergunta sempre me pega na hora da entrevista."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The end of this movie always gets to me, I can't help but cry.", "tl": "O final desse filme sempre me pega, não consigo não chorar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "What gets me in this situation is that nobody said anything beforehand.", "tl": "O que me pega nessa situação é que ninguém avisou nada antes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I try to wake up early, but tiredness always catches up with me in the middle of the afternoon.", "tl": "Eu tento acordar cedo, mas o cansaço sempre me pega no meio da tarde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3517, "expression_id": 3543, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "pobre de espírito", "english_gloss": "mean-spirited", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't be happy about his mistake; that is being very mean-spirited.", "tl": "Não fiques feliz com o erro dele; isso é ser muito pobre de espírito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She spends the day speaking ill of others; she is a very small-minded person.", "tl": "Ela passa o dia a falar mal dos outros, é uma pessoa muito pobre de espírito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The boss was mean-spirited by not recognizing the team's work.", "tl": "O chefe foi pobre de espírito ao não reconhecer o trabalho da equipa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He refused to help his own brother out of pure selfishness; what a mean-spirited man.", "tl": "Ele recusou-se a ajudar o próprio irmão por puro egoísmo; que homem pobre de espírito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Making nasty comments on the internet about someone's appearance is being very small-minded.", "tl": "Fazer comentários maldosos na internet sobre a aparência de alguém é ser muito pobre de espírito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I prefer to stay away from mean-spirited people who cannot stand to see others succeed.", "tl": "Eu prefiro afastar-me de pessoas pobres de espírito que não conseguem ver o sucesso dos outros."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3516, "expression_id": 3542, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "do céu", "english_gloss": "for heaven's sake", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For heaven's sake, why did you take so long to reply?", "tl": "Meu Deus do céu, por que você demorou tanto para responder?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Good heavens, did you guys see how heavy the rain was last night?", "tl": "Gente do céu, vocês viram o tamanho daquela chuva ontem à noite?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "For heaven's sake, turn off that TV, I need to study!", "tl": "Meu Deus do céu, desligue essa TV que eu preciso estudar!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For heaven's sake, where on earth did I leave the car keys?", "tl": "Meu Deus do céu, onde foi que eu deixei as chaves do carro?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For heaven's sake, I can't believe they canceled the concert at the last minute.", "tl": "Gente do céu, eu não acredito que eles cancelaram o show de última hora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "For heaven's sake, stop complaining and help me clean the kitchen.", "tl": "Meu Deus do céu, pare de reclamar e me ajude a limpar a cozinha."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3515, "expression_id": 3541, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "veio encher do saco", "english_gloss": "came to annoy people", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I was working peacefully when the boss came to annoy me about the report.", "tl": "Eu estava trabalhando tranquilo quando o chefe veio encher o saco por causa do relatório."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My sister came to annoy me because I borrowed her t-shirt.", "tl": "Minha irmã veio encher o saco porque eu peguei a camiseta dela emprestada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They came to annoy me just because I decided not to go to the party yesterday.", "tl": "Eles vieram encher o saco só porque eu decidi não ir à festa ontem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The neighbor came to annoy us again because of my dog's noise.", "tl": "O vizinho veio encher o saco de novo por causa do barulho do meu cachorro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That telemarketer came to annoy me right at my lunchtime.", "tl": "Aquele vendedor de telemarketing veio encher o saco bem na hora do meu almoço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I can't believe my ex-boyfriend came to annoy me right on my birthday.", "tl": "Não acredito que meu ex-namorado veio encher o saco logo no meu aniversário."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3514, "expression_id": 3540, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "virou alvo de", "english_gloss": "became the target of", "youtube_id": "OIqRVYUTwtY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The mayor became the target of criticism after canceling the New Year's event.", "tl": "O prefeito virou alvo de críticas após cancelar o evento de Ano Novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After that controversy, the supermarket chain became the target of investigations.", "tl": "Depois daquela polêmica, a rede de supermercados virou alvo de investigações."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The soccer player became the target of jokes on the internet because of his mistake in the game.", "tl": "O jogador de futebol virou alvo de piadas na internet por causa do seu erro no jogo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The new traffic law became the target of protests in several cities across the country.", "tl": "A nova lei de trânsito virou alvo de protestos em várias cidades do país."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She became the target of gossip in the office after she got the promotion.", "tl": "Ela virou alvo de fofocas no escritório depois que recebeu a promoção."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The abandoned mansion in the city center became the target of vandalism.", "tl": "O casarão abandonado no centro da cidade virou alvo de vandalismo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3513, "expression_id": 3539, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "alle prese con", "english_gloss": "dealing with", "youtube_id": "lL-w9A_EuN8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Right now I am dealing with a very complicated project at work.", "tl": "In questo momento sono alle prese con un progetto molto complicato al lavoro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Marco is at home, dealing with his son's math homework.", "tl": "Marco è a casa, alle prese con i compiti di matematica di suo figlio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We are dealing with a technical problem that we can't seem to solve.", "tl": "Siamo alle prese con un problema tecnico che non riusciamo a risolvere."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Are you still dealing with the documents for the move to Spain?", "tl": "Sei ancora alle prese con i documenti per il trasferimento in Spagna?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My grandmother is in the kitchen, busy preparing dinner for the whole family.", "tl": "Mia nonna è in cucina, alle prese con la preparazione della cena per tutta la famiglia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Many students are dealing with the seasonal flu at this time.", "tl": "Molti studenti sono alle prese con l'influenza stagionale in questo periodo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3512, "expression_id": 3538, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "circolo vizioso", "english_gloss": "vicious cycle", "youtube_id": "lL-w9A_EuN8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you don't get enough sleep, you get stressed, and this creates a vicious cycle that is hard to break.", "tl": "Se non dormi abbastanza, ti stressi, e questo crea un circolo vizioso difficile da interrompere."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Asking for another loan to pay off previous debts is the beginning of a vicious cycle.", "tl": "Chiedere un altro prestito per pagare i debiti precedenti è l'inizio di un circolo vizioso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The more you isolate yourself from others, the more you are afraid of talking to people: it's a real vicious cycle.", "tl": "Più ti isoli dagli altri, più hai paura di parlare con la gente: è un vero circolo vizioso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Many young people can't find a job because they don't have experience, but they can't get experience without a job: a cl", "tl": "Molti giovani non trovano lavoro perché non hanno esperienza, ma non possono fare esperienza senza un lavoro: un classic"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Eating junk food when you are sad makes you feel guilty, feeding a vicious cycle.", "tl": "Mangiare cibo spazzatura quando sei triste ti fa sentire in colpa, alimentando un circolo vizioso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We need to find a way to get out of this vicious cycle of procrastination and anxiety.", "tl": "Dobbiamo trovare un modo per uscire da questo circolo vizioso di procrastinazione e ansia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3511, "expression_id": 3537, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fare fatica", "english_gloss": "to struggle", "youtube_id": "lL-w9A_EuN8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I always struggle to wake up early in the morning.", "tl": "Faccio sempre fatica a svegliarmi presto la mattina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Marco struggled a lot to finish the work on time.", "tl": "Marco ha fatto molta fatica a finire il lavoro in tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We are struggling to understand how this new program works.", "tl": "Facciamo fatica a capire come funziona questo nuovo programma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "At the beginning, I struggled to speak in Italian, but now it's going better.", "tl": "All'inizio facevo fatica a parlare in italiano, ma ora va meglio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you don't study regularly, you will struggle to pass the exam.", "tl": "Se non studi regolarmente, farai fatica a superare l'esame."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Many elderly people struggle with modern technology.", "tl": "Molti anziani fanno fatica con la tecnologia moderna."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3510, "expression_id": 3536, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "le vent a tourné", "english_gloss": "the tide has turned / things have changed", "youtube_id": "ws4pscEVktE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "At first, the company was losing money, but the tide has turned and we are now making a profit.", "tl": "Au début, l'entreprise perdait de l'argent, mais le vent a tourné et nous faisons maintenant des bénéfices."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our team was losing the match, but the tide turned in the second half.", "tl": "Notre équipe perdait le match, mais le vent a tourné en deuxième mi-temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The polls show that the tide has turned for the current government.", "tl": "Les sondages montrent que le vent a tourné pour le gouvernement actuel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I've had a lot of bad luck this year, but I feel that the tide has finally turned.", "tl": "J'ai eu beaucoup de malchance cette année, mais je sens que le vent a enfin tourné."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When he presented his evidence, the tide turned in his favor.", "tl": "Quand il a présenté ses preuves, le vent a tourné en sa faveur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Customers are no longer buying this product; the tide has turned toward more eco-friendly options.", "tl": "Les clients n'achètent plus ce produit ; le vent a tourné vers des options plus écologiques."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3509, "expression_id": 3535, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tenir en respect", "english_gloss": "to keep at bay / hold at bay", "youtube_id": "ws4pscEVktE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The police officers managed to keep the crowd at bay behind the barriers.", "tl": "Les policiers ont réussi à tenir la foule en respect derrière les barrières."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "With a simple stick, he was able to keep the aggressive dog at bay.", "tl": "Avec un simple bâton, il a pu tenir le chien agressif en respect."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our team kept the opponent at bay during the entire first half.", "tl": "Notre équipe a tenu l'adversaire en respect pendant toute la première mi-temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The soldiers used smoke bombs to keep the enemies at bay.", "tl": "Les soldats ont utilisé des fumigènes pour tenir les ennemis en respect."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Thanks to this new strategy, we are keeping our competitors at bay.", "tl": "Grâce à cette nouvelle stratégie, nous tenons nos concurrents en respect."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This medical treatment keeps the disease at bay for now.", "tl": "Ce traitement médical permet de tenir la maladie en respect pour l'instant."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3508, "expression_id": 3534, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se mettre à la page", "english_gloss": "to get up to date", "youtube_id": "ws4pscEVktE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our company absolutely needs to get up to date regarding new technologies.", "tl": "Notre entreprise doit absolument se mettre à la page concernant les nouvelles technologies."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My grandfather finally got up to date and now uses social media.", "tl": "Mon grand-père s'est enfin mis à la page et utilise maintenant les réseaux sociaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you want to work in fashion, you have to get up to date.", "tl": "Si tu veux travailler dans la mode, tu dois te mettre à la page."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "With all these changes, we are going to have to get up to date quickly.", "tl": "Avec tous ces changements, nous allons devoir nous mettre à la page rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He never reads the news, he really should get up to date.", "tl": "Il ne lit jamais les nouvelles, il devrait vraiment se mettre à la page."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I took a training course to get up to date on this new software.", "tl": "J'ai suivi une formation pour me mettre à la page sur ce nouveau logiciel."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3507, "expression_id": 3533, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "chair à canon", "english_gloss": "cannon fodder", "youtube_id": "ws4pscEVktE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "During the First World War, millions of young soldiers were used as cannon fodder.", "tl": "Pendant la Première Guerre mondiale, des millions de jeunes soldats ont été utilisés comme de la chair à canon."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In this big company, interns sometimes feel like they are cannon fodder.", "tl": "Dans cette grande entreprise, les stagiaires ont parfois l'impression d'être de la chair à canon."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The people refuse to be cannon fodder for the ambitions of their leaders.", "tl": "Le peuple refuse d'être de la chair à canon pour les ambitions de ses dirigeants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In this video game, you have to send these small units first; they serve as cannon fodder.", "tl": "Dans ce jeu vidéo, tu dois envoyer ces petites unités en premier, elles servent de chair à canon."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The general doesn't care about his men; he simply treats them as cannon fodder.", "tl": "Le général ne se soucie pas de ses hommes, il les traite simplement comme de la chair à canon."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The poorest workers are often the cannon fodder of the economy in times of crisis.", "tl": "Les travailleurs les plus pauvres sont souvent la chair à canon de l'économie en temps de crise."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3506, "expression_id": 3532, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à la merci de", "english_gloss": "at the mercy of", "youtube_id": "ws4pscEVktE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Without an umbrella, we were at the mercy of the rain.", "tl": "Sans parapluie, nous étions à la merci de la pluie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Small businesses are often at the mercy of large corporations.", "tl": "Les petits commerces sont souvent à la merci des grandes entreprises."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you don't protect your computer, you are at the mercy of hackers.", "tl": "Si tu ne protèges pas ton ordinateur, tu es à la merci des pirates informatiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "By traveling without a reservation, you find yourself at the mercy of hotel availability.", "tl": "En voyageant sans réservation, on se retrouve à la merci de la disponibilité des hôtels."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He doesn't want to show his feelings so as not to be at the mercy of others.", "tl": "Il ne veut pas montrer ses sentiments pour ne pas être à la merci des autres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The broken-down boat was at the mercy of the waves and the wind.", "tl": "Le bateau en panne était à la merci des vagues et du vent."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3505, "expression_id": 3531, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "sous cloche", "english_gloss": "under wraps / isolated / protected", "youtube_id": "ws4pscEVktE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You can't raise your children in a bubble; they have to learn to face the real world.", "tl": "On ne peut pas élever ses enfants sous cloche ; ils doivent apprendre à faire face au monde réel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The government decided to keep this scientific project under wraps to prevent leaks.", "tl": "Le gouvernement a décidé de mettre ce projet scientifique sous cloche pour éviter les fuites."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "During the pandemic, the entire population felt like they were living in a bubble for months.", "tl": "Pendant la pandémie, toute la population a eu l'impression de vivre sous cloche pendant des mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Protecting this forest doesn't mean sealing it off completely and banning all public access.", "tl": "Protéger cette forêt ne signifie pas la mettre sous cloche et interdire tout accès au public."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since her breakup, she prefers to stay in her shell and avoid meeting new people.", "tl": "Depuis sa rupture amoureuse, elle préfère rester sous cloche et éviter de faire de nouvelles rencontres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He grew up in a bubble, highly protected by his parents, and is having a hard time adapting to student life.", "tl": "Il a grandi sous cloche, très protégé par ses parents, et a du mal à s'adapter à la vie étudiante."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3504, "expression_id": 3530, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "sorti de nulle part", "english_gloss": "out of nowhere", "youtube_id": "vjB86T0-g0Y", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "A dog came out of nowhere and crossed the road right in front of my car.", "tl": "Un chien est sorti de nulle part et a traversé la route juste devant ma voiture."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This idea came out of nowhere, but it turned out to be excellent for our project.", "tl": "Cette idée est sortie de nulle part, mais elle s'est avérée excellente pour notre projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "A violent storm, coming out of nowhere, ruined our afternoon at the beach.", "tl": "Un violent orage, sorti de nulle part, a gâché notre après-midi à la plage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He appeared in front of me, as if he had come out of nowhere.", "tl": "Il est apparu devant moi, comme s'il était sorti de nulle part."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Her question was completely out of nowhere and really threw me off.", "tl": "Sa question était complètement sortie de nulle part et m'a beaucoup déstabilisé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This young player, coming out of nowhere, managed to beat the world champion.", "tl": "Ce jeune joueur, sorti de nulle part, a réussi à battre le champion du monde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3503, "expression_id": 3529, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en toute franchise", "english_gloss": "in all honesty", "youtube_id": "vjB86T0-g0Y", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In all honesty, I think this project is going to take more time than expected.", "tl": "En toute franchise, je pense que ce projet va demander plus de temps que prévu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Tell me what you think about it, in all honesty.", "tl": "Dis-moi ce que tu en penses, en toute franchise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In all honesty, I didn't like this movie at all.", "tl": "En toute franchise, ce film ne m'a pas du tout plu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We need to speak in all honesty if we want to solve this problem.", "tl": "Nous devons parler en toute franchise si nous voulons résoudre ce problème."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In all honesty, I prefer to stay home tonight.", "tl": "En toute franchise, je préfère rester chez moi ce soir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I must admit, in all honesty, that I don't know the answer.", "tl": "Je dois avouer, en toute franchise, que je ne connais pas la réponse."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3502, "expression_id": 3528, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en bloc", "english_gloss": "outright", "youtube_id": "vjB86T0-g0Y", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The committee rejected all of our reform proposals outright.", "tl": "Le comité a rejeté en bloc toutes nos propositions de réforme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is impossible to buy these items separately; they are sold as a whole.", "tl": "Il est impossible d'acheter ces articles séparément, ils sont vendus en bloc."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You shouldn't accept his explanations outright without asking yourself any questions.", "tl": "Tu ne devrais pas accepter ses explications en bloc sans te poser de questions."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Following the scandal, the members of the board of directors resigned en masse.", "tl": "Suite au scandale, les membres du conseil d'administration ont démissionné en bloc."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The accused denies all the accusations brought against him outright.", "tl": "L'accusé nie en bloc toutes les accusations portées contre lui."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The MPs voted on the new environmental bill as a whole.", "tl": "Les députés ont voté en bloc le nouveau projet de loi sur l'environnement."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3501, "expression_id": 3527, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fare pressione", "english_gloss": "to put pressure", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The journalists are putting pressure on the government to get answers.", "tl": "I giornalisti stanno facendo pressione sul governo per avere risposte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My father pressured me to study law.", "tl": "Mio padre ha fatto pressione su di me perché studiassi legge."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We must not put pressure on the client, otherwise they will change their mind.", "tl": "Non dobbiamo fare pressione sul cliente, altrimenti cambierà idea."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My friends were pressuring me to go out, but I was too tired.", "tl": "I miei amici facevano pressione su di me per uscire, ma ero troppo stanco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you keep pressuring her, she will end up getting angry.", "tl": "Se continui a farle pressione, finirà per arrabbiarsi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The director will put pressure on the team to finish the project on time.", "tl": "Il direttore farà pressione sul team per finire il progetto in tempo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3499, "expression_id": 3525, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "per l'ennesima volta", "english_gloss": "for the umpteenth time", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I lost my house keys for the umpteenth time.", "tl": "Ho perso le chiavi di casa per l'ennesima volta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Marco arrived late for the umpteenth time, and the boss got angry.", "tl": "Marco è arrivato in ritardo per l'ennesima volta, e il capo si è arrabbiato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My computer froze for the umpteenth time while I was working.", "tl": "Il mio computer si è bloccato per l'ennesima volta mentre stavo lavorando."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We discussed the same problem for the umpteenth time.", "tl": "Abbiamo discusso dello stesso problema per l'ennesima volta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The train to Rome was canceled for the umpteenth time this week.", "tl": "Il treno per Roma è stato cancellato per l'ennesima volta questa settimana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I'm telling you for the umpteenth time that you need to be careful when driving.", "tl": "Ti ripeto per l'ennesima volta che devi fare attenzione quando guidi."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3497, "expression_id": 3523, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fare più affidamento", "english_gloss": "to rely more", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We need to rely more on our colleagues to finish this project.", "tl": "Dobbiamo fare più affidamento sui nostri colleghi per finire questo progetto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I would like to rely more on the GPS, but sometimes it is wrong.", "tl": "Vorrei fare più affidamento sul navigatore, ma a volte si sbaglia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The parents started to rely more on their older children.", "tl": "I genitori hanno iniziato a fare più affidamento sui figli grandi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You should rely more on your own abilities instead of always asking for help.", "tl": "Dovresti fare più affidamento sulle tue capacità invece di chiedere sempre aiuto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I think the company should rely more on local resources.", "tl": "Penso che l'azienda debba fare più affidamento sulle risorse locali."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In the future, we will rely more on public transport to reduce pollution.", "tl": "In futuro faremo più affidamento sui trasporti pubblici per ridurre l'inquinamento."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3496, "expression_id": 3522, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "fühlen sich ... unter Druck", "english_gloss": "to feel pressured", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I often feel pressured at work because I have so many tasks.", "tl": "Ich fühle mich bei der Arbeit oft unter Druck, weil ich so viele Aufgaben habe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Do you feel pressured by your parents to study medicine?", "tl": "Fühlst du dich von deinen Eltern unter Druck, Medizin zu studieren?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many students feel extremely pressured during the exam period.", "tl": "Viele Studenten fühlen sich während der Prüfungsphase extrem unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We shouldn't ask her for an answer right away, otherwise she will feel pressured.", "tl": "Wir sollten sie nicht sofort nach einer Antwort fragen, sonst fühlt sie sich unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since we started the new project, we constantly feel pressured.", "tl": "Seit wir das neue Projekt gestartet haben, fühlen wir uns ständig unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He felt pressured to make a quick decision.", "tl": "Er fühlte sich unter Druck, eine schnelle Entscheidung zu treffen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3495, "expression_id": 3521, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "macht schon was her", "english_gloss": "is quite impressive / looks good", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Your new suit really looks impressive!", "tl": "Dein neuer Anzug macht schon was her!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new kitchen was expensive, but it really looks great.", "tl": "Die neue Küche war zwar teuer, aber sie macht schon was her."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "An internship abroad looks really impressive on a CV.", "tl": "Ein Praktikum im Ausland macht im Lebenslauf schon was her."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "These big rims really make the car look impressive.", "tl": "Diese großen Felgen machen an dem Auto schon was her."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company's new website looks quite impressive.", "tl": "Die neue Website der Firma macht schon was her."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The decorations for the party look really impressive, don't you think?", "tl": "Die Dekoration für die Party macht schon was her, findest du nicht?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3494, "expression_id": 3520, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ausgedachter Humbug", "english_gloss": "made-up nonsense", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Do you really believe what is written in this newspaper? That is all just made-up nonsense!", "tl": "Glaubst du wirklich, was in dieser Zeitung steht? Das ist doch alles nur ausgedachter Humbug!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "His explanation for the delay sounds like completely made-up nonsense.", "tl": "Seine Erklärung für die Verspätung klingt wie völlig ausgedachter Humbug."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many people believe in horoscopes, but for me, that is all made-up nonsense.", "tl": "Viele Leute glauben an Horoskope, aber für mich ist das alles ausgedachter Humbug."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't tell me fairy tales! Your whole story is nothing but made-up nonsense.", "tl": "Erzähl mir keine Märchen! Deine ganze Geschichte ist nichts als ausgedachter Humbug."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The professor quickly proved that the company's claims were just made-up nonsense.", "tl": "Der Professor bewies schnell, dass die Behauptungen der Firma nur ausgedachter Humbug waren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't believe these rumors, it's all made-up nonsense from start to finish.", "tl": "Ich schenke diesen Gerüchten keinen Glauben, das ist doch alles von vorne bis hinten ausgedachter Humbug."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3493, "expression_id": 3519, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf den eigenen Instinkt zu vertrauen", "english_gloss": "to trust one's own instinct", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In difficult situations, it is important to trust one's own instinct.", "tl": "Es ist in schwierigen Situationen wichtig, auf den eigenen Instinkt zu vertrauen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I have learned to always trust my own instinct in my job.", "tl": "Ich habe gelernt, in meinem Beruf immer auf meinen eigenen Instinkt zu vertrauen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With this important decision, I am trusting my own instinct completely.", "tl": "Bei dieser wichtigen Entscheidung vertraue ich ganz auf meinen eigenen Instinkt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You should try to trust your own instinct more when looking for a partner.", "tl": "Du solltest versuchen, bei der Partnersuche mehr auf deinen eigenen Instinkt zu vertrauen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "As the boss of the company, she often has to trust her own instinct.", "tl": "Als Chefin der Firma muss sie oft auf ihren eigenen Instinkt vertrauen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Sometimes it is better to trust one's own instinct than to listen to the opinion of others.", "tl": "Manchmal ist es besser, auf den eigenen Instinkt zu vertrauen, als auf die Meinung anderer zu hören."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3492, "expression_id": 3518, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "kein Zufall zu sein", "english_gloss": "to be no coincidence", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That we are meeting here today seems to be no coincidence.", "tl": "Dass wir uns heute hier treffen, scheint kein Zufall zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Her quick promotion seems to be no coincidence, because she worked very hard.", "tl": "Ihre schnelle Beförderung scheint kein Zufall zu sein, denn sie hat sehr hart gearbeitet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That flight prices are rising just before the holidays seems to be no coincidence.", "tl": "Dass die Preise für Flüge genau vor den Ferien steigen, scheint kein Zufall zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It seems to be no coincidence that the boss is in such a good mood today.", "tl": "Es scheint kein Zufall zu sein, dass der Chef heute so gute Laune hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That both washing machines broke down on the same day seems to be no coincidence.", "tl": "Dass beide Waschmaschinen am selben Tag kaputtgingen, scheint kein Zufall zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Her sudden cancellation seems to be no coincidence; she definitely didn't want to come.", "tl": "Ihre plötzliche Absage scheint kein Zufall zu sein; sie wollte bestimmt nicht kommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3491, "expression_id": 3517, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Einfluss ... zu nehmen", "english_gloss": "to exert influence on something", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The citizens want to influence the city's political decisions.", "tl": "Die Bürger wollen Einfluss auf die politischen Entscheidungen der Stadt nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My boss tried to influence my decision.", "tl": "Mein Chef hat versucht, Einfluss auf meine Entscheidung zu nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Parents often try to influence their children's development.", "tl": "Eltern versuchen oft, Einfluss auf die Entwicklung ihrer Kinder zu nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is not easy to influence other people's opinions.", "tl": "Es ist nicht leicht, Einfluss auf die Meinung anderer Menschen zu nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Advertising constantly tries to influence our purchasing decisions.", "tl": "Werbung versucht ständig, Einfluss auf unsere Kaufentscheidungen zu nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Through regular exercise, one can positively influence one's health.", "tl": "Durch regelmäßigen Sport kann man positiv Einfluss auf seine Gesundheit nehmen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3490, "expression_id": 3516, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Anhaltspunkte dafür", "english_gloss": "clues or indications of this", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "So far, there are no indications that it is a crime.", "tl": "Es gibt bisher keine Anhaltspunkte dafür, dass es sich um ein Verbrechen handelt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We have concrete indications that prices will rise soon.", "tl": "Wir haben konkrete Anhaltspunkte dafür, dass die Preise bald steigen werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The doctor found no indications that the pain has a serious cause.", "tl": "Der Arzt fand keine Anhaltspunkte dafür, dass die Schmerzen eine ernste Ursache haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Are there any indications that the weather will change tomorrow?", "tl": "Gibt es irgendwelche Anhaltspunkte dafür, dass sich das Wetter morgen ändert?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The police are looking for clues that the thief had help.", "tl": "Die Polizei sucht nach Anhaltspunkten dafür, dass der Dieb Hilfe hatte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I see no indications that he is dissatisfied with his work.", "tl": "Ich sehe keine Anhaltspunkte dafür, dass er unzufrieden mit seiner Arbeit ist."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3489, "expression_id": 3515, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "dahinter steckt", "english_gloss": "is behind it / is the cause", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The website suddenly isn't working. What could be behind it?", "tl": "Die Website funktioniert plötzlich nicht mehr. Was steckt wohl dahinter?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She suddenly changed her mind. I'm sure there is a plan behind it.", "tl": "Sie hat ihre Meinung plötzlich geändert. Ich bin sicher, dahinter steckt ein Plan."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The offer sounds almost too good. There is definitely a trick behind it.", "tl": "Das Angebot klingt fast zu gut. Dahinter steckt bestimmt ein Trick."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He has had a headache for days. Hopefully there is no serious illness behind it.", "tl": "Er hat seit Tagen Kopfschmerzen. Hoffentlich steckt keine ernste Krankheit dahinter."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Someone sent me flowers anonymously. I would like to know who is behind it.", "tl": "Jemand hat mir anonym Blumen geschickt. Ich würde gerne wissen, wer dahintersteckt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The project was a great success, but weeks of hard work are behind it.", "tl": "Das Projekt war ein großer Erfolg, aber dahinter steckt wochenlange harte Arbeit."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3488, "expression_id": 3514, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ist da die Rede", "english_gloss": "there is talk of something", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Which new project is actually being talked about there?", "tl": "Von welchem neuen Projekt ist da eigentlich die Rede?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Is there talk of me by any chance? I have nothing to do with it.", "tl": "Ist da etwa von mir die Rede? Ich habe nichts damit zu tun."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Is there talk of job cuts in the cost-cutting measures too?", "tl": "Ist da bei den Sparmaßnahmen auch von Stellenabbau die Rede?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "What exactly is being talked about there? I don't understand the context.", "tl": "Wovon ist da genau die Rede? Ich verstehe den Zusammenhang nicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In the news, there is talk of severe storms on the weekend.", "tl": "In den Nachrichten ist da von heftigen Stürmen am Wochenende die Rede."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Is there really talk of a wedding? They have only known each other for a month!", "tl": "Ist da wirklich von einer Hochzeit die Rede? Die beiden kennen sich doch erst seit einem Monat!"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3487, "expression_id": 3513, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "schlecht machen", "english_gloss": "to badmouth or disparage someone", "youtube_id": "QOCBa9wxIEE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He always badmouths his colleagues behind their backs.", "tl": "Er macht seine Kollegen hinter ihrem Rücken immer schlecht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Why did you badmouth my new girlfriend so much in front of your parents?", "tl": "Warum hast du meine neue Freundin vor deinen Eltern so schlecht gemacht?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There is no point in disparaging others' work just to make yourself look better.", "tl": "Es bringt nichts, die Arbeit von anderen schlechtzumachen, nur um selbst besser dazustehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I worked hard for this success and won't let anyone run it down.", "tl": "Ich habe hart für diesen Erfolg gearbeitet und lasse mir das von niemandem schlecht machen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you are dissatisfied, talk to him in person instead of badmouthing him everywhere.", "tl": "Wenn du unzufrieden bist, sprich mit ihm persönlich, anstatt ihn überall schlechtzumachen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The competition often tries to disparage our products, but the customers trust us.", "tl": "Die Konkurrenz versucht oft, unsere Produkte schlechtzumachen, aber die Kunden vertrauen uns."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3483, "expression_id": 3509, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür liegen", "english_gloss": "to have supplies readily available nearby", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry about the snowstorm, we have supplies readily available nearby anyway.", "tl": "Mach dir keine Sorgen wegen des Schneesturms, bei uns liegen ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If visitors come over the weekend, that's no problem, since we have supplies readily available anyway.", "tl": "Wenn am Wochenende Besuch kommt, ist das kein Problem, da ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We don't need to go out to the supermarket today because we already have supplies lying right outside the door anyway.", "tl": "Wir müssen heute nicht extra in den Supermarkt gehen, weil ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In case of an emergency, it is reassuring to know that supplies are readily available nearby anyway.", "tl": "Für den Notfall ist es beruhigend zu wissen, dass ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why did you buy so much bread when we have supplies readily available nearby anyway?", "tl": "Warum hast du so viel Brot gekauft, wenn bei uns ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür liegen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In our mountain cabin, we don't have to worry about food, as we have supplies readily available nearby anyway.", "tl": "In unserer Berghütte müssen wir uns keine Sorgen um Essen machen, da ohnehin Vorräte vor der Tür liegen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3477, "expression_id": 3503, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "vor der Tür liegen", "english_gloss": "to be readily available / stored nearby", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "All the firewood is stored right outside the door, so we don't have to walk far in winter.", "tl": "Das ganze Kaminholz liegt direkt vor der Tür, sodass wir im Winter nicht weit laufen müssen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You don't have to travel far to experience adventure; good things are often right at your doorstep.", "tl": "Du musst nicht weit reisen, um Abenteuer zu erleben; das Gute liegt oft direkt vor der Tür."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The mail carrier didn't leave the package with the neighbor; it is lying right outside the door.", "tl": "Der Postbote hat das Paket nicht beim Nachbarn abgegeben, es liegt direkt vor der Tür."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After graduation, many great career opportunities are practically right at your doorstep.", "tl": "Nach dem Studium liegen dir viele tolle Karrieremöglichkeiten quasi vor der Tür."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I love this apartment because the park and a large supermarket are located right on our doorstep.", "tl": "Ich liebe diese Wohnung, weil der Park und ein großer Supermarkt direkt vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You don't need to buy expensive stones; all the building material is lying right outside in the garden anyway.", "tl": "Du brauchst keine teuren Steine zu kaufen, das ganze Baumaterial liegt doch direkt vor der Tür im Garten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3476, "expression_id": 3502, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "unter Druck geraten", "english_gloss": "to come under pressure", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Because of the new project, our team has come under a lot of pressure.", "tl": "Wegen des neuen Projekts ist unser Team stark unter Druck geraten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The politician is coming under pressure because he did not keep his promises.", "tl": "Der Politiker gerät unter Druck, weil er seine Versprechen nicht gehalten hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many small businesses came under financial pressure during the crisis.", "tl": "Viele kleine Geschäfte sind während der Krise finanziell unter Druck geraten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Students often come under a lot of pressure before exams.", "tl": "Schüler geraten oft vor den Prüfungen stark unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't want to come under pressure, so I prefer to start the work early.", "tl": "Ich möchte nicht unter Druck geraten, deshalb fange ich lieber früh mit der Arbeit an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After the first goal against them, the team came under complete pressure.", "tl": "Nach dem ersten Gegentor ist die Mannschaft völlig unter Druck geraten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3475, "expression_id": 3501, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "im Zuge von", "english_gloss": "in the course of", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the course of restructurings in the company, new departments were established.", "tl": "Im Zuge von Umstrukturierungen in der Firma wurden neue Abteilungen gegründet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In the course of construction work, the main street is closed on the weekend.", "tl": "Im Zuge von Bauarbeiten ist die Hauptstraße am Wochenende gesperrt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "As part of new school reforms, digital learning is being promoted more strongly.", "tl": "Im Zuge von neuen Schulreformen wird das digitale Lernen stärker gefördert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In the course of climate changes, we have to adapt our way of life.", "tl": "Im Zuge von Klimaveränderungen müssen wir unsere Lebensweise anpassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In the course of medical examinations, all employees were tested.", "tl": "Im Zuge von medizinischen Untersuchungen wurden alle Mitarbeiter getestet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In the course of police investigations, important evidence was found.", "tl": "Im Zuge von polizeilichen Ermittlungen wurden wichtige Beweise gefunden."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3473, "expression_id": 3499, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "hinterherarbeitet", "english_gloss": "to work to keep up / react constantly", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Because we are understaffed, we are only playing catch-up in the office.", "tl": "Weil wir zu wenig Personal haben, arbeiten wir im Büro nur noch hinterher."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We need to plan better so we don't constantly work to keep up with deadlines.", "tl": "Wir müssen besser planen, um nicht ständig den Terminen hinterherzuarbeiten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After my vacation, I spent a whole week just working to catch up.", "tl": "Nach meinem Urlaub habe ich eine Woche lang nur hinterhergearbeitet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our software is so old that the IT department is always just reacting to the errors.", "tl": "Unsere Software ist so alt, dass die IT-Abteilung den Fehlern immer nur hinterherarbeitet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I would rather prepare my tasks instead of constantly having to work just to keep up.", "tl": "Ich möchte meine Aufgaben lieber vorbereiten, statt ständig nur hinterherarbeiten zu müssen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Since the new shop opened, we've just been working flat out to keep up with the many orders.", "tl": "Seit der neue Laden geöffnet hat, arbeiten wir den vielen Bestellungen nur noch hinterher."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3472, "expression_id": 3498, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "dringend angewiesen", "english_gloss": "urgently dependent", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I don't have a car and am therefore urgently dependent on public transportation.", "tl": "Ich habe kein Auto und bin daher dringend auf die öffentlichen Verkehrsmittel angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For the success of this project, we are urgently relying on your help.", "tl": "Für den Erfolg dieses Projekts sind wir dringend auf deine Hilfe angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many low-income families are urgently dependent on government support.", "tl": "Viele Familien mit geringem Einkommen sind dringend auf staatliche Unterstützung angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The sick man is urgently dependent on a new medication from the USA.", "tl": "Der kranke Mann ist dringend auf ein neues Medikament aus den USA angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since I work from home, I am urgently dependent on a stable internet connection.", "tl": "Da ich im Homeoffice arbeite, bin ich dringend auf eine stabile Internetverbindung angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "As a small, new company, we are urgently dependent on our customers' feedback.", "tl": "Als kleines, neues Unternehmen sind wir dringend auf das Feedback unserer Kunden angewiesen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3470, "expression_id": 3496, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "zur Not", "english_gloss": "if necessary / in an emergency", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If we don't find a hotel, we can sleep in the car in a pinch.", "tl": "Wenn wir kein Hotel finden, können wir zur Not im Auto schlafen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If necessary, I can also work on Sunday to finish the project.", "tl": "Ich kann zur Not auch am Sonntag arbeiten, um das Projekt fertigzustellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We don't have fresh tomatoes, but in a pinch, we can use canned ones.", "tl": "Wir haben keine frischen Tomaten, aber zur Not können wir Tomaten aus der Dose nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If the train doesn't run, I will take a taxi if necessary.", "tl": "Wenn der Zug nicht fährt, nehme ich zur Not ein Taxi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The table is small, but if necessary, six people can fit here.", "tl": "Der Tisch ist klein, aber zur Not passen hier sechs Personen hin."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My laptop is broken, but in a pinch, I can write the emails on my phone.", "tl": "Mein Laptop ist kaputt, aber zur Not kann ich die E-Mails auf dem Handy schreiben."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3469, "expression_id": 3495, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die sie unter Druck setzen", "english_gloss": "that put them under pressure", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "She works for two managers who constantly put her under pressure.", "tl": "Sie arbeitet für zwei Manager, die sie ständig unter Druck setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Many students suffer from the high expectations that put them under pressure.", "tl": "Viele Schüler leiden unter den hohen Erwartungen, die sie unter Druck setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The employees have tight deadlines this week that are putting them under pressure.", "tl": "Die Mitarbeiter haben diese Woche enge Fristen, die sie unter Druck setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The parents have financial problems that put them under pressure every day.", "tl": "Die Eltern haben finanzielle Probleme, die sie jeden Tag unter Druck setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is often social media that puts them under pressure to be perfect.", "tl": "Es sind oft die sozialen Medien, die sie unter Druck setzen, perfekt zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The athletes are complaining about the new rules that put them under pressure.", "tl": "Die Sportler beschweren sich über die neuen Regeln, die sie unter Druck setzen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3463, "expression_id": 3489, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich dafür einsetzen", "english_gloss": "to advocate for / support", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We must advocate for our city becoming greener.", "tl": "Wir müssen uns dafür einsetzen, dass unsere Stadt grüner wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The works council is campaigning to improve working conditions.", "tl": "Der Betriebsrat setzt sich dafür ein, die Arbeitsbedingungen zu verbessern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many parents are advocating for the school to be modernized.", "tl": "Viele Eltern setzen sich dafür ein, dass die Schule modernisiert wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She has always championed equal opportunities for all people.", "tl": "Sie hat sich immer dafür eingesetzt, dass alle Menschen die gleichen Chancen haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why don't you advocate for us getting a new sports field?", "tl": "Warum setzt du dich nicht dafür ein, dass wir einen neuen Sportplatz bekommen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our boss is pushing for us to get more flexible working hours.", "tl": "Unser Chef setzt sich dafür ein, dass wir flexiblere Arbeitszeiten bekommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3458, "expression_id": 3484, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "den Betrieb ... bereits einstellen", "english_gloss": "to already cease operations", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The small bakery on the corner has already ceased operations.", "tl": "Die kleine Bäckerei an der Ecke hat den Betrieb bereits eingestellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Because of the bad weather, the ferry has already ceased operations.", "tl": "Wegen des schlechten Wetters hat die Fähre den Betrieb bereits eingestellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I heard that the old factory on the outskirts of town has already ceased operations.", "tl": "Ich habe gehört, dass die alte Fabrik am Stadtrand den Betrieb bereits eingestellt hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Since there were too few users, the online platform has already ceased operations.", "tl": "Da es zu wenige Nutzer gab, hat die Online-Plattform den Betrieb bereits eingestellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The swimming pool already had to cease operations due to high energy costs.", "tl": "Das Schwimmbad musste wegen der hohen Energiekosten den Betrieb bereits einstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Although it was only founded last year, the start-up has already ceased operations.", "tl": "Obwohl es erst letztes Jahr gegründet wurde, hat das Start-up den Betrieb bereits eingestellt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3456, "expression_id": 3482, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "am Fliegenfänger hängen", "english_gloss": "to be left high and dry", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My colleague just fell ill, and now I'm left high and dry with the whole project.", "tl": "Mein Kollege ist einfach krankgeworden, und jetzt hänge ich mit dem ganzen Projekt am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If the bus leaves without us, we'll be left high and dry here.", "tl": "Wenn der Bus ohne uns abfährt, hängen wir hier am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Without the bank's financial support, the small company is left high and dry.", "tl": "Ohne die finanzielle Unterstützung der Bank hängt die kleine Firma am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You promised to help me; please don't leave me high and dry now!", "tl": "Du hast mir versprochen zu helfen; bitte lass mich jetzt nicht am Fliegenfänger hängen!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When the internet suddenly went down, all the employees in the office were left high and dry.", "tl": "Als das Internet plötzlich ausfiel, hingen alle Mitarbeiter im Büro am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The helpers didn't show up, and I was left completely high and dry on moving day.", "tl": "Die Helfer sind nicht gekommen, und ich hing am Umzugstag völlig am Fliegenfänger."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3455, "expression_id": 3481, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "zum Opfer gefallen sind", "english_gloss": "to fall victim to", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Many old trees in the city park fell victim to the severe storm.", "tl": "Viele alte Bäume im Stadtpark sind dem schweren Sturm zum Opfer gefallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Unfortunately, many older people fell victim to this online scam.", "tl": "Leider sind viele ältere Menschen diesem Online-Betrug zum Opfer gefallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Some small shops in the city center fell victim to the economic crisis.", "tl": "Einige kleine Geschäfte in der Innenstadt sind der Wirtschaftskrise zum Opfer gefallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Unfortunately, my vacation plans fell victim to the flu.", "tl": "Meine Urlaubspläne sind leider der Grippe zum Opfer gefallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The planned cultural project fell victim to the city's budget cuts.", "tl": "Das geplante Kulturprojekt ist den Sparmaßnahmen der Stadt zum Opfer gefallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Many historical buildings fell victim to the great fire back then.", "tl": "Viele historische Gebäude sind damals dem großen Brand zum Opfer gefallen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3452, "expression_id": 3478, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "anzugehen", "english_gloss": "to tackle / address", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We need to find a way to tackle this project together.", "tl": "Wir müssen einen Weg finden, dieses Projekt gemeinsam anzugehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is important to address this problem as quickly as possible.", "tl": "Es ist wichtig, dieses Problem so schnell wie möglich anzugehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I have decided to approach my fitness goals with more motivation this year.", "tl": "Ich habe beschlossen, meine Fitnessziele dieses Jahr motivierter anzugehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In order to address the conflict, we should speak openly with each other.", "tl": "Um den Konflikt anzugehen, sollten wir offen miteinander sprechen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "How do you plan to tackle this difficult task?", "tl": "Wie planst du, diese schwierige Aufgabe anzugehen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It requires a lot of courage to actively tackle one's fears.", "tl": "Es erfordert viel Mut, seine Ängste aktiv anzugehen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3450, "expression_id": 3476, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "angewiesen ist", "english_gloss": "to be dependent on something", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Since my car is broken, I am dependent on the bus this week.", "tl": "Da mein Auto kaputt ist, bin ich diese Woche auf den Bus angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Many students are dependent on their parents' financial support during their studies.", "tl": "Viele Studenten sind im Studium auf die finanzielle Unterstützung ihrer Eltern angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In our profession, one is often dependent on the help of colleagues.", "tl": "In unserem Beruf ist man oft auf die Hilfe von Kollegen angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Nowadays, almost every company is dependent on a fast internet connection.", "tl": "Heutzutage ist fast jedes Unternehmen auf eine schnelle Internetverbindung angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "As a farmer, one is highly dependent on good weather.", "tl": "Als Landwirt ist man stark auf gutes Wetter angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After the accident, he was dependent on a wheelchair for a few weeks.", "tl": "Nach dem Unfall war er für einige Wochen auf einen Rollstuhl angewiesen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3449, "expression_id": 3475, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "soit au rendez-vous", "english_gloss": "to turn up / meet expectations", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I hope the sun will show up for our weekend at the beach.", "tl": "J'espère que le soleil sera au rendez-vous pour notre week-end à la plage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The movie's script is excellent, but the actors need to deliver.", "tl": "Le scénario du film est excellent, mais il faut que les acteurs soient au rendez-vous."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We worked hard on this project, and fortunately, success was there.", "tl": "Nous avons beaucoup travaillé pour ce projet, et heureusement, le succès a été au rendez-vous."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The festival organizers hope that the public will turn up tonight.", "tl": "Les organisateurs du festival espèrent que le public sera au rendez-vous ce soir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For such an expensive restaurant, you expect the quality to meet expectations.", "tl": "Pour un restaurant si cher, on s'attend à ce que la qualité soit au rendez-vous."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Despite the rain, good spirits were present during the family party.", "tl": "Malgré la pluie, la bonne humeur était au rendez-vous lors de la fête de famille."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3448, "expression_id": 3474, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "renaît de ses cendres", "english_gloss": "to rise from the ashes", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After a serious financial crisis, this family business is rising from its ashes.", "tl": "Après une grave crise financière, cette entreprise familiale renaît de ses cendres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After several defeats in a row, the football team is rising from its ashes.", "tl": "Après plusieurs défaites d'affilée, l'équipe de football renaît de ses cendres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Destroyed by the war, the old town is slowly rising from its ashes thanks to the inhabitants.", "tl": "Détruite par la guerre, la vieille ville renaît lentement de ses cendres grâce aux habitants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't worry, after this difficult breakup, you will rise from your ashes.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, après cette rupture difficile, tu renaîtras de tes cendres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This old artistic project that everyone had forgotten is finally rising from its ashes.", "tl": "Ce vieux projet artistique que tout le monde avait oublié renaît enfin de ses cendres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This magnificent castle, ravaged by a fire, is rising from its ashes after years of work.", "tl": "Ce magnifique château, ravagé par un incendie, renaît de ses cendres après des années de travaux."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3446, "expression_id": 3472, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tourne au ralenti", "english_gloss": "to run at a slow pace", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My computer is very old and it has been running slowly since this morning.", "tl": "Mon ordinateur est très vieux et il tourne au ralenti depuis ce matin."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "During the month of August, the whole company runs at a slow pace.", "tl": "Pendant le mois d'août, toute l'entreprise tourne au ralenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I didn't get enough sleep last night, so my brain is running in slow motion today.", "tl": "Je n'ai pas assez dormi cette nuit, alors mon cerveau tourne au ralenti aujourd'hui."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Because of the strike, public transport is running at a crawl throughout the city.", "tl": "À cause de la grève, les transports en commun tournent au ralenti dans toute la ville."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In winter, economic activity in this seaside resort slows to a crawl.", "tl": "En hiver, l'activité économique de cette station balnéaire tourne au ralenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Since he has been sick, his body is running slow and he needs a lot of rest.", "tl": "Depuis qu'il est malade, son corps tourne au ralenti et il a besoin de beaucoup de repos."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3445, "expression_id": 3471, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tant bien que mal", "english_gloss": "somehow or other / with difficulty", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Despite the breakdown, he managed to fix his car somehow or other to get back home.", "tl": "Malgré la panne, il a réussi à réparer sa voiture tant bien que mal pour rentrer chez lui."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Since she didn't speak Spanish, she made herself understood as best she could using gestures.", "tl": "Comme elle ne parlait pas espagnol, elle s'est fait comprendre tant bien que mal avec des gestes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With an injured ankle, the hiker continued to walk with difficulty to the mountain shelter.", "tl": "Blessé à la cheville, le randonneur a continué à marcher tant bien que mal jusqu'au refuge."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We slept as best we could on the train despite the noise and the lack of space.", "tl": "Nous avons dormi tant bien que mal dans le train malgré le bruit et le manque de place."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The team finished the project somehow or other before the deadline.", "tl": "L'équipe a terminé le projet tant bien que mal avant la date limite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The tents withstood last night's storm as best they could.", "tl": "Les tentes ont résisté tant bien que mal à la tempête de cette nuit."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3444, "expression_id": 3470, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "retrouve des couleurs", "english_gloss": "to show signs of recovery", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After a few days of rest, your face is getting its color back.", "tl": "Après quelques jours de repos, ton visage retrouve des couleurs."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Local tourism has finally shown signs of recovery this summer.", "tl": "Le tourisme local a enfin retrouvé des couleurs cet été."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our team's players are showing signs of recovery after their last victory.", "tl": "Les joueurs de notre équipe retrouvent des couleurs après leur dernière victoire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Thanks to last night's rain, the garden is looking healthy again.", "tl": "Grâce à la pluie d'hier soir, le jardin retrouve des couleurs."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company is slowly starting to get back on its feet after the crisis.", "tl": "L'entreprise commence lentement à retrouver des couleurs après la crise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I'm glad to see that you've got your color back since last week.", "tl": "Je suis content de voir que tu as retrouvé des couleurs depuis la semaine dernière."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3443, "expression_id": 3469, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "d'autant plus... que", "english_gloss": "all the more... because", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Her success is all the more impressive because she learned everything on her own.", "tl": "Son succès est d'autant plus impressionnant qu'elle a tout appris par elle-même."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The hike will be all the more difficult because it rained all night.", "tl": "La randonnée sera d'autant plus difficile qu'il a plu toute la nuit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This news is all the more surprising because no one was expecting it.", "tl": "Cette nouvelle est d'autant plus surprenante que personne ne s'y attendait."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is all the more easy to learn Italian because you already speak Spanish.", "tl": "Il est d'autant plus facile d'apprendre l'italien que tu parles déjà espagnol."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "His anger was all the more justified because they had lied to him from the start.", "tl": "Sa colère était d'autant plus juste qu'on lui avait menti depuis le début."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This offer is all the more interesting because shipping is free.", "tl": "Cette offre est d'autant plus intéressante que les frais de port sont gratuits."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3441, "expression_id": 3467, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "bleibt abzuwarten", "english_gloss": "remains to be seen", "youtube_id": "qZOA4bwJ0As", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Whether the weather will be good at the weekend remains to be seen.", "tl": "Ob das Wetter am Wochenende gut wird, bleibt abzuwarten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It remains to be seen how the government reacts to the protests.", "tl": "Es bleibt abzuwarten, wie die Regierung auf die Proteste reagiert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I have a good feeling after the job interview, but the result remains to be seen.", "tl": "Ich habe ein gutes Gefühl nach dem Vorstellungsgespräch, aber das Ergebnis bleibt abzuwarten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It remains to be seen whether the new smartphone will be a success.", "tl": "Es bleibt abzuwarten, ob das neue Smartphone ein Erfolg wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It remains to be seen whether the new therapy helps the patient.", "tl": "Es bleibt abzuwarten, ob die neue Therapie dem Patienten hilft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our team has trained hard, but it remains to be seen whether we can win the game.", "tl": "Unsere Mannschaft hat hart trainiert, aber es bleibt abzuwarten, ob wir das Spiel gewinnen können."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3440, "expression_id": 3466, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "vollkommen naheliegend", "english_gloss": "completely obvious", "youtube_id": "qZOA4bwJ0As", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After the success of the first project, the decision to continue was completely obvious.", "tl": "Nach dem Erfolg des ersten Projekts war die Entscheidung für eine Fortsetzung vollkommen naheliegend."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For me, this solution was completely obvious, but my colleague had a completely different idea.", "tl": "Für mich war diese Lösung vollkommen naheliegend, aber mein Kollege hatte eine ganz andere Idee."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With this rain, it is completely obvious that we have to cancel the picnic.", "tl": "Bei diesem Regen ist es vollkommen naheliegend, dass wir das Picknick absagen müssen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His explanation sounded completely obvious to everyone in the room.", "tl": "Seine Erklärung klang für alle im Raum vollkommen naheliegend."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since she loves animals, her career choice as a veterinarian was completely obvious.", "tl": "Da sie Tiere liebt, war ihre Berufswahl als Tierärztin vollkommen naheliegend."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The app is designed so simply that how to use it is completely obvious.", "tl": "Die App ist so einfach gestaltet, dass die Bedienung vollkommen naheliegend ist."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3439, "expression_id": 3465, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "lässt den Schluss zu", "english_gloss": "allows for the conclusion", "youtube_id": "qZOA4bwJ0As", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The dark sky allows for the conclusion that it will rain soon.", "tl": "Der dunkle Himmel lässt den Schluss zu, dass es bald regnen wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The rising sales allow for the conclusion that our new strategy is working.", "tl": "Der steigende Umsatz lässt den Schluss zu, dass unsere neue Strategie funktioniert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "His reaction allows for the conclusion that he was surprised by the news.", "tl": "Seine Reaktion lässt den Schluss zu, dass er von der Nachricht überrascht war."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The study allows for the conclusion that regular exercise is healthy.", "tl": "Die Studie lässt den Schluss zu, dass regelmäßiger Sport gesund ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The tracks at the crime scene allow for the conclusion that the burglar had help.", "tl": "Die Spuren am Tatort lassen den Schluss zu, dass der Einbrecher Hilfe hatte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The simple design allows for the conclusion that the app was developed for older people.", "tl": "Das einfache Design lässt den Schluss zu, dass die App für ältere Menschen entwickelt wurde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3438, "expression_id": 3464, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "schutzlos ausgeliefert", "english_gloss": "completely defenseless against", "youtube_id": "qZOA4bwJ0As", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Without an umbrella, we were completely defenseless against the strong storm.", "tl": "Ohne Regenschirm waren wir dem starken Sturm schutzlos ausgeliefert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Without a good antivirus program, the computer is completely defenseless against hackers.", "tl": "Ohne ein gutes Antivirenprogramm ist der Computer den Hackern schutzlos ausgeliefert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we don't eat healthily, our immune system is completely defenseless against viruses.", "tl": "Wenn wir uns nicht gesund ernähren, ist unser Immunsystem den Viren schutzlos ausgeliefert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Small shops are often completely defenseless against competition from large online retailers.", "tl": "Kleine Geschäfte sind der Konkurrenz durch große Online-Händler oft schutzlos ausgeliefert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In that moment, she felt completely defenseless against her own fears.", "tl": "In diesem Moment fühlte sie sich ihren eigenen Ängsten schutzlos ausgeliefert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Since no more trains were running, the travelers were completely defenseless against the cold at the station.", "tl": "Da kein Zug mehr fuhr, waren die Reisenden der Kälte am Bahnhof schutzlos ausgeliefert."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3437, "expression_id": 3463, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "gerade so am Limit", "english_gloss": "just barely at the limit", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I have so much work this week, I am just barely at my limit.", "tl": "Ich habe diese Woche so viel Arbeit, ich bin gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "With the rising prices, our monthly budget is just barely at the limit.", "tl": "Mit den steigenden Preisen ist unser monatliches Budget gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the long workout, I was physically just barely at my limit.", "tl": "Nach dem langen Training war ich körperlich gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The storage space on my phone is just barely at the limit, I have to delete videos.", "tl": "Der Speicherplatz auf meinem Handy ist gerade so am Limit, ich muss Videos löschen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Before the difficult exam, I was mentally just barely at my limit.", "tl": "Vor der schweren Prüfung war ich mental gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Yesterday evening, the small bar was just barely at its limit with eighty guests.", "tl": "Die kleine Bar war gestern Abend mit achtzig Gästen gerade so am Limit."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3432, "expression_id": 3458, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "er sich dafür einsetzen will", "english_gloss": "he wants to advocate/campaign for it", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The mayor said that he wants to advocate for making the city's parks cleaner.", "tl": "Der Bürgermeister hat gesagt, dass er sich dafür einsetzen will, die Parks in der Stadt sauberer zu machen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My colleague thinks the new project is great and he wants to campaign for us to get more budget.", "tl": "Mein Kollege findet das neue Projekt super und er will sich dafür einsetzen, dass wir mehr Budget bekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If he wants to advocate for improving environmental protection, he also has to use less plastic himself.", "tl": "Wenn er sich dafür einsetzen will, den Umweltschutz zu verbessern, muss er auch selbst weniger Plastik benutzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The boss promised: He wants to advocate for all employees having more flexible working hours.", "tl": "Der Chef hat versprochen: Er will sich dafür einsetzen, dass alle Mitarbeiter flexiblere Arbeitszeiten haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I think it's good that he wants to campaign to improve the situation of the homeless in our city.", "tl": "Ich finde es gut, dass er sich dafür einsetzen will, die Situation der Obdachlosen in unserer Stadt zu verbessern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He explained to the citizens why he wants to advocate for quickly expanding the bike path in the neighborhood.", "tl": "Er hat den Bürgern erklärt, warum er sich dafür einsetzen will, den Radweg im Viertel schnell auszubauen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3430, "expression_id": 3456, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Lebensader für die Industrie", "english_gloss": "lifeline for the industry", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The Rhine has been an important lifeline for the industry in this region for centuries.", "tl": "Der Rhein ist seit Jahrhunderten eine wichtige Lebensader für die Industrie in dieser Region."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Without a stable power supply, this lifeline for the industry will collapse.", "tl": "Ohne eine stabile Stromversorgung bricht diese Lebensader für die Industrie zusammen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The railway network is considered the green lifeline for the domestic industry.", "tl": "Das Schienennetz gilt als die grüne Lebensader für die heimische Industrie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The Port of Hamburg is not only important for the city, but a lifeline for the entire industry of the country.", "tl": "Der Hamburger Hafen ist nicht nur für die Stadt wichtig, sondern eine Lebensader für die gesamte Industrie des Landes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Nowadays, fast internet has become an indispensable lifeline for modern industry.", "tl": "Heutzutage ist schnelles Internet zu einer unverzichtbaren Lebensader für die moderne Industrie geworden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If the supply chains are interrupted, this lifeline for the industry is in danger.", "tl": "Wenn die Lieferketten unterbrochen werden, ist diese Lebensader für die Industrie in Gefahr."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3424, "expression_id": 3450, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Lebensader", "english_gloss": "lifeline / vital artery", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For centuries, the Rhine has been the most important lifeline for the economy in this region.", "tl": "Der Rhein ist seit Jahrhunderten die wichtigste Lebensader für die Wirtschaft in dieser Region."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Subway line 1 is considered the lifeline of the city, as it connects the north with the south.", "tl": "Die U-Bahn-Linie 1 gilt als die Lebensader der Stadt, da sie den Norden mit dem Süden verbindet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "For the small village in the mountains, tourism is the only lifeline.", "tl": "Für das kleine Dorf in den Bergen ist der Tourismus die einzige Lebensader."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Without a stable internet connection, many modern businesses are cut off from their lifeline.", "tl": "Ohne eine stabile Internetverbindung sind viele moderne Unternehmen von ihrer Lebensader abgeschnitten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The water pipeline is the lifeline for the farms in this dry area.", "tl": "Die Wasserleitung ist die Lebensader für die Farmen in dieser trockenen Gegend."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This shopping street used to be the lifeline of the neighborhood, but today many shops are empty.", "tl": "Diese Einkaufsstraße war früher die Lebensader des Viertels, aber heute stehen viele Geschäfte leer."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3423, "expression_id": 3449, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf die Schiene bringen", "english_gloss": "to put on track / shift to rail", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We need to get this project on track as quickly as possible.", "tl": "Wir müssen dieses Projekt so schnell wie möglich auf die Schiene bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The government has decided on new measures to shift more freight to rail.", "tl": "Die Regierung hat neue Maßnahmen beschlossen, um mehr Güter auf die Schiene zu bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After months of planning, we have finally got the new app on track.", "tl": "Nach monatelanger Planung haben wir die neue App endlich auf die Schiene gebracht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It won't be easy to get these political reforms on track.", "tl": "Es wird nicht einfach sein, diese politischen Reformen auf die Schiene zu bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If we want to protect the climate, we must shift more traffic to rail.", "tl": "Wenn wir das Klima schützen wollen, müssen wir mehr Verkehr auf die Schiene bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Thanks to the good cooperation, we were able to quickly get the project on track.", "tl": "Dank der guten Zusammenarbeit konnten wir das Vorhaben schnell auf die Schiene bringen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3422, "expression_id": 3448, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "das Problem kurzfristig anzugehen", "english_gloss": "to tackle/address a problem", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is important to tackle the problem in the short term to avoid further costs.", "tl": "Es ist wichtig, das Problem kurzfristig anzugehen, um weitere Kosten zu vermeiden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We have to address the problem in the short term, otherwise we will lose our customers.", "tl": "Wir müssen das Problem kurzfristig angehen, sonst verlieren wir unsere Kunden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company tackled the problem in the short term and found a quick solution.", "tl": "Die Firma hat das Problem kurzfristig angegangen und eine schnelle Lösung gefunden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our team is currently trying to tackle the problem in the short term.", "tl": "Unser Team versucht derzeit, das Problem kurzfristig anzugehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Because we addressed the problem in the short term, there were no complaints in the end.", "tl": "Weil wir das Problem kurzfristig angegangen sind, gab es am Ende keine Beschwerden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Let's tackle the problem in the short term before it gets even worse.", "tl": "Lassen Sie uns das Problem kurzfristig angehen, bevor es noch schlimmer wird."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3420, "expression_id": 3446, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "hängen echt am Fliegenfänger", "english_gloss": "to be left high and dry / helpless", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Without the new data, we can't continue working and are really left high and dry.", "tl": "Ohne die neuen Daten können wir nicht weiterarbeiten und hängen echt am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The last bus is gone, and now we are really left high and dry here in the middle of the night.", "tl": "Der letzte Bus ist weg, und jetzt hängen wir hier mitten in der Nacht echt am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If the bank doesn't approve the loan, the small company will really be left high and dry.", "tl": "Wenn die Bank den Kredit nicht bewilligt, hängt die kleine Firma echt am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My partner just abandoned the project, and now I'm really left high and dry.", "tl": "Mein Partner hat das Projekt einfach abgebrochen, und ich hänge jetzt echt am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since the system crashed and no technician is available, we are really left high and dry.", "tl": "Da das System abgestürzt ist und kein Techniker erreichbar ist, hängen wir echt am Fliegenfänger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The caterer canceled at short notice; without your help, we'll be really left high and dry at the party.", "tl": "Der Caterer hat kurzfristig abgesagt; ohne deine Hilfe hängen wir bei der Party echt am Fliegenfänger."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3418, "expression_id": 3444, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf die Schnelle", "english_gloss": "quickly / at short notice", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I can whip up a soup for us quickly if you're hungry.", "tl": "Ich kann uns auf die Schnelle eine Suppe kochen, wenn du Hunger hast."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Can we discuss this quickly this afternoon?", "tl": "Können wir das heute Nachmittag auf die Schnelle besprechen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I couldn't find the answer quickly on the internet.", "tl": "Ich habe die Antwort auf die Schnelle nicht im Internet gefunden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He packed his suitcases in a hurry this morning.", "tl": "Er hat heute Morgen auf die Schnelle seine Koffer gepackt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I'm sorry, I just wanted to drop by quickly and say hello.", "tl": "Tut mir leid, ich wollte nur auf die Schnelle vorbeikommen und Hallo sagen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Can you fix the bike quickly, or will it take longer?", "tl": "Kannst du das Fahrrad auf die Schnelle reparieren oder dauert das länger?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3417, "expression_id": 3443, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Vorräte vor der Tür liegen", "english_gloss": "to be just outside / on one's doorstep", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The delivery service was here, so the new supplies are now lying directly on the doorstep.", "tl": "Der Lieferdienst war da, sodass die neuen Vorräte jetzt direkt vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Before the big snowstorm, we wanted to make sure that enough supplies were lying on our doorstep.", "tl": "Vor dem großen Schneesturm wollten wir sicherstellen, dass genügend Vorräte vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When we reach the mountain cabin, the ordered supplies will hopefully already be lying on the doorstep.", "tl": "Wenn wir die Berghütte erreichen, werden die bestellten Vorräte hoffentlich schon vor der Tür liegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When I was sick, my neighbor made sure that fresh supplies were lying on my doorstep every morning.", "tl": "Als ich krank war, hat meine Nachbarin dafür gesorgt, dass jeden Morgen frische Vorräte vor meiner Tür lagen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We have no more space in the basement, which is why some supplies have to lie outside the door.", "tl": "Wir haben im Keller keinen Platz mehr, weshalb einige Vorräte vor der Tür liegen müssen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I was quite surprised this morning when suddenly useful supplies were lying on my doorstep.", "tl": "Ich habe heute Morgen nicht schlecht gestaunt, als plötzlich nützliche Vorräte vor der Tür lagen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3416, "expression_id": 3442, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "darauf hinwirken", "english_gloss": "to work towards that goal", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We must all work towards ensuring that the project is finished on time.", "tl": "Wir müssen alle darauf hinwirken, dass das Projekt rechtzeitig fertig wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The government wants to work towards reducing plastic waste in cities.", "tl": "Die Regierung möchte darauf hinwirken, den Plastikmüll in den Städten zu reduzieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The teachers are working towards getting the students to learn more independently.", "tl": "Die Lehrer wirken darauf hin, dass die Schüler selbstständiger lernen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I have worked for years towards finding a healthy work-life balance.", "tl": "Ich habe jahrelang darauf hingewirkt, eine gesunde Work-Life-Balance zu finden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We should work together to ensure that there are fewer misunderstandings in the team.", "tl": "Wir sollten gemeinsam darauf hinwirken, dass es im Team weniger Missverständnisse gibt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our customer service always works towards solving customers' problems quickly.", "tl": "Unser Kundenservice wirkt stets darauf hin, die Probleme der Kunden schnell zu lösen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3415, "expression_id": 3441, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Auf lange Sicht", "english_gloss": "In the long run", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the long run, you save a lot of money if you buy an energy-efficient car.", "tl": "Auf lange Sicht spart man viel Geld, wenn man ein energieeffizientes Auto kauft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "A healthy diet is better for the body in the long run than any diet.", "tl": "Eine gesunde Ernährung ist auf lange Sicht besser für den Körper als jede Diät."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It is worth it in the long run to learn a new language.", "tl": "Es lohnt sich auf lange Sicht, eine neue Sprache zu lernen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This decision could lead to problems for the company in the long run.", "tl": "Diese Entscheidung könnte auf lange Sicht zu Problemen für die Firma führen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Honesty is always the best way in a relationship in the long run.", "tl": "Ehrlichkeit ist in einer Beziehung auf lange Sicht immer der beste Weg."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In the long run, we must significantly reduce our plastic consumption.", "tl": "Auf lange Sicht müssen wir unseren Plastikkonsum deutlich reduzieren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3414, "expression_id": 3440, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen ist", "english_gloss": "to be urgently dependent on the transports", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The small factory has to close if the delivery fails to arrive because it is urgently dependent on the transports.", "tl": "Die kleine Fabrik muss schließen, wenn die Lieferung ausbleibt, weil sie auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The people in the disaster region are urgently dependent on the transports to receive clean water.", "tl": "Die Menschen in der Katastrophenregion sind auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen, um sauberes Wasser zu erhalten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our pharmacy was urgently dependent on the transports last month to get important medicines.", "tl": "Unsere Apotheke war im letzten Monat auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen, um wichtige Medikamente zu bekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The islanders explain that their entire economy is urgently dependent on the transports.", "tl": "Die Inselbewohner erklären, dass ihre gesamte Wirtschaft auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We cannot interrupt the work because our company is urgently dependent on the transports.", "tl": "Wir können die Arbeit nicht unterbrechen, da unsere Firma auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is no secret that the supermarket in the village is urgently dependent on the transports to fill the shelves.", "tl": "Es ist kein Geheimnis, dass der Supermarkt im Dorf auf die Transporte dringend angewiesen ist, um die Regale zu füllen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3413, "expression_id": 3439, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die sind gerade so am Limit", "english_gloss": "they are just at their limit", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We simply have too many projects this month, we are just at our limit.", "tl": "Wir haben diesen Monat einfach zu viele Projekte, wir sind gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The players gave their all in the second half, but they are just at their limit.", "tl": "Die Spieler haben in der zweiten Halbzeit alles gegeben, aber die sind gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Because of high inflation, many families can hardly afford anything anymore – they are just at their limit.", "tl": "Wegen der hohen Inflation können sich viele Familien kaum noch etwas leisten – die sind gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We urgently need to upgrade our servers, they are just at their limit.", "tl": "Wir müssen dringend unsere Server aufrüsten, die sind gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The nurses have been working overtime for weeks, they are just at their limit.", "tl": "Die Krankenschwestern machen seit Wochen Überstunden, die sind gerade so am Limit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I have to work, study, and take care of the household – I am just at my limit.", "tl": "Ich muss arbeiten, studieren und mich um den Haushalt kümmern – ich bin gerade so am Limit."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3412, "expression_id": 3438, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer gefallen sind", "english_gloss": "have fallen victim to a budget cut", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It's a pity that the free swimming lessons for children fell victim to a budget cut.", "tl": "Es ist schade, dass die kostenlosen Schwimmkurse für Kinder einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer gefallen sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Many small museums in our region complain that their Sunday opening hours fell victim to a budget cut.", "tl": "Viele kleine Museen in unserer Region beklagen, dass ihre Sonntagsöffnungszeiten einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer gefall"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new research projects at the university cannot start because the funds fell victim to a budget cut.", "tl": "Die neuen Forschungsprojekte an der Universität können nicht starten, weil die Gelder einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer g"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The bus connection to our village was discontinued because it fell victim to a budget cut.", "tl": "Die Busverbindung in unser Dorf wurde eingestellt, weil sie einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer gefallen ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The planned renovation of the gym has unfortunately fallen victim to a budget cut.", "tl": "Die geplante Renovierung der Turnhalle ist leider einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer gefallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We had to stop the social counseling for seniors because the positions fell victim to a budget cut.", "tl": "Wir mussten die Sozialberatung für Senioren einstellen, da die Stellen einer Haushaltskürzung zum Opfer gefallen sind."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3411, "expression_id": 3437, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ein wenig versandet wäre", "english_gloss": "petered out a bit", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I was afraid that our joint project had petered out a bit over the holidays.", "tl": "Ich hatte Angst, dass unser gemeinsames Projekt über die Feiertage ein wenig versandet wäre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It looked as if the discussion in the forum had petered out a bit after a few days.", "tl": "Es sah so aus, als ob die Diskussion im Forum nach ein paar Tagen ein wenig versandet wäre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He feared that contact with his old school friends had petered out a bit.", "tl": "Er befürchtete, dass der Kontakt zu seinen alten Schulfreunden ein wenig versandet wäre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The police admitted that the investigation would have petered out a bit without new clues.", "tl": "Die Polizei gab zu, dass die Ermittlung ohne neue Hinweise ein wenig versandet wäre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Nobody wanted to risk the new environmental campaign having petered out a bit after just one week.", "tl": "Niemand wollte riskieren, dass die neue Umweltkampagne schon nach einer Woche ein wenig versandet wäre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I already thought that my application at this big company had petered out a bit, but today the answer arrived.", "tl": "Ich dachte schon, dass meine Bewerbung bei dieser großen Firma ein wenig versandet wäre, aber heute kam die Antwort."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3410, "expression_id": 3436, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch", "english_gloss": "were still on the table", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Which documents were still on the table when the meeting was over?", "tl": "Welche Dokumente lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch, als das Meeting vorbei war?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "How many magazines were still on the table in the waiting room?", "tl": "Wie viele Zeitschriften lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch im Wartezimmer?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Which gifts were still on the table after all the guests had left?", "tl": "Welche Geschenke lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch, nachdem alle Gäste gegangen waren?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "What kind of books were still on the table when you left the library?", "tl": "Was für Bücher lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch, als du die Bibliothek verlassen hast?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Which keys were still on the table before you locked the door?", "tl": "Welche Schlüssel lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch, bevor du die Tür abgeschlossen hast?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "How many brochures were still on the table after the trade fair was over?", "tl": "Wie viele Prospekte lagen denn noch auf dem Tisch, nachdem die Messe zu Ende war?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3409, "expression_id": 3435, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "darauf abgezielt", "english_gloss": "aimed at that", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new advertising campaign aimed to appeal to younger customers.", "tl": "Die neue Werbekampagne hat darauf abgezielt, jüngere Kunden anzusprechen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "His rude remark was aimed at provoking me in front of my colleagues.", "tl": "Seine unhöfliche Bemerkung hat darauf abgezielt, mich vor den Kollegen zu provozieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new rules aimed to calm the traffic in the city center.", "tl": "Die neuen Regeln haben darauf abgezielt, den Verkehr in der Innenstadt zu beruhigen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The workshop was aimed at improving teamwork in our department.", "tl": "Der Workshop hat darauf abgezielt, die Teamarbeit in unserer Abteilung zu verbessern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't think his criticism was aimed at attacking you personally.", "tl": "Ich glaube nicht, dass seine Kritik darauf abgezielt hat, dich persönlich anzugreifen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The update aimed to significantly shorten the app's loading times.", "tl": "Das Update hat darauf abgezielt, die Ladezeiten der App deutlich zu verkürzen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3408, "expression_id": 3434, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ist nicht nur Lebensader", "english_gloss": "is not only a lifeline", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The Rhine is not only a lifeline for the economy, but also a popular excursion destination.", "tl": "Der Rhein ist nicht nur eine Lebensader für die Wirtschaft, sondern auch ein beliebtes Ausflugsziel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The subway is not only the city's lifeline, but also connects millions of people every day.", "tl": "Die U-Bahn ist nicht nur die Lebensader der Stadt, sondern verbindet auch täglich Millionen von Menschen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Tourism is not only a lifeline for the region, it also creates many jobs.", "tl": "Der Tourismus ist nicht nur eine Lebensader für die Region, er schafft auch viele Arbeitsplätze."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Today, the internet is not only a lifeline for businesses, but for our entire society.", "tl": "Das Internet ist heute nicht nur eine Lebensader für Unternehmen, sondern für unsere gesamte Gesellschaft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Forests are not only lifelines for the climate, but also provide a habitat for countless animals.", "tl": "Wälder sind nicht nur Lebensadern für das Klima, sondern bieten auch Lebensraum für unzählige Tiere."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The small shops in the old town are not only a lifeline for the community, but also shape the cityscape.", "tl": "Die kleinen Geschäfte in der Altstadt sind nicht nur eine Lebensader für die Gemeinschaft, sondern prägen auch das Stadt"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3407, "expression_id": 3433, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "mehr Waren auf die Schiene bringen", "english_gloss": "to get more goods onto the rails", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To protect the climate, we urgently need to transfer more goods to rail.", "tl": "Um das Klima zu schützen, müssen wir dringend mehr Waren auf die Schiene bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our logistics company plans to transfer more goods to rail in the coming years.", "tl": "Unser Logistikunternehmen plant, in den nächsten Jahren mehr Waren auf die Schiene zu bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we transfer more goods to rail, there will be fewer traffic jams on the highways.", "tl": "Wenn wir mehr Waren auf die Schiene bringen, gibt es weniger Staus auf den Autobahnen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The government wants to financially support companies that transfer more goods to rail.", "tl": "Die Regierung will Firmen finanziell unterstützen, die mehr Waren auf die Schiene bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Last year, we successfully transferred more goods to rail than ever before.", "tl": "Im letzten Jahr haben wir erfolgreich mehr Waren auf die Schiene gebracht als je zuvor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is not that easy to transfer more goods to rail because the rail network is often overloaded.", "tl": "Es ist nicht so einfach, mehr Waren auf die Schiene zu bringen, weil das Schienennetz oft überlastet ist."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3406, "expression_id": 3432, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "den Betrieb ... einstellen", "english_gloss": "to cease operations / stop running", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to construction work, the subway has to cease operations on the weekend.", "tl": "Wegen der Bauarbeiten muss die U-Bahn am Wochenende den Betrieb einstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After thirty years, the small family business unfortunately had to cease operations.", "tl": "Nach dreißig Jahren musste das kleine Familiengeschäft leider den Betrieb einstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The factory will cease operations at the end of the year because it is no longer profitable.", "tl": "Die Fabrik wird Ende des Jahres den Betrieb einstellen, da sie nicht mehr rentabel ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The online forum officially ceased operations yesterday.", "tl": "Das Online-Forum hat gestern offiziell den Betrieb eingestellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Due to the heavy snowstorm, the airport had to temporarily cease operations.", "tl": "Wegen des starken Schneesturms musste der Flughafen vorübergehend den Betrieb einstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The ferry ceases operations completely in winter.", "tl": "Die Fähre stellt im Winter den Betrieb komplett ein."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3405, "expression_id": 3431, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "dringend angewiesen ist", "english_gloss": "to be urgently dependent on something", "youtube_id": "_i_ViJ9yCAQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Since my car is broken, I am urgently dependent on the train.", "tl": "Da mein Auto kaputt ist, bin ich dringend auf die Bahn angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our team is urgently dependent on your help to finish the project on time.", "tl": "Unser Team ist dringend auf deine Hilfe angewiesen, um das Projekt rechtzeitig fertigzustellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many elderly people are urgently dependent on regular care.", "tl": "Viele ältere Menschen sind dringend auf regelmäßige Pflege angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "As a student, he is urgently dependent on the money from his parents.", "tl": "Als Student ist er dringend auf das Geld von seinen Eltern angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For working from home, one is urgently dependent on a stable internet connection.", "tl": "Für das Homeoffice ist man dringend auf eine stabile Internetverbindung angewiesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The farmers in this region are urgently dependent on rain.", "tl": "Die Bauern in dieser Region sind dringend auf Regen angewiesen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3404, "expression_id": 3430, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "hacer la caja", "english_gloss": "to cash in / make a quick profit", "youtube_id": "fIZLLZMyrj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With yesterday's concert, the organizers managed to cash in for the whole year.", "tl": "Con el concierto de ayer, los organizadores consiguieron hacer la caja de todo el año."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The coastal hotels hope to make a quick profit during this summer season.", "tl": "Los hoteles de la costa esperan hacer la caja durante esta temporada de verano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He sold his shares at just the right time to cash in before the crisis.", "tl": "Vendió sus acciones en el momento justo para hacer la caja antes de la crisis."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Many toy stores make their main profit of the year in the month of December.", "tl": "Muchas tiendas de juguetes hacen la caja de todo el año en el mes de diciembre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The food stall made a huge profit for the month thanks to the music festival.", "tl": "El puesto de comida hizo la caja del mes gracias al festival de música."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They bought the tickets cheap and resold them to make a quick profit.", "tl": "Compraron las entradas baratas y las revendieron para hacer la caja rápidamente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3403, "expression_id": 3429, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "rondando", "english_gloss": "hovering around / being around", "youtube_id": "fIZLLZMyrj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "There has been a black cat hanging around the garden for a few days.", "tl": "Hay un gato negro rondando por el jardín desde hace unos días."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The rent price in this area is hovering around eight hundred euros.", "tl": "El precio del alquiler en esta zona está rondando los ochocientos euros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I have a business idea lingering in my mind, but I need partners.", "tl": "Tengo una idea de negocio rondándome la cabeza, pero necesito socios."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I think I'm going to get sick; there is a very strong virus going around the office.", "tl": "Creo que me voy a enfermar; hay un virus muy fuerte rondando por la oficina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We saw a strange man loitering around the neighbors' house and called the police.", "tl": "Vimos a un hombre extraño rondando la casa de los vecinos y llamamos a la policía."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My uncle is already getting close to sixty years old, but he stays very young.", "tl": "Mi tío ya está rondando los sesenta años, pero se mantiene muy joven."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3402, "expression_id": 3428, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "velara por", "english_gloss": "to watch over / ensure / safeguard", "youtube_id": "fIZLLZMyrj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The grandfather asked that someone watch over the children's safety during the trip.", "tl": "El abuelo pidió que alguien velara por la seguridad de los niños durante el viaje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It was necessary for the government to safeguard the workers' rights.", "tl": "Era necesario que el gobierno velara por los derechos de los trabajadores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She was always looking for a friend who would look after her well-being.", "tl": "Ella siempre buscaba un amigo que velara por su bienestar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The director wanted to hire a lawyer who would protect the company's interests.", "tl": "El director quería contratar a un abogado que velara por los intereses de la empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The town demanded that the law safeguard the conservation of the forests.", "tl": "El pueblo exigió que la ley velara por la conservación de los bosques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My parents wanted a trusted doctor to watch over my health.", "tl": "Mis padres querían que un médico de confianza velara por mi salud."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3401, "expression_id": 3427, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "se barajan", "english_gloss": "are being considered / are on the table", "youtube_id": "fIZLLZMyrj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For the new director position, several highly experienced candidates are being considered.", "tl": "Para el nuevo puesto de director, se barajan varios candidatos con mucha experiencia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We still don't know when the wedding will be, but several dates in September are on the table.", "tl": "Todavía no sabemos cuándo será la boda, pero se barajan varias fechas en septiembre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "To reduce traffic in the city center, different ecological measures are being considered.", "tl": "Para reducir el tráfico en el centro, se barajan distintas medidas ecológicas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The police still don't know what happened, but two main hypotheses are being considered.", "tl": "La policía aún no sabe qué pasó, pero se barajan dos hipótesis principales."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For the end-of-year trip, destinations like Rome, Paris, or London are being considered.", "tl": "Para el viaje de fin de curso se barajan destinos como Roma, París o Londres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Among the names being considered for the new brand, this one is my favorite.", "tl": "Entre los nombres que se barajan para la nueva marca, este es mi favorito."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3400, "expression_id": 3426, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "alentar", "english_gloss": "to encourage / incite / stir up", "youtube_id": "fIZLLZMyrj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My parents always encouraged me to pursue my dreams, no matter how difficult they were.", "tl": "Mis padres siempre me alentaron a seguir mis sueños, sin importar lo difíciles que fueran."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss wants to encourage teamwork to improve the office atmosphere.", "tl": "El jefe quiere alentar el trabajo en equipo para mejorar el ambiente de la oficina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The government has launched a campaign to encourage the use of public transportation.", "tl": "El gobierno ha lanzado una campaña para alentar el uso del transporte público."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Thousands of fans went to the stadium to cheer on their team in the final.", "tl": "Miles de aficionados fueron al estadio para alentar a su equipo en la final."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The teacher encourages us to participate in class, even if we are afraid of making mistakes.", "tl": "La profesora nos alienta a participar en clase, aunque tengamos miedo de cometer errores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We should not encourage that kind of selfish behavior in children.", "tl": "No debemos alentar ese tipo de comportamiento egoísta en los niños."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3399, "expression_id": 3425, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "tras la pista de", "english_gloss": "on the track of / hot on the trail of", "youtube_id": "fIZLLZMyrj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The police are on the trail of the robbery suspect.", "tl": "La policía está tras la pista del sospechoso del robo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The journalist has been on the track of a major political scandal for months.", "tl": "El periodista lleva meses tras la pista de un gran escándalo político."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The archaeologists are on the trail of a lost tomb in the jungle.", "tl": "Los arqueólogos están tras la pista de una tumba perdida en la selva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I've been on the track of that old book for days, but I can't find it anywhere.", "tl": "Llevo días tras la pista de ese libro antiguo, pero no lo encuentro por ninguna parte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The rescue dog ran through the forest on the trail of the lost hiker.", "tl": "El perro de rescate corrió por el bosque tras la pista del excursionista perdido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our company is on the track of the new trends in the technology market.", "tl": "Nuestra empresa está tras la pista de las nuevas tendencias del mercado tecnológico."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3398, "expression_id": 3424, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "en torno a", "english_gloss": "around, regarding, concerning", "youtube_id": "3BxWydYznPQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We will meet in the cafeteria around six in the evening.", "tl": "Nos reuniremos en la cafetería en torno a las seis de la tarde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Today's meeting will revolve around the company's new projects.", "tl": "La reunión de hoy girará en torno a los nuevos proyectos de la empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There is a lot of controversy surrounding the new traffic law.", "tl": "Hay mucha polémica en torno a la nueva ley de tráfico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "All the students sat around the table to listen to the teacher.", "tl": "Todos los estudiantes se sentaron en torno a la mesa para escuchar al profesor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The price of the new phone will be around five hundred euros.", "tl": "El precio del nuevo teléfono estará en torno a los quinientos euros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "His latest detective novel develops around a mysterious unsolved crime.", "tl": "Su última novela policíaca se desarrolla en torno a un misterioso crimen sin resolver."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3397, "expression_id": 3423, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "en favor de", "english_gloss": "in favor of, on behalf of", "youtube_id": "3BxWydYznPQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Most of the neighbors voted in favor of renovating the neighborhood park.", "tl": "La mayoría de los vecinos votó en favor de renovar el parque del barrio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The charity concert raised funds on behalf of homeless children.", "tl": "El concierto benéfico recaudó fondos en favor de los niños sin hogar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There are many arguments in favor of reducing the work week.", "tl": "Hay muchos argumentos en favor de reducir la jornada laboral."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The judge ruled in favor of the plaintiff after seeing the evidence.", "tl": "El juez falló en favor del demandante después de ver las pruebas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You always speak in favor of your brother, even when he is wrong.", "tl": "Siempre hablas en favor de tu hermano, incluso cuando no tiene razón."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The government approved a new law in favor of the environment.", "tl": "El gobierno aprobó una nueva ley en favor del medio ambiente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3396, "expression_id": 3422, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "dejar de lado", "english_gloss": "to set aside, to ignore", "youtube_id": "3BxWydYznPQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We must set aside our differences and work together on this project.", "tl": "Debemos dejar de lado nuestras diferencias y trabajar juntos en este proyecto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He decided to set aside his fears and apply for the job.", "tl": "Él decidió dejar de lado sus miedos y postularse para el puesto de trabajo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Lately you have set aside your friends because of studying so much.", "tl": "Últimamente has dejado de lado a tus amigos por estudiar tanto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If I were you, I would set aside those worries and enjoy the trip.", "tl": "Yo que tú, dejaría de lado esas preocupaciones y disfrutaría del viaje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You cannot solve the problem by setting aside the main issue.", "tl": "No puedes resolver el problema dejando de lado el asunto principal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is important that we do not set aside our values in difficult times.", "tl": "Es importante que no dejemos de lado nuestros valores en momentos difíciles."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3395, "expression_id": 3421, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "poner punto y final", "english_gloss": "to bring to a close / end", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After so many arguments, they decided to put an end to their relationship.", "tl": "Después de tantas discusiones, decidieron poner punto y final a su relación."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We want to bring this project to a close before the summer holidays.", "tl": "Queremos poner punto y final a este proyecto antes de las vacaciones de verano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The famous writer brought his career to a close with one last mystery novel.", "tl": "El famoso escritor puso punto y final a su carrera con una última novela de misterio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I think it's about time you put an end to that matter and moved on.", "tl": "Creo que ya es hora de que pongas punto y final a ese asunto y sigas adelante."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The neighbors have put an end to the conflict with an amicable agreement.", "tl": "Los vecinos han puesto punto y final al conflicto con un acuerdo amistoso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If we don't reach an agreement today, we will have to bring the negotiations to a close.", "tl": "Si no llegamos a un acuerdo hoy, tendremos que poner punto y final a las negociaciones."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3394, "expression_id": 3420, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "estar frente a un espejismo", "english_gloss": "to be facing an illusion / mirage", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I thought I had found the perfect job, but I soon realized I was facing an illusion.", "tl": "Pensé que había encontrado el trabajo perfecto, pero pronto me di cuenta de que estaba frente a un espejismo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't be fooled by his words; you are facing an illusion and you are going to suffer.", "tl": "No te dejes engañar por sus palabras; estás frente a un espejismo y vas a sufrir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Although the company's profits seem high this month, we might be facing an illusion.", "tl": "Aunque las ganancias de la empresa parecen altas este mes, podríamos estar frente a un espejismo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The citizens believed the crisis was over, but in reality they were facing an illusion.", "tl": "Los ciudadanos creyeron que la crisis había terminado, pero en realidad estaban frente a un espejismo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Sometimes we believe everything is going well in life, when in reality we are facing an illusion.", "tl": "A veces creemos que todo va bien en la vida, cuando en realidad estamos frente a un espejismo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After walking for hours through the desert, the explorers feared they were facing a mirage.", "tl": "Después de caminar durante horas por el desierto, los exploradores temían estar frente a un espejismo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3393, "expression_id": 3419, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "lanzarse a", "english_gloss": "to rush to do something / throw oneself into", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After thinking about it a lot, he decided to take the plunge and open his own coffee shop.", "tl": "Después de pensarlo mucho, decidió lanzarse a abrir su propia cafetería."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You shouldn't rush into buying that car without checking the engine first.", "tl": "No deberías lanzarte a comprar ese coche sin antes revisar el motor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She threw herself into learning programming and now works at a big company.", "tl": "Ella se lanzó a aprender programación y ahora trabaja en una gran empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We jumped into organizing the music festival even though we didn't have much experience.", "tl": "Nos lanzamos a organizar el festival de música aunque no teníamos mucha experiencia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Before rushing into speaking in public, take a deep breath and organize your thoughts.", "tl": "Antes de lanzarte a hablar en público, respira hondo y organiza tus ideas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They took the plunge and went to live abroad without knowing the language very well.", "tl": "Ellos se lanzaron a vivir en el extranjero sin saber muy bien el idioma."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3392, "expression_id": 3418, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "de gran envergadura", "english_gloss": "of great magnitude / large-scale", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government has announced a large-scale construction project to improve the highways.", "tl": "El gobierno ha anunciado un proyecto de construcción de gran envergadura para mejorar las carreteras."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The merger of these two companies is an event of great magnitude for the country's economy.", "tl": "La fusión de estas dos empresas es un evento de gran envergadura para la economía del país."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Scientists warn that climate change could cause large-scale natural disasters.", "tl": "Los científicos advierten que el cambio climático podría causar desastres naturales de gran envergadura."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Organizing a large-scale music festival requires months of preparation and a lot of money.", "tl": "Organizar un festival de música de gran envergadura requiere meses de preparación y mucho dinero."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new president proposed a major educational reform that will affect all schools.", "tl": "El nuevo presidente propuso una reforma educativa de gran envergadura que afectará a todas las escuelas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Although he had never led a large-scale project, he accepted the challenge with great enthusiasm.", "tl": "Aunque nunca había liderado un trabajo de gran envergadura, aceptó el reto con mucho entusiasmo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3391, "expression_id": 3417, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "No es la primera vez que", "english_gloss": "it is not the first time that", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is not the first time that you arrive late to the meeting.", "tl": "No es la primera vez que llegas tarde a la reunión."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is not the first time that we lose the car keys.", "tl": "No es la primera vez que perdemos las llaves del coche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It is not the first time that this computer shuts down suddenly.", "tl": "No es la primera vez que este ordenador se apaga de repente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is not the first time that I travel to Madrid for work.", "tl": "No es la primera vez que viajo a Madrid por trabajo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is not the first time that they argue over a misunderstanding.", "tl": "No es la primera vez que ellos discuten por un malentendido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is not the first time that my brother burns dinner.", "tl": "No es la primera vez que a mi hermano se le quema la cena."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3390, "expression_id": 3416, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "y es que", "english_gloss": "and the thing is", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I haven't been able to finish the report, and the thing is, the computer broke down twice today.", "tl": "No he podido terminar el informe, y es que el ordenador se ha roto dos veces hoy."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I find it very hard to understand native speakers, and the thing is, they speak too fast for my level.", "tl": "Me cuesta mucho entender a los nativos, y es que hablan demasiado rápido para mi nivel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I think I'm not going out for dinner tonight, and the thing is, I've spent a lot of money this week.", "tl": "Creo que no voy a salir a cenar esta noche, y es que he gastado mucho dinero esta semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We couldn't go to the beach on Saturday, and the thing is, it rained all day without stopping.", "tl": "No pudimos ir a la playa el sábado, y es que llovió durante todo el día sin parar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He decided not to buy that car, and the thing is, the price of the insurance was too expensive for him.", "tl": "Decidió no comprar ese coche, y es que el precio del seguro era demasiado caro para él."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I prefer to cook at home, and the thing is, eating at restaurants every day is very unhealthy.", "tl": "Prefiero cocinar en casa, y es que comer en restaurantes todos los días es muy poco saludable."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3389, "expression_id": 3415, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "estar frente a", "english_gloss": "to be facing", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We are in front of the museum, right next to the main entrance.", "tl": "Estamos frente al museo, justo al lado de la entrada principal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I feel like I am facing one of the most difficult decisions of my life.", "tl": "Siento que estoy frente a una de las decisiones más difíciles de mi vida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new offices are facing the central park, so they have a beautiful view.", "tl": "Las nuevas oficinas están frente al parque central, así que tienen una vista hermosa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When you are in front of the supermarket, turn left and you will see my house.", "tl": "Cuando estés frente al supermercado, gira a la izquierda y verás mi casa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The director admitted that the company is facing a great financial challenge this year.", "tl": "El director admitió que la empresa está frente a un gran reto financiero este año."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Are you sure we are in front of the correct address? I don't see any sign.", "tl": "¿Estás seguro de que estamos frente a la dirección correcta? No veo ningún cartel."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3388, "expression_id": 3414, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "superando por mucho", "english_gloss": "far exceeding", "youtube_id": "eUxtS46bdaI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This month's sales are far exceeding our expectations.", "tl": "Las ventas de este mes están superando por mucho nuestras expectativas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The young runner won the race, far exceeding his previous record.", "tl": "El joven corredor ganó la carrera, superando por mucho su marca anterior."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new phone model is far exceeding the sales of the previous one.", "tl": "El nuevo modelo de teléfono está superando por mucho en ventas al anterior."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She passed the exam, far exceeding the minimum grade required.", "tl": "Ella aprobó el examen, superando por mucho la nota mínima requerida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This year, the number of tourists is far exceeding last year's figures.", "tl": "Este año, el número de turistas está superando por mucho las cifras del año pasado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The quality of the hotel was excellent, far exceeding what we paid for it.", "tl": "La calidad del hotel era excelente, superando por mucho lo que pagamos por él."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3387, "expression_id": 3413, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "s'échinent à", "english_gloss": "to slave away / strain to", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Parents wear themselves out trying to explain the importance of school to their children.", "tl": "Les parents s'échinent à expliquer l'importance des études à leurs enfants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I struggle and wear myself out trying to please him, but nothing seems to work.", "tl": "Je m'échine à lui faire plaisir, mais rien ne semble marcher."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She is struggling hard to clean this stain, but it won't come out.", "tl": "Elle s'échine à nettoyer cette tache, mais elle ne part pas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They are working themselves to the bone to finish this difficult project before tonight.", "tl": "Ils s'échinent à terminer ce projet difficile avant ce soir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why are you wearing yourself out trying to fix this old radio that won't work anymore?", "tl": "Pourquoi t'échines-tu à réparer cette vieille radio qui ne marchera plus ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We are struggling to find a solution, but the problem is very complex.", "tl": "Nous nous échinons à trouver une solution, mais le problème est très complexe."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3386, "expression_id": 3412, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "jusqu'à nouvel ordre", "english_gloss": "until further notice", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The office will remain closed until further notice due to the renovations.", "tl": "Le bureau restera fermé jusqu'à nouvel ordre en raison des travaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "All trains to Paris are canceled until further notice.", "tl": "Tous les trains vers Paris sont annulés jusqu'à nouvel ordre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You cannot use my car until further notice, understood?", "tl": "Tu ne peux pas utiliser ma voiture jusqu'à nouvel ordre, compris ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Wearing a mask remains mandatory inside the hospital until further notice.", "tl": "Le port du masque reste obligatoire à l'intérieur de l'hôpital jusqu'à nouvel ordre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "PE classes are suspended until further notice.", "tl": "Les cours de sport sont suspendus jusqu'à nouvel ordre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our store is only open in the morning until further notice.", "tl": "Notre magasin est uniquement ouvert le matin jusqu'à nouvel ordre."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3385, "expression_id": 3411, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "devant de la scène", "english_gloss": "the forefront", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This young MP quickly returned to the forefront of the political scene.", "tl": "Ce jeune député est rapidement revenu sur le devant de la scène politique."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "With this new invention, the company finds itself in the spotlight.", "tl": "Avec cette nouvelle invention, l'entreprise se retrouve sur le devant de la scène."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After years of absence, this actress is once again in the spotlight.", "tl": "Après des années d'absence, cette actrice occupe à nouveau le devant de la scène."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The issue of climate change is now at the forefront.", "tl": "La question du changement climatique est aujourd'hui sur le devant de la scène."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He prefers to work behind the scenes rather than being in the spotlight.", "tl": "Il préfère travailler dans l'ombre plutôt que d'être sur le devant de la scène."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Thanks to his victory yesterday, this young athlete has been propelled into the spotlight.", "tl": "Grâce à sa victoire d'hier, ce jeune athlète est propulsé sur le devant de la scène."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3384, "expression_id": 3410, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se ruent", "english_gloss": "to rush / flock eagerly", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As soon as the sales start, customers flock to the stores to find the best deals.", "tl": "Dès l'ouverture des soldes, les clients se ruent dans les magasins pour trouver les meilleures affaires."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Fans rush to buy tickets as soon as they go on sale online.", "tl": "Les fans se ruent sur les billets dès qu'ils sont mis en vente en ligne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When it's hot, city dwellers flock to the beaches to cool off.", "tl": "Quand il fait chaud, les citadins se ruent vers les plages pour se rafraîchir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "All the influencers are flocking to this new restaurant that everyone is talking about.", "tl": "Tous les influenceurs se ruent dans ce nouveau restaurant dont tout le monde parle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Tech enthusiasts rush to buy the latest smartphone model as soon as it is released.", "tl": "Les passionnés de technologie se ruent sur le dernier modèle de smartphone dès sa sortie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "As soon as it starts to rain, people rush to the subway entrances.", "tl": "Dès qu'il commence à pleuvoir, les gens se ruent vers les bouches de métro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3383, "expression_id": 3409, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se retrouvent vacants", "english_gloss": "end up vacant", "youtube_id": "8cWZJ-_ujB8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After the students leave in June, many studio apartments end up vacant.", "tl": "Après le départ des étudiants en juin, beaucoup de studios se retrouvent vacants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Following this restructuring, several key positions end up vacant within the company.", "tl": "Suite à cette restructuration, plusieurs postes clés se retrouvent vacants au sein de l'entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If the reservations are not confirmed, these seats will end up vacant just before the show.", "tl": "Si les réservations ne sont pas confirmées, ces sièges se retrouveront vacants juste avant le spectacle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Since the director resigned, his office has ended up vacant.", "tl": "Depuis que le directeur a démissionné, son bureau se retrouve vacant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the winter, many holiday homes end up vacant.", "tl": "Pendant l'hiver, de nombreuses maisons de vacances se retrouvent vacantes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "With the economic crisis, several commercial premises downtown end up vacant.", "tl": "Avec la crise économique, plusieurs locaux commerciaux du centre-ville se retrouvent vacants."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3382, "expression_id": 3408, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "No entanto", "english_gloss": "however / nevertheless", "youtube_id": "3d5T_sHm4P4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The weather was cold and rainy; however, we decided to go for a walk in the park.", "tl": "O tempo estava frio e chuvoso; no entanto, decidimos ir dar um passeio no parque."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She studied hard for the driving test. However, she didn't manage to pass on the first try.", "tl": "Ela estudou muito para o exame de condução. No entanto, não conseguiu passar à primeira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This cell phone is quite expensive; however, it has an excellent camera that is worth it.", "tl": "Este telemóvel é bastante caro; no entanto, tem uma câmara excelente que vale a pena."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He promised he was going to start a diet; however, he continued to eat sweets every day.", "tl": "Ele prometeu que ia começar a fazer dieta; no entanto, continuou a comer doces todos os dias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The hotel was not five-star; however, the service was fantastic and very welcoming.", "tl": "O hotel não era de cinco estrelas; no entanto, o serviço era fantástico e muito acolhedor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We hadn't spoken to each other in many years; however, the reunion was very natural and fun.", "tl": "Nós não nos falávamos há muitos anos; no entanto, o reencontro foi muito natural e divertido."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3381, "expression_id": 3407, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "por trás", "english_gloss": "behind / underlying", "youtube_id": "3d5T_sHm4P4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I would like to know the truth behind that decision.", "tl": "Eu gostaria de saber a verdade por trás daquela decisão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The cat ran and hid behind the sofa.", "tl": "O gato correu e se escondeu por trás do sofá."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She is the brilliant mind behind this whole project.", "tl": "Ela é a mente brilhante por trás de todo este projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I think there is a hidden motive behind his words.", "tl": "Acho que há uma segunda intenção por trás das palavras dele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The parking lot is right behind the supermarket.", "tl": "O estacionamento fica bem por trás do supermercado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "What is the real reason behind the cancellation of the event?", "tl": "Qual é o verdadeiro motivo por trás do cancelamento do evento?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3380, "expression_id": 3406, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "para dizer o mínimo", "english_gloss": "to say the least", "youtube_id": "3d5T_sHm4P4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The math exam was difficult, to say the least.", "tl": "O exame de matemática foi difícil, para dizer o mínimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The service at that hotel was terrible, to say the least.", "tl": "O serviço daquele hotel era péssimo, para dizer o mínimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "His reaction to the news was surprising, to say the least.", "tl": "A reação dele à notícia foi surpreendente, para dizer o mínimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Organizing this event is going to be a challenge, to say the least.", "tl": "Organizar este evento vai ser um desafio, para dizer o mínimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The traffic in the city today was chaotic, to say the least.", "tl": "O trânsito na cidade hoje estava caótico, para dizer o mínimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Apartment prices in this area are overpriced, to say the least.", "tl": "Os preços dos apartamentos nesta zona são exagerados, para dizer o mínimo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3379, "expression_id": 3405, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "terreno fértil", "english_gloss": "fertile ground / breeding ground", "youtube_id": "3d5T_sHm4P4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That city is a fertile ground for new technology companies.", "tl": "Aquela cidade é um terreno fértil para novas empresas de tecnologia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The lack of clear communication creates a breeding ground for rumors and misunderstandings.", "tl": "A falta de comunicação clara cria um terreno fértil para boatos e mal-entendidos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "School should be a fertile ground for children's imagination.", "tl": "A escola deve ser um terreno fértil para a imaginação das crianças."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They bought a property with fertile ground to grow organic vegetables.", "tl": "Eles compraram uma propriedade com um terreno fértil para cultivar legumes orgânicos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The financial crisis ended up being a breeding ground for the population's discontent.", "tl": "A crise financeira acabou por ser um terreno fértil para o descontentamento da população."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "A collaborative work environment is a fertile ground for the emergence of new ideas.", "tl": "Um ambiente de trabalho colaborativo é um terreno fértil para o surgimento de novas ideias."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3378, "expression_id": 3404, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "Para efeito de comparação", "english_gloss": "for comparison purposes", "youtube_id": "3d5T_sHm4P4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For comparison purposes, last year's model cost almost half the price.", "tl": "Para efeito de comparação, o modelo do ano passado custava quase metade do preço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This city is small; for comparison purposes, it is the same size as my neighborhood.", "tl": "Esta cidade é pequena; para efeito de comparação, ela tem o mesmo tamanho do meu bairro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "For comparison purposes, let's analyze the average salaries of other companies in the sector.", "tl": "Para efeito de comparação, vamos analisar os salários médios de outras empresas do setor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Today is very cold, but for comparison purposes, yesterday was even worse.", "tl": "Hoje está muito frio, mas para efeito de comparação, ontem estava ainda pior."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For comparison purposes, the new electric car consumes much less energy than the old model.", "tl": "Para efeito de comparação, o novo carro elétrico consome muito menos energia do que o modelo antigo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The direct flight takes eight hours, while the road trip, for comparison purposes, would take three days.", "tl": "O voo direto leva oito horas, enquanto a viagem de carro, para efeito de comparação, demoraria três dias."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3377, "expression_id": 3403, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "meia dúzia", "english_gloss": "a handful / a few", "youtube_id": "3d5T_sHm4P4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Only a handful of people showed up at yesterday's meeting.", "tl": "Só apareceu meia dúzia de pessoas na reunião de ontem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I went to the supermarket just to buy a few things that were missing.", "tl": "Fui ao supermercado comprar apenas meia dúzia de coisas que estavam a faltar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I only know how to speak a handful of words in German, but I can make myself understood.", "tl": "Eu só sei falar meia dúzia de palavras em alemão, mas consigo fazer-me entender."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He lived in Paris for a few months before returning to Portugal.", "tl": "Ele viveu em Paris durante meia dúzia de meses antes de voltar para Portugal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Don't worry about others' opinions, it's just a handful of people who don't know you.", "tl": "Não te preocupes com a opinião dos outros, são apenas meia dúzia de pessoas que não te conhecem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I took a few books on vacation, but I didn't have time to read any of them.", "tl": "Levei meia dúzia de livros para as férias, mas não tive tempo de ler nenhum."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3376, "expression_id": 3402, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "lobo de olho no galinheiro", "english_gloss": "wolf watching the chicken coop", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Leaving the former manager to take care of the company's accounts is like putting a wolf to watch the chicken coop.", "tl": "Deixar o ex-gerente cuidar das contas da empresa é como colocar um lobo de olho no galinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He says he only wants to help with the inheritance, but to me, he is a wolf watching the chicken coop.", "tl": "Ele diz que só quer ajudar com a herança, mas para mim ele é um lobo de olho no galinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Putting that politician to inspect the contracts is the same as leaving the wolf to watch the chicken coop.", "tl": "Colocar aquele político para fiscalizar os contratos é o mesmo que deixar o lobo de olho no galinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't tell your business plans to your competitor; he is a wolf watching the chicken coop.", "tl": "Não conte seus planos de negócios para o seu concorrente; ele é um lobo de olho no galinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Giving the key to the stockroom to that dishonest employee is leaving the wolf to watch the chicken coop.", "tl": "Dar a chave do estoque para aquele funcionário desonesto é deixar o lobo de olho no galinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Hiring a hacker to take care of data security seems like a wolf watching the chicken coop.", "tl": "Contratar um hacker para cuidar da segurança dos dados parece um lobo de olho no galinheiro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3370, "expression_id": 3396, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "braço direito", "english_gloss": "right-hand man/woman", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Ana is the director's right-hand woman; she solves all of the company's problems.", "tl": "A Ana é o braço direito do diretor; ela resolve todos os problemas da empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My brother is my right-hand man at the restaurant; I don't know what I would do without him.", "tl": "O meu irmão é o meu braço direito no restaurante; não sei o que faria sem ele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The secretary is the president's right-hand man and organizes her entire schedule.", "tl": "O secretário é o braço direito da presidente e organiza toda a sua agenda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I need to find a right-hand man to help me organize this new project.", "tl": "Preciso de encontrar um braço direito para me ajudar a organizar este novo projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since my assistant left the company, I feel like I've lost my right-hand man.", "tl": "Desde que o meu assistente saiu da empresa, sinto que perdi o meu braço direito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The assistant coach is the head coach's right-hand man.", "tl": "O treinador adjunto é o braço direito do técnico principal."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3367, "expression_id": 3393, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "segundas intenções", "english_gloss": "ulterior motives", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He offered to help me with my bags, but I think he had ulterior motives.", "tl": "Ele ofereceu-se para me ajudar com as malas, mas acho que ele tinha segundas intenções."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When a company offers something for free, there are usually ulterior motives behind it.", "tl": "Quando uma empresa oferece algo de graça, geralmente há segundas intenções por trás."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't trust him very much; it seems like he always acts with ulterior motives.", "tl": "Eu não confio muito nele; parece que ele sempre age com segundas intenções."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She was very nice to me today, which makes me suspect ulterior motives.", "tl": "Ela foi muito simpática comigo hoje, o que me faz suspeitar de segundas intenções."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The politician guaranteed that his proposal was honest and without ulterior motives.", "tl": "O político garantiu que a sua proposta era honesta e sem segundas intenções."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You have to be careful with your boss's compliments, he might have ulterior motives.", "tl": "Tens de ter cuidado com os elogios do teu chefe, ele pode ter segundas intenções."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3366, "expression_id": 3392, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "ci nuotava dentro", "english_gloss": "to swim in it / be immersed in it", "youtube_id": "3AanKASuxT8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My younger brother tried on my heavy jacket, but he was swimming in it.", "tl": "Mio fratello minore ha provato la mia giacca pesante, ma ci nuotava dentro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I bought a huge double bed; now I'm swimming in it!", "tl": "Ho comprato un letto matrimoniale enorme; adesso ci nuoto dentro!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With all the money they inherited, they are swimming in it now.", "tl": "Con tutti i soldi che hanno ereditato, ormai ci nuotano dentro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "That apartment was too big for the two of us, we were swimming in it.", "tl": "Quell'appartamento era troppo grande per noi due, ci nuotavamo dentro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That shirt is two sizes too big, you're swimming in it!", "tl": "Quella camicia è di due taglie più grande, ci nuoti dentro!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't worry about the data analysis, Marco is completely in his element.", "tl": "Non ti preoccupare per l'analisi dei dati, Marco ci nuota dentro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3365, "expression_id": 3391, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "aveva contezza", "english_gloss": "to have knowledge of / be aware of", "youtube_id": "3AanKASuxT8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The director was not aware of the gravity of the situation.", "tl": "Il direttore non aveva contezza della gravità della situazione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Citizens must be aware of their rights before voting.", "tl": "I cittadini devono avere contezza dei propri diritti prima di votare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I was not aware of the fact that the meeting had been canceled.", "tl": "Non avevo contezza del fatto che la riunione fosse stata cancellata."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If I had been aware of the danger, I wouldn't have gone there alone.", "tl": "Se avessi avuto contezza del pericolo, non sarei andato lì da solo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The archaeologists were not yet fully aware of the value of the discovery.", "tl": "Gli archeologi non avevano ancora piena contezza del valore della scoperta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Are you already aware of the estimated costs for this new project?", "tl": "Ha già contezza dei costi previsti per questo nuovo progetto?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3364, "expression_id": 3390, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "bene o male che sia", "english_gloss": "whether it is good or bad", "youtube_id": "3AanKASuxT8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We have to make a decision, whether it is good or bad.", "tl": "Dobbiamo prendere una decisione, bene o male che sia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This news will change things, whether for better or worse.", "tl": "Questa notizia cambierà le cose, bene o male che sia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I want to remember every moment of this trip, whether it is good or bad.", "tl": "Voglio ricordare ogni momento di questo viaggio, bene o male che sia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I will accept the exam result, whether it is good or bad.", "tl": "Accetterò il risultato dell'esame, bene o male che sia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Technology has changed the way we communicate, whether for better or worse.", "tl": "La tecnologia ha cambiato il modo di comunicare, bene o male che sia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We must accept the truth, whether it is good or bad.", "tl": "Dobbiamo accettare la verità, bene o male che sia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3363, "expression_id": 3389, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "hai a che fare", "english_gloss": "to deal with / have to do with", "youtube_id": "3AanKASuxT8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I don't like my job because I always have to deal with angry customers.", "tl": "Non mi piace il mio lavoro perché ho sempre a che fare con clienti arrabbiati."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Be careful, you don't know who you are dealing with.", "tl": "Fai attenzione, non sai con chi hai a che fare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This time we are dealing with a really complicated problem.", "tl": "Questa volta abbiamo a che fare con un problema davvero complicato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "As a doctor, she often has to deal with emergency situations.", "tl": "Come medico, lei ha spesso a che fare con situazioni di emergenza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I have nothing to do with it, they have nothing to do with this story.", "tl": "Io non c'entro nulla, loro non hanno niente a che fare con questa storia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you work at a school, you deal with children of all ages.", "tl": "Se lavorate a scuola, avete a che fare con bambini di tutte le età."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3362, "expression_id": 3388, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "messo in piedi", "english_gloss": "to set up / establish / organize", "youtube_id": "3VSVcVdQ8mo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In a few weeks, the team set up a fantastic project.", "tl": "In poche settimane, il team ha messo in piedi un progetto fantastico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They organized a surprise birthday party in no time.", "tl": "Hanno messo in piedi una festa di compleanno a sorpresa in pochissimo tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My brother set up a small gardening business.", "tl": "Mio fratello ha messo in piedi una piccola impresa di giardinaggio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Last year we set up an association to help stray dogs.", "tl": "L'anno scorso abbiamo messo in piedi un'associazione per aiutare i cani randagi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This music festival was organized thanks to the town's volunteers.", "tl": "Questo festival musicale è stato messo in piedi grazie ai volontari del paese."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The school put on a really moving theater show.", "tl": "La scuola ha messo in piedi uno spettacolo teatrale davvero emozionante."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3361, "expression_id": 3387, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "farsene carico", "english_gloss": "to take responsibility for / bear the cost of", "youtube_id": "3VSVcVdQ8mo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry about the travel expenses, we will bear the cost of them.", "tl": "Non ti preoccupare per le spese del viaggio, ce ne facciamo carico noi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Marco loves his family and took responsibility for them during difficult times.", "tl": "Marco ama la sua famiglia e se ne è fatto carico nei momenti difficili."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This is a serious problem and the director must take responsibility for it as soon as possible.", "tl": "Questo è un problema serio e il direttore deve farsene carico al più presto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If nobody wants to organize the meeting, I will take charge of it.", "tl": "Se nessuno vuole organizzare la riunione, me ne farò carico io."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If we entrusted you with this task, would you gladly take responsibility for it?", "tl": "Se vi affidassimo questo compito, ve ne fareste carico volentieri?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Who will pay for the damages? The event organizers are bearing the cost of them.", "tl": "Chi pagherà per i danni? Se ne fanno carico gli organizzatori dell'evento."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3360, "expression_id": 3386, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "partite molto a rilento", "english_gloss": "to progress very slowly / drag on", "youtube_id": "3VSVcVdQ8mo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sales of the new model got off to a very slow start, but now they are improving.", "tl": "Le vendite del nuovo modello sono partite molto a rilento, ma ora stanno migliorando."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The negotiations between the two companies started very slowly due to some disagreements.", "tl": "Le trattative tra le due aziende sono partite molto a rilento a causa di alcuni disaccordi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This year, university classes got off to a very slow start due to organizational reasons.", "tl": "Quest'anno le lezioni all'università sono partite molto a rilento per motivi organizzativi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Research for the new drug started very slowly, but the first results are promising.", "tl": "Le ricerche per il nuovo farmaco sono partite molto a rilento, ma i primi risultati sono promettenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The shipments of Christmas gifts got off to a very slow start this year.", "tl": "Le spedizioni dei regali di Natale sono partite molto a rilento quest'anno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you got off to a very slow start with work, you will have to work overtime this week.", "tl": "Se siete partite molto a rilento con il lavoro, dovrete fare gli straordinari questa settimana."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3359, "expression_id": 3385, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "Al di là dell'aspetto", "english_gloss": "beyond / apart from / regardless of", "youtube_id": "3VSVcVdQ8mo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Regardless of appearance, Marco is a really intelligent and sensitive person.", "tl": "Al di là dell'aspetto, Marco è una persona davvero intelligente e sensibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Regardless of the financial aspect, I am very passionate about this project.", "tl": "Al di là dell'aspetto economico, questo progetto mi appassiona molto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Beyond the outward appearance, I prefer to buy clothes that are comfortable.", "tl": "Al di là dell'aspetto esteriore, preferisco comprare vestiti che siano comodi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Regardless of the look of the place, the food here is always of excellent quality.", "tl": "Al di là dell'aspetto del locale, il cibo qui è sempre di ottima qualità."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Beyond the technical aspect, we must also consider the human side of the situation.", "tl": "Al di là dell'aspetto tecnico, dobbiamo considerare anche il lato umano della situazione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Regardless of the messy appearance of his room, Luca is a very responsible guy.", "tl": "Al di là dell'aspetto disordinato della sua camera, Luca è un ragazzo molto responsabile."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3358, "expression_id": 3384, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "deixou muito, muito à vontade", "english_gloss": "to make comfortable / to put at ease", "youtube_id": "xX62Z8ol-G4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The interviewer made me feel very, very at ease from the beginning of the conversation.", "tl": "O entrevistador me deixou muito, muito à vontade desde o início da conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When I visited my in-laws, they made me feel very, very welcome in their home.", "tl": "Quando visitei os meus sogros, eles me deixaram muito, muito à vontade na casa deles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I was nervous, but the doctor made me feel very, very comfortable during the exam.", "tl": "Eu estava nervoso, mas o médico me deixou muito, muito à vontade durante o exame."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My new boss made me feel very, very comfortable suggesting new ideas.", "tl": "A minha nova chefe me deixou muito, muito à vontade para sugerir novas ideias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Maria welcomed us very well and made us feel very, very at ease in her apartment.", "tl": "A Maria nos recebeu muito bem e nos deixou muito, muito à vontade no seu apartamento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The Portuguese teacher always makes the students feel very, very comfortable speaking, even when making mistakes.", "tl": "O professor de português sempre deixa os alunos muito, muito à vontade para falar, mesmo cometendo erros."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3357, "expression_id": 3383, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "pente fino", "english_gloss": "fine-tooth comb / thorough check", "youtube_id": "xX62Z8ol-G4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The police went through the apartment with a fine-tooth comb, but found no clues.", "tl": "A polícia passou um pente fino no apartamento, mas não encontrou nenhuma pista."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Before sending the report to the boss, I'm going to go over it with a fine-tooth comb to correct the mistakes.", "tl": "Antes de enviar o relatório para o chefe, vou passar um pente fino para corrigir os erros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The tax authority did a thorough check on the company's accounts this month.", "tl": "A receita federal fez um pente fino nas contas da empresa este mês."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The human resources department went through all the received resumes with a fine-tooth comb.", "tl": "O departamento de recursos humanos passou um pente fino em todos os currículos recebidos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We need to do a thorough check of the suitcases to make sure we didn't forget anything.", "tl": "Nós precisamos fazer um pente fino nas malas para garantir que não esquecemos nada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Event security did a thorough check at the entrance to avoid any problems.", "tl": "A segurança do evento fez um pente fino na entrada para evitar qualquer problema."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3356, "expression_id": 3382, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "criando picuinha", "english_gloss": "to bicker / to create petty squabbles", "youtube_id": "xX62Z8ol-G4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Stop creating petty squabbles with your coworkers over silly things.", "tl": "Pare de criar picuinha com seus colegas de trabalho por causa de coisas bobas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They spent the whole afternoon bickering with each other.", "tl": "Eles passaram a tarde inteira criando picuinha um com o outro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't want to argue today, so please don't start picking petty fights.", "tl": "Eu não quero discutir hoje, então por favor não venha criar picuinha."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Instead of helping with the project, he just keeps creating petty squabbles with the group.", "tl": "Em vez de ajudar no projeto, ele fica só criando picuinha com o grupo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The neighbor is always starting petty arguments about the noise, even when we are quiet.", "tl": "A vizinha está sempre criando picuinha por causa do barulho, mesmo quando estamos em silêncio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We were very young and always bickered over any silly thing.", "tl": "Nós éramos muito jovens e sempre criávamos picuinha por qualquer bobagem."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3355, "expression_id": 3381, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tendo em vista", "english_gloss": "keeping in mind / considering", "youtube_id": "xX62Z8ol-G4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Keeping in mind the limited budget, we have to choose cheaper options.", "tl": "Tendo em vista o orçamento limitado, temos de escolher opções mais baratas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We decided to postpone the trip, considering the bad weather forecast for the weekend.", "tl": "Decidimos adiar a viagem, tendo em vista o mau tempo previsto para o fim de semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Considering that the exam is tomorrow, I think it's better to go to bed early today.", "tl": "Tendo em vista que o exame é amanhã, acho melhor ir para a cama cedo hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Keeping his health in mind, he decided to quit smoking.", "tl": "Tendo em vista a sua saúde, ele decidiu parar de fumar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company hired new employees, keeping in mind the increase in sales at the end of the year.", "tl": "A empresa contratou novos funcionários, tendo em vista o aumento das vendas no final do ano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Keeping your preferences in mind, I chose an Italian restaurant for our dinner.", "tl": "Tendo em vista as suas preferências, escolhi um restaurante italiano para o nosso jantar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3354, "expression_id": 3380, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "teria a intenção de", "english_gloss": "to intend to", "youtube_id": "xX62Z8ol-G4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I wouldn't intend to change jobs if the work environment were better.", "tl": "Eu não teria a intenção de mudar de emprego se o ambiente de trabalho fosse melhor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She explained that she wouldn't intend to offend anyone with that comment.", "tl": "Ela explicou que não teria a intenção de ofender ninguém com aquele comentário."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We would intend to travel next month, but the flights are very expensive.", "tl": "Nós teríamos a intenção de viajar no próximo mês, mas os voos estão muito caros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Would you intend to sell your old car before the end of the year?", "tl": "Você teria a intenção de vender o seu carro antigo antes do fim do ano?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They would intend to start a new course if they had more free time.", "tl": "Eles teriam a intenção de começar um novo curso se tivessem mais tempo livre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I would intend to buy that house, but it needs a lot of renovation work.", "tl": "Eu teria a intenção de comprar aquela casa, mas ela precisa de muitas obras."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3353, "expression_id": 3379, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dar o aval", "english_gloss": "to give the green light / to approve", "youtube_id": "xX62Z8ol-G4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The director has already given the green light to start the new project.", "tl": "O diretor já deu o aval para começarmos o novo projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My parents finally gave their approval for me to go on the trip alone.", "tl": "Os meus pais finalmente deram o aval para eu fazer a viagem sozinho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The doctor needs to give the green light before the athlete returns to training.", "tl": "O médico precisa de dar o aval antes de o atleta voltar a treinar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The city council hasn't given the green light for the construction of the building yet.", "tl": "A câmara municipal ainda não deu o aval para a construção do edifício."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We hope the manager gives the green light today so we can close the deal.", "tl": "Esperamos que o gerente dê o aval ainda hoje para podermos fechar o negócio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We can only move forward with the advertising campaign if the client gives their approval.", "tl": "Só podemos avançar com a campanha de publicidade se o cliente der o aval."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3352, "expression_id": 3378, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de mãos atadas", "english_gloss": "with one's hands tied", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I really wanted to help you with this problem, but without the boss's authorization, my hands are tied.", "tl": "Eu queria muito te ajudar com esse problema, mas, sem a autorização do chefe, estou de mãos atadas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The police know who committed the crime, but without concrete evidence, their hands are tied.", "tl": "A polícia sabe quem cometeu o crime, mas sem provas concretas eles estão de mãos atadas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "As a mother, I feel helpless when I see my son make wrong decisions.", "tl": "Como mãe, eu me sinto de mãos atadas quando vejo meu filho tomar decisões erradas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Because of the financial crisis, the company's hands were tied and they had to cancel the new projects.", "tl": "Por causa da crise financeira, a empresa ficou de mãos atadas e teve que cancelar os novos projetos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The system went down and we were helpless all day, unable to assist the customers.", "tl": "O sistema caiu e nós ficamos de mãos atadas o dia todo, sem poder atender os clientes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We signed the contract, so now our hands are tied and we cannot change the rules.", "tl": "Nós assinamos o contrato, então agora estamos de mãos atadas e não podemos mudar as regras."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3351, "expression_id": 3377, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "fecha a porta", "english_gloss": "shuts the door on / excludes", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Whenever he leaves the office, he closes the door carefully.", "tl": "Sempre que ele sai do escritório, ele fecha a porta com cuidado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you reject that proposal, you close the door to new career opportunities.", "tl": "Se você recusar essa proposta, fecha a porta para novas oportunidades na carreira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The wind was so strong that she ran and closed the balcony door.", "tl": "O vento estava tão forte que ela correu e fechou a porta da varanda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is important that you close the door before turning on the air conditioning.", "tl": "É importante que você feche a porta antes de ligar o ar-condicionado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Unfortunately, that old argument closed the door to a reconciliation between the brothers.", "tl": "Infelizmente, aquela discussão antiga fechou a porta para uma reconciliação entre os irmãos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't close the door to new ideas just because you are afraid to change.", "tl": "Não feche a porta para novas ideias só porque tem medo de mudar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3350, "expression_id": 3376, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "foi por água abaixo", "english_gloss": "went down the drain / failed", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "All of our planning for the holidays went down the drain because of the rain.", "tl": "Todo o nosso planeamento para as férias foi por água abaixo por causa da chuva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The project we worked on for months went down the drain when the client canceled the contract.", "tl": "O projeto em que trabalhámos durante meses foi por água abaixo quando o cliente cancelou o contrato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I invested a lot of money in that company, but now everything has gone down the drain.", "tl": "Investi muito dinheiro naquela empresa, mas agora tudo foi por água abaixo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After that lie, all the trust I had in him went down the drain.", "tl": "Depois daquela mentira, toda a confiança que eu tinha nele foi por água abaixo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I ate a whole cake yesterday and my diet went down the drain.", "tl": "Comi um bolo inteiro ontem e a minha dieta foi por água abaixo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The concert was canceled and our weekend trip went down the drain.", "tl": "O concerto foi cancelado e a nossa viagem de fim de semana foi por água abaixo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3349, "expression_id": 3375, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "sair da defensiva", "english_gloss": "to stop being on the defensive", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you want to solve the problem, you need to stop being defensive and listen to what she has to say.", "tl": "Se você quer resolver o problema, precisa sair da defensiva e ouvir o que ela tem a dizer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After receiving the criticism, the employee finally stopped being defensive and accepted the advice.", "tl": "Depois de receber a crítica, o funcionário finalmente saiu da defensiva e aceitou os conselhos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I realized I was wrong and decided to stop being defensive so we could have a mature conversation.", "tl": "Eu percebi que estava errado e decidi sair da defensiva para termos uma conversa madura."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I'm not attacking you, so please, stop being defensive for a moment.", "tl": "Não estou te atacando, então por favor, saia da defensiva por um momento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company needs to stop being defensive and propose a real solution to the customers.", "tl": "A empresa precisa sair da defensiva e propor uma solução real para os clientes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When both of us stopped being defensive, we finally managed to make peace.", "tl": "Quando nós dois saímos da defensiva, conseguimos finalmente fazer as pazes."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3348, "expression_id": 3374, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "encarar a realidade", "english_gloss": "to face reality", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After losing his job, he had to face reality and look for something new.", "tl": "Depois de perder o emprego, ele teve que encarar a realidade e procurar algo novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We need to face reality: our plan is not working.", "tl": "Nós precisamos encarar a realidade: o nosso plano não está funcionando."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's time for you to face reality and accept that things have changed.", "tl": "É hora de você encarar a realidade e aceitar que as coisas mudaram."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you don't face reality now, the problems will only increase.", "tl": "Se você não encarar a realidade agora, os problemas só vão aumentar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She finally faced reality and decided to end that toxic relationship.", "tl": "Ela finalmente encarou a realidade e decidiu terminar aquele relacionamento tóxico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Avoiding the subject won't help; you need to face reality sooner or later.", "tl": "Evitar o assunto não vai ajudar; vocês precisam encarar a realidade mais cedo ou mais tarde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3347, "expression_id": 3373, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tem razão", "english_gloss": "is right", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I think you are right, we should have left earlier to avoid the traffic.", "tl": "Acho que você tem razão, devíamos ter saído mais cedo para evitar o trânsito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "See? I was right, the museum is closed today.", "tl": "Vês? Eu tinha razão, o museu está fechado hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We are right to be worried about their delay.", "tl": "Nós temos razão em ficar preocupados com o atraso deles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The customers are right when they complain about the bad service.", "tl": "Os clientes têm razão quando reclamam do mau serviço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You're right, it's not worth arguing over something so simple.", "tl": "Tens razão, não vale a pena discutir por uma coisa tão simples."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It's possible that she is right, but I prefer to check the data first.", "tl": "É possível que ela tenha razão, mas prefiro verificar os dados primeiro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3346, "expression_id": 3372, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "faz me rir", "english_gloss": "makes me laugh (you must be joking)", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Do you really think you're going to beat the national champion? Don't make me laugh!", "tl": "Tu achas mesmo que vais vencer o campeão nacional? Faz-me rir!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "That comedian isn't very well-known, but his style of humor always makes me laugh.", "tl": "Aquele comediante não é muito conhecido, mas o seu estilo de humor sempre me faz rir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They want to charge two hundred euros for such a simple service? That proposal is a joke!", "tl": "Eles querem cobrar duzentos euros por este serviço tão simples? Essa proposta faz-me rir!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Whenever I'm sad, my dog does something silly that makes me laugh.", "tl": "Sempre que estou triste, o meu cão faz alguma parvoíce que me faz rir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He claims he does all the work alone, but that makes me laugh because we help him every day.", "tl": "Ele afirma que faz todo o trabalho sozinho, mas isso faz-me rir porque nós o ajudamos todos os dias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Remembering the trips we took in high school always makes us laugh.", "tl": "Recordar as viagens que fizemos no secundário sempre nos faz rir."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3345, "expression_id": 3371, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "calaria a boca", "english_gloss": "would silence / shut up", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If I knew it would cause so much trouble, I would shut my mouth immediately.", "tl": "Se eu soubesse que ia causar tanta confusão, calaria a boca imediatamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She thought the money would silence the witness, but she was mistaken.", "tl": "Ela achava que o dinheiro calaria a boca da testemunha, mas estava enganada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you were in my shoes, would you shut your mouth or tell the truth?", "tl": "Se você estivesse no meu lugar, calaria a boca ou diria a verdade?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I would shut my mouth if you asked me more politely.", "tl": "Eu calaria a boca se você me pedisse com mais educação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "A good argument would silence those critics once and for all.", "tl": "Um bom argumento calaria a boca daqueles críticos de uma vez por todas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Who would silence such a brave journalist?", "tl": "Quem calaria a boca de um jornalista tão corajoso?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3344, "expression_id": 3370, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "conversa fiada", "english_gloss": "idle talk / nonsense", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't believe what he says about the raise; it's just empty talk.", "tl": "Não acredite no que ele diz sobre o aumento; é apenas conversa fiada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Politicians always promise many things before elections, but most of it is just empty talk.", "tl": "Os políticos prometem sempre muitas coisas antes das eleições, mas a maioria é conversa fiada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He tried to convince me with that sweet talk, but I already know his tricks.", "tl": "Ele tentou me convencer com aquela conversa fiada, mas eu já conheço os truques dele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Let's get straight to the point and put the small talk aside, please.", "tl": "Vamos direto ao assunto e deixar a conversa fiada de lado, por favor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He said he was going to buy a new car next week, but I think it's just talk.", "tl": "Ele disse que ia comprar um carro novo na próxima semana, mas eu acho que é conversa fiada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't have time for nonsense; tell me right away how much the service will cost.", "tl": "Não tenho tempo para conversa fiada; diga-me logo quanto vai custar o serviço."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3343, "expression_id": 3369, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "pegou muita gente de surpresa", "english_gloss": "caught many people by surprise", "youtube_id": "SlMNxs3OJmg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The heavy rain in the late afternoon caught many people by surprise downtown.", "tl": "A chuva forte no fim da tarde pegou muita gente de surpresa no centro da cidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss's decision to close the office on Friday caught many people by surprise.", "tl": "A decisão do chefe de fechar o escritório na sexta-feira pegou muita gente de surpresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The ending of that movie was amazing and caught many people by surprise.", "tl": "O final daquele filme foi incrível e pegou muita gente de surpresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The new app update caught many people by surprise this week.", "tl": "A nova atualização do aplicativo pegou muita gente de surpresa esta semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The sudden increase in gas prices caught many people by surprise.", "tl": "O aumento repentino no preço da gasolina pegou muita gente de surpresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "That difficult question on the math test caught many people by surprise.", "tl": "Aquela pergunta difícil na prova de matemática pegou muita gente de surpresa."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3342, "expression_id": 3368, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "andrebbe bene", "english_gloss": "would be fine", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Would it be okay for you to meet at five in the afternoon?", "tl": "Per te andrebbe bene trovarci alle cinque del pomeriggio?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "A simple salad would be fine for me too, I'm not very hungry.", "tl": "Per me andrebbe bene anche una semplice insalata, non ho molta fame."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we moved the exam date, would that be okay with the professor?", "tl": "Se spostassimo la data dell'esame, andrebbe bene al professore?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Would it be okay if I brought my dog to the office tomorrow?", "tl": "Andrebbe bene se domani portassi il mio cane in ufficio?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Any day next week would be fine for the interview.", "tl": "Qualsiasi giorno della prossima settimana andrebbe bene per il colloquio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "A room without a sea view would also be fine for us.", "tl": "Per noi andrebbe bene anche una camera senza vista mare."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3341, "expression_id": 3367, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "scaricato tutta la colpa", "english_gloss": "shifted all the blame", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After the mistake in the project, the boss shifted all the blame onto Marco.", "tl": "Dopo l'errore nel progetto, il capo ha scaricato tutta la colpa su Marco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Instead of apologizing, they shifted all the blame onto their friends.", "tl": "Invece di chiedere scusa, hanno scaricato tutta la colpa sui loro amici."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's not fair that you shifted all the blame onto your younger brother.", "tl": "Non è giusto che tu abbia scaricato tutta la colpa su tuo fratello minore."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After the accident, the other driver shifted all the blame onto me.", "tl": "Dopo l'incidente, l'altro guidatore ha scaricato tutta la colpa su di me."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why did you shift all the blame onto your colleagues instead of admitting the mistake?", "tl": "Perché hai scaricato tutta la colpa sui tuoi colleghi invece di ammettere l'errore?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is easy to shift all the blame onto the government when things go wrong.", "tl": "È facile scaricare tutta la colpa sul governo quando le cose vanno male."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3340, "expression_id": 3366, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "tratto in inganno", "english_gloss": "misled / deceived", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I'm sorry, but I was misled by the product description on the website.", "tl": "Mi dispiace, ma sono stato tratto in inganno dalla descrizione del prodotto sul sito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Giulia was misled by the similarity between the two street names.", "tl": "Giulia è stata tratta in inganno dalla somiglianza tra i due nomi delle vie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many readers were misled by that exaggerated newspaper headline.", "tl": "Molti lettori sono stati tratti in inganno da quel titolo di giornale esagerato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't let yourself be deceived by his kind words; he is not a sincere person.", "tl": "Non farti trarre in inganno dalle sue parole gentili; non è una persona sincera."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The customers were misled by a discount that didn't actually exist.", "tl": "Le clienti sono state tratte in inganno da uno sconto che in realtà non esisteva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This morning's sun misled us, and now it's pouring rain.", "tl": "Il sole di stamattina ci ha tratti in inganno, e ora sta piovendo a dirotto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3339, "expression_id": 3365, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "tenendo conto", "english_gloss": "taking into account", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We have to plan the trip taking our budget into account.", "tl": "Dobbiamo pianificare il viaggio tenendo conto del nostro budget."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I will make a decision taking your advice into account.", "tl": "Prenderò una decisione tenendo conto dei tuoi consigli."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They organized the outdoor party, taking the weather forecast into account.", "tl": "Hanno organizzato la festa all'aperto, tenendo conto delle previsioni del tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The boss evaluated my work taking the initial difficulties into account.", "tl": "Il capo ha valutato il mio lavoro tenendo conto delle difficoltà iniziali."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The teacher gives grades taking into account also the students' effort.", "tl": "Il professore dà i voti tenendo conto anche dell'impegno degli studenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We chose this house taking into account the proximity to the subway.", "tl": "Abbiamo scelto questa casa tenendo conto della vicinanza alla metropolitana."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3338, "expression_id": 3364, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fare più affidamento ai", "english_gloss": "to rely more on", "youtube_id": "iTAuXb8ICDA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You should rely more on your colleagues instead of doing everything yourself.", "tl": "Dovresti fare più affidamento ai tuoi colleghi invece di fare tutto da solo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For this project, we need to rely more on real data than on opinions.", "tl": "Per questo progetto, dobbiamo fare più affidamento ai dati reali che alle opinioni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many young people prefer to rely more on GPS navigators than on paper maps.", "tl": "Molti giovani preferiscono fare più affidamento ai navigatori satellitari che alle mappe cartacee."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In emergency situations, one must rely more on one's own senses.", "tl": "In situazioni di emergenza, bisogna fare più affidamento ai propri sensi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If we want to reduce pollution, we must rely more on public transport.", "tl": "Se vogliamo ridurre l'inquinamento, dobbiamo fare più affidamento ai mezzi pubblici."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I learned to rely more on the advice of experienced people.", "tl": "Ho imparato a fare più affidamento ai consigli delle persone esperte."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3337, "expression_id": 3363, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "agrodolce", "english_gloss": "bittersweet", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I really like the sweet and sour sauce they serve with the spring rolls.", "tl": "Mi piace molto la salsa agrodolce che servono con gli involtini primavera."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Leaving my hometown to go to university was a bittersweet moment.", "tl": "Lasciare la mia città natale per andare all'università è stato un momento agrodolce."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The movie has a bittersweet ending that makes the viewer reflect a lot.", "tl": "Il film ha un finale agrodolce che fa riflettere molto lo spettatore."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I have a bittersweet memory of that summer spent working in a beach bar.", "tl": "Ho un ricordo agrodolce di quell'estate passata a lavorare in un bar sulla spiaggia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My grandmother always prepares sweet and sour onions as a side dish for the meat.", "tl": "Mia nonna prepara sempre le cipolle in agrodolce come contorno per la carne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Winning the match without our best player left a bittersweet taste.", "tl": "Vincere la partita senza il nostro migliore giocatore ha lasciato un sapore agrodolce."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3336, "expression_id": 3362, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "dato l'assist", "english_gloss": "to set someone up", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With that joke, you gave me the perfect assist to change the subject.", "tl": "Con quella battuta mi hai dato l'assist perfetto per cambiare argomento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss set me up during the meeting, and I was able to present my project.", "tl": "Il capo mi ha dato l'assist durante la riunione e ho potuto presentare il mio progetto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I wanted to talk about vacations, and Marco gave me the perfect cue by asking me where I'm going this summer.", "tl": "Volevo parlare di vacanze e Marco mi ha dato l'assist chiedendomi dove andrò quest'estate."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Your question gave me the opportunity to clear up this misunderstanding once and for all.", "tl": "La tua domanda mi ha dato l'assist per chiarire una volta per tutte questo malinteso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I set him up by talking about his passions, so he could make a good impression on Giulia.", "tl": "Gli ho dato l'assist parlando delle sue passioni, così ha potuto fare bella figura con Giulia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The client practically set me up when he complained about his old supplier.", "tl": "Il cliente mi ha praticamente dato l'assist quando si è lamentato del suo vecchio fornitore."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3335, "expression_id": 3361, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "spesso e volentieri", "english_gloss": "more often than not", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "On weekends, more often than not we go for a walk by the lake.", "tl": "Nel fine settimana, spesso e volentieri andiamo a fare una passeggiata al lago."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When there is a storm, more often than not the internet connection cuts out.", "tl": "Quando c'è un temporale, spesso e volentieri la connessione internet si interrompe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My brother forgets his house keys on the table more often than not.", "tl": "Mio fratello dimentica spesso e volentieri le chiavi di casa sul tavolo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "During rush hour, the trains are late more often than not.", "tl": "Durante l'ora di punta, i treni sono spesso e volentieri in ritardo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you eat junk food, more often than not you feel tired and lacking energy.", "tl": "Se mangi cibo spazzatura, spesso e volentieri ti senti stanco e senza forze."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When I go to the supermarket without a list, more often than not I buy useless things.", "tl": "Quando vado al supermercato senza una lista, spesso e volentieri compro cose inutili."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3332, "expression_id": 3358, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "nei limiti del possibile", "english_gloss": "as far as possible", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I will try to finish the project by today, as far as possible.", "tl": "Cercherò di finire il progetto entro oggi, nei limiti del possibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We always try to satisfy customers' requests, as far as possible.", "tl": "Cerchiamo sempre di soddisfare le richieste dei clienti, nei limiti del possibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Try to avoid stress, as far as possible.", "tl": "Cerca di evitare lo stress, nei limiti del possibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I would like to travel by train instead of by plane, as far as possible.", "tl": "Vorrei viaggiare in treno invece che in aereo, nei limiti del possibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We must respect the arrival time, as far as possible.", "tl": "Dobbiamo rispettare l'orario di arrivo, nei limiti del possibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I will help you with the move, as far as possible.", "tl": "Ti aiuterò con il trasloco, nei limiti del possibile."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3331, "expression_id": 3357, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "nel bene e nel male", "english_gloss": "for better or for worse", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Family always supports you, for better or for worse.", "tl": "La famiglia ti sostiene sempre, nel bene e nel male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I decided to accept this job and I will accept the consequences, for better or for worse.", "tl": "Ho deciso di accettare questo lavoro e accetterò le conseguenze, nel bene e nel male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The internet has profoundly changed our lives, for better or for worse.", "tl": "Internet ha cambiato profondamente le nostre vite, nel bene e nel male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We have been friends for twenty years and we have always helped each other, for better or for worse.", "tl": "Siamo amici da vent'anni e ci siamo sempre aiutati, nel bene e nel male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This choice will change our future, for better or for worse.", "tl": "Questa scelta cambierà il nostro futuro, nel bene e nel male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "True fans support their city's team, for better or for worse.", "tl": "I veri tifosi sostengono la squadra della propria città nel bene e nel male."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3330, "expression_id": 3356, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "loro malgrado", "english_gloss": "in spite of themselves", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The employees, in spite of themselves, had to accept the new working hours.", "tl": "I dipendenti, loro malgrado, hanno dovuto accettare il nuovo orario di lavoro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Marco and Giulia found themselves, in spite of themselves, at the center of a nasty argument.", "tl": "Marco e Giulia si sono trovati, loro malgrado, al centro di una brutta discussione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In spite of myself, I have to cancel our dinner tonight due to an unexpected event.", "tl": "Mio malgrado, devo annullare la nostra cena di stasera per un imprevisto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The tourists were stuck at the airport, in spite of themselves, because of the strike.", "tl": "I turisti sono rimasti bloccati in aeroporto, loro malgrado, a causa dello sciopero."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Luca became, in spite of himself, the protagonist of this strange story.", "tl": "Luca è diventato, suo malgrado, il protagonista di questa strana storia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our neighbors had to sell their house, in spite of themselves, for financial reasons.", "tl": "I nostri vicini hanno dovuto vendere la casa, loro malgrado, per motivi economici."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3329, "expression_id": 3355, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "punto di vista", "english_gloss": "point of view", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "From my point of view, this project has great potential.", "tl": "Dal mio punto di vista, questo progetto ha un grande potenziale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I understand your point of view, but we also have to consider the costs.", "tl": "Capisco il tuo punto di vista, ma dobbiamo considerare anche i costi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This movie shows the story from a very original point of view.", "tl": "Questo film mostra la storia da un punto di vista molto originale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you change your point of view, you will see that the situation is not so bad.", "tl": "Se cambi punto di vista, vedrai che la situazione non è così grave."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "On this topic, there are many different points of view.", "tl": "Su questo argomento ci sono molti punti di vista diversi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "From an economic point of view, the agreement is very advantageous for us.", "tl": "Dal punto di vista economico, l'accordo è molto vantaggioso per noi."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3328, "expression_id": 3354, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fai leva su", "english_gloss": "to leverage", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To sell this product, we need to leverage the customers' emotions.", "tl": "Per vendere questo prodotto, dobbiamo fare leva sulle emozioni dei clienti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you want to convince your father, appeal to his sense of responsibility.", "tl": "Se vuoi convincere tuo padre, fai leva sul suo senso di responsabilità."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Politicians often leverage people's fear to get votes.", "tl": "I politici spesso fanno leva sulla paura della gente per ottenere voti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In your resume, I advise you to highlight your language skills.", "tl": "Nel tuo curriculum, ti consiglio di fare leva sulle tue competenze linguistiche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "To overcome this problem, let's leverage our strengths.", "tl": "Per superare questo problema, facciamo leva sui nostri punti di forza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The advertisement leveraged the public's desire for youth.", "tl": "La pubblicità ha fatto leva sul desiderio di giovinezza del pubblico."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3327, "expression_id": 3353, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "giocare facile", "english_gloss": "to take the easy way out", "youtube_id": "mNub43ONwGc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It's easy to talk when you risk nothing; you're taking the easy way out that way!", "tl": "È facile parlare quando non rischi nulla; così giochi facile!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To pass the exam, he decided to study only the easiest things; in short, he wanted to take the easy way out.", "tl": "Per superare l'esame ha deciso di studiare solo le cose più semplici, insomma ha voluto giocare facile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't like winning this way, I prefer a real challenge instead of taking the easy way out.", "tl": "Non mi piace vincere in questo modo, preferisco una sfida vera invece di giocare facile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Always choosing the same destination for holidays means taking the easy way out.", "tl": "Scegliere sempre la stessa destinazione per le vacanze significa giocare facile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Instead of looking for a new job, Marco decided to take the easy way out and accept his uncle's offer.", "tl": "Invece di cercare un nuovo lavoro, Marco ha deciso di giocare facile e accettare l'offerta di suo zio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you want to improve as a writer, you can't always take the easy way out with simple stories.", "tl": "Se vuoi migliorare come scrittore, non puoi sempre giocare facile con storie semplici."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3326, "expression_id": 3352, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "por lo general", "english_gloss": "generally", "youtube_id": "_VaRguwx6do", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Generally, the weather in this region is quite mild during the autumn.", "tl": "Por lo general, el clima en esta región es bastante templado durante el otoño."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Generally, I prefer to work from home on Fridays to avoid the traffic.", "tl": "Por lo general, prefiero trabajar desde casa los viernes para evitar el tráfico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Supermarkets, generally, close earlier on Sundays and holidays.", "tl": "Los supermercados, por lo general, cierran más temprano los domingos y días festivos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Generally, the people in this town are very friendly to tourists.", "tl": "Por lo general, la gente de este pueblo es muy amable con los turistas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't usually drink coffee in the afternoon because, generally, it keeps me awake.", "tl": "No suelo tomar café por la tarde porque, por lo general, me quita el sueño."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Final exams, generally, represent forty percent of the grade.", "tl": "Los exámenes finales, por lo general, representan el cuarenta por ciento de la nota."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3325, "expression_id": 3351, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "en qué consiste", "english_gloss": "what it consists of", "youtube_id": "_VaRguwx6do", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Could you explain to me what exactly your new job consists of?", "tl": "¿Podrías explicarme en qué consiste exactamente tu nuevo trabajo?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I don't quite understand what the project you presented yesterday consists of.", "tl": "No entiendo bien en qué consiste el proyecto que presentaste ayer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The doctor explained to me what the tests they are going to do to me consist of.", "tl": "El médico me explicó en qué consisten las pruebas que me van a hacer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Before we start playing, tell us what this board game consists of.", "tl": "Antes de empezar a jugar, dinos en qué consiste este juego de mesa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In yesterday's interview they asked me what my previous job consisted of.", "tl": "En la entrevista de ayer me preguntaron en qué consistía mi anterior empleo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I want to sign up for the course, but first I need to know what it consists of.", "tl": "Quiero apuntarme al curso, pero primero necesito saber en qué consiste."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3324, "expression_id": 3350, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "en conjunto", "english_gloss": "together", "youtube_id": "_VaRguwx6do", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If we work together, we will finish the project much faster.", "tl": "Si trabajamos en conjunto, terminaremos el proyecto mucho más rápido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We made the decision together after discussing all the options.", "tl": "Tomamos la decisión en conjunto después de discutir todas las opciones."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You must evaluate the situation as a whole and not just look at the small problems.", "tl": "Debes evaluar la situación en conjunto y no solo ver los pequeños problemas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The colors of the room look very good together.", "tl": "Los colores de la sala se ven muy bien en conjunto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The two departments analyzed the data together for the report.", "tl": "Los dos departamentos analizaron los datos en conjunto para el informe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The team achieved victory thanks to the collective effort of all the players.", "tl": "El equipo logró la victoria gracias al esfuerzo en conjunto de todos los jugadores."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3323, "expression_id": 3349, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "a diario", "english_gloss": "daily", "youtube_id": "_VaRguwx6do", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I usually take the subway daily to go to the office.", "tl": "Suelo tomar el metro a diario para ir a la oficina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is important to drink enough water daily to stay hydrated.", "tl": "Es importante beber suficiente agua a diario para mantenerse hidratado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She checks her email daily so she doesn't miss any important messages.", "tl": "Ella revisa su correo electrónico a diario para no perderse ningún mensaje importante."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My grandfather goes out for a walk daily in the neighborhood park.", "tl": "Mi abuelo sale a caminar a diario por el parque del barrio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you practice Spanish daily, you will notice a big improvement in a few months.", "tl": "Si practicas español a diario, notarás una gran mejora en pocos meses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In this house we cook daily because we prefer fresh food.", "tl": "En esta casa cocinamos a diario porque preferimos la comida fresca."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3322, "expression_id": 3348, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tem como", "english_gloss": "has as", "youtube_id": "Fh_l5SRQJZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Is there any way you can send me that report by email?", "tl": "Tem como você me enviar aquele relatório por e-mail?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Unfortunately, there is no way to change the travel date now.", "tl": "Infelizmente, não tem como mudar a data da viagem agora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Is it possible to go to the city center on foot or is it too far?", "tl": "Tem como ir para o centro da cidade a pé ou é muito longe?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Do you think there's a way for us to solve this problem without calling support?", "tl": "Será que tem como a gente resolver esse problema sem ligar para o suporte?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "There was no way for me to know that the store would be closed today.", "tl": "Não tinha como eu saber que a loja estaria fechada hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you are not too busy, would it be possible to give me a ride?", "tl": "Se você não estiver muito ocupado, teria como me dar uma carona?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3321, "expression_id": 3347, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dar tempo", "english_gloss": "to be in time", "youtube_id": "Fh_l5SRQJZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Do you think there's still time to catch the six o'clock bus?", "tl": "Será que ainda dá tempo de pegar o ônibus das seis?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I wanted to say goodbye to him at the airport, but there wasn't enough time.", "tl": "Eu queria me despedir dele no aeroporto, mas não deu tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you hurry, I think there's still time for us to have lunch together.", "tl": "Se você se apressar, acho que ainda dá tempo de almoçarmos juntos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't worry, there will be enough time to finish the report before the meeting.", "tl": "Não se preocupe, vai dar tempo de terminar o relatório antes da reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Unfortunately, there wasn't enough time to stop by the supermarket yesterday.", "tl": "Infelizmente não deu tempo de passar no supermercado ontem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If there is time, we can have a coffee after work.", "tl": "Se der tempo, nós podemos tomar um café depois do trabalho."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3320, "expression_id": 3346, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "em contradição com", "english_gloss": "in contradiction with", "youtube_id": "Fh_l5SRQJZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "What he does is in contradiction with what he says.", "tl": "O que ele faz está em contradição com o que ele diz."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This new rule is in contradiction with the previous regulation.", "tl": "Esta nova regra está em contradição com o regulamento anterior."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Her testimony contradicts the police evidence.", "tl": "O testemunho dela entra em contradição com as provas da polícia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His attitude is in contradiction with the company's values.", "tl": "A atitude dele está em contradição com os valores da empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The director's decision is in contradiction with what was decided at the meeting.", "tl": "A decisão do diretor está em contradição com o que foi decidido na reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The research results seem to be in contradiction with the initial theory.", "tl": "Os resultados da pesquisa parecem estar em contradição com a teoria inicial."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3319, "expression_id": 3345, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "segundo a qual", "english_gloss": "according to which", "youtube_id": "Fh_l5SRQJZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The theory according to which the Earth is flat has long been debunked.", "tl": "A teoria segundo a qual a Terra é plana já foi superada há muito tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They passed a new law according to which smoking in public parks is prohibited.", "tl": "Eles aprovaram uma nova lei segundo a qual é proibido fumar em parques públicos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't believe his version, according to which the accident was the other driver's fault.", "tl": "Não acredito na versão dele, segundo a qual o acidente foi culpa do outro motorista."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She defends the idea according to which remote work improves productivity.", "tl": "Ela defende a ideia segundo a qual o trabalho remoto melhora a produtividade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company has a strict rule according to which no employee can accept gifts from clients.", "tl": "A empresa tem uma regra estrita segundo a qual nenhum funcionário pode aceitar presentes de clientes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Scientists presented a hypothesis according to which the climate will change drastically in the coming years.", "tl": "Os cientistas apresentaram uma hipótese segundo a qual o clima vai mudar drasticamente nos próximos anos."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3318, "expression_id": 3344, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vai se constituindo", "english_gloss": "is gradually being formed", "youtube_id": "Fh_l5SRQJZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "A young person's identity is gradually being formed through their life experiences.", "tl": "A identidade de um jovem vai se constituindo através das suas experiências de vida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "A new neighborhood is gradually taking shape around the new subway station.", "tl": "Um novo bairro vai se constituindo ao redor da nova estação de metrô."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Public opinion on the topic is gradually being formed as the debate progresses.", "tl": "A opinião pública sobre o tema vai se constituindo à medida que o debate avança."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The working group is gradually being formed little by little, with professionals from various fields.", "tl": "O grupo de trabalho vai se constituindo aos poucos, com profissionais de várias áreas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Scientific knowledge doesn't appear out of nowhere; it is gradually built up over the years.", "tl": "O conhecimento científico não surge do nada; ele vai se constituindo ao longo dos anos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "A company's culture is gradually formed on a day-to-day basis, through small actions.", "tl": "A cultura de uma empresa vai se constituindo no dia a dia, através das pequenas ações."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3317, "expression_id": 3343, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "zuvorkommen", "english_gloss": "to forestall / preempt", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I wanted to buy the last ticket, but someone beat me to it.", "tl": "Ich wollte das letzte Ticket kaufen, aber jemand ist mir zuvorgekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We have to act quickly to forestall the competition.", "tl": "Wir müssen schnell handeln, um der Konkurrenz zuvorzukommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She wanted to tell the truth before someone else beat her to it.", "tl": "Sie wollte die Wahrheit sagen, bevor ihr jemand anderes zuvorkam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I was just about to apologize, but you beat me to it.", "tl": "Ich wollte mich gerade entschuldigen, aber du bist mir zuvorgekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "With this measure, we want to preempt potential problems.", "tl": "Mit dieser Maßnahme wollen wir möglichen Problemen zuvorkommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He asked the question to beat his colleague to it.", "tl": "Er stellte die Frage, um seinem Kollegen zuvorzukommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3316, "expression_id": 3342, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf Verdacht", "english_gloss": "just in case / on suspicion", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The doctor prescribed me an antibiotic just in case, although the test results aren't in yet.", "tl": "Der Arzt hat mir auf Verdacht ein Antibiotikum verschrieben, obwohl die Testergebnisse noch nicht da sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Because it was cloudy, I took an umbrella with me just in case.", "tl": "Weil es bewölkt war, habe ich auf Verdacht einen Regenschirm mitgenommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The police arrested the man on suspicion, but released him the next day.", "tl": "Die Polizei nahm den Mann auf Verdacht fest, ließ ihn aber am nächsten Tag wieder frei."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I bought two movie tickets just in case you have time tonight.", "tl": "Ich habe auf Verdacht zwei Kinokarten gekauft, falls du heute Abend Zeit hast."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We had the old heating system replaced just in case, before winter starts.", "tl": "Wir haben die alte Heizung auf Verdacht austauschen lassen, bevor der Winter anfängt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I cooked a bit more pasta just in case, because I didn't know how hungry you were.", "tl": "Ich habe auf Verdacht etwas mehr Nudeln gekocht, weil ich nicht wusste, wie hungrig du bist."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3315, "expression_id": 3341, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "unter Druck zu setzen", "english_gloss": "to put under pressure", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My boss often tries to put me under pressure so that I work faster.", "tl": "Mein Chef versucht oft, mich unter Druck zu setzen, damit ich schneller arbeite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The journalists put the politician under a lot of pressure with their questions.", "tl": "Die Journalisten haben den Politiker mit ihren Fragen stark unter Druck gesetzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You shouldn't let your friends pressure you.", "tl": "Du solltest dich von deinen Freunden nicht unter Druck setzen lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The tight deadline is putting the entire team under extreme pressure.", "tl": "Der knappe Abgabetermin setzt das gesamte Team extrem unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I need time for my decision, please don't try to pressure me.", "tl": "Ich brauche Zeit für meine Entscheidung, bitte versuch nicht, mich unter Druck zu setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Many parents put their children under too much pressure because of school grades.", "tl": "Viele Eltern setzen ihre Kinder wegen der Schulnoten zu sehr unter Druck."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3314, "expression_id": 3340, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da", "english_gloss": "how is the country doing militarily", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After the many budget cuts, many are wondering: how is the country doing militarily right now?", "tl": "Nach den vielen Kürzungen im Haushalt fragen sich viele: Wie steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "General, if we look at the current crisis, how is the country doing militarily right now?", "tl": "Herr General, wenn wir die aktuelle Krise betrachten, wie steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We have to be honest and ask ourselves: where does the country stand militarily right now if a conflict breaks out tomor", "tl": "Wir müssen ehrlich sein und uns fragen: Wie steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da, wenn morgen ein Konflikt ausbrich"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't follow the news very often, so how is the country doing militarily right now?", "tl": "Ich verfolge die Nachrichten nicht so oft, also wie steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Ten years ago the situation was different, but how is the country doing militarily right now?", "tl": "Vor zehn Jahren war die Situation anders, aber wie steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In view of the new threats in Europe, the question arises: how is the country doing militarily right now?", "tl": "Angesichts der neuen Bedrohungen in Europa stellt sich die Frage: Wie steht das Land denn militärisch gerade da?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3313, "expression_id": 3339, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die Initiative übernommen", "english_gloss": "to take the initiative", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Because no one wanted to make a decision, Sarah finally took the initiative.", "tl": "Weil niemand eine Entscheidung treffen wollte, hat Sarah schließlich die Initiative übernommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you want a raise, you have to take the initiative yourself.", "tl": "Wenn du eine Gehaltserhöhung willst, musst du selbst die Initiative übernehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Which of you will take the initiative and plan the next meeting?", "tl": "Wer von euch übernimmt die Initiative und plant das nächste Treffen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "A neighbor took the initiative and organized a big street party.", "tl": "Ein Nachbar hat die Initiative übernommen und ein großes Straßenfest organisiert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is important to sometimes take the initiative at work.", "tl": "Es ist wichtig, im Beruf manchmal die Initiative zu übernehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I am glad that you took the initiative and apologized to him.", "tl": "Ich bin froh, dass du die Initiative übernommen und dich bei ihm entschuldigt hast."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3312, "expression_id": 3338, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "wie eingefroren zu sein", "english_gloss": "to be frozen / at a standstill", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Suddenly nothing worked anymore; the screen was frozen.", "tl": "Plötzlich ging gar nichts mehr, der Bildschirm war wie eingefroren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When she heard the noise in the dark, she stood there as if frozen.", "tl": "Als sie das Geräusch im Dunkeln hörte, stand sie wie eingefroren da."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There has been no progress for weeks; the project seems to be at a standstill.", "tl": "Seit Wochen gibt es keine Fortschritte, das Projekt scheint wie eingefroren zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Nothing was moving forward on the highway; the entire traffic was at a complete standstill.", "tl": "Auf der Autobahn ging nichts mehr vorwärts, der gesamte Verkehr war wie eingefroren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "After his rude comment, the atmosphere in the room was like frozen.", "tl": "Nach seinem unhöflichen Kommentar war die Stimmung im Raum wie eingefroren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Since our argument, contact between us has been at a standstill.", "tl": "Seit unserem Streit ist der Kontakt zwischen uns wie eingefroren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3311, "expression_id": 3337, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ums Leben gekommen", "english_gloss": "to lose one's life", "youtube_id": "ngCcjjIrjNg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "A man lost his life yesterday in the severe car accident on the highway.", "tl": "Bei dem schweren Autounfall auf der Autobahn ist gestern ein Mann ums Leben gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Unfortunately, many people lost their lives due to the strong earthquake.", "tl": "Durch das starke Erdbeben sind leider viele Menschen ums Leben gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My great-grandfather lost his life in the Second World War.", "tl": "Mein Urgroßvater ist im Zweiten Weltkrieg ums Leben gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Fortunately, nobody lost their life in the fire downtown.", "tl": "Zum Glück ist bei dem Brand in der Innenstadt niemand ums Leben gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Two mountain climbers lost their lives during the sudden blizzard in the Alps.", "tl": "Zwei Bergsteiger sind bei dem plötzlichen Schneesturm in den Alpen ums Leben gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Three workers lost their lives in the explosion at the factory.", "tl": "Bei der Explosion in der Fabrik sind drei Arbeiter ums Leben gekommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3310, "expression_id": 3336, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "aus dem Rennen genommen", "english_gloss": "taken out of the race", "youtube_id": "GBMrrdmGf-U", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to a knee injury, the runner was taken out of the race shortly before the final.", "tl": "Wegen einer Knieverletzung wurde der Läufer kurz vor dem Finale aus dem Rennen genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Because the product didn't sell well, the company quickly withdrew it from the market.", "tl": "Weil das Produkt sich nicht gut verkaufte, hat die Firma es schnell aus dem Rennen genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the first job interview, three applicants were eliminated from the running.", "tl": "Nach dem ersten Vorstellungsgespräch wurden drei Bewerber aus dem Rennen genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The politician took himself out of the running after the scandal.", "tl": "Der Politiker hat sich nach dem Skandal selbst aus dem Rennen genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Unfortunately, our team was already knocked out of the competition in the first round.", "tl": "Unser Team wurde leider schon in der ersten Runde des Wettbewerbs aus dem Rennen genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The flu completely took me out of action for a whole week.", "tl": "Die Grippe hat mich für eine ganze Woche komplett aus dem Rennen genommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3309, "expression_id": 3335, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "von sich reden machen", "english_gloss": "to make a name for oneself", "youtube_id": "GBMrrdmGf-U", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new startup from Berlin is making a name for itself in the tech industry.", "tl": "Das neue Start-up aus Berlin macht in der Technologiebranche von sich reden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The young painter has made a name for herself abroad with her latest exhibition.", "tl": "Die junge Malerin hat mit ihrer letzten Ausstellung im Ausland von sich reden gemacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I am sure that this young soccer player will soon make a name for himself in the Bundesliga.", "tl": "Ich bin sicher, dass dieser junge Fußballspieler bald in der Bundesliga von sich reden machen wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "A few years ago, the small village made a name for itself through an innovative environmental project.", "tl": "Vor einigen Jahren machte das kleine Dorf durch ein innovatives Umweltprojekt von sich reden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The research group is currently getting people talking with a new study on climate change.", "tl": "Die Forschergruppe macht zurzeit mit einer neuen Studie über den Klimawandel von sich reden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "With this extraordinary voice, the singer will surely make a name for herself soon.", "tl": "Mit dieser außergewöhnlichen Stimme wird die Sängerin sicher bald von sich reden machen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3308, "expression_id": 3334, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "nimmt die Sache mit Humor", "english_gloss": "takes the matter with humor", "youtube_id": "GBMrrdmGf-U", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Although his car won't start this morning, he takes the matter with humor and rides his bike.", "tl": "Obwohl sein Auto heute Morgen nicht anspringt, nimmt er die Sache mit Humor und fährt mit dem Fahrrad."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't worry about the rain on our wedding day, just take the matter with humor!", "tl": "Mach dir keine Sorgen wegen des Regens an unserem Hochzeitstag, nimm die Sache einfach mit Humor!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The dinner was completely burned, but our guests took the matter with humor.", "tl": "Das Abendessen ist völlig verbrannt, aber unsere Gäste haben die Sache mit Humor genommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our flight is delayed by three hours, but we are taking the matter with humor and having a coffee first.", "tl": "Unser Flug hat drei Stunden Verspätung, aber wir nehmen die Sache mit Humor und trinken erst mal einen Kaffee."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You can't control everything in everyday life; sometimes you just have to take the matter with humor.", "tl": "Man kann im Alltag nicht alles kontrollieren, manchmal muss man die Sache einfach mit Humor nehmen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She accidentally put on two different socks, but she takes the matter with humor.", "tl": "Sie hat aus Versehen zwei verschiedene Socken angezogen, aber sie nimmt die Sache mit Humor."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3307, "expression_id": 3333, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf Linie", "english_gloss": "in line with the official policy", "youtube_id": "GBMrrdmGf-U", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In this company, all employees must be in line with policy, otherwise there is trouble with the management.", "tl": "In dieser Firma müssen alle Mitarbeiter auf Linie sein, sonst gibt es Ärger mit der Geschäftsführung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The party leader has been trying for weeks to bring the dissatisfied members back into line.", "tl": "Der Parteichef versucht seit Wochen, die unzufriedenen Mitglieder wieder auf Linie zu bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The newspaper is known for its articles always being strictly in line with the government's policy.", "tl": "Die Zeitung ist bekannt dafür, dass ihre Artikel immer streng auf Linie der Regierung sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Before the important client meeting, we need to bring the entire team into line.", "tl": "Vor dem wichtigen Kundentermin müssen wir das gesamte Team auf Linie bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Some teachers refuse to be in line with the new school reform.", "tl": "Einige Lehrer weigern sich, bei der neuen Schulreform auf Linie zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Anyone who is not in line with policy in this club is quickly excluded.", "tl": "Wer in diesem Verein nicht auf Linie ist, wird schnell ausgeschlossen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3306, "expression_id": 3332, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich in Sicherheit bringen", "english_gloss": "to get to safety", "youtube_id": "ETxP3LNYnh8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When the thunderstorm started, the hikers quickly got to safety.", "tl": "Als das Gewitter anfing, brachten sich die Wanderer schnell in Sicherheit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Please get to safety immediately, the building is on fire!", "tl": "Bitte bringen Sie sich sofort in Sicherheit, das Gebäude brennt!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The cat got to safety on the tree from the big dog.", "tl": "Die Katze hat sich vor dem großen Hund auf dem Baum in Sicherheit gebracht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Because of the flood, the residents of the street had to get to safety.", "tl": "Wegen des Hochwassers mussten sich die Bewohner der Straße in Sicherheit bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During an earthquake, you should get to safety under a sturdy table.", "tl": "Bei einem Erdbeben sollte man sich unter einem stabilen Tisch in Sicherheit bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We managed to get to safety in the basement just in time before the storm came.", "tl": "Wir konnten uns gerade noch rechtzeitig im Keller in Sicherheit bringen, bevor der Sturm kam."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3305, "expression_id": 3331, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "dauert es noch, bis", "english_gloss": "it will still take time until", "youtube_id": "ETxP3LNYnh8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It will certainly take another half hour until dinner is ready.", "tl": "Es dauert bestimmt noch eine halbe Stunde, bis das Abendessen fertig ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "How much longer will it take until we get the results of the project?", "tl": "Wie lange dauert es noch, bis wir die Ergebnisse des Projekts bekommen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Unfortunately, it will still take a few months until it gets really warm again.", "tl": "Leider dauert es noch ein paar Monate, bis es wieder richtig warm wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Will it still take a long time until the train finally departs?", "tl": "Dauert es noch lange, bis der Zug endlich abfährt?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Even though I study hard, it will still take time until I can speak German fluently.", "tl": "Obwohl ich fleißig lerne, dauert es noch, bis ich fließend Deutsch sprechen kann."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Will it still take a very long time until the new app version is available in the store?", "tl": "Dauert es noch sehr lange, bis die neue App-Version im Store verfügbar ist?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3304, "expression_id": 3330, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "für den Notfall", "english_gloss": "for emergencies", "youtube_id": "ETxP3LNYnh8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I always have some cash with me for emergencies.", "tl": "Ich habe immer etwas Bargeld für den Notfall dabei."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Save this number in your phone for emergencies.", "tl": "Speicher diese Nummer für den Notfall in deinem Handy ab."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We should keep a few canned foods in the basement for emergencies.", "tl": "Wir sollten ein paar Konserven für den Notfall im Keller haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I am leaving a spare key with my neighbor for emergencies.", "tl": "Ich lasse meinen Nachbarn einen Zweitschlüssel für den Notfall da."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Take these pills with you on the trip for emergencies.", "tl": "Nimm diese Tabletten für den Notfall mit auf die Reise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "For emergencies, there is a flashlight in the drawer.", "tl": "Für den Notfall liegt eine Taschenlampe in der Schublade."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3303, "expression_id": 3329, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "schon lange nicht mehr", "english_gloss": "not for a long time", "youtube_id": "ETxP3LNYnh8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I haven't visited my grandparents for a long time.", "tl": "Ich habe meine Großeltern schon lange nicht mehr besucht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We haven't been to the cinema for a long time.", "tl": "Wir waren schon lange nicht mehr im Kino."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It hasn't rained here for a long time.", "tl": "Es hat hier schon lange nicht mehr geregnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I haven't played tennis for a long time, so I'm a bit out of practice.", "tl": "Ich habe schon lange nicht mehr Tennis gespielt, deshalb bin ich etwas aus der Übung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I haven't cooked this dish for a long time.", "tl": "Dieses Gericht habe ich schon lange nicht mehr gekocht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She hasn't felt this happy for a long time.", "tl": "Sie hat sich schon lange nicht mehr so glücklich gefühlt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3302, "expression_id": 3328, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "als sonst", "english_gloss": "than usual", "youtube_id": "ETxP3LNYnh8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Today it is much colder than usual in October.", "tl": "Heute ist es viel kälter als sonst im Oktober."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I got up earlier than usual today to avoid the traffic jam.", "tl": "Ich bin heute früher aufgestanden als sonst, um den Stau zu vermeiden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Why are you so quiet today? You are speaking much less than usual.", "tl": "Warum bist du heute so ruhig? Du sprichst viel weniger als sonst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In December, we have many more customers in the shop than usual.", "tl": "Im Dezember haben wir im Geschäft viel mehr Kunden als sonst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "After the workout yesterday, I feel more tired than usual today.", "tl": "Nach dem Training gestern fühle ich mich heute müder als sonst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The internet connection is much slower than usual tonight.", "tl": "Die Internetverbindung ist heute Abend viel langsamer als sonst."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3301, "expression_id": 3327, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "vor allem", "english_gloss": "especially, above all", "youtube_id": "ETxP3LNYnh8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I like reading books, especially historical novels.", "tl": "Ich lese gerne Bücher, vor allem historische Romane."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In summer I like to travel, especially to the sea.", "tl": "Im Sommer reise ich gerne, vor allem ans Meer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "One should drink a lot of water, especially when it is hot.", "tl": "Man sollte viel Wasser trinken, vor allem wenn es heiß ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For this project we need patience above all.", "tl": "Für dieses Projekt brauchen wir vor allem Geduld."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He eats healthily, especially a lot of fresh vegetables.", "tl": "Er isst gesund, vor allem viel frisches Gemüse."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "To learn a language, you have to practice regularly above all.", "tl": "Um eine Sprache zu lernen, muss man vor allem regelmäßig üben."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3300, "expression_id": 3326, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire le buzz", "english_gloss": "to create a buzz, go viral", "youtube_id": "hG1dRsyDSnA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Her new video on TikTok went viral in just a few hours.", "tl": "Sa nouvelle vidéo sur TikTok a fait le buzz en seulement quelques heures."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Do you think our project is going to create a buzz on social media?", "tl": "Tu penses que notre projet va faire le buzz sur les réseaux sociaux ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This clothing brand is always looking to create a buzz with original advertisements.", "tl": "Cette marque de vêtements cherche toujours à faire le buzz avec des publicités originales."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I didn't expect my photo to go viral on the internet.", "tl": "Je ne m'attendais pas à ce que ma photo fasse le buzz sur Internet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The young singer went viral after his appearance on television.", "tl": "Le jeune chanteur a fait le buzz après son passage à la télévision."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Sometimes, all it takes is a simple idea to create a buzz and attract customers.", "tl": "Parfois, il suffit d'une idée simple pour faire le buzz et attirer des clients."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3299, "expression_id": 3325, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faisaient déjà l'objet d'une", "english_gloss": "to be the subject of, undergo", "youtube_id": "hG1dRsyDSnA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The factory's old machines were already the subject of daily monitoring.", "tl": "Les anciennes machines de l'usine faisaient déjà l'objet d'une surveillance quotidienne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "These safety rules were already undergoing a re-evaluation by management.", "tl": "Ces règles de sécurité faisaient déjà l'objet d'une réévaluation par la direction."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "His first paintings were already the subject of great admiration among critics.", "tl": "Ses premières peintures faisaient déjà l'objet d'une grande admiration parmi les critiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The endangered species of this region were already subject to strict protection.", "tl": "Les espèces menacées de cette région faisaient déjà l'objet d'une protection stricte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The old buildings in the city center were already undergoing a complete renovation.", "tl": "Les vieux bâtiments du centre-ville faisaient déjà l'objet d'une rénovation complète."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "These bills were already the subject of a lively discussion in the Assembly.", "tl": "Ces propositions de loi faisaient déjà l'objet d'une vive discussion à l'Assemblée."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3298, "expression_id": 3324, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "prennent davantage pour cible", "english_gloss": "to target, choose as a target", "youtube_id": "hG1dRsyDSnA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sports brands are targeting young people under twenty more.", "tl": "Les marques de sport prennent davantage pour cible les jeunes de moins de vingt ans."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Nowadays, hackers are targeting small businesses more.", "tl": "De nos jours, les pirates informatiques prennent davantage pour cible les petites entreprises."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Journalists are targeting the government's economic decisions more.", "tl": "Les journalistes prennent davantage pour cible les décisions économiques du gouvernement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In summer, these insects target people wearing perfume more.", "tl": "En été, ces insectes prennent davantage pour cible les personnes qui portent du parfum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new prevention campaigns are targeting students more.", "tl": "Les nouvelles campagnes de prévention prennent davantage pour cible les étudiants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Streaming platforms are increasingly targeting documentary lovers.", "tl": "Les plateformes de streaming prennent davantage pour cible les amateurs de documentaires."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3297, "expression_id": 3323, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "est au cœur de", "english_gloss": "to be at the heart of, central to", "youtube_id": "hG1dRsyDSnA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Regular practice is at the heart of language learning.", "tl": "La pratique régulière est au cœur de l'apprentissage d'une langue."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Environmental protection is at the heart of current debates.", "tl": "La protection de l'environnement est au cœur des débats actuels."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Customer satisfaction is at the heart of our business strategy.", "tl": "La satisfaction du client est au cœur de notre stratégie d'entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Trust is at the heart of any friendly or professional relationship.", "tl": "La confiance est au cœur de toute relation amicale ou professionnelle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This new technology is at the heart of the research project.", "tl": "Cette nouvelle technologie est au cœur du projet de recherche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Impossible love is at the heart of this famous novel.", "tl": "L'amour impossible est au cœur de ce célèbre roman."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3296, "expression_id": 3322, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "revenir sur", "english_gloss": "to look back on, return to a topic", "youtube_id": "hG1dRsyDSnA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I would like to return to an important point that we discussed yesterday.", "tl": "J'aimerais revenir sur un point important que nous avons abordé hier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The director went back on his decision after speaking with the team.", "tl": "Le directeur est revenu sur sa décision après avoir parlé avec l'équipe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In his latest book, the author looks back on his difficult childhood.", "tl": "Dans son dernier livre, l'auteur revient sur son enfance difficile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We absolutely must return to this question during our next meeting.", "tl": "Nous devons absolument revenir sur cette question lors de notre prochaine réunion."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You can't go back on your promise now, it's too late.", "tl": "Tu ne peux pas revenir sur ta promesse maintenant, c'est trop tard."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If we look back on the past year, we realize that a lot of things have changed.", "tl": "Si on revient sur l'année passée, on se rend compte que beaucoup de choses ont changé."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3295, "expression_id": 3321, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "rester à l'écart", "english_gloss": "to stay out of, keep away from", "youtube_id": "hG1dRsyDSnA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I prefer to stay away from the noise when I have a headache.", "tl": "Je préfère rester à l'écart du bruit quand j'ai mal à la tête."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She decided to stay out of this family argument.", "tl": "Elle a décidé de rester à l'écart de cette dispute familiale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "During the meeting, they stayed on the sidelines and said nothing.", "tl": "Pendant la réunion, ils sont restés à l'écart et n'ont rien dit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Stay away from this neighborhood at night, it's safer.", "tl": "Restez à l'écart de ce quartier pendant la nuit, c'est plus sûr."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since we were sick, we stayed away from the others.", "tl": "Comme nous étions malades, nous sommes restés à l'écart des autres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He prefers to stay out of political discussions at the office.", "tl": "Il préfère rester à l'écart des discussions politiques au bureau."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3294, "expression_id": 3320, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de última hora", "english_gloss": "at the last minute", "youtube_id": "M0YjAuQVJRw", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I had to buy a ticket at the last minute because something unexpected came up.", "tl": "Tive de comprar um bilhete de última hora porque surgiu um imprevisto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The meeting was canceled at the last minute and I was already on my way to the office.", "tl": "A reunião foi cancelada de última hora e eu já estava a caminho do escritório."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They decided to change plans at the last minute, which caused us some problems.", "tl": "Eles decidiram mudar de planos de última hora, o que nos causou alguns problemas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I didn't buy anything in advance, so I had to choose a last-minute gift.", "tl": "Não comprei nada com antecedência, por isso tive de escolher um presente de última hora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She invited us to dinner at the last minute, but unfortunately we already had plans.", "tl": "Ela convidou-nos para o jantar de última hora, mas infelizmente já tínhamos compromissos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "To avoid problems, I prefer not to make last-minute reservations.", "tl": "Para evitar problemas, eu prefiro não fazer reservas de última hora."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3293, "expression_id": 3319, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "pai soluça, o filho desmaia", "english_gloss": "like father, like son (exaggerated)", "youtube_id": "M0YjAuQVJRw", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Pedro loves football and his son already wants to be a professional player. It's really a case of: like father, like son", "tl": "O Pedro adora futebol e o filho dele já quer ser jogador profissional. É mesmo aquele caso: pai soluça, o filho desmaia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If my husband gets worried about the bills, our son can't even sleep. In our house, it's like father, like son.", "tl": "Se o meu marido fica preocupado com as contas, o nosso filho nem consegue dormir. Lá em casa, o pai soluça e o filho des"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My father doesn't eat soup and I refuse to eat any vegetables. As they say: like father, like son.", "tl": "O meu pai não come sopa e eu recuso-me a comer qualquer legume. Como se costuma dizer: pai soluça, o filho desmaia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The boss is very disorganized, but his son, who now works with us, manages to be even worse. It's like father, like son.", "tl": "O patrão é muito desorganizado, mas o filho dele, que agora trabalha connosco, consegue ser ainda pior. É o pai soluça, "}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When João has a mild cold, his son wants to go to the hospital right away. It's very true: like father, like son.", "tl": "Quando o João tem uma constipação leve, o filho dele quer logo ir para o hospital. É bem verdade que o pai soluça e o fi"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The musician spends the day playing guitar and his young daughter already cries if they don't let her play piano. Over t", "tl": "O músico passa o dia a tocar guitarra e a filha pequena já chora se não a deixarem tocar piano. Ali, o pai soluça e o fi"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3292, "expression_id": 3318, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "cantou a pedra", "english_gloss": "to call it / predict something correctly", "youtube_id": "M0YjAuQVJRw", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "João called it that they were going to break up before the end of the year.", "tl": "O João cantou a pedra que eles iam terminar antes do fim do ano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I had already called it that that project wasn't going to work out.", "tl": "Eu já tinha cantado a pedra que aquele projeto não ia dar certo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The commentator called it regarding the opposing team's tactics.", "tl": "O comentarista cantou a pedra sobre a tática do time adversário."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My mother called it and told me to bring an umbrella.", "tl": "Minha mãe cantou a pedra e disse para eu levar um guarda-chuva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You called the ending of the movie in the very first minutes.", "tl": "Você cantou a pedra sobre o final do filme logo nos primeiros minutos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We called it, but nobody wanted to believe us.", "tl": "Nós cantamos a pedra, mas ninguém quis acreditar na gente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3291, "expression_id": 3317, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "fora de órbita", "english_gloss": "out of touch / crazy", "youtube_id": "M0YjAuQVJRw", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He is completely spaced out today; he didn't hear anything I said in the meeting.", "tl": "Ele está completamente fora de órbita hoje, não ouviu nada do que eu disse na reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "That politician is out of touch if he thinks people can pay that price.", "tl": "Aquele político está fora de órbita se acha que as pessoas podem pagar esse preço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Sorry, I've been a bit out of it lately because I haven't been sleeping well.", "tl": "Desculpa, ando um pouco fora de órbita ultimamente porque tenho dormido mal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You want to buy a luxury car now? You are completely out of your mind!", "tl": "Tu queres comprar um carro de luxo agora? Estás completamente fora de órbita!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When she starts thinking about the future, she immediately spaces out and doesn't even answer.", "tl": "Quando ela começa a pensar no futuro, fica logo fora de órbita e nem responde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My grandfather is a bit out of touch when it comes to new technologies.", "tl": "O meu avô está um pouco fora de órbita em relação às novas tecnologias."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3290, "expression_id": 3316, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "más viejo que el hilo negro", "english_gloss": "older than the hills / cliché", "youtube_id": "v0IyIZ0lPis", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That joke you told me is older than the hills; my grandfather already knew it.", "tl": "Ese chiste que me contaste es más viejo que el hilo negro; ya se lo sabía mi abuelo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I don't know why you still keep that mobile phone, it's older than the hills and doesn't have internet.", "tl": "No sé por qué todavía guardas ese teléfono móvil, si es más viejo que el hilo negro y no tiene internet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That excuse about forgetting your keys is older than the hills; make up something better.", "tl": "Esa excusa de que se te olvidaron las llaves es más vieja que el hilo negro; inventa algo mejor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Although you think you've discovered a new fashion trend, wearing wide pants is older than the hills.", "tl": "Aunque pienses que has descubierto una nueva moda, llevar pantalones anchos es más viejo que el hilo negro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That love story between those two is older than the hills, the whole neighborhood knows about it.", "tl": "Esa historia de amor entre ellos dos es más vieja que el hilo negro, todo el barrio la conoce."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The trick of studying at the last minute is older than the hills and almost never works.", "tl": "El truco de estudiar a última hora es más viejo que el hilo negro y casi nunca funciona."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3289, "expression_id": 3315, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "cierren filas", "english_gloss": "close ranks / unite in support", "youtube_id": "v0IyIZ0lPis", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the face of the current crisis, the party members decided to close ranks around their leader.", "tl": "Ante la crisis actual, los miembros del partido decidieron cerrar filas en torno a su líder."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When things get difficult, our family always closes ranks to help each other.", "tl": "Cuando las cosas se ponen difíciles, nuestra familia siempre cierra filas para ayudarse."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The coach asked us to close ranks and stay united for the next game.", "tl": "El entrenador nos pidió que cerremos filas y nos mantengamos unidos para el próximo partido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The employees closed ranks to defend the project against criticism from the press.", "tl": "Los empleados cerraron filas para defender el proyecto contra las críticas de la prensa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is time for us neighbors to close ranks and demand more safety in the neighborhood.", "tl": "Es hora de que los vecinos cerremos filas y exijamos más seguridad en el barrio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The board of directors is closing ranks to prevent the company from splitting.", "tl": "La junta directiva está cerrando filas para evitar que la empresa se divida."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3288, "expression_id": 3314, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "devueltos en caliente", "english_gloss": "summarily deported / pushed back immediately", "youtube_id": "v0IyIZ0lPis", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The migrants who jumped the Ceuta fence were summarily deported without being able to apply for asylum.", "tl": "Los migrantes que saltaron la valla de Ceuta fueron devueltos en caliente sin poder pedir asilo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The European Court of Human Rights has debated whether it is legal for a foreigner to be immediately pushed back.", "tl": "El Tribunal Europeo de Derechos Humanos ha debatido si es legal que un extranjero sea devuelto en caliente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Several organizations denounce that many people are summarily deported at the southern border.", "tl": "Varias organizaciones denuncian que muchas personas son devueltas en caliente en la frontera sur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The police detained the young men at the border and summarily deported them that same night.", "tl": "La policía detuvo a los jóvenes en la frontera y los devolvió en caliente esa misma noche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "According to current law, those who enter illegally can be pushed back immediately.", "tl": "Según la ley actual, los que entran de forma ilegal pueden ser devueltos en caliente inmediatamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She tried to cross the river, but was discovered by the guards and immediately pushed back to her country.", "tl": "Ella intentó cruzar el río, pero fue descubierta por los guardias y devuelta en caliente a su país."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3287, "expression_id": 3313, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "se ha visto obligada a", "english_gloss": "has found itself forced to", "youtube_id": "v0IyIZ0lPis", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to the crisis, the company has found itself forced to reduce its staff.", "tl": "Debido a la crisis, la empresa se ha visto obligada a reducir su personal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The director has found himself forced to cancel this afternoon's meeting due to a last-minute problem.", "tl": "El director se ha visto obligado a cancelar la reunión de esta tarde por un problema de última hora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many neighbors have found themselves forced to change their cars because of the new pollution regulations.", "tl": "Muchos vecinos se han visto obligados a cambiar sus coches por las nuevas normas de contaminación."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The schools in the area have found themselves forced to suspend classes due to the severe storm.", "tl": "Las escuelas de la zona se han visto obligadas a suspender las clases por el fuerte temporal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She has found herself forced to look for a second job to be able to pay the apartment rent.", "tl": "Ella se ha visto obligada a buscar un segundo trabajo para poder pagar el alquiler del piso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The tourists have found themselves forced to stay at the hotel due to the transport strike.", "tl": "Los turistas se han visto obligados a quedarse en el hotel por la huelga de transporte."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3286, "expression_id": 3312, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "está exenta de", "english_gloss": "is not free from", "youtube_id": "b9oOjJWadhs", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "No person is free from making mistakes at work.", "tl": "Ninguna persona está exenta de cometer errores en el trabajo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This small company is exempt from paying taxes this year.", "tl": "Esta pequeña empresa está exenta de pagar impuestos este año."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Although the neighborhood is safe, no place is completely free from danger.", "tl": "Aunque el barrio es seguro, ningún lugar está completamente exento de peligro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Low-income families are exempt from this new municipal fee.", "tl": "Las familias con bajos ingresos están exentas de esta nueva tasa municipal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The government's new plan is not free from criticism by the opposition.", "tl": "El nuevo plan del gobierno no está exento de críticas por parte de la oposición."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Her new life in the countryside is free from the worries of the big city.", "tl": "Su nueva vida en el campo está exenta de las preocupaciones de la gran ciudad."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3285, "expression_id": 3311, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "el talón de Aquiles", "english_gloss": "Achilles' heel", "youtube_id": "b9oOjJWadhs", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Cybersecurity remains this company's Achilles' heel.", "tl": "La seguridad informática sigue siendo el talón de Aquiles de esta empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I speak English very well, but pronunciation is my Achilles' heel.", "tl": "Hablo muy bien inglés, pero la pronunciación es mi talón de Aquiles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Defense is the team's Achilles' heel this year; they always score goals against us at the end.", "tl": "La defensa es el talón de Aquiles del equipo este año; siempre nos meten goles al final."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Impatience is his Achilles' heel, and it often causes him problems at work.", "tl": "La impaciencia es su talón de Aquiles y a menudo le causa problemas en el trabajo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new phone is excellent, but its battery life is its Achilles' heel.", "tl": "El nuevo teléfono es excelente, pero la duración de la batería es su talón de Aquiles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Math has always been my Achilles' heel, which is why I prefer humanities.", "tl": "Las matemáticas siempre han sido mi talón de Aquiles, por eso prefiero las letras."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3284, "expression_id": 3310, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "a largo plazo", "english_gloss": "in the long term", "youtube_id": "b9oOjJWadhs", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Saving a little money every month is a good investment in the long term.", "tl": "Ahorrar un poco de dinero cada mes es una buena inversión a largo plazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Eating well and exercising has many health benefits in the long term.", "tl": "Comer bien y hacer ejercicio tiene muchos beneficios para la salud a largo plazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Learning a new language is a project that is worth it in the long term.", "tl": "Aprender un nuevo idioma es un proyecto que vale la pena a largo plazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The company needs a long-term strategy to survive in the market.", "tl": "La empresa necesita una estrategia a largo plazo para sobrevivir en el mercado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We must take measures now if we want to see positive results in the long term.", "tl": "Debemos tomar medidas ahora si queremos ver resultados positivos a largo plazo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I am not looking for a temporary job, but rather a stable position in the long term.", "tl": "No busco un trabajo temporal, sino un puesto estable a largo plazo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3283, "expression_id": 3309, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "a todas luces", "english_gloss": "clearly / by all accounts", "youtube_id": "b9oOjJWadhs", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "His proposal is, by all accounts, the best option for the company.", "tl": "Su propuesta es, a todas luces, la mejor opción para la empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It was clearly obvious that they did not get along.", "tl": "Era a todas luces evidente que ellos no se llevaban bien."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The result of the match was clearly unfair.", "tl": "El resultado del partido fue a todas luces injusto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Driving without a seatbelt is, by all accounts, reckless.", "tl": "Conducir sin el cinturón de seguridad es, a todas luces, una imprudencia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The project was clearly a success, thanks to everyone's effort.", "tl": "El proyecto fue un éxito a todas luces, gracias al esfuerzo de todos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "His explanation was clearly contradictory and nobody believed him.", "tl": "Su explicación era a todas luces contradictoria y nadie le creyó."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3282, "expression_id": 3308, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "ne vont faire que se multiplier", "english_gloss": "will do nothing but multiply", "youtube_id": "DyHvU64ntsE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With the development of artificial intelligence, these types of jobs will do nothing but multiply.", "tl": "Avec le développement de l'intelligence artificielle, ces types d'emplois ne vont faire que se multiplier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If we don't change our habits, natural disasters will do nothing but multiply.", "tl": "Si nous ne changeons pas nos habitudes, les catastrophes naturelles ne vont faire que se multiplier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In this fast-growing sector, career opportunities will do nothing but multiply.", "tl": "Dans ce secteur en pleine croissance, les opportunités de carrière ne vont faire que se multiplier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we don't fix this bug quickly, customer complaints will do nothing but multiply.", "tl": "Si on ne résout pas ce bug rapidement, les plaintes des clients ne vont faire que se multiplier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "With the aging of the population, healthcare needs will do nothing but multiply.", "tl": "Avec le vieillissement de la population, les besoins en soins de santé ne vont faire que se multiplier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Without better public transit, traffic jams in this city will do nothing but multiply.", "tl": "Sans de meilleurs transports en commun, les embouteillages dans cette ville ne vont faire que se multiplier."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3281, "expression_id": 3307, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "serais à leur place", "english_gloss": "to be in their shoes", "youtube_id": "DyHvU64ntsE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I wouldn't want to be in their shoes today with this bad news.", "tl": "Je ne serais pas à leur place aujourd'hui avec cette mauvaise nouvelle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you were in their shoes, would you sign this contract?", "tl": "Si tu étais à leur place, est-ce que tu signerais ce contrat ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In my opinion, if she were in their shoes, she would refuse to leave.", "tl": "À mon avis, elle serait à leur place, elle refuserait de partir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we were in their shoes, we would take a vacation right away.", "tl": "Nous serions à leur place, nous prendrions des vacances tout de suite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I wouldn't want to be in their shoes for this important presentation in front of the director.", "tl": "Je ne serais pas à leur place pour cette présentation importante devant le directeur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you were in their shoes, you would have probably reacted the same way.", "tl": "Vous seriez à leur place, vous auriez probablement réagi de la même manière."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3280, "expression_id": 3306, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "point de bascule", "english_gloss": "tipping point", "youtube_id": "DyHvU64ntsE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Scientists fear that we have already reached a tipping point for the climate.", "tl": "Les scientifiques craignent que nous ayons déjà atteint un point de bascule pour le climat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "His resignation was the tipping point that pushed him to start his own business.", "tl": "Sa démission a été le point de bascule qui l'a poussé à créer sa propre entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This presidential election could be the tipping point for the country's future.", "tl": "Cette élection présidentielle pourrait être le point de bascule pour l'avenir du pays."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The arrival of smartphones marked a tipping point in the way we communicate.", "tl": "L'arrivée des smartphones a marqué un point de bascule dans notre façon de communiquer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "After months of fatigue, this argument was the tipping point and I decided to stop everything.", "tl": "Après des mois de fatigue, cette dispute a été le point de bascule et j'ai décidé de tout arrêter."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When prices doubled, society reached a tipping point and the protests began.", "tl": "Quand les prix ont doublé, la société a atteint un point de bascule et les manifestations ont commencé."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3279, "expression_id": 3305, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "parti en fumée", "english_gloss": "to go up in smoke", "youtube_id": "DyHvU64ntsE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "All his efforts and his life savings went up in smoke because of the crisis.", "tl": "Tous ses efforts et ses économies de toute une vie sont partis en fumée à cause de la crise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our travel plans went up in smoke when the airline cancelled our flight.", "tl": "Notre projet de voyage est parti en fumée quand la compagnie aérienne a annulé notre vol."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I forgot to save my document, and my entire afternoon's work went up in smoke.", "tl": "J'ai oublié de sauvegarder mon document, et tout mon travail de l'après-midi est parti en fumée."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Their hopes of victory went up in smoke after the opposing team's first goal.", "tl": "Leurs espoirs de victoire sont partis en fumée après le premier but de l'équipe adverse."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Unfortunately, the old barn behind the house went up in smoke during the storm.", "tl": "Malheureusement, la vieille grange derrière la maison est partie en fumée pendant l'orage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you don't pay attention to your spending, your entire budget will go up in smoke before the end of the month.", "tl": "Si tu ne fais pas attention à tes dépenses, tout ton budget va partir en fumée avant la fin du mois."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3278, "expression_id": 3304, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dar um salto de qualidade", "english_gloss": "to make a leap in quality", "youtube_id": "rUK8H-vkE-4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new phone model made a big leap in quality compared to the previous one.", "tl": "O novo modelo de telemóvel deu um grande salto de qualidade em relação ao anterior."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After doing the intensive course, my English made a leap in quality.", "tl": "Depois de fazer o curso intensivo, o meu inglês deu um salto de qualidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we hire a professional designer, our website will make a leap in quality.", "tl": "Se contratarmos um designer profissional, o nosso site vai dar um salto de qualidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The team has made an incredible leap in quality since the new coach arrived.", "tl": "A equipa deu um salto de qualidade incrível desde que o novo treinador chegou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "With the change of ingredients, the food at this restaurant made a leap in quality.", "tl": "Com a mudança de ingredientes, a comida deste restaurante deu um salto de qualidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We need to make a leap in quality in our project if we want to get a good grade.", "tl": "Precisamos de dar um salto de qualidade no nosso projeto se queremos ter uma boa nota."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3277, "expression_id": 3303, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "afinal de contas", "english_gloss": "after all / at the end of the day", "youtube_id": "rUK8H-vkE-4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry; after all, everything is going to be fine.", "tl": "Não te preocupes; afinal de contas, tudo vai correr bem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I decided not to buy the new car; after all, mine still works well.", "tl": "Decidi não comprar o carro novo; afinal de contas, o meu ainda funciona bem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You should forgive your brother; after all, he is family.", "tl": "Deves perdoar o teu irmão; afinal de contas, ele é da tua família."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We worked hard, but at the end of the day, we couldn't finish the project on time.", "tl": "Trabalhámos muito, mas, afinal de contas, não conseguimos terminar o projeto a tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We are not going to cancel the trip; after all, it's only going to rain on Sunday.", "tl": "Não vamos cancelar a viagem; afinal de contas, só vai chover no domingo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He was right; after all, I didn't know the whole truth.", "tl": "Ele tinha razão; afinal de contas, eu não sabia toda a verdade."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3276, "expression_id": 3302, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "se apoderou", "english_gloss": "took over / seized control of", "youtube_id": "rUK8H-vkE-4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Panic took over the crowd when the alarm started to ring.", "tl": "O pânico se apoderou da multidão quando o alarme começou a tocar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new board of directors took over control of the company quickly.", "tl": "A nova diretoria se apoderou do controle da empresa de forma rápida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "A deep silence took over the room after the sad news.", "tl": "Um silêncio profundo se apoderou da sala após a triste notícia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The rebel group took over the local radio station to broadcast their message.", "tl": "O grupo rebelde se apoderou da rádio local para transmitir sua mensagem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "A great nostalgia took over him when looking at the old childhood photos.", "tl": "Uma grande nostalgia se apoderou dele ao rever as fotos antigas da infância."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Tiredness took over me and I fell asleep right after dinner.", "tl": "O cansaço se apoderou de mim e eu dormi logo depois do jantar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3275, "expression_id": 3301, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tretas", "english_gloss": "drama, beef, or trouble", "youtube_id": "rUK8H-vkE-4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I prefer to mind my own business and not get involved in drama at work.", "tl": "Eu prefiro ficar na minha e não me envolver em tretas no trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They are always arguing on the internet, it seems like they love drama.", "tl": "Eles estão sempre discutindo na internet, parece que adoram tretas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't care about their beef, I just want them to make up.", "tl": "Eu não quero saber das tretas deles, só quero que eles façam as pazes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Avoid that group of people, they only bring trouble and confusion.", "tl": "Evita aquele grupo de pessoas, eles só trazem tretas e confusão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Last Christmas, there was a big family drama over money.", "tl": "No Natal passado, houve uma grande treta na família por causa de dinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't look for trouble with me today, because I'm not in the mood.", "tl": "Não procures tretas comigo hoje, porque não estou com paciência."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3274, "expression_id": 3300, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "puxar o gancho", "english_gloss": "to build on a point / use as a hook", "youtube_id": "rUK8H-vkE-4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I want to build on what Maria said to present our new proposal.", "tl": "Quero puxar o gancho do que a Maria disse para apresentar a nossa nova proposta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I'm going to use your last sentence as a hook and ask about the future of the project.", "tl": "Vou puxar o gancho da sua última frase e perguntar sobre o futuro do projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Building on the previous topic, I think we should schedule another meeting.", "tl": "Puxando o gancho do assunto anterior, acho que devíamos marcar outra reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To build on his presentation, I would like to show this chart.", "tl": "Para puxar o gancho da apresentação dele, gostaria de mostrar este gráfico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She built on our conversation from yesterday and solved the problem quickly.", "tl": "Ela puxou o gancho da nossa conversa de ontem e resolveu o problema rapidamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We can use this idea as a hook to create a better marketing campaign.", "tl": "Podemos puxar o gancho dessa ideia para criar uma campanha de marketing melhor."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3273, "expression_id": 3299, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "tenere ben presente", "english_gloss": "to keep firmly in mind", "youtube_id": "h95mj39hSAk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We must keep the project deadline firmly in mind.", "tl": "Dobbiamo tenere ben presente la scadenza del progetto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When you travel abroad, keep firmly in mind that the rules can change.", "tl": "Quando viaggi all'estero, tieni ben presente che le regole possono cambiare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Students should keep the importance of grammar firmly in mind.", "tl": "Gli studenti dovrebbero tenere ben presente l'importanza della grammatica."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Keep firmly in mind that the oven must already be hot before putting the cake in.", "tl": "Tieni ben presente che il forno deve essere già caldo prima di infornare la torta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I kept your advice firmly in mind during the job interview.", "tl": "Ho tenuto ben presente i tuoi consigli durante il colloquio di lavoro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Before buying a new house, one must keep one's budget firmly in mind.", "tl": "Prima di comprare una casa nuova, bisogna tenere ben presente il proprio budget."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3272, "expression_id": 3298, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "si smarcano da", "english_gloss": "to distance oneself from", "youtube_id": "h95mj39hSAk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Many MPs are distancing themselves from the party leader's latest statements.", "tl": "Molti deputati si smarcano dalle ultime dichiarazioni del leader del partito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The young manager distanced himself from the company's old decisions to propose something new.", "tl": "Il giovane manager si è smarcato dalle vecchie decisioni dell'azienda per proporre qualcosa di nuovo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We distance ourselves from this way of working; we prefer to be more transparent.", "tl": "Noi ci smarchiamo da questo modo di lavorare, preferiamo essere più trasparenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "With this interview, the director distances himself from the criticisms of his latest film.", "tl": "Con questa intervista, il regista si smarca dalle critiche sul suo ultimo film."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The students immediately distanced themselves from the violent actions of the protest group.", "tl": "Gli studenti si sono subito smarcati dalle azioni violente del gruppo di protesta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I am distancing myself from this useless controversy and prefer to focus on my work.", "tl": "Io mi smarco da questa polemica inutile e preferisco concentrarmi sul mio lavoro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3271, "expression_id": 3297, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "va' a crederci", "english_gloss": "yeah, right / hard to believe", "youtube_id": "h95mj39hSAk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He promised he won't be late anymore, but yeah, right!", "tl": "Ha promesso che non farà più tardi, ma va' a crederci!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The forecast says it will be sunny tomorrow, but it's hard to believe with this crazy weather.", "tl": "Le previsioni dicono che domani ci sarà il sole, ma va' a crederci con questo tempo pazzo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That shop is offering a ninety percent discount... yeah, right, it's definitely a scam.", "tl": "Quel negozio offre uno sconto del novanta percento... va' a crederci, sarà sicuramente una truffa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Marco says he lost his phone and that's why he didn't reply, yeah, right!", "tl": "Marco dice che ha perso il telefono e per questo non ha risposto, va' a crederci!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "There's a rumor they are getting married soon, but it's hard to believe after everything that happened.", "tl": "Gira voce che si sposeranno presto, ma va' a crederci dopo tutto quello che è successo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Politicians always say they will solve all the problems in a few months, yeah, right!", "tl": "I politici dicono sempre che risolveranno tutti i problemi in pochi mesi, va' a crederci!"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3270, "expression_id": 3296, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "ha fatto leva", "english_gloss": "to leverage / exploit", "youtube_id": "h95mj39hSAk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The salesman leveraged the customer's sense of guilt to convince him to buy.", "tl": "Il venditore ha fatto leva sul senso di colpa del cliente per convincerlo a comprare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This advertising campaign leverages young people's desire for freedom.", "tl": "Questa campagna pubblicitaria fa leva sul desiderio di libertà dei giovani."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "During the interview, they leveraged their long experience in the sector.", "tl": "Durante il colloquio, hanno fatto leva sulla loro lunga esperienza nel settore."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They convinced him to work overtime by leveraging his fear of losing his job.", "tl": "Lo hanno convinto a fare gli straordinari facendo leva sulla sua paura di perdere il lavoro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The candidate will leverage the economic crisis to get more votes in the election.", "tl": "Il candidato farà leva sulla crisi economica per ottenere più voti alle elezioni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I had to use a screwdriver as leverage to open that old wooden box.", "tl": "Ho dovuto fare leva con un cacciavite per aprire quella vecchia scatola di legno."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3269, "expression_id": 3295, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "si è fatto notare", "english_gloss": "to get noticed / stand out", "youtube_id": "h95mj39hSAk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Marco stood out immediately during his first day of work because of his precision.", "tl": "Marco si è fatto notare subito durante il primo giorno di lavoro per la sua precisione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At university, Giulia got noticed thanks to her excellent presentations.", "tl": "All'università, Giulia si è fatta notare grazie alle sue ottime presentazioni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new players made themselves noticed from the very first minutes of the match.", "tl": "I nuovi giocatori si sono fatti notare fin dai primi minuti della partita."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He is a shy guy, but when he speaks he always stands out for his smart ideas.", "tl": "È un ragazzo timido, ma quando parla si fa sempre notare per le sue idee intelligenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She didn't want to attract attention, but with that red dress she got noticed by everyone.", "tl": "Non voleva attirare l'attenzione, ma con quel vestito rosso si è fatta notare da tutti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you want to get a promotion, you need to make yourself noticed more by the boss.", "tl": "Se vuoi ottenere una promozione, devi farti notare di più dal capo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3268, "expression_id": 3294, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fa sognare", "english_gloss": "to make someone dream / inspire hope", "youtube_id": "h95mj39hSAk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sardinia is a wonderful island that makes all tourists dream.", "tl": "La Sardegna è un'isola meravigliosa che fa sognare tutti i turisti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The writer's new novel makes millions of readers dream.", "tl": "Il nuovo romanzo dello scrittore fa sognare milioni di lettori."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That love song makes me dream every time I listen to it.", "tl": "Quella canzone d'amore mi fa sognare ogni volta che la ascolto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The idea of traveling in space makes many children dream.", "tl": "L'idea di viaggiare nello spazio fa sognare molti bambini."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That adventure movie has a soundtrack that makes you dream.", "tl": "Quel film d'avventura ha una colonna sonora che fa sognare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our team is playing so well that it makes the fans dream.", "tl": "La nostra squadra sta giocando così bene che fa sognare i tifosi."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3267, "expression_id": 3293, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "mis au point", "english_gloss": "to develop / to perfect", "youtube_id": "Z-gMP6OTb0o", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our team has developed a new application to help students.", "tl": "Notre équipe a mis au point une nouvelle application pour aider les étudiants."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The researchers have developed a more effective treatment for this disease.", "tl": "Les chercheurs ont mis au point un traitement plus efficace contre cette maladie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We need to develop a new action plan for this project.", "tl": "Nous devons mettre au point un nouveau plan d'action pour ce projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The chef has perfected an original recipe for the autumn menu.", "tl": "Le chef a mis au point une recette originale pour le menu d'automne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This school has developed a unique method for learning languages quickly.", "tl": "Cette école a mis au point une méthode unique pour apprendre les langues rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After several attempts, they finally finalized the security system.", "tl": "Après plusieurs essais, ils ont enfin mis au point le système de sécurité."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3266, "expression_id": 3292, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "baisse pas les bras", "english_gloss": "to give up / to throw in the towel", "youtube_id": "Z-gMP6OTb0o", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I know the exam was difficult, but don't give up now!", "tl": "Je sais que l'examen était difficile, mais baisse pas les bras maintenant !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Even if the project is rejected, we mustn't throw in the towel.", "tl": "Même si le projet est rejeté, il ne faut pas baisser les bras."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Why did you give up so quickly? You had every chance of succeeding.", "tl": "Pourquoi tu as baissé les bras si vite ? Tu avais toutes tes chances."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The situation is complicated, but don't give up, we are going to find a solution.", "tl": "La situation est compliquée, mais ne baissez pas les bras, nous allons trouver une solution."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They are a very brave person who never gives up in the face of an obstacle.", "tl": "C'est quelqu'un de très courageux qui ne baisse jamais les bras devant un obstacle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you give up at the first sign of difficulty, you will never make it.", "tl": "Si tu baisses les bras à la première difficulté, tu n'y arriveras jamais."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3265, "expression_id": 3291, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à l'égard de", "english_gloss": "with regard to / towards", "youtube_id": "Z-gMP6OTb0o", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He has always been very respectful towards his colleagues.", "tl": "Il a toujours été très respectueux à l'égard de ses collègues."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The population is quite skeptical with regard to the new economic measures.", "tl": "La population est assez sceptique à l'égard des nouvelles mesures économiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She feels great gratitude towards her parents.", "tl": "Elle ressent une grande gratitude à l'égard de ses parents."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The company must be more attentive towards its customers.", "tl": "L'entreprise doit se montrer plus attentive à l'égard de ses clients."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We must be fair towards everyone, without exception.", "tl": "Nous devons être justes à l'égard de tout le monde, sans exception."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Younger generations have a different attitude towards the environment.", "tl": "Les jeunes générations ont une attitude différente à l'égard de l'environnement."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3264, "expression_id": 3290, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "sans précédent", "english_gloss": "unprecedented", "youtube_id": "Z-gMP6OTb0o", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The region experienced an unprecedented heatwave this summer.", "tl": "La région a connu une canicule sans précédent cet été."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new video game achieved unprecedented success as soon as it was released.", "tl": "Le nouveau jeu vidéo a remporté un succès sans précédent dès sa sortie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Faced with this unprecedented crisis, the government must take rapid measures.", "tl": "Face à cette crise sans précédent, le gouvernement doit prendre des mesures rapides."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Scientists have made an unprecedented discovery in the field of medicine.", "tl": "Les scientifiques ont fait une découverte sans précédent dans le domaine de la médecine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Yesterday's protest gathered an unprecedented crowd in the streets of Paris.", "tl": "La manifestation d'hier a rassemblé une foule sans précédent dans les rues de Paris."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our company is going through a period of unprecedented growth thanks to our new partners.", "tl": "Notre entreprise traverse une période de croissance sans précédent grâce à nos nouveaux partenaires."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3263, "expression_id": 3289, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "a fait le même constat", "english_gloss": "to make the same observation", "youtube_id": "Z-gMP6OTb0o", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After analyzing the figures, the director made the same observation: we must reduce our expenses.", "tl": "Après avoir analysé les chiffres, le directeur a fait le même constat : nous devons réduire nos dépenses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Several doctors have made the same observation regarding the effects of sleep deprivation.", "tl": "Plusieurs médecins ont fait le même constat concernant les effets du manque de sommeil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "While walking around the neighborhood, we made the same observation: there are too many cars.", "tl": "En nous promenant dans le quartier, nous avons fait le même constat : il y a trop de voitures."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The French teacher made the same observation: students are reading less and less.", "tl": "La professeure de français a fait le même constat : les élèves lisent de moins en moins."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Technology experts made the same observation about smartphone use among young people.", "tl": "Les experts en technologie ont fait le même constat sur l'utilisation des smartphones chez les jeunes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I visited three apartments yesterday and I made the same observation: the rents are too expensive.", "tl": "J'ai visité trois appartements hier et j'ai fait le même constat : les loyers sont trop chers."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3262, "expression_id": 3288, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "a voce alta", "english_gloss": "out loud / publicly", "youtube_id": "nBJ0ltSFZBU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Can you read this email out loud? I can't find my glasses.", "tl": "Puoi leggere a voce alta questa email? Non riesco a trovare gli occhiali."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't be afraid to say what you think out loud.", "tl": "Non aver paura di dire quello che pensi a voce alta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You can't speak in a loud voice in the library, otherwise we will disturb the others.", "tl": "In biblioteca non si può parlare a voce alta, altrimenti disturbiamo gli altri."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Sorry, I was just thinking out loud, I didn't mean to interrupt you.", "tl": "Scusa, stavo solo pensando a voce alta, non volevo interromperti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Speak up, please, there is too much noise in here.", "tl": "Parla a voce alta, per favore, c'è troppo rumore qui dentro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "To memorize new vocabulary, I prefer to repeat it out loud.", "tl": "Per memorizzare i nuovi vocaboli, preferisco ripeterli a voce alta."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3261, "expression_id": 3287, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "spina nel fianco", "english_gloss": "thorn in one's side", "youtube_id": "nBJ0ltSFZBU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That lazy colleague has always been a thorn in the boss's side.", "tl": "Quel collega pigro è sempre stato una spina nel fianco per il capo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Mathematics has always been a thorn in my side since elementary school.", "tl": "La matematica è sempre stata la mia spina nel fianco fin dalle scuole elementari."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Bureaucracy is a real thorn in the side for those who want to open a new business.", "tl": "La burocrazia è una vera spina nel fianco per chi vuole aprire una nuova attività."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "That opposing team has always been a thorn in our side.", "tl": "Quella squadra avversaria è sempre stata una spina nel fianco per noi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This old computer has become a thorn in my side for my daily work.", "tl": "Questo vecchio computer è diventato una spina nel fianco per il mio lavoro quotidiano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The neighbors' dog, which barks all night, is a thorn in the side of the whole neighborhood.", "tl": "Il cane dei vicini, che abbaia tutta la notte, è una spina nel fianco per l'intero quartiere."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3260, "expression_id": 3286, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "andata... giù", "english_gloss": "gone down well", "youtube_id": "nBJ0ltSFZBU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That lie really didn't go down well with me.", "tl": "Quella bugia non mi è proprio andata giù."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Yesterday's defeat didn't go down well with the fans.", "tl": "La sconfitta di ieri non è andata giù ai tifosi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The news of his departure didn't go down well with anyone in the office.", "tl": "La notizia della sua partenza non è andata giù a nessuno in ufficio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "How did his answer go down with you?", "tl": "Come ti è andata giù la sua risposta?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That sarcastic joke didn't go down well with him at all.", "tl": "Quella battuta sarcastica non gli è andata giù per niente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I know the boss's decision didn't go down well with you, but we have to accept it.", "tl": "So che la decisione del capo non ti è andata giù, ma dobbiamo accettarla."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3259, "expression_id": 3285, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "messo nero su bianco", "english_gloss": "put in writing", "youtube_id": "nBJ0ltSFZBU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Before starting the work, I want the agreement to be put in writing.", "tl": "Prima di iniziare i lavori, voglio che l'accordo sia messo nero su bianco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I trust you, but I prefer to have your promises put down in black and white.", "tl": "Mi fido di te, ma preferisco avere le tue promesse messe nero su bianco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The boss accepted my proposal, but we still need to put it in writing.", "tl": "Il capo ha accettato la mia proposta, ma dobbiamo ancora metterla nero su bianco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Everything we said to each other verbally has now been put in writing in the contract.", "tl": "Tutto quello che ci siamo detti a voce ora è stato messo nero su bianco nel contratto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I have many ideas for the new project; tonight I will put them down in writing.", "tl": "Ho molte idee per il nuovo progetto, stasera le metterò nero su bianco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If we don't put the house rules in writing, we will end up arguing.", "tl": "Se non mettiamo nero su bianco le regole della casa, finiremo per litigare."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3258, "expression_id": 3284, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "fuga in avanti", "english_gloss": "unilateral leap forward", "youtube_id": "nBJ0ltSFZBU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The mayor's decision was a unilateral leap forward that angered the allies.", "tl": "La decisione del sindaco è stata una fuga in avanti che ha fatto arrabbiare gli alleati."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We shouldn't make any unilateral moves; we need to talk to the boss first.", "tl": "Non dobbiamo fare fughe in avanti; dobbiamo prima parlarne con il capo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Marco suggested buying a house together, but it seems like a premature leap to me since we've only been together for a m", "tl": "Marco ha proposto di comprare casa insieme, ma mi sembra una fuga in avanti visto che stiamo insieme da un mese."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The announcement of the new product was a preemptive move to beat the competition.", "tl": "L'annuncio del nuovo prodotto è stato una fuga in avanti per battere la concorrenza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In the group project, his unilateral action created a lot of confusion among his classmates.", "tl": "Nel lavoro di gruppo, la sua fuga in avanti ha creato molta confusione tra i compagni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Without a precise plan, any unilateral leap forward risks being a failure.", "tl": "Senza un piano preciso, qualsiasi fuga in avanti rischia di essere un fallimento."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3257, "expression_id": 3283, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "tallone d'Achille", "english_gloss": "Achilles' heel", "youtube_id": "nBJ0ltSFZBU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Math has always been my Achilles' heel at school.", "tl": "La matematica è sempre stata il mio tallone d'Achille a scuola."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The defense is the real Achilles' heel of this soccer team.", "tl": "La difesa è il vero tallone d'Achille di questa squadra di calcio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Public speaking is unfortunately my Achilles' heel.", "tl": "Parlare in pubblico è purtroppo il mio tallone d'Achille."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The lack of organization is the company's Achilles' heel.", "tl": "La mancanza di organizzazione è il tallone d'Achille dell'azienda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This smartphone is fantastic, but the battery is its Achilles' heel.", "tl": "Questo smartphone è fantastico, ma la batteria è il suo tallone d'Achille."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Laziness is Marco's Achilles' heel, otherwise he would be an excellent student.", "tl": "La pigrizia è il tallone d'Achille di Marco, altrimenti sarebbe un ottimo studente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3256, "expression_id": 3282, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "prendere ispirazione", "english_gloss": "to draw inspiration", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Many chefs draw inspiration from their grandmother's traditional recipes.", "tl": "Molti chef prendono ispirazione dalle ricette tradizionali della nonna."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To write his latest novel, the author drew inspiration from a trip to Japan.", "tl": "Per scrivere il suo ultimo romanzo, l'autore ha preso ispirazione da un viaggio in Giappone."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you don't know how to decorate the bedroom, you can draw inspiration from this design magazine.", "tl": "Se non sai come arredare la camera, puoi prendere ispirazione da questa rivista di design."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Where did you draw inspiration from for this beautiful drawing?", "tl": "Da dove hai preso ispirazione per questo bellissimo disegno?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I drew inspiration from an internet video to do this DIY project.", "tl": "Ho preso ispirazione da un video su internet per fare questo lavoretto di bricolage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We should draw inspiration from our competitors to improve customer service.", "tl": "Dovremmo prendere ispirazione dai nostri concorrenti per migliorare il servizio clienti."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3255, "expression_id": 3281, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "cadere l'illusione", "english_gloss": "to lose one's illusion / be disillusioned", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When I discovered the truth, I lost the illusion of having a perfect relationship.", "tl": "Quando ho scoperto la verità, mi è caduta l'illusione di avere una relazione perfetta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Over time, many young people lose their illusions about the working world.", "tl": "Con il tempo, a molti giovani cadono le illusioni sul mondo del lavoro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the government's latest decisions, the citizens lost any illusion of change.", "tl": "Dopo le ultime decisioni del governo, ai cittadini è caduta ogni illusione di cambiamento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you keep lying to us, we will lose even the last illusion we had about you.", "tl": "Se continui a mentirci, ci cadrà anche l'ultima illusione che avevamo su di te."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You've lost the illusion of being able to do everything on your own, haven't you?", "tl": "Ti è caduta l'illusione di poter fare tutto da solo, vero?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She lost her illusion about that singer after meeting him in person.", "tl": "Le è caduta l'illusione su quel cantante dopo averlo incontrato di persona."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3254, "expression_id": 3280, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "far passare il tempo", "english_gloss": "to pass the time / kill time", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I always read a book on the train to make the time pass faster.", "tl": "Leggo sempre un libro sul treno per far passare il tempo più velocemente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When we were young, we used to play cards to pass the time during rainy afternoons.", "tl": "Quando eravamo piccoli, giocavamo a carte per far passare il tempo durante i pomeriggi di pioggia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I downloaded a new game on my phone just to pass the time while I wait for the doctor.", "tl": "Ho scaricato un nuovo gioco sul telefono solo per far passare il tempo mentre aspetto il medico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I listen to podcasts while I clean the house, it helps me pass the time.", "tl": "Ascolto i podcast mentre pulisco la casa, mi aiuta a far passare il tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "There was nothing to do in the office today, so we chatted to pass the time.", "tl": "Non c'era niente da fare in ufficio oggi, quindi abbiamo chiacchierato per far passare il tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "During the long flight to New York, I watched three movies to pass the time.", "tl": "Durante il lungo volo per New York, ho guardato tre film per far passare il tempo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3253, "expression_id": 3279, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "ultima ruota del carro", "english_gloss": "the lowest of the low / fifth wheel", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "At work, nobody ever listens to me; I always feel like the lowest of the low.", "tl": "Al lavoro non mi ascolta mai nessuno; mi sento sempre l'ultima ruota del carro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They organized the whole vacation without asking me anything, as if I were a fifth wheel.", "tl": "Hanno organizzato tutta la vacanza senza chiedermi nulla, come se fossi l'ultima ruota del carro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Being the newest arrival at the company, I know very well that I'm at the bottom of the ladder for now.", "tl": "Essendo l'ultimo arrivato in azienda, so bene di essere l'ultima ruota del carro per adesso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't want to come to the party if you make me feel like a fifth wheel the whole time.", "tl": "Non voglio venire alla festa se mi fate sentire l'ultima ruota del carro tutto il tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In that project, the boss treated me like the lowest of the low, so I decided to leave.", "tl": "In quel progetto il capo mi trattava come l'ultima ruota del carro, quindi ho deciso di andarmene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "On the soccer team I never play; they just consider me the least important person.", "tl": "Nella squadra di calcio non gioco mai; mi considerano solo l'ultima ruota del carro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3252, "expression_id": 3278, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "limare le asperità", "english_gloss": "to smooth out the rough edges", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Before signing the contract, we need to smooth out the final rough edges of the project.", "tl": "Prima di firmare il contratto, dobbiamo limare le ultime asperità del progetto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At the beginning of living together we argued often, but over time we smoothed out the rough edges.", "tl": "All'inizio della nostra convivenza litigavamo spesso, ma con il tempo abbiamo limato le asperità."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The text of the presentation is good, but it still needs a bit of work to smooth out the rough edges.", "tl": "Il testo della presentazione è buono, ma serve ancora un po' di lavoro per limare le asperità."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we want this collaboration to work, we must be ready to smooth out the rough edges of our personalities.", "tl": "Se vogliamo che questa collaborazione funzioni, dobbiamo essere pronti a limare le asperità caratteriali."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Another meeting will be necessary to smooth out the rough edges between the two company departments.", "tl": "Un altro incontro sarà necessario per limare le asperità tra i due reparti dell'azienda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "With experience, one learns to smooth out the rough edges of one's character to live better with others.", "tl": "Con l'esperienza si impara a limare le asperità del proprio carattere per vivere meglio con gli altri."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3251, "expression_id": 3277, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "compagni di merende", "english_gloss": "partners in crime / close buddies", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Marco and Luca have always been partners in crime, ever since elementary school.", "tl": "Marco e Luca sono sempre stati compagni di merende, fin dai tempi della scuola elementare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Those two colleagues really seem like partners in crime; they spend hours whispering in the hallway.", "tl": "Quei due colleghi sembrano proprio due compagni di merende: passano ore a confabulare in corridoio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The dog and the cat have become partners in crime: one opens the pantry and the other steals the food.", "tl": "Il cane e il gatto sono diventati compagni di merende: uno apre la dispensa e l'altro ruba il cibo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you need help organizing the prank, Giulio and I will be your partners in crime.", "tl": "Se hai bisogno di aiuto per organizzare lo scherzo, io e Giulio saremo i tuoi compagni di merende."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't trust those two; they always act like partners in crime who are hiding something.", "tl": "Non mi fido di quei due; si comportano sempre come compagni di merende che nascondono qualcosa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Do you remember when we were partners in crime and used to run away from home to go play at the river?", "tl": "Ricordi quando eravamo compagni di merende e scappavamo di casa per andare a giocare al fiume?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 3250, "expression_id": 3276, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "portarsi dietro", "english_gloss": "to carry with oneself / to bring along", "youtube_id": "-3uG9H_PTXQ", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When I go out, I always bring a book along to read on the subway.", "tl": "Quando esco, mi porto sempre dietro un libro da leggere in metropolitana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You should bring an umbrella with you, because the sky is very cloudy.", "tl": "Dovresti portarti dietro l'ombrello, perché il cielo è molto nuvoloso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "For the weekend in the mountains, Marco brought along too many heavy clothes.", "tl": "Per il weekend in montagna, Marco si è portato dietro troppi vestiti pesanti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For the trip to the lake, are we bringing something to eat with us or are we buying everything there?", "tl": "Per la gita al lago, ci portiamo dietro qualcosa da mangiare o compriamo tutto lì?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you go to the park, you should bring a blanket along to sit on the grass.", "tl": "Se andate al parco, vi conviene portarvi dietro una coperta per sedervi sull'erba."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "During their honeymoon, they also brought their dog along with them.", "tl": "Durante il viaggio di nozze, si sono portati dietro anche il loro cane."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3249, "expression_id": 3275, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "springen auf... an", "english_gloss": "react to / bite on", "youtube_id": "RMv494zkvPE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Why do you always react immediately to his provocations?", "tl": "Warum springst du immer sofort auf seine Provokationen an?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Customers are responding very well to our new advertising campaign.", "tl": "Die Kunden springen sehr gut auf unsere neue Werbekampagne an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I suggested a compromise to him, but he didn't bite.", "tl": "Ich habe ihm einen Kompromiss vorgeschlagen, aber er ist nicht darauf angesprungen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our cat doesn't react to the new food at all.", "tl": "Unsere Katze springt überhaupt nicht auf das neue Futter an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you offer him money, he usually bites immediately.", "tl": "Wenn man ihm Geld anbietet, springt er normalerweise sofort darauf an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I was surprised how quickly the children took to the new game idea.", "tl": "Ich war überrascht, wie schnell die Kinder auf die neue Spielidee angesprungen sind."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3248, "expression_id": 3274, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "keinen Cent zahlen", "english_gloss": "not pay a single cent", "youtube_id": "RMv494zkvPE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I was not satisfied with the service at all, so I will not pay a single cent.", "tl": "Ich war mit dem Service überhaupt nicht zufrieden, deshalb werde ich keinen Cent zahlen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He didn't want to pay a single cent for this broken washing machine.", "tl": "Für diese kaputte Waschmaschine wollte er keinen Cent zahlen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If the app is not free, I wouldn't pay a single cent for it.", "tl": "Wenn die App nicht kostenlos ist, würde ich keinen Cent dafür zahlen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My brother didn't pay a single cent for the concert because he won the tickets.", "tl": "Mein Bruder hat für das Konzert keinen Cent gezahlt, weil er die Tickets gewonnen hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We don't have to pay a single cent for the repair since we still have a warranty.", "tl": "Wir müssen für die Reparatur keinen Cent zahlen, da wir noch Garantie haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You shouldn't pay a single cent for this advice; it was completely useless.", "tl": "Du solltest für diese Beratung keinen Cent zahlen, sie war völlig nutzlos."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3247, "expression_id": 3273, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "gerechnet hätten", "english_gloss": "would have expected", "youtube_id": "RMv494zkvPE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We won the project, which to be honest we wouldn't have expected.", "tl": "Wir haben das Projekt gewonnen, womit wir ehrlich gesagt nicht gerechnet hätten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They probably wouldn't have expected such a heavy thunderstorm in August.", "tl": "Mit so einem heftigen Gewitter im August hätten sie wohl nicht gerechnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Would you have expected such a quick reply from the authority?", "tl": "Hätten Sie mit einer so schnellen Antwort von der Behörde gerechnet?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "So many people came to our party; we would never have expected this big rush.", "tl": "Es kamen so viele Leute zu unserem Fest; mit diesem großen Ansturm hätten wir nie gerechnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The renovation was expensive, but they really wouldn't have expected such high costs.", "tl": "Die Renovierung war teuer, aber mit so hohen Kosten hätten sie wirklich nicht gerechnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We thought the highway would be clear; we wouldn't have expected so much traffic on Sunday.", "tl": "Wir dachten, die Autobahn wäre frei; mit so viel Stau hätten wir am Sonntag nicht gerechnet."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3246, "expression_id": 3272, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Halten wir fest", "english_gloss": "let's state / establish", "youtube_id": "RMv494zkvPE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Let's establish that we will meet next Tuesday at 10 a.m.", "tl": "Halten wir fest, dass wir uns am nächsten Dienstag um 10 Uhr treffen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Let's state one thing: despite the minor problems, the project was a great success.", "tl": "Halten wir fest: Trotz der kleinen Probleme war das Projekt ein großer Erfolg."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "First, let's establish who is responsible for which task.", "tl": "Zuerst halten wir fest, wer für welche Aufgabe verantwortlich ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "So, let's establish that we need more time for preparation.", "tl": "Halten wir also fest, dass wir noch mehr Zeit für die Vorbereitung brauchen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Let's state for the record that all participants were present.", "tl": "Halten wir für das Protokoll fest, dass alle Teilnehmer anwesend waren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Let's quickly write down who is going shopping this weekend.", "tl": "Halten wir schnell fest, wer am Wochenende einkaufen geht."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3245, "expression_id": 3271, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Spuren gefolgt", "english_gloss": "followed leads / trails", "youtube_id": "RMv494zkvPE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The police followed several new leads but have not yet arrested a suspect.", "tl": "Die Polizei ist mehreren neuen Spuren gefolgt, hat aber noch keinen Verdächtigen festgenommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We followed the tracks in the snow and finally found a small cabin in the forest.", "tl": "Wir sind den Spuren im Schnee gefolgt und haben schließlich eine kleine Hütte im Wald gefunden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The detective followed the money trail to uncover the fraud.", "tl": "Der Detektiv ist den Spuren des Geldes gefolgt, um den Betrug aufzudecken."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I followed my cat's tracks and found her in the neighbor's garden.", "tl": "Ich bin den Spuren meiner Katze gefolgt und habe sie im Garten des Nachbarn gefunden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The archaeologists followed the traces of the ancient civilization.", "tl": "Die Archäologen sind den Spuren der alten Zivilisation gefolgt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The journalist followed the leads of the scandal and wrote an interesting article.", "tl": "Die Journalistin ist den Spuren des Skandals gefolgt und hat einen interessanten Artikel geschrieben."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3244, "expression_id": 3270, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend", "english_gloss": "sounds plausible at first", "youtube_id": "KYJIZDC8ZLU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As a plan, that admittedly sounds plausible at first, but we simply don't have enough money for it.", "tl": "Als Plan klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend, aber wir haben einfach nicht genug Geld dafür."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To laypeople, that sounds plausible at first, but scientists see it quite differently.", "tl": "Für Laien klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend, aber Wissenschaftler sehen das ganz anders."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In theory, that sounds plausible at first, but in practice, it often doesn't work.", "tl": "In der Theorie klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend, aber in der Praxis funktioniert es oft nicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Without prior knowledge, that admittedly sounds plausible at first, but reality is much more complicated.", "tl": "Ohne Vorkenntnisse klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend, aber die Realität ist viel komplizierter."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "As an argument, that sounds plausible at first, but it still doesn't entirely convince me.", "tl": "Als Argument klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend, aber es überzeugt mich trotzdem nicht ganz."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "To the customer, that sounds plausible at first, but technically it is hardly feasible.", "tl": "Für den Kunden klingt das zwar erst mal einleuchtend, aber technisch ist das kaum machbar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3243, "expression_id": 3269, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf dem Radar", "english_gloss": "on the radar / under observation", "youtube_id": "KYJIZDC8ZLU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We need to keep this new project on our radar so we don't miss the deadline.", "tl": "Wir müssen dieses neue Projekt auf dem Radar behalten, damit wir die Frist nicht verpassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The young player has been on the radar of the big clubs for months.", "tl": "Der junge Spieler steht schon seit Monaten auf dem Radar der großen Vereine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Artificial intelligence is a topic that every company should have on its radar now.", "tl": "Künstliche Intelligenz ist ein Thema, das jetzt jedes Unternehmen auf dem Radar haben sollte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Sorry, I didn't have this appointment on my radar at all.", "tl": "Entschuldigung, diesen Termin hatte ich überhaupt nicht auf dem Radar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The police had had the suspect on their radar for a long time.", "tl": "Die Polizei hatte den Verdächtigen schon lange auf dem Radar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Iceland has been on my radar for a long time for the next vacation.", "tl": "Island steht schon lange auf meinem Radar für den nächsten Urlaub."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3242, "expression_id": 3268, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf dem Tisch", "english_gloss": "on the table / up for discussion", "youtube_id": "KYJIZDC8ZLU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Your glasses are on the table next to the coffee cup.", "tl": "Deine Brille liegt auf dem Tisch neben der Kaffeetasse."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The other company's offer is already on the table.", "tl": "Das Angebot der anderen Firma liegt bereits auf dem Tisch."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Just leave the documents on the table, I will read them later.", "tl": "Lass die Dokumente einfach auf dem Tisch liegen, ich lese sie später."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We need to find a solution because the problem is now on the table.", "tl": "Wir müssen eine Lösung finden, denn das Problem liegt jetzt auf dem Tisch."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Dinner is already on the table, please come here!", "tl": "Das Abendessen steht schon auf dem Tisch, komm bitte her!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "There are various proposals that are currently on the table.", "tl": "Es gibt verschiedene Vorschläge, die aktuell auf dem Tisch liegen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3241, "expression_id": 3267, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf freien Fuß gesetzt", "english_gloss": "to release / set free", "youtube_id": "KYJIZDC8ZLU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After being questioned by the police, the suspect was released again.", "tl": "Nach der Befragung durch die Polizei wurde der Verdächtige wieder auf freien Fuß gesetzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The judge decided to release the accused due to a lack of evidence.", "tl": "Der Richter entschied, den Angeklagten mangels Beweisen auf freien Fuß zu setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The protesters were all released the next morning.", "tl": "Die Demonstranten wurden am nächsten Morgen alle wieder auf freien Fuß gesetzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The police released the innocent man after a few hours.", "tl": "Die Polizei hat den unschuldigen Mann nach wenigen Stunden auf freien Fuß gesetzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When will the prisoner finally be released?", "tl": "Wann wird der Gefangene endlich auf freien Fuß gesetzt?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If he pays the bail, he will be released immediately.", "tl": "Wenn er die Kaution bezahlt, wird er sofort auf freien Fuß gesetzt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3240, "expression_id": 3266, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "uns durch die Finger gleiten lassen", "english_gloss": "to let slip through our fingers", "youtube_id": "KYJIZDC8ZLU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We must not let this unique opportunity slip through our fingers.", "tl": "Wir dürfen uns diese einmalige Chance nicht durch die Finger gleiten lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I simply let this great job offer slip through my fingers.", "tl": "Ich habe mir dieses tolle Jobangebot einfach durch die Finger gleiten lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In the end, they still let the victory slip through their fingers.", "tl": "Am Ende haben sie sich den Sieg noch durch die Finger gleiten lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We let all the money slip through our fingers without noticing it.", "tl": "Wir haben uns das ganze Geld durch die Finger gleiten lassen, ohne es zu merken."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She is a great woman, you shouldn't let her slip through your fingers.", "tl": "Sie ist eine tolle Frau, du solltest sie dir nicht durch die Finger gleiten lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He let his dream apartment slip through his fingers because he waited too long.", "tl": "Er hat sich die Traumwohnung durch die Finger gleiten lassen, weil er zu lange gewartet hat."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3239, "expression_id": 3265, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern", "english_gloss": "ill-fated / off to a bad start", "youtube_id": "lwmEB6fgFrg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our new project has been off to a really bad start from the very beginning.", "tl": "Unser neues Projekt steht von Anfang an unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Unfortunately, their marriage was ill-fated and only lasted for a year.", "tl": "Ihre Ehe stand leider unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern und hielt nur ein Jahr."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This vacation was off to a really bad start; first the storm and then the theft.", "tl": "Dieser Urlaub stand unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern; zuerst der Sturm und dann der Diebstahl."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The planned garden party was ill-fated because it rained the whole day.", "tl": "Die geplante Gartenparty stand unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern, weil es den ganzen Tag regnete."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My first day at work was off to a really bad start because I had forgotten my keys.", "tl": "Mein erster Arbeitstag stand unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern, da ich meinen Schlüssel vergessen hatte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The soccer match was off to a really bad start when our best player got injured.", "tl": "Das Fußballspiel stand unter einem wirklich schlechten Stern, als sich unser bester Spieler verletzte."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3238, "expression_id": 3264, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die Luft wird dünn", "english_gloss": "the air gets thin / things get critical", "youtube_id": "lwmEB6fgFrg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If sales figures continue to fall, things will slowly get critical for the boss.", "tl": "Wenn die Verkaufszahlen weiter sinken, wird die Luft für den Chef langsam dünn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After the third defeat in a row, things are getting extremely tight for the team's coach.", "tl": "Nach der dritten Niederlage in Folge wird die Luft für den Trainer der Mannschaft extrem dünn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You didn't do your homework again? Things are starting to get really tight for you now!", "tl": "Du hast die Hausaufgaben schon wieder nicht gemacht? Jetzt wird die Luft aber langsam dünn für dich!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Without a part-time job, things get pretty tight financially at the end of the month.", "tl": "Ohne einen Nebenjob wird die Luft am Ende des Monats finanziell ziemlich dünn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The police have found new evidence, and things are getting critical for the suspect now.", "tl": "Die Polizei hat neue Beweise gefunden, und für den Verdächtigen wird die Luft jetzt dünn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "There are only two days left until the exam and I've barely studied – things are getting tight.", "tl": "Bis zur Prüfung sind es nur noch zwei Tage und ich habe kaum gelernt – da wird die Luft dünn."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3237, "expression_id": 3263, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in die Hose gehen", "english_gloss": "to go wrong / to fail", "youtube_id": "lwmEB6fgFrg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The plan went completely wrong.", "tl": "Der Plan ist völlig in die Hose gegangen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I hope the exam tomorrow doesn't go wrong.", "tl": "Ich hoffe, dass die Prüfung morgen nicht in die Hose geht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Without good preparation, the whole project will go wrong.", "tl": "Ohne gute Vorbereitung wird das ganze Projekt in die Hose gehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our vacation went completely wrong because of the weather.", "tl": "Unser Urlaub ist wegen des Wetters total in die Hose gegangen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Be careful, otherwise the surprise will end up going wrong!", "tl": "Sei vorsichtig, sonst geht die Überraschung am Ende noch in die Hose!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The presentation went wrong because the laptop didn't work.", "tl": "Die Präsentation ist in die Hose gegangen, weil der Laptop nicht funktionierte."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3236, "expression_id": 3262, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die Gunst der Stunde", "english_gloss": "the favorable opportunity", "youtube_id": "lwmEB6fgFrg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Since my boss was in a good mood today, I seized the opportunity and asked for a raise.", "tl": "Da mein Chef heute gute Laune hatte, nutzte ich die Gunst der Stunde und fragte nach einer Gehaltserhöhung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The weather was finally dry in the afternoon, so we took advantage of the moment to go for a walk.", "tl": "Das Wetter war am Nachmittag endlich trocken, also nutzten wir die Gunst der Stunde für einen Spaziergang."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The shoes were reduced by fifty percent, and I seized the opportunity to buy them immediately.", "tl": "Die Schuhe waren um fünfzig Prozent reduziert, und ich habe die Gunst der Stunde genutzt, um sie sofort zu kaufen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Because the teacher briefly left the room, the students took advantage of the moment to copy the homework.", "tl": "Weil die Lehrerin kurz den Raum verließ, nutzten die Schüler die Gunst der Stunde, um die Hausaufgaben abzuschreiben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "There was hardly any traffic on the highway this morning, and we seized the opportunity to reach our destination quickly", "tl": "Es gab heute Morgen kaum Stau auf der Autobahn, und wir nutzten die Gunst der Stunde, um schnell ans Ziel zu kommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When all the other guests were briefly in the kitchen, he seized the opportunity to speak with her alone.", "tl": "Als alle anderen Gäste kurz in der Küche waren, nutzte er die Gunst der Stunde, um allein mit ihr zu sprechen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3235, "expression_id": 3261, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "für ein Appl und ein Ei", "english_gloss": "for a song / dirt cheap", "youtube_id": "lwmEB6fgFrg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I got this used bicycle at the flea market for a song.", "tl": "Ich habe dieses gebrauchte Fahrrad auf dem Flohmarkt für ein Appl und ein Ei bekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He sold his old sofa on the internet for next to nothing because he had to move quickly.", "tl": "Er hat sein altes Sofa im Internet für ein Appl und ein Ei verkauft, weil er schnell umziehen musste."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Last year you could still book flights to Mallorca for dirt cheap.", "tl": "Letztes Jahr konnte man Flüge nach Mallorca noch für ein Appl und ein Ei buchen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I snagged this beautiful jacket in the sale for a song.", "tl": "Diese schöne Jacke habe ich im Ausverkauf für ein Appl und ein Ei ergattert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I am not going to sacrifice my free time for peanuts.", "tl": "Ich werde meine Freizeit nicht für ein Appl und ein Ei opfern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They bought the old house in the country for next to nothing and are now renovating it themselves.", "tl": "Sie haben das alte Haus auf dem Land für ein Appl und ein Ei gekauft und renovieren es jetzt selbst."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3234, "expression_id": 3260, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "das Zeitliche gesegnet", "english_gloss": "passed away / kicked the bucket", "youtube_id": "lwmEB6fgFrg", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My grandfather peacefully passed away yesterday after a long life.", "tl": "Mein Großvater hat gestern nach einem langen Leben friedlich das Zeitliche gesegnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My old car finally kicked the bucket on the highway.", "tl": "Mein altes Auto hat auf der Autobahn endgültig das Zeitliche gesegnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our beloved dog passed away last week at the age of fifteen.", "tl": "Unser geliebter Hund hat letzte Woche im Alter von fünfzehn Jahren das Zeitliche gesegnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Have you heard? The old neighbor from the third floor has passed away.", "tl": "Hast du schon gehört? Der alte Nachbar aus dem dritten Stock hat das Zeitliche gesegnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Unfortunately, my washing machine kicked the bucket right in the middle of the wash cycle.", "tl": "Mitten im Waschgang hat meine Waschmaschine leider das Zeitliche gesegnet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The famous writer passed away yesterday at the age of ninety.", "tl": "Der berühmte Schriftsteller hat gestern im Alter von neunzig Jahren das Zeitliche gesegnet."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3233, "expression_id": 3259, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "pour répondre à l'urgence", "english_gloss": "to respond to the emergency", "youtube_id": "OjY6KP5OTSA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government has released exceptional funds to respond to the emergency in hospitals.", "tl": "Le gouvernement a débloqué des fonds exceptionnels pour répondre à l'urgence dans les hôpitaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We must change our consumption habits to address the climate emergency.", "tl": "Nous devons changer nos habitudes de consommation pour répondre à l'urgence climatique."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Temporary shelters were set up to respond to the urgency of the situation.", "tl": "Des abris temporaires ont été installés pour répondre à l'urgence de la situation."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The team worked all night to address the emergency reported by the client.", "tl": "L'équipe a travaillé toute la nuit pour répondre à l'urgence signalée par le client."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Associations are mobilizing on the ground to respond to the humanitarian emergency.", "tl": "Les associations se mobilisent sur le terrain pour répondre à l'urgence humanitaire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The principal took immediate measures to respond to the health emergency in the school.", "tl": "Le directeur a pris des mesures immédiates pour répondre à l'urgence sanitaire dans l'école."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3232, "expression_id": 3258, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "fait état de", "english_gloss": "reports / documents / shows", "youtube_id": "OjY6KP5OTSA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The latest police report reports several minor injuries.", "tl": "Le dernier rapport de police fait état de plusieurs blessés légers."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The director reports a drop in sales this quarter.", "tl": "Le directeur fait état d'une baisse des ventes ce trimestre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The scientific study shows very encouraging results for the future.", "tl": "L'étude scientifique fait état de résultats très encourageants pour l'avenir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Local newspapers report tensions between the residents and the city hall.", "tl": "Les journaux locaux font état de tensions entre les habitants et la mairie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the meeting, she expressed her concerns about the project.", "tl": "Lors de la réunion, elle a fait état de ses inquiétudes concernant le projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The annual report documents a clear improvement in the situation.", "tl": "Le rapport annuel fait état d'une nette amélioration de la situation."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3231, "expression_id": 3257, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "fait face à", "english_gloss": "is facing / is dealing with", "youtube_id": "OjY6KP5OTSA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our company is facing serious financial difficulties this year.", "tl": "Notre entreprise fait face à de graves difficultés financières cette année."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Coastal countries are facing rising sea levels.", "tl": "Les pays côtiers font face à la montée du niveau de la mer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She is facing her fears and has decided to speak in public.", "tl": "Elle fait face à ses peurs et a décidé de parler en public."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We are facing a very complex problem that we need to solve quickly.", "tl": "Nous faisons face à un problème très complexe que nous devons résoudre rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The government is facing a lot of criticism regarding its new law.", "tl": "Le gouvernement fait face à de nombreuses critiques concernant sa nouvelle loi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You are facing a difficult choice, but I know you will make the right decision.", "tl": "Tu fais face à un choix difficile, mais je sais que tu prendras la bonne décision."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3230, "expression_id": 3256, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en lui-même", "english_gloss": "in and of itself / itself", "youtube_id": "OjY6KP5OTSA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The project itself is not difficult, it's just that we are short on time.", "tl": "Le projet en lui-même n'est pas difficile, c'est juste qu'on manque de temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The idea in and of itself is good, but its implementation is going to cause problems.", "tl": "L'idée en elle-même est bonne, mais sa réalisation va poser problème."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This job isn't very well paid, but the position itself is very interesting.", "tl": "Ce travail n'est pas très bien payé, mais le poste en lui-même est très intéressant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The trip itself was very long, but we loved the destination.", "tl": "Le voyage en lui-même a été très long, mais nous avons adoré la destination."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The decision itself was not easy for the director to make.", "tl": "La décision en elle-même n'a pas été facile à prendre pour le directeur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The problem itself is simple, but its consequences are serious.", "tl": "Le problème en lui-même est simple, mais ses conséquences sont graves."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3229, "expression_id": 3255, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tenez-vous bien", "english_gloss": "believe it or not / brace yourselves", "youtube_id": "OjY6KP5OTSA", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "And believe it or not, he won first prize without even practicing!", "tl": "Et tenez-vous bien, il a gagné le premier prix sans même s'entraîner !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They decided to sell everything to travel the world, and brace yourselves, they leave tomorrow!", "tl": "Ils ont décidé de tout vendre pour faire le tour du monde, et tenez-vous bien, ils partent demain !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our new director is actually the secretary's cousin, believe it or not!", "tl": "Notre nouveau directeur est en fait le cousin de la secrétaire, tenez-vous bien !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After ten years of medical school, believe it or not, she decided to become a baker.", "tl": "Après dix ans d'études en médecine, tenez-vous bien, elle a décidé de devenir boulangère."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This tiny apartment costs, brace yourselves, more than a million euros.", "tl": "Cet appartement minuscule coûte, tenez-vous bien, plus d'un million d'euros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It hasn't rained here for six months and, believe it or not, they are forecasting snow for this weekend.", "tl": "Il n'a pas plu ici depuis six mois et, tenez-vous bien, ils annoncent de la neige pour ce week-end."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3228, "expression_id": 3254, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "por el camino", "english_gloss": "along the way", "youtube_id": "wD8XLR8RxzE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We were heading to the beach and stopped to eat in a town along the way.", "tl": "Íbamos hacia la playa y nos paramos a comer en un pueblo por el camino."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I had the keys in my pocket, but I think I dropped them along the way.", "tl": "Tenía las llaves en el bolsillo, pero creo que se me cayeron por el camino."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "During the backpacking trip, we learned many things along the way.", "tl": "Durante el viaje de mochileros, aprendimos muchas cosas por el camino."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I was going to your house and I ran into Juan along the way.", "tl": "Iba a tu casa y me encontré con Juan por el camino."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The train ride is long, but there are very beautiful landscapes along the way.", "tl": "El viaje en tren es largo, pero hay paisajes muy bonitos por el camino."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't worry about the details now, we can decide it along the way.", "tl": "No te preocupes por los detalles ahora, podemos decidirlo por el camino."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3227, "expression_id": 3253, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "a disposición de", "english_gloss": "at the disposal of", "youtube_id": "wD8XLR8RxzE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The company director made himself available to the new employees to answer their questions.", "tl": "El director de la empresa se puso a disposición de los nuevos empleados para resolver sus dudas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "All hotel services are at the guests' disposal during their stay.", "tl": "Todos los servicios del hotel están a disposición de los huéspedes durante su estancia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We have made a large number of resources available to the students on the website.", "tl": "Hemos puesto una gran cantidad de recursos a disposición de los estudiantes en la página web."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you need help with the move, my car is entirely at your disposal.", "tl": "Si necesitas ayuda con la mudanza, mi coche está a tu entera disposición."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The city council has made a free bus available to elderly citizens.", "tl": "El ayuntamiento ha puesto un autobús gratuito a disposición de los ciudadanos mayores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The project documents are now available to all team members.", "tl": "Los documentos del proyecto ya están a disposición de todos los miembros del equipo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3226, "expression_id": 3252, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "en el medio de", "english_gloss": "in the midst of", "youtube_id": "wD8XLR8RxzE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We ran out of gas in the middle of nowhere.", "tl": "Nos quedamos sin gasolina en el medio de la nada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She called me on the phone in the middle of an important meeting.", "tl": "Ella me llamó por teléfono en el medio de una reunión importante."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The boat found itself trapped in the midst of a terrible storm.", "tl": "El barco se encontró atrapado en el medio de una tormenta terrible."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't want to be in the middle of their family problems.", "tl": "No quiero estar en el medio de sus problemas familiares."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They built a beautiful park in the middle of the historic center.", "tl": "Construyeron un parque hermoso en el medio del centro histórico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I forgot what I was going to say in the middle of my presentation.", "tl": "Se me olvidó lo que iba a decir en el medio de mi presentación."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3225, "expression_id": 3251, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "ir paso a paso", "english_gloss": "to go step by step", "youtube_id": "wD8XLR8RxzE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To learn a language, it is better to go step by step and not try to memorize everything in one day.", "tl": "Para aprender un idioma, es mejor ir paso a paso y no intentar memorizar todo en un día."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't worry about the future, now you have to go step by step with your recovery.", "tl": "No te preocupes por el futuro, ahora tienes que ir paso a paso con tu recuperación."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When we started the business, we decided to go step by step to avoid making serious mistakes.", "tl": "Cuando empezamos el negocio, decidimos ir paso a paso para no cometer errores graves."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is important that we go step by step in this project so that everything turns out well.", "tl": "Es importante que vayamos paso a paso en este proyecto para que todo salga bien."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We are going step by step with the move so we don't get too stressed.", "tl": "Estamos yendo paso a paso con la mudanza para no estresarnos demasiado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you want to solve this math problem, you must go step by step.", "tl": "Si quieres resolver este problema matemático, debes ir paso a paso."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3224, "expression_id": 3250, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "dado de alta", "english_gloss": "registered / enrolled", "youtube_id": "NU4gt3958kk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "They have already registered me on the university platform, so I can see my courses.", "tl": "Ya me han dado de alta en la plataforma de la universidad, así que puedo ver mis cursos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To be able to use the gym pool, you first have to be registered as a member.", "tl": "Para poder usar la piscina del gimnasio, primero tienes que estar dado de alta como socio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Are you already registered with social security to start working tomorrow?", "tl": "¿Ya estás dado de alta en la seguridad social para empezar a trabajar mañana?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The water and electricity are already activated in the new apartment.", "tl": "El agua y la luz ya están dadas de alta en el nuevo apartamento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you don't want to receive any more emails, you can check if you are still signed up for the newsletter.", "tl": "Si no quieres recibir más correos, puedes comprobar si sigues dado de alta en el boletín."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Once you have been registered in the system, you will receive a confirmation email.", "tl": "Una vez que hayas sido dado de alta en el sistema, recibirás un correo de confirmación."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3223, "expression_id": 3249, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "recién salida del horno", "english_gloss": "fresh out of the oven", "youtube_id": "NU4gt3958kk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Be careful when eating the bread, it is fresh out of the oven and you could burn yourself.", "tl": "Ten cuidado al comer el pan, que está recién salido del horno y te puedes quemar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Here is the latest edition of the magazine, fresh out of the oven.", "tl": "Aquí tienes la última edición de la revista, recién salida del horno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In this bakery, they always have cakes fresh out of the oven.", "tl": "En esta pastelería siempre tienen tartas recién salidas del horno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We have just published the new product catalog; it is fresh out of the oven.", "tl": "Acabamos de publicar el nuevo catálogo de productos, está recién salido del horno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Pizza fresh out of the oven is much tastier than reheated pizza.", "tl": "La pizza recién salida del horno es mucho más rica que la recalentada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I have a proposal fresh out of the oven that you are going to love for the project.", "tl": "Tengo una propuesta recién salida del horno que te va a encantar para el proyecto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3222, "expression_id": 3248, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "haciendo historia", "english_gloss": "making history", "youtube_id": "NU4gt3958kk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our neighborhood's soccer team is making history by reaching the final.", "tl": "El equipo de fútbol de nuestro barrio está haciendo historia al llegar a la final."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She always dreamed of making history in the field of medicine.", "tl": "Ella siempre soñó con hacer historia en el campo de la medicina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The astronauts who reached the Moon made history for all of humanity.", "tl": "Los astronautas que llegaron a la Luna hicieron historia para toda la humanidad."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This young singer makes history by being the first to win three awards in the same night.", "tl": "Esta joven cantante hace historia al ser la primera en ganar tres premios en la misma noche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If we pass this environmental protection law, we will be making history.", "tl": "Si aprobamos esta ley de protección ambiental, estaremos haciendo historia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our company has made history by creating the region's first fully eco-friendly car.", "tl": "Nuestra empresa ha hecho historia al crear el primer coche totalmente ecológico de la región."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3221, "expression_id": 3247, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "por ninguna vía", "english_gloss": "by no means / through no channel", "youtube_id": "NU4gt3958kk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We tried to contact the director, but it was not possible by any means.", "tl": "Intentamos comunicarnos con el director, pero no fue posible por ninguna vía."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We cannot allow this confidential information to be leaked through any channel.", "tl": "No podemos permitir que se filtre esta información confidencial por ninguna vía."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We have looked for a solution, but there doesn't seem to be an easy way out through any channel.", "tl": "Hemos buscado una solución, pero por ninguna vía parece haber una salida fácil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My package hasn't arrived yet and I haven't received any news through any channel.", "tl": "No me ha llegado el paquete todavía y no he recibido noticias por ninguna vía."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The bank assured us that the money would not be lost by any means during the transfer.", "tl": "El banco nos aseguró que el dinero no se perdería por ninguna vía durante la transferencia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If they don't answer you by email, try calling them; we can't be left without an answer by any means.", "tl": "Si no te contestan por correo, intenta llamarlos; no podemos quedarnos sin respuesta por ninguna vía."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3220, "expression_id": 3246, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "lejos de", "english_gloss": "far from / instead of", "youtube_id": "NU4gt3958kk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My new house is quite far from the center, but the neighborhood is very quiet.", "tl": "Mi nueva casa está bastante lejos del centro, pero el barrio es muy tranquilo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Far from apologizing for the mistake, he tried to blame his coworker.", "tl": "Lejos de disculparse por el error, él intentó culpar a su compañero de trabajo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The project is still very far from being finished; we have a lot of work left.", "tl": "El proyecto todavía está muy lejos de estar terminado; nos falta mucho trabajo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Far from being discouraged by the failure, she decided to try it one more time.", "tl": "Lejos de desanimarse por el fracaso, ella decidió intentarlo una vez más."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't like living far from my family, so I try to visit them every weekend.", "tl": "No me gusta vivir lejos de mi familia, así que intento visitarlos todos los fines de semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The country's real situation is very far from what the media shows.", "tl": "La situación real del país está muy lejos de lo que muestran los medios de comunicación."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3219, "expression_id": 3245, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "nada que ver con", "english_gloss": "nothing to do with", "youtube_id": "NU4gt3958kk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This year's weather has nothing to do with last year's.", "tl": "El clima de este año no tiene nada que ver con el del año pasado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "What you are saying has nothing to do with the real problem.", "tl": "Lo que estás diciendo no tiene nada que ver con el problema real."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The movie is fun, but it has nothing to do with the original book.", "tl": "La película es divertida, pero no tiene nada que ver con el libro original."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Juan is very shy; he is nothing like his older brother.", "tl": "Juan es muy tímido, no tiene nada que ver con su hermano mayor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I am only the designer; I have nothing to do with the project's budget.", "tl": "Yo solo soy el diseñador, no tengo nada que ver con el presupuesto del proyecto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She insists that she has nothing to do with the office theft.", "tl": "Ella insiste en que no tiene nada que ver con el robo de la oficina."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3218, "expression_id": 3244, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "se han visto obligados a", "english_gloss": "have been forced to", "youtube_id": "PwRbNgH_Ew8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to the crisis, many local businesses have been forced to close their doors.", "tl": "Debido a la crisis, muchos comercios locales se han visto obligados a cerrar sus puertas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For health reasons, the director has been forced to cancel her trip.", "tl": "Por motivos de salud, la directora se ha visto obligada a cancelar su viaje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We have been forced to take drastic measures to solve the water problem.", "tl": "Nos hemos visto obligados a tomar medidas drásticas para solucionar el problema del agua."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The players have been forced to train in the rain due to a lack of space.", "tl": "Las jugadoras se han visto obligadas a entrenar bajo la lluvia por falta de espacio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My grandfather has been forced to learn how to use his mobile phone to do banking transactions.", "tl": "Mi abuelo se ha visto obligado a aprender a usar el móvil para hacer trámites bancarios."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The flight passengers have been forced to spend the night at the airport.", "tl": "Los pasajeros del vuelo se han visto obligados a pasar la noche en el aeropuerto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3217, "expression_id": 3243, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "más allá de que", "english_gloss": "beyond the fact that", "youtube_id": "PwRbNgH_Ew8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Beyond the fact that we have different opinions, we are still great friends.", "tl": "Más allá de que tengamos opiniones diferentes, seguimos siendo grandes amigos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Beyond the fact that the salary is good, I don't like the atmosphere in that office.", "tl": "Más allá de que el sueldo sea bueno, no me gusta el ambiente de esa oficina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Regardless of whether it rains or is sunny, tomorrow we will go on a trip to the countryside.", "tl": "Más allá de que llueva o haga sol, mañana iremos de excursión al campo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Beyond the fact that this phone is expensive, it has an excellent camera.", "tl": "Más allá de que este teléfono sea caro, tiene una cámara excelente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Beyond the fact that you don't have experience, I think you should go to the interview.", "tl": "Más allá de que no tengas experiencia, creo que deberías presentarte a la entrevista."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Beyond the fact that the city is far away, it is worth visiting for its history.", "tl": "Más allá de que la ciudad esté lejos, vale la pena visitarla por su historia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3216, "expression_id": 3242, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "En el corto plazo", "english_gloss": "in the short term", "youtube_id": "PwRbNgH_Ew8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the short term, the company does not plan to hire more staff.", "tl": "En el corto plazo, la empresa no planea contratar a más personal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This diet works in the short term, but it is not sustainable forever.", "tl": "Esta dieta funciona en el corto plazo, pero no es sostenible para siempre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The government wants to reduce inflation in the short term with these new measures.", "tl": "El gobierno quiere reducir la inflación en el corto plazo con estas nuevas medidas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In the short term, my goal is to pass the certification exam.", "tl": "En el corto plazo, mi objetivo es aprobar el examen de certificación."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Buying a used car is cheaper in the short term, but it can bring problems later.", "tl": "Comprar un coche usado es más barato en el corto plazo, pero puede traer problemas después."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We cannot see the results of the project now, but in the short term there will be improvements.", "tl": "No podemos ver los resultados del proyecto ahora, pero en el corto plazo habrá mejoras."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3215, "expression_id": 3241, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "con lo cual", "english_gloss": "as a result of which", "youtube_id": "PwRbNgH_Ew8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The train was delayed by half an hour, as a result of which I arrived late to the meeting.", "tl": "El tren se retrasó media hora, con lo cual llegué tarde a la reunión."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Tomorrow it's going to rain all day, as a result of which we will have to cancel the excursion.", "tl": "Mañana va a llover todo el día, con lo cual tendremos que cancelar la excursión."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I have started exercising daily, as a result of which I feel much more energetic.", "tl": "He empezado a hacer ejercicio diario, con lo cual me siento con mucha más energía."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He didn't study at all for the exam, as a result of which he ended up failing the subject.", "tl": "No estudió nada para el examen, con lo cual acabó suspendiendo la asignatura."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company has bought new computers, as a result of which we now work much faster.", "tl": "La empresa ha comprado ordenadores nuevos, con lo cual ahora trabajamos mucho más rápido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I lost my house keys, as a result of which I had to call a locksmith.", "tl": "Perdí las llaves de casa, con lo cual tuve que llamar a un cerrajero."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3214, "expression_id": 3240, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "batió... un nuevo récord", "english_gloss": "broke a new record", "youtube_id": "PwRbNgH_Ew8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The Kenyan athlete broke a new world record in yesterday's marathon.", "tl": "El atleta keniano batió un nuevo récord mundial en la maratón de ayer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our company will break a new sales record if we keep going like this this month.", "tl": "Nuestra empresa batirá un nuevo récord de ventas si seguimos así este mes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Last summer, a new maximum temperature record was broken in the south of the country.", "tl": "El verano pasado se batió un nuevo récord de temperaturas máximas en el sur del país."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The pop singer has broken a new streaming record in just twenty-four hours.", "tl": "La cantante de pop ha batido un nuevo récord de reproducciones en solo veinticuatro horas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Tourism in the city broke a new record during the Easter holidays.", "tl": "El turismo en la ciudad batió un nuevo récord durante las vacaciones de Semana Santa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The young video game player broke a new high score record in the national tournament.", "tl": "El joven jugador de videojuegos batió un nuevo récord de puntuación en el torneo nacional."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3213, "expression_id": 3239, "lang": "es", "idiom_text": "ha dado un impulso", "english_gloss": "has given a boost", "youtube_id": "PwRbNgH_Ew8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new TV commercial has given a boost to the company's sales.", "tl": "El nuevo anuncio de televisión ha dado un impulso a las ventas de la empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Your advice has given me a boost to keep studying this language.", "tl": "Tu consejo me ha dado un impulso para seguir estudiando este idioma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This year's music festival has given a boost to the city's tourism.", "tl": "El festival de música de este año ha dado un impulso al turismo de la ciudad."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The arrival of the new director has given a boost to the technology project.", "tl": "La llegada del nuevo director ha dado un impulso al proyecto de tecnología."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Last Sunday's victory has given a boost to the team for the rest of the season.", "tl": "La victoria del domingo pasado ha dado un impulso al equipo para el resto de la temporada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The government has given a boost to public education with new scholarships.", "tl": "El gobierno ha dado un impulso a la educación pública con nuevas becas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3212, "expression_id": 3238, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se joue", "english_gloss": "is playing out / is at stake", "youtube_id": "m3USArLy5Ks", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is during this interview that everything is at stake for his professional future.", "tl": "C'est pendant cet entretien que tout se joue pour son avenir professionnel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The match is very close, the victory is decided in the final minutes.", "tl": "Le match est très serré, la victoire se joue dans les dernières minutes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The future of our planet is at stake now, we must act quickly.", "tl": "L'avenir de notre planète se joue maintenant, nous devons agir vite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't worry, nothing serious is at stake during this meeting.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, rien de grave ne se joue lors de cette réunion."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You can feel that a drama is playing out between these two characters.", "tl": "On sent qu'un drame se joue entre ces deux personnages."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The success of this project hinges on details that we must not overlook.", "tl": "Le succès de ce projet se joue sur des détails que nous ne devons pas négliger."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3211, "expression_id": 3237, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "fait son grand retour", "english_gloss": "makes his major comeback", "youtube_id": "m3USArLy5Ks", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Vinyl records are making a major comeback among young people this year.", "tl": "Le disque vinyle fait son grand retour auprès des jeunes cette année."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After a ten-year absence, this famous singer is making his major comeback with a new album.", "tl": "Après dix ans d'absence, ce célèbre chanteur fait son grand retour avec un nouvel album."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Watch out, the cold weather is making a major comeback starting this weekend across the whole country.", "tl": "Attention, le froid fait son grand retour dès ce week-end sur tout le pays."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After his serious knee injury, the champion is making his major comeback on the field.", "tl": "Après sa grave blessure au genou, le champion fait son grand retour sur le terrain."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This drink from the 90s is making a major comeback in our supermarkets.", "tl": "Cette boisson des années 90 fait son grand retour dans nos supermarchés."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This cult series is making its major comeback on our screens for a third season.", "tl": "Cette série culte fait son grand retour sur nos écrans pour une troisième saison."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3210, "expression_id": 3236, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "peinent à", "english_gloss": "struggle to", "youtube_id": "m3USArLy5Ks", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Many young graduates struggle to find a stable first job.", "tl": "Beaucoup de jeunes diplômés peinent à trouver un premier emploi stable."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My grandparents struggle to use new technologies.", "tl": "Mes grands-parents peinent à utiliser les nouvelles technologies."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Small businesses are struggling to recruit qualified staff this summer.", "tl": "Les petites entreprises peinent à recruter du personnel qualifié cet été."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After a long day of work, I struggle to fall asleep.", "tl": "Après une longue journée de travail, je peine à m'endormir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Buses struggle to get around downtown because of the roadworks.", "tl": "Les bus peinent à circuler dans le centre-ville à cause des travaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Despite his efforts, he struggles to understand his new colleague's accent.", "tl": "Malgré ses efforts, il peine à comprendre l'accent de son nouveau collègue."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3209, "expression_id": 3235, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "fait rage", "english_gloss": "is raging", "youtube_id": "m3USArLy5Ks", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The storm is raging outside, it's better to stay indoors.", "tl": "La tempête fait rage dehors, il vaut mieux rester à l'intérieur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The debate over the reform has been raging in Parliament for several days.", "tl": "Le débat sur la réforme fait rage au Parlement depuis plusieurs jours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In winter, the flu epidemic rages throughout the region.", "tl": "En hiver, l'épidémie de grippe fait rage dans toute la région."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The fire is raging in the forest and the firefighters are fighting against the wind.", "tl": "L'incendie fait rage dans la forêt et les pompiers luttent contre le vent."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Competition is raging between these two major smartphone brands.", "tl": "La concurrence fait rage entre ces deux grandes marques de smartphones."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The battle is raging between the two teams to get first place.", "tl": "La bataille fait rage entre les deux équipes pour obtenir la première place."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3208, "expression_id": 3234, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "dans le même temps", "english_gloss": "at the same time / meanwhile", "youtube_id": "m3USArLy5Ks", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government wants to lower taxes and, at the same time, improve public services.", "tl": "Le gouvernement veut baisser les impôts et, dans le même temps, améliorer les services publics."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She started her new job and, at the same time, she had to move to another city.", "tl": "Elle a commencé son nouveau travail et, dans le même temps, elle a dû déménager dans une autre ville."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "E-book sales are increasing, but at the same time, people continue to buy paper books.", "tl": "Les ventes de livres numériques augmentent, mais dans le même temps, les gens continuent d'acheter des livres papier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The company must reduce its costs, but at the same time, it must invest in innovation.", "tl": "L'entreprise doit réduire ses coûts, mais dans le même temps, elle doit investir dans l'innovation."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He is preparing for his end-of-year exams and, at the same time, he is looking for an internship for this summer.", "tl": "Il prépare ses examens de fin d'année et, dans le même temps, il cherche un stage pour cet été."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The city wants to encourage bicycle use, but at the same time, it is building new parking lots for cars.", "tl": "La ville veut encourager l'usage du vélo, mais dans le même temps, elle construit de nouveaux parkings pour voitures."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3207, "expression_id": 3233, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "passe-droit", "english_gloss": "special privilege", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In this company, everyone must follow the rules; there are no special privileges.", "tl": "Dans cette entreprise, tout le monde doit respecter les règles, il n'y a aucun passe-droit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He got a spot in this school thanks to a special privilege, which angered the other candidates.", "tl": "Il a obtenu une place dans cette école grâce à un passe-droit, ce qui a mis en colère les autres candidats."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Just because you are the director's son doesn't mean you are entitled to special favors.", "tl": "Ce n'est pas parce que tu es le fils du directeur que tu as le droit à des passe-droits."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Wait in line like everyone else, you have no special privileges here!", "tl": "Faites la queue comme tout le monde, vous n'avez aucun passe-droit ici !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The law must be the same for everyone, without any special treatment for influential people.", "tl": "La loi doit être la même pour tous, sans aucun passe-droit pour les personnes influentes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I cannot give you the exam answers; that would be an unfair privilege over your classmates.", "tl": "Je ne peux pas te donner les réponses de l'examen, ce serait un passe-droit injuste pour tes camarades."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3206, "expression_id": 3232, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "diviser pour régner", "english_gloss": "divide and conquer", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The manager uses the strategy of divide and conquer to prevent the employees from uniting against him.", "tl": "Le directeur utilise la stratégie de diviser pour régner pour éviter que les employés ne s'unissent contre lui."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Historically, many empires applied the principle of \"divide and conquer\" to control vast territories.", "tl": "Historiquement, de nombreux empires ont appliqué le principe « diviser pour régner » pour contrôler de vastes territoire"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In this group of friends, she always tries to divide and conquer to remain the center of attention.", "tl": "Dans ce groupe d'amis, elle essaie toujours de diviser pour régner afin de rester au centre de l'attention."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our team leader prefers to divide and conquer rather than encourage true collaboration.", "tl": "Notre chef d'équipe préfère diviser pour régner plutôt que de favoriser une véritable collaboration."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Some media outlets seek to divide and conquer by emphasizing the differences between citizens.", "tl": "Certains médias cherchent à diviser pour régner en insistant sur les différences entre les citoyens."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't let them create conflicts between us; their goal is simply to divide and conquer.", "tl": "Ne les laisse pas créer des conflits entre nous ; leur but est simplement de diviser pour régner."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3205, "expression_id": 3231, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en contrepartie de", "english_gloss": "in exchange for", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In exchange for his overtime hours, he received two days off.", "tl": "En contrepartie de ses heures supplémentaires, il a reçu deux jours de congé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The company offers a discount in exchange for your loyalty.", "tl": "L'entreprise offre une réduction en contrepartie de votre fidélité."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She agreed to help him move in exchange for a good meal.", "tl": "Elle a accepté de l'aider pour son déménagement en contrepartie d'un bon repas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In exchange for your signature, we will hand over the keys to the apartment.", "tl": "En contrepartie de votre signature, nous vous remettrons les clés de l'appartement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He gives math lessons in exchange for guitar lessons.", "tl": "Il donne des cours de maths en contrepartie de leçons de guitare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They are housed for free in exchange for some work in the garden.", "tl": "Ils sont logés gratuitement en contrepartie de quelques travaux dans le jardin."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3204, "expression_id": 3230, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "dézoomer le conflit", "english_gloss": "to take a step back from the conflict", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sometimes, in a couple, you have to know how to take a step back from the conflict to understand what is wrong.", "tl": "Parfois, dans un couple, il faut savoir dézoomer le conflit pour comprendre ce qui ne va pas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The mediator helped us take a step back from the conflict and find a peaceful solution.", "tl": "Le médiateur nous a aidés à dézoomer le conflit et à trouver une solution pacifique."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you are too angry, you won't manage to take a step back from the conflict to see the big picture.", "tl": "Si tu es trop en colère, tu n'arriveras pas à dézoomer le conflit pour voir la situation globale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Let's try to take a step back from the conflict before making a decision we will regret.", "tl": "Essayons de dézoomer le conflit avant de prendre une décision que nous allons regretter."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "To analyze this political crisis, it is necessary to take a step back from the conflict and study its history.", "tl": "Pour analyser cette crise politique, il est nécessaire de dézoomer le conflit et d'étudier son histoire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My manager advised me to take a step back from the conflict so as not to get overwhelmed by my emotions.", "tl": "Mon manager m'a conseillé de dézoomer le conflit pour ne pas me laisser déborder par mes émotions."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3203, "expression_id": 3229, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts", "english_gloss": "it claimed tens of thousands of lives", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The Spanish flu was terrible; it claimed tens of thousands of lives in a few months.", "tl": "La grippe espagnole a été terrible ; elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts en quelques mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This natural disaster is the worst in the country's history: it claimed tens of thousands of lives.", "tl": "Cette catastrophe naturelle est la pire de l'histoire du pays : elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We often forget this civil war, but it claimed tens of thousands of lives at the time.", "tl": "On oublie souvent cette guerre civile, mais elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts à l'époque."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The heatwave of that summer was historic, and it claimed tens of thousands of lives across Europe.", "tl": "La canicule de cet été-là a été historique, et elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts à travers l'Europe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The epidemic spread rapidly in the region and it claimed tens of thousands of lives.", "tl": "L'épidémie s'est propagée rapidement dans la région et elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Although the storm has passed, we remember that it claimed tens of thousands of lives.", "tl": "Bien que la tempête soit passée, on se souvient qu'elle a fait des dizaines de milliers de morts."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3202, "expression_id": 3228, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "avoir de leurs nouvelles", "english_gloss": "to hear from them", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I haven't heard from them since they left on vacation.", "tl": "Je n'ai pas eu de leurs nouvelles depuis leur départ en vacances."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Did you finally manage to hear from them?", "tl": "Est-ce que tu as enfin réussi à avoir de leurs nouvelles ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I hope to hear from them very soon.", "tl": "J'espère avoir de leurs nouvelles très bientôt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we don't hear from them by tomorrow, we will call them.", "tl": "Si nous n'avons pas de leurs nouvelles d'ici demain, nous les appellerons."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The clients are very busy, but we should hear from them this week.", "tl": "Les clients sont très occupés, mais nous devrions avoir de leurs nouvelles cette semaine."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My parents are worried because they haven't heard from them yet.", "tl": "Mes parents s'inquiètent parce qu'ils n'ont pas encore eu de leurs nouvelles."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3201, "expression_id": 3227, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "avant toute chose", "english_gloss": "first and foremost", "youtube_id": "alBiFl61ZdE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "First and foremost, I would like to thank the team for their excellent work.", "tl": "Avant toute chose, je voudrais remercier l'équipe pour son excellent travail."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Before anything else, don't forget to check the validity of your passport.", "tl": "Avant toute chose, n'oublie pas de vérifier la validité de ton passeport."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "First of all, you need to preheat the oven to 180 degrees.", "tl": "Avant toute chose, il faut préchauffer le four à 180 degrés."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Before doing anything else, we must analyze the risks of this project.", "tl": "Avant toute chose, nous devons analyser les risques de ce projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In a friendship, I look for sincerity first and foremost.", "tl": "Dans une amitié, je recherche avant toute chose la sincérité."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If your computer is no longer working, check first and foremost if it is properly plugged in.", "tl": "Si ton ordinateur ne marche plus, vérifie avant toute chose s'il est bien branché."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3200, "expression_id": 3226, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de quebra", "english_gloss": "as a bonus / on top of that", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We traveled to Rio de Janeiro and, as a bonus, managed to see the sunset in Ipanema.", "tl": "Viajamos para o Rio de Janeiro e, de quebra, conseguimos ver o pôr do sol em Ipanema."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He finished the report early and, on top of that, helped his colleagues with the project.", "tl": "Ele terminou o relatório mais cedo e, de quebra, ajudou os colegas com o projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I bought a new cell phone and got a case as a bonus.", "tl": "Comprei um celular novo e ganhei uma capinha de quebra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I started walking every day to lose weight and, as a bonus, improved my sleep.", "tl": "Comecei a caminhar todos os dias para emagrecer e, de quebra, melhorei meu sono."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She prepared a wonderful dinner and, on top of that, made a delicious dessert.", "tl": "Ela preparou um jantar maravilhoso e, de quebra, fez uma sobremesa deliciosa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Taking this course helped me at work and, as a bonus, I met amazing people.", "tl": "Fazer esse curso me ajudou no trabalho e, de quebra, conheci pessoas incríveis."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3199, "expression_id": 3225, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "deu no que deu", "english_gloss": "look what happened / ended up like that", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "They spent more than they could on their credit card and look what happened: now they are deep in debt.", "tl": "Eles gastaram mais do que podiam no cartão de crédito e deu no que deu: agora estão cheios de dívidas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We didn't talk about the problem at the time and we saw how that turned out, we ended up having a huge fight.", "tl": "Nós não conversamos sobre o problema na época e deu no que deu, acabamos brigando feio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He decided to do the report at the last minute and look what happened, the boss didn't like the result.", "tl": "Ele decidiu fazer o relatório de última hora e deu no que deu, o chefe não gostou do resultado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I warned him to take a coat, but he didn't listen to me and look what happened: he caught a cold.", "tl": "Eu avisei para ele levar um casaco, mas ele não me ouviu e deu no que deu: pegou um resfriado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She tried to fix the washing machine by herself and look what happened, now the kitchen floor is flooded.", "tl": "Ela tentou consertar a máquina de lavar sozinha e deu no que deu, agora o chão da cozinha está inundado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We took a shortcut without knowing the way and we saw how that turned out, we were lost for two hours.", "tl": "Nós pegamos um atalho sem conhecer o caminho e deu no que deu, ficamos perdidos por duas horas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3198, "expression_id": 3224, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dava risada", "english_gloss": "laughed / used to laugh", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Whenever I told that joke, my grandfather used to laugh.", "tl": "Sempre que eu contava aquela piada, meu avô dava risada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The children laughed at their uncle's antics at the party.", "tl": "As crianças davam risada das palhaçadas do tio na festa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We used to laugh at any silly thing when we were teenagers.", "tl": "Nós dávamos risada de qualquer bobagem quando éramos adolescentes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I laughed when I saw the old photo you sent me.", "tl": "Eu dei risada quando vi a foto antiga que você me mandou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She couldn't stand the silence in the middle of the meeting and laughed.", "tl": "Ela não aguentou o silêncio no meio da reunião e deu risada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He was a serious man, but he used to laugh at comedy movies.", "tl": "Ele era um homem sério, mas dava risada com os filmes de comédia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3197, "expression_id": 3223, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "custe o que custar", "english_gloss": "at all costs / whatever it takes", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We have to deliver this project by Friday, whatever it takes.", "tl": "Temos que entregar este projeto até sexta-feira, custe o que custar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I am going to pass my driving test, whatever it takes.", "tl": "Eu vou conseguir passar no exame de condução, custe o que custar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She promised to protect her family, at all costs.", "tl": "Ela prometeu proteger a sua família, custe o que custar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This year we are going on vacation to Japan, whatever it takes.", "tl": "Este ano nós vamos de férias para o Japão, custe o que custar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They want to buy that house, at all costs.", "tl": "Eles querem comprar aquela casa, custe o que custar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I will find out the truth, whatever it takes.", "tl": "Eu vou descobrir a verdade, custe o que custar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3196, "expression_id": 3222, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "enchendo o meu saco", "english_gloss": "annoying me / bugging me", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My boss has been bugging me all day about this report.", "tl": "O meu chefe está o dia todo enchendo o meu saco com esse relatório."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Stop talking about that! You're already annoying me.", "tl": "Para de falar disso! Você já está enchendo o meu saco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "These unknown numbers keep calling me and bugging me.", "tl": "Esses números desconhecidos ficam me ligando e enchendo o meu saco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He keeps bugging me to go to the party with him.", "tl": "Ele continua enchendo o meu saco para eu ir à festa com ele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The cat is annoying me because it wants food right now.", "tl": "O gato está enchendo o meu saco porque quer comida agora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "That construction noise has been bugging me since early this morning.", "tl": "Aquele barulho da obra está enchendo o meu saco desde cedo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3195, "expression_id": 3221, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "acredite se quiser", "english_gloss": "believe it or not", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Believe it or not, I finally learned how to cook this year.", "tl": "Acredite se quiser, eu finalmente aprendi a cozinhar este ano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Believe it or not, we met by chance in the middle of Paris.", "tl": "Acredite se quiser, nós nos encontramos por acaso no meio de Paris."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Believe it or not, but it hasn't rained at all this month.", "tl": "Acredite se quiser, mas ainda não choveu nada este mês."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Believe it or not, he started working at the company as an intern and today he is the director.", "tl": "Acredite se quiser, ele começou a trabalhar na empresa como estagiário e hoje é o diretor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She lives in Rio de Janeiro but, believe it or not, she hates going to the beach.", "tl": "Ela mora no Rio de Janeiro mas, acredite se quiser, ela detesta ir à praia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Believe it or not, this old watch cost only ten euros at a flea market.", "tl": "Acredite se quiser, este relógio antigo custou apenas dez euros em uma feira."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3194, "expression_id": 3220, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "ter dó", "english_gloss": "to feel sorry for", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I feel sorry for that stray dog, he looks so skinny and hungry.", "tl": "Eu tenho dó daquele cachorro de rua, ele parece tão magro e faminto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At first, the neighbors felt sorry for him, but then they realized he didn't want to work.", "tl": "No início, os vizinhos tinham dó dele, mas depois perceberam que ele não queria trabalhar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Please, have mercy on me and don't tell me the ending of the movie!", "tl": "Por favor, tenha dó de mim e não me conte o final do filme!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It's hard not to feel sorry for the people who lost everything in the flood.", "tl": "É difícil não ter dó das pessoas que perderam tudo na enchente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We felt sorry for the secretary because she had to work late on her birthday.", "tl": "Nós tivemos dó da secretária porque ela teve que trabalhar até tarde no aniversário dela."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "That boss has no pity on anyone; he demands that everyone work overtime without complaining.", "tl": "Aquele chefe não tem dó de ninguém; ele exige que todos façam horas extras sem reclamar."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3193, "expression_id": 3219, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vergonhas alheias", "english_gloss": "secondhand embarrassments", "youtube_id": "Hceg_UaUwco", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I had to turn off the television because that scene gave me a lot of secondhand embarrassment.", "tl": "Eu tive que desligar a televisão porque aquela cena me deu muita vergonha alheia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "That comedy show is full of secondhand embarrassments that I can barely watch.", "tl": "Aquele programa de comédia é cheio de vergonhas alheias que eu mal consigo assistir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I feel a huge secondhand embarrassment when I see someone going through that situation on the street.", "tl": "Eu sinto uma vergonha alheia enorme quando vejo alguém passando por essa situação na rua."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I avoid watching these videos on the internet to save my heart from so many secondhand embarrassments.", "tl": "Evito ver esses vídeos na internet para poupar o meu coração de tantas vergonhas alheias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He tried to tell a joke in the middle of the meeting, but only caused secondhand embarrassment to everyone.", "tl": "Ele tentou contar uma piada no meio da reunião, mas só causou vergonha alheia em todo mundo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't like reality shows because they are full of secondhand embarrassments from beginning to end.", "tl": "Não gosto de reality shows porque eles estão cheios de vergonhas alheias do início ao fim."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3192, "expression_id": 3218, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "al di là della", "english_gloss": "beyond / apart from", "youtube_id": "QWKc_cJNxpY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Apart from her opinion, we need to make a decision immediately.", "tl": "Al di là della sua opinione, dobbiamo prendere una decisione subito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "There is a beautiful path beyond the hill.", "tl": "C'è un bellissimo sentiero al di là della collina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Beyond her cold appearance, she is a very sweet person.", "tl": "Al di là della sua apparenza fredda, è una persona molto dolce."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Apart from the financial issue, this project is very interesting.", "tl": "Al di là della questione economica, questo progetto è molto interessante."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Beyond the general rule, there are always some exceptions.", "tl": "Al di là della regola generale, ci sono sempre delle eccezioni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Beyond the initial effort, running in the morning is very good for you.", "tl": "Al di là della fatica iniziale, correre la mattina fa molto bene."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3191, "expression_id": 3217, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "da qui a", "english_gloss": "between now and", "youtube_id": "QWKc_cJNxpY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Between now and the end of the month, we have to finish this project.", "tl": "Da qui alla fine del mese dobbiamo finire questo progetto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Between now and five years from now, I would like to buy a house in the countryside.", "tl": "Da qui a cinque anni mi piacerebbe comprare una casa in campagna."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Things can change a lot between now and tomorrow.", "tl": "Le cose possono cambiare molto da qui a domani."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Between now and Friday, we need to decide where to go on vacation.", "tl": "Da qui a venerdì dobbiamo decidere dove andare in vacanza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I have a lot to study between now and next week's exam.", "tl": "Ho molto da studiare da qui all'esame della prossima settimana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We need to hire three new people between now and the end of the year.", "tl": "Dobbiamo assumere tre nuove persone da qui a fine anno."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3190, "expression_id": 3216, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "sul posto", "english_gloss": "on the spot / on site", "youtube_id": "QWKc_cJNxpY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The police arrived on the scene a few minutes after the accident.", "tl": "La polizia è arrivata sul posto pochi minuti dopo l'incidente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is better to buy the tickets on-site to avoid online fees.", "tl": "È meglio comprare i biglietti sul posto per evitare le commissioni online."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The technician repaired the washing machine directly on-site.", "tl": "Il tecnico ha riparato la lavatrice direttamente sul posto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We don't know how to handle the situation yet, we will decide on the spot.", "tl": "Non sappiamo ancora come gestire la situazione, decideremo sul posto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The journalists are already on the scene to follow the developments of the story.", "tl": "I giornalisti sono già sul posto per seguire gli sviluppi della vicenda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you need information during the fair, you will find staff on-site.", "tl": "Se hai bisogno di informazioni durante la fiera, troverai del personale sul posto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3189, "expression_id": 3215, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "ha reso noto", "english_gloss": "made known / disclosed", "youtube_id": "QWKc_cJNxpY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The company director made it known that the new project will start in January.", "tl": "Il direttore dell'azienda ha reso noto che il nuovo progetto inizierà a gennaio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The mayor disclosed the plan to improve the city's public transport.", "tl": "Il sindaco ha reso noto il piano per migliorare i trasporti pubblici della città."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The famous actress announced her marriage through a social media post.", "tl": "La famosa attrice ha reso noto il suo matrimonio attraverso un post sui social."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The ministry of health made it known that the situation is under control.", "tl": "Il ministero della salute ha reso noto che la situazione è sotto controllo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The university has made known the class schedule for the next semester.", "tl": "L'università ha reso noto il calendario delle lezioni per il prossimo semestre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The police have not yet disclosed the motive for the theft.", "tl": "La polizia non ha ancora reso noto il movente del furto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3188, "expression_id": 3214, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "deixar bem claro", "english_gloss": "to make it very clear", "youtube_id": "CNfQIoa84js", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I want to make it very clear that I don't agree with this decision.", "tl": "Eu quero deixar bem claro que não concordo com essa decisão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss made it very clear that the deadline is Friday.", "tl": "O chefe deixou bem claro que o prazo final é sexta-feira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I hope she makes it very clear what she really wants.", "tl": "Espero que ela deixe bem claro o que realmente quer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They made it very clear that they won't accept late projects.", "tl": "Eles deixaram bem claro que não vão aceitar projetos atrasados."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She made it very clear to him that they are just friends.", "tl": "Ela deixou bem claro para ele que eles são apenas amigos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is important to make it very clear what the rules of the game are.", "tl": "É importante deixar bem claro quais são as regras do jogo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3187, "expression_id": 3213, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "volto a falar", "english_gloss": "reiterate", "youtube_id": "CNfQIoa84js", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I reiterate that data security is our highest priority.", "tl": "Volto a falar que a segurança dos dados é a nossa maior prioridade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I reiterate the importance of planning the trip in advance.", "tl": "Volto a falar sobre a importância de planejar a viagem com antecedência."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you have doubts, we will talk about this again tomorrow.", "tl": "Se você tiver dúvidas, nós voltamos a falar sobre isso amanhã."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The report reiterates the need to reduce the company's costs.", "tl": "O relatório volta a falar da necessidade de reduzir os custos da empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I reiterate: without the original document, you won't be able to enroll.", "tl": "Volto a falar: sem o documento original, você não poderá fazer a matrícula."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't want to talk again about what happened last year.", "tl": "Não quero voltar a falar sobre o que aconteceu no ano passado."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3186, "expression_id": 3212, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dar visibilidade", "english_gloss": "to give visibility", "youtube_id": "CNfQIoa84js", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Instagram's new algorithm helps to give visibility to small businesses.", "tl": "O novo algoritmo do Instagram ajuda a dar visibilidade aos pequenos negócios."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The charity campaign wants to raise awareness of (give visibility to) the situation of homeless people.", "tl": "A campanha de solidariedade quer dar visibilidade à situação das pessoas sem-abrigo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The director promised to give more visibility to our project at the next meeting.", "tl": "O diretor prometeu dar mais visibilidade ao nosso projeto na próxima reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Television should give visibility to these social problems more often.", "tl": "A televisão devia dar visibilidade a estes problemas sociais com mais frequência."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This art festival serves to give visibility to local artists.", "tl": "Este festival de arte serve para dar visibilidade aos artistas locais."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The radio interview gave a lot of exposure (visibility) to the writer's new book.", "tl": "A entrevista na rádio deu muita visibilidade ao novo livro do escritor."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3185, "expression_id": 3211, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "perseguição descabida", "english_gloss": "unwarranted persecution", "youtube_id": "CNfQIoa84js", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The employee felt he was suffering unwarranted persecution from his new boss.", "tl": "O funcionário sentia que sofria uma perseguição descabida por parte do seu novo chefe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The press engaged in an unwarranted hounding of the politician after the debate.", "tl": "A imprensa fez uma perseguição descabida ao político após o debate."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She decided to change schools to escape that unwarranted harassment from her classmates.", "tl": "Ela decidiu mudar de escola para escapar daquela perseguição descabida dos colegas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The lawyer argued that his client was the target of unwarranted persecution by the authorities.", "tl": "O advogado argumentou que o seu cliente era alvo de uma perseguição descabida pelas autoridades."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Many celebrities complain about the unwarranted hounding by photographers in their daily lives.", "tl": "Muitos famosos queixam-se da perseguição descabida dos fotógrafos no seu dia a dia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't understand the reason for so much anger; this seems like unwarranted persecution.", "tl": "Não entendo o motivo de tanta raiva; isto parece uma perseguição descabida."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3184, "expression_id": 3210, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vive gritando", "english_gloss": "constantly shouts", "youtube_id": "CNfQIoa84js", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The upstairs neighbor is always shouting at his dog.", "tl": "O vizinho do andar de cima vive gritando com o cachorro dele."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She is constantly shouting when she is stressed at work.", "tl": "Ela vive gritando quando está estressada no trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That engaged couple is constantly shouting at each other over any little thing.", "tl": "Aqueles noivos vivem gritando um com o outro por qualquer bobagem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't know why he is always shouting at me; I didn't do anything wrong.", "tl": "Eu não sei por que ele vive gritando comigo; eu não fiz nada de errado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our boss is constantly shouting in meetings when the results are bad.", "tl": "Nosso chefe vive gritando nas reuniões quando os resultados são ruins."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The children are constantly shouting while playing video games in the living room.", "tl": "As crianças vivem gritando enquanto jogam videogame na sala."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3183, "expression_id": 3209, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tornou-se alvo de", "english_gloss": "became the target of", "youtube_id": "CNfQIoa84js", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The young politician became the target of criticism after his latest decision.", "tl": "O jovem político tornou-se alvo de críticas após a sua última decisão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The technology company became the target of a cyber attack last week.", "tl": "A empresa de tecnologia tornou-se alvo de um ataque cibernético na semana passada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Because he was very shy, the new student became the target of jokes at school.", "tl": "Por ser muito tímido, o aluno novo tornou-se alvo de piadas na escola."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "That small neighborhood store became the target of interest from major investors.", "tl": "Aquela pequena loja de bairro tornou-se alvo de interesse de grandes investidores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The football coach became the target of difficult questions during the press conference.", "tl": "O treinador de futebol tornou-se alvo de perguntas difíceis durante a conferência de imprensa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The city's natural park became the target of debates on environmental conservation.", "tl": "O parque natural da cidade tornou-se alvo de debates sobre a conservação ambiental."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3182, "expression_id": 3208, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "com o tempo", "english_gloss": "over time", "youtube_id": "Yi1qjOhE0NY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Over time, you will see that speaking Portuguese gets easier.", "tl": "Com o tempo, vais ver que falar português fica mais fácil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At first I didn't like this job, but over time I got used to it.", "tl": "No início eu não gostava deste trabalho, mas com o tempo habituei-me."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Over time, the wounds of the past end up healing.", "tl": "Com o tempo, as feridas do passado acabam por curar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you practice every day, over time you will notice a big difference.", "tl": "Se praticares todos os dias, com o tempo vais notar uma grande diferença."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "People adapt to new technologies over time.", "tl": "As pessoas adaptam-se às novas tecnologias com o tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I forgot many details of that trip over time.", "tl": "Esqueci-me de muitos detalhes daquela viagem com o tempo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3181, "expression_id": 3207, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "para te falar bem a verdade", "english_gloss": "to tell you the honest truth", "youtube_id": "Yi1qjOhE0NY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To tell you the honest truth, I would prefer to work from home today.", "tl": "Para te falar bem a verdade, eu preferia trabalhar de casa hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To tell you the honest truth, I didn't really like the ending of that movie.", "tl": "Para te falar bem a verdade, eu não gostei muito do final daquele filme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "To tell you the honest truth, I am too tired to go to the party tonight.", "tl": "Para te falar bem a verdade, estou cansado demais para ir à festa hoje à noite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To tell you the honest truth, the food at that new restaurant isn't all that good.", "tl": "Para te falar bem a verdade, a comida daquele restaurante novo não é tão boa assim."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "To tell you the honest truth, I still have a bit of difficulty with grammar.", "tl": "Para te falar bem a verdade, eu ainda tenho um pouco de dificuldade com a gramática."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "To tell you the honest truth, I had completely forgotten about our appointment.", "tl": "Para te falar bem a verdade, eu tinha esquecido completamente do nosso compromisso."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3180, "expression_id": 3206, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de vez em quando", "english_gloss": "once in a while", "youtube_id": "Yi1qjOhE0NY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I try to eat healthy, but once in a while I eat a hamburger.", "tl": "Eu tento comer de forma saudável, mas de vez em quando como um hambúrguer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We don't live in the same city anymore, but once in a while we still meet up for a coffee.", "tl": "Nós já não moramos na mesma cidade, mas de vez em quando ainda nos encontramos para um café."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She prefers to read fiction books, but once in a while she likes to watch a documentary.", "tl": "Ela prefere ler livros de ficção, mas de vez em quando gosta de ver um documentário."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The weather here is very dry, but once in a while it rains in the late afternoon.", "tl": "O clima aqui é muito seco, mas de vez em quando chove no final da tarde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I usually work from home, but once in a while I need to go to the office for meetings.", "tl": "Eu costumo trabalhar em casa, mas de vez em quando preciso ir ao escritório para reuniões."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Once in a while, I think about going back to studying and doing a new course.", "tl": "De vez em quando, eu penso em voltar a estudar e fazer um novo curso."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3179, "expression_id": 3205, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "perdi a conta", "english_gloss": "lost count", "youtube_id": "Yi1qjOhE0NY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I've seen this movie so many times that I've lost count.", "tl": "Já vi esse filme tantas vezes que perdi a conta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I lost count of how many coffees I drank this morning.", "tl": "Perdi a conta de quantos cafés tomei hoje de manhã."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She has traveled to Paris so many times that she lost count.", "tl": "Ela já viajou para Paris tantas vezes que perdeu a conta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I tried calling him today and lost count of how many times it rang.", "tl": "Tentei ligar para ele hoje e perdi a conta de quantas vezes chamou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My son asks so many questions that I've already lost count.", "tl": "O meu filho faz tantas perguntas que eu já perdi a conta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We made so many mistakes on that project that we even lost count.", "tl": "Nós cometemos tantos erros naquele projeto que até perdemos a conta."}]}, {"idiom_id": 3178, "expression_id": 3204, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dando risada", "english_gloss": "laughing", "youtube_id": "Yi1qjOhE0NY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "They are in the bedroom laughing at some joke on the internet.", "tl": "Eles estão no quarto dando risada de alguma piada na internet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Everyone laughed when the dog tried to catch its own tail.", "tl": "Todo mundo deu risada quando o cachorro tentou pegar a própria cauda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's impossible not to laugh while watching this comedy.", "tl": "É impossível não dar risada assistindo a essa comédia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why are you there laughing by yourself looking at your phone?", "tl": "Por que você está aí dando risada sozinho olhando para o celular?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She was laughing out loud in the middle of the library and everyone looked at her.", "tl": "Ela estava dando risada alto no meio da biblioteca e todos olharam par
