l, "ord": 6, "en": "This business partnership needs to be a two-way street so that both sides profit.", "tl": "Essa parceria de negócios precisa ser uma via de mão dupla para que ambos os lados tenham lucro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 406, "expression_id": 427, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "antes de mais", "english_gloss": "first of all", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "First of all, I would like to thank you all for your presence today.", "tl": "Antes de mais, gostaria de agradecer a todos pela vossa presença hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "First of all, we have to solve the problem with the server.", "tl": "Antes de mais, temos de resolver o problema com o servidor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "First of all, you need to pack your bags if you want to travel tomorrow.", "tl": "Antes de mais, precisas de fazer as malas se queres viajar amanhã."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "First of all, I want to make it clear that this is just my opinion.", "tl": "Antes de mais, quero deixar claro que esta é apenas a minha opinião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "First of all, you must wash all the vegetables well.", "tl": "Antes de mais, deves lavar bem todos os legumes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "First of all, we need to define the budget for this project.", "tl": "Antes de mais, precisamos de definir o orçamento para este projeto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 405, "expression_id": 426, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "quando se trata de", "english_gloss": "when it comes to", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When it comes to cooking, my brother is the best in the family.", "tl": "Quando se trata de cozinhar, o meu irmão é o melhor da família."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He is very organized when it comes to saving money.", "tl": "Ele é muito organizado quando se trata de poupar dinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When it comes to making difficult decisions, I prefer to ask for advice.", "tl": "Quando se trata de tomar decisões difíceis, prefiro pedir conselhos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She never gives up when it comes to achieving her health goals.", "tl": "Ela nunca desiste quando se trata de atingir os seus objetivos de saúde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When it comes to choosing a hotel, location is the most important thing.", "tl": "Quando se trata de escolher um hotel, a localização é o mais importante."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Young people learn very quickly when it comes to new technologies.", "tl": "Os jovens aprendem muito rápido quando se trata de novas tecnologias."}]}, {"idiom_id": 404, "expression_id": 425, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tem a ver com", "english_gloss": "has to do with", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "His problem doesn't have to do with a lack of money, but rather a lack of time.", "tl": "O problema dele não tem a ver com falta de dinheiro, mas sim com falta de tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "These new rules have to do with everyone's safety in the office.", "tl": "Estas novas regras têm a ver com a segurança de todos no escritório."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I thought the argument had to do with the project, but it was something personal.", "tl": "Eu achava que a discussão tinha a ver com o projeto, mas era algo pessoal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "What does that have to do with what we are talking about?", "tl": "O que é que isso tem a ver com o que estamos a falar?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My decision to move cities has nothing to do with my current job.", "tl": "A minha decisão de mudar de cidade não tem nada a ver com o meu trabalho atual."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The success of this restaurant has to do with the quality of the food and the good service.", "tl": "O sucesso deste restaurante tem a ver com a qualidade da comida e o bom serviço."}]}, {"idiom_id": 403, "expression_id": 424, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "passar por", "english_gloss": "to go through / experience", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We went through difficult times last year, but now everything is better.", "tl": "Nós passamos por momentos difíceis no ano passado, mas agora tudo está melhor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The company is going through many changes this month.", "tl": "A empresa está passando por muitas mudanças este mês."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I never want to go through a surgery like that again.", "tl": "Eu nunca quero passar por uma cirurgia como aquela novamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I understand how you feel because I've already gone through that.", "tl": "Eu entendo o que você sente porque já passei por isso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She had to go through several tests before getting the job.", "tl": "Ela teve que passar por vários testes antes de conseguir o emprego."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "All teenagers go through this rebellious phase.", "tl": "Todos os adolescentes passam por essa fase de rebeldia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 402, "expression_id": 423, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "por necessidade", "english_gloss": "out of necessity", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He accepted that job out of necessity, not because he liked the work.", "tl": "Ele aceitou aquele emprego por necessidade, não porque gostava do trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We had to sell the car out of necessity, as we needed the money urgently.", "tl": "Tivemos de vender o carro por necessidade, pois precisávamos do dinheiro com urgência."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She moved to the big city out of necessity, to find better living conditions.", "tl": "Ela mudou-se para a cidade grande por necessidade, para encontrar melhores condições de vida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I learned to cook out of necessity when I went to live on my own.", "tl": "Aprendi a cozinhar por necessidade quando fui morar sozinho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Nowadays, many people buy only the essentials out of necessity.", "tl": "Hoje em dia, muitas pessoas compram apenas o essencial por necessidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He had to change his diet out of necessity, after discovering a health problem.", "tl": "Ele teve de mudar a sua dieta por necessidade, depois de descobrir um problema de saúde."}]}, {"idiom_id": 401, "expression_id": 422, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "nos nossos dias", "english_gloss": "nowadays / in this day and age", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Nowadays, almost everyone uses their mobile phone to work.", "tl": "Nos nossos dias, quase toda a gente usa o telemóvel para trabalhar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is difficult to find time to relax in this day and age, as life is very fast-paced.", "tl": "É difícil encontrar tempo para relaxar nos nossos dias, pois a vida é muito rápida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Nowadays, speaking a second language is essential to get a good job.", "tl": "Nos nossos dias, falar uma segunda língua é essencial para conseguir um bom emprego."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Climate change is one of the biggest concerns in this day and age.", "tl": "As alterações climáticas são uma das maiores preocupações nos nossos dias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Nowadays, many people prefer to shop online instead of going to the shops.", "tl": "Nos nossos dias, muitas pessoas preferem fazer compras online em vez de ir às lojas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is very easy to share information in this day and age, but there is also a lot of fake news.", "tl": "É muito fácil partilhar informação nos nossos dias, mas também há muitas notícias falsas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 400, "expression_id": 421, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "por um lado... por outro lado", "english_gloss": "on one hand... on the other hand", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "On one hand, I would like to accept the new job; on the other hand, I will miss my current colleagues.", "tl": "Por um lado, eu gostava de aceitar o novo emprego; por outro lado, vou ter saudades dos meus colegas atuais."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "On one hand, living in the city is very convenient; on the other hand, the cost of living is very high.", "tl": "Por um lado, morar na cidade é muito conveniente; por outro lado, o custo de vida é muito alto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "On one hand, buying an electric car saves money on fuel; on the other hand, the purchase price is still high.", "tl": "Por um lado, comprar um carro elétrico poupa dinheiro em combustível; por outro lado, o preço de compra ainda é elevado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "On one hand, tourism helps the local economy; on the other hand, it brings a lot of noise and trash to the streets.", "tl": "Por um lado, o turismo ajuda a economia local; por outro lado, traz muito barulho e lixo para as ruas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "On one hand, social networks bring people closer; on the other hand, they can cause a lot of distraction and anxiety.", "tl": "Por um lado, as redes sociais aproximam as pessoas; por outro lado, podem causar muita distração e ansiedade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "On one hand, studying abroad is an excellent opportunity; on the other hand, it is difficult to live far from family.", "tl": "Por um lado, estudar no estrangeiro é uma excelente oportunidade; por outro lado, é difícil viver longe da família."}]}, {"idiom_id": 399, "expression_id": 420, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "do que costumavam", "english_gloss": "than they used to", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Nowadays, children play indoors more than they used to.", "tl": "Hoje em dia, as crianças brincam mais dentro de casa do que costumavam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Prices at the supermarket are much higher than they used to be.", "tl": "Os preços no supermercado estão muito mais altos do que costumavam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My grandparents travel much more now than they used to.", "tl": "Os meus avós viajam muito mais agora do que costumavam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Winters in this region are warmer than they used to be.", "tl": "Os invernos nesta região estão mais quentes do que costumavam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My friends send fewer messages than they used to.", "tl": "Os meus amigos mandam menos mensagens do que costumavam."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The employees of that company work more hours than they used to.", "tl": "Os funcionários daquela empresa trabalham mais horas do que costumavam."}]}, {"idiom_id": 398, "expression_id": 419, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "não há razão para que", "english_gloss": "there is no reason why", "youtube_id": "8lQ2JLqq0QA", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "There is no reason why the project shouldn't be delivered on time.", "tl": "Não há razão para que o projeto não seja entregue a tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "There is no reason why we should be worried about that now.", "tl": "Não há razão para que fiquemos preocupados com isso agora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There is no reason why the website shouldn't work today.", "tl": "Não há razão para que o site não funcione hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "There is no reason why the event should be canceled at the last minute.", "tl": "Não há razão para que o evento seja cancelado à última hora."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "There is no reason why you should argue over such a small thing.", "tl": "Não há razão para que vocês discutam por uma coisa tão pequena."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "There is no reason why he shouldn't get the job.", "tl": "Não há razão para que ele não consiga o emprego."}]}, {"idiom_id": 397, "expression_id": 418, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "termo de comparação", "english_gloss": "basis of comparison", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Without a basis of comparison, it's difficult to know if this computer is cheap or expensive.", "tl": "Sem um termo de comparação, é difícil saber se este computador está barato ou caro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To evaluate the success of the project, we need to use last year as a basis of comparison.", "tl": "Para avaliar o sucesso do projeto, precisamos de usar o ano passado como termo de comparação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Since he has never left his hometown, he has no other basis of comparison.", "tl": "Como ele nunca saiu da sua cidade natal, não tem outro termo de comparação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The doctor said that the first exam will serve as a basis of comparison for the next ones.", "tl": "O médico disse que o primeiro exame vai servir de termo de comparação para os próximos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The quality of this wine is so high that there is no basis of comparison in this price range.", "tl": "A qualidade deste vinho é tão alta que não existe nenhum termo de comparação nesta faixa de preço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is unfair to compare the two students because they don't have the same basis of comparison.", "tl": "É injusto comparar os dois alunos porque eles não têm o mesmo termo de comparação."}]}, {"idiom_id": 396, "expression_id": 417, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "um atrás do outro", "english_gloss": "one after another or in succession", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This morning, I received three important emails, one after another.", "tl": "Hoje de manhã, recebi três e-mails importantes, um atrás do outro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We watched the episodes of the new series, one after another, last weekend.", "tl": "Nós assistimos aos episódios da nova série, um atrás do outro, no último fim de semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "At my house, the children got sick, one after another.", "tl": "Na minha casa, as crianças ficaram doentes, uma atrás da outra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Three buses passed, one after another, but none was the one I needed to take.", "tl": "Passaram três ônibus, um atrás do outro, mas nenhum era o que eu precisava pegar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He was so hungry that he ate three sandwiches, one after another.", "tl": "Ele estava com tanta fome que comeu três sanduíches, um atrás do outro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This week was difficult because several problems arose, one after another.", "tl": "Esta semana foi difícil porque surgiram vários problemas, um atrás do outro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 395, "expression_id": 416, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "para valer", "english_gloss": "for real or seriously", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This year I'm going to start studying Spanish for real.", "tl": "Este ano eu vou começar a estudar espanhol para valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They had been dating for months, but now the commitment is for real.", "tl": "Eles namoravam há meses, mas agora o compromisso é para valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The storm hasn't started yet, but when it does, it's going to be for real.", "tl": "A tempestade ainda não começou, mas quando começar, vai ser para valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we want to open this company, we have to work seriously.", "tl": "Se quisermos abrir esta empresa, temos de trabalhar para valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Yesterday's game was just a practice, but tomorrow's is already for real.", "tl": "O jogo de ontem foi apenas um treino, mas o de amanhã já é para valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This time I'm going to join the gym and work out for real.", "tl": "Desta vez eu vou entrar na academia e treinar para valer."}]}, {"idiom_id": 394, "expression_id": 415, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "inadvertidamente", "english_gloss": "inadvertently or unintentionally", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sorry, I inadvertently deleted your message while cleaning out my inbox.", "tl": "Desculpe, eu apaguei a sua mensagem inadvertidamente enquanto limpava a minha caixa de entrada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "During the meeting, she inadvertently revealed the plans for the surprise party.", "tl": "Durante a reunião, ela revelou inadvertidamente os planos para a festa surpresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I inadvertently took the office key home.", "tl": "Eu levei a chave do escritório para casa inadvertidamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We inadvertently took the longer route because the GPS wasn't working well.", "tl": "Nós pegamos o caminho mais longo inadvertidamente porque o GPS não estava funcionando bem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The player inadvertently touched the ball with his hand, but the referee didn't call a foul.", "tl": "O jogador tocou a bola com a mão inadvertidamente, mas o árbitro não marcou falta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The report contained some errors because some old data was inadvertently included.", "tl": "O relatório continha alguns erros porque alguns dados antigos foram incluídos inadvertidamente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 393, "expression_id": 414, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "faz com que", "english_gloss": "causes or makes something happen", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Drinking water regularly makes your skin healthier.", "tl": "Beber água regularmente faz com que a tua pele fique mais saudável."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The heavy rain caused the flight to be canceled.", "tl": "A chuva forte fez com que o voo fosse cancelado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This new system makes it easier to organize daily work.", "tl": "Este novo sistema faz com que seja mais fácil organizar o trabalho diário."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Social media makes people feel more connected.", "tl": "As redes sociais fazem com que as pessoas se sintam mais conectadas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Drinking coffee in the late afternoon makes me unable to sleep at night.", "tl": "Tomar café ao fim da tarde faz com que eu não consiga dormir à noite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The lack of organization causes the project to cost more.", "tl": "A falta de organização faz com que o projeto custe mais caro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 392, "expression_id": 413, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "a céu aberto", "english_gloss": "open-air or outdoor", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the summer, I prefer to shop at the city's open-air market.", "tl": "No verão, prefiro fazer compras no mercado a céu aberto da cidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Yesterday we watched an open-air theater play in the park.", "tl": "Ontem assistimos a uma peça de teatro a céu aberto no parque."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This small historic town is like an open-air museum.", "tl": "Esta pequena vila histórica é como um museu a céu aberto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "During the trip, we decided to camp and sleep in the open air.", "tl": "Durante a viagem, decidimos acampar e dormir a céu aberto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The restaurant has a fantastic terrace for dining in the open air.", "tl": "O restaurante tem uma esplanada fantástica para jantar a céu aberto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The sculpture exhibition will take place outdoors in the botanical garden.", "tl": "A exposição de esculturas vai decorrer a céu aberto no jardim botânico."}]}, {"idiom_id": 391, "expression_id": 412, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vamos combinar que", "english_gloss": "let's face it or let's agree that", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Let's face it, yesterday's pizza was much better than today's.", "tl": "Vamos combinar que a pizza de ontem estava muito melhor que a de hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Let's agree that the boss doesn't have much patience for long meetings.", "tl": "Vamos combinar que o chefe não tem muita paciência para reuniões longas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Let's face it, traveling in winter is much cheaper, but the cold gets in the way a bit.", "tl": "Vamos combinar que viajar no inverno é bem mais barato, mas o frio atrapalha um pouco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Let's face it, learning Portuguese is not as easy as it seems.", "tl": "Vamos combinar que aprender português não é tão fácil quanto parece."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Let's agree that this new phone is beautiful, but the price is absurd.", "tl": "Vamos combinar que esse celular novo é bonito, mas o preço é absurdo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Let's face it, the end of the movie was quite disappointing, don't you think?", "tl": "Vamos combinar que o final do filme foi bem decepcionante, não acha?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 390, "expression_id": 411, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vendeu barato", "english_gloss": "sold out cheaply or undervalued", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He needed money urgently, so he sold his car very cheaply.", "tl": "Ele precisava de dinheiro urgente, por isso vendeu o carro muito barato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She accepted the first salary they offered; I think she undervalued herself.", "tl": "Ela aceitou o primeiro salário que ofereceram; acho que se vendeu barato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They wanted to get rid of the old furniture and sold everything cheaply online.", "tl": "Eles queriam se livrar dos móveis antigos e venderam tudo barato na internet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You are an excellent designer, you shouldn't sell yourself so cheaply to clients.", "tl": "Você é um excelente designer, não deveria se vender tão barato para os clientes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The real estate market was down, so he sold the apartment cheaply.", "tl": "O mercado imobiliário estava em baixa, então ele vendeu o apartamento barato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The inventor didn't know the value of his creation and sold the patent very cheaply.", "tl": "O inventor não sabia o valor da sua criação e vendeu a patente muito barato."}]}, {"idiom_id": 389, "expression_id": 410, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "voltar atrás", "english_gloss": "to backtrack or change one's mind", "youtube_id": "7TahKTbYmj4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He made a decision and now he can no longer go back on it.", "tl": "Ele tomou uma decisão e agora já não pode voltar atrás."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We had an agreement, so you can't go back on your word.", "tl": "Nós tínhamos um acordo, por isso não podes voltar atrás com a tua palavra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If I could go back in time, I would do everything differently.", "tl": "Se eu pudesse voltar atrás no tempo, faria tudo de maneira diferente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The company decided to cancel the project and there is no way to backtrack.", "tl": "A empresa decidiu cancelar o projeto e não há forma de voltar atrás."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She said she was going to the movies with us, but she ended up changing her mind.", "tl": "Ela disse que ia connosco ao cinema, mas acabou por voltar atrás."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Think carefully before signing the contract, because afterwards you won't be able to back out.", "tl": "Pensa bem antes de assinar o contrato, porque depois não vais conseguir voltar atrás."}]}, {"idiom_id": 388, "expression_id": 409, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "empoisonnent la vie", "english_gloss": "make life miserable / ruin", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "These minor administrative hassles have been making my life miserable for weeks.", "tl": "Ces petits soucis administratifs m'empoisonnent la vie depuis des semaines."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "His lack of self-confidence makes his daily life miserable.", "tl": "Son manque de confiance en lui lui empoisonne la vie au quotidien."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You shouldn't let stress at work ruin your life.", "tl": "Il ne faut pas laisser le stress au travail vous empoisonner la vie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The constant noise from the upstairs neighbors is making our lives miserable.", "tl": "Les bruits constants des voisins du dessus nous empoisonnent la vie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is often the small details that ruin our lives rather than the big problems.", "tl": "Ce sont souvent les petits détails qui nous empoisonnent la vie au lieu des grands problèmes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This family argument made my parents' lives miserable for years.", "tl": "Cette dispute familiale a empoisonné la vie de mes parents pendant des années."}]}, {"idiom_id": 387, "expression_id": 408, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "ferme complètement la porte", "english_gloss": "completely shuts the door (on someone)", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Please close the door completely so that the cat doesn't go out.", "tl": "S'il te plaît, ferme complètement la porte pour que le chat ne sorte pas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "With this new decision, the government is completely shutting the door to discussions.", "tl": "Avec cette nouvelle décision, le gouvernement ferme complètement la porte aux discussions."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After their last argument, she completely shut the door on a possible return.", "tl": "Après leur dernière dispute, elle a fermé complètement la porte à un éventuel retour."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You must close the door completely if you want the heating to work well.", "tl": "Tu dois fermer complètement la porte si tu veux que le chauffage fonctionne bien."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you refuse this job offer, you are completely shutting the door to other opportunities in this company.", "tl": "Si tu refuses cette offre d'emploi, tu fermes complètement la porte à d'autres opportunités dans cette entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The school principal completely shut the door on our trip project.", "tl": "Le directeur de l'école a fermé complètement la porte à notre projet de voyage."}]}, {"idiom_id": 386, "expression_id": 407, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "aux normes", "english_gloss": "up to code / compliant", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our apartment is no longer up to electrical code; we absolutely need to do some work.", "tl": "Notre appartement n'est plus aux normes électriques, il faut absolument faire des travaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The restaurant owner must quickly bring his kitchen up to hygiene standards.", "tl": "Le propriétaire du restaurant doit rapidement mettre sa cuisine aux normes d'hygiène."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Make sure this toy complies with European standards before buying it for your son.", "tl": "Assure-toi que ce jouet est bien aux normes européennes avant de l'acheter pour ton fils."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The new offices are fully up to code for welcoming people with disabilities.", "tl": "Les nouveaux bureaux sont entièrement aux normes pour l'accueil des personnes handicapées."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My car didn't pass inspection because the headlights weren't up to standard.", "tl": "Ma voiture n'est pas passée au contrôle technique car les phares n'étaient pas aux normes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Before selling the house, we need to check if all the plumbing is up to code.", "tl": "Avant de vendre la maison, nous devons vérifier si toute la plomberie est aux normes."}]}, {"idiom_id": 385, "expression_id": 406, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire en sorte que", "english_gloss": "to make sure that / ensure that", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I will make sure everything is ready for your arrival.", "tl": "Je vais faire en sorte que tout soit prêt pour ton arrivée."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Make sure the windows are closed before leaving.", "tl": "Faites en sorte que les fenêtres soient fermées avant de partir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He made sure his team won the match.", "tl": "Il a fait en sorte que son équipe gagne le match."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We must make sure that this problem does not happen again.", "tl": "Nous devons faire en sorte que ce problème ne se reproduise plus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She makes sure her children do their homework before dinner.", "tl": "Elle fait en sorte que ses enfants fassent leurs devoirs avant le dîner."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You should make sure that the dog doesn't get out of the garden.", "tl": "Tu devrais faire en sorte que le chien ne sorte pas du jardin."}]}, {"idiom_id": 384, "expression_id": 405, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à deux reprises", "english_gloss": "on two occasions / twice", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I tried calling him twice, but he didn't answer.", "tl": "J'ai essayé de l'appeler à deux reprises, mais il n'a pas répondu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She had to redo this report on two occasions before validating it.", "tl": "Elle a dû recommencer ce rapport à deux reprises avant de le valider."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We visited this museum twice during our stay in Paris.", "tl": "Nous avons visité ce musée à deux reprises lors de notre séjour à Paris."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The doctor advised him to take this medication on two occasions during the day.", "tl": "Le médecin lui a conseillé de prendre ce médicament à deux reprises dans la journée."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The train stopped twice right in the middle of the countryside.", "tl": "Le train s'est arrêté à deux reprises en plein milieu de la campagne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This young athlete won the gold medal on two occasions.", "tl": "Ce jeune athlète a remporté la médaille d'or à deux reprises."}]}, {"idiom_id": 383, "expression_id": 404, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "entre guillemets", "english_gloss": "so to speak / quote-unquote", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It's an \"easy\" job, so to speak, but it requires a lot of patience.", "tl": "C'est un travail facile, entre guillemets, mais cela demande beaucoup de patience."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They are on vacation, quote-unquote, since they spend the whole day working.", "tl": "Ils sont en vacances, entre guillemets, puisqu'ils passent toute la journée à travailler."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This movie is a \"masterpiece\", quote-unquote, but personally I found it very boring.", "tl": "Ce film est un chef-d'œuvre, entre guillemets, mais personnellement je l'ai trouvé très ennuyeux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I live in a \"castle\", so to speak, because my apartment is only twenty square meters.", "tl": "J'habite dans un château, entre guillemets, car mon appartement fait seulement vingt mètres carrés."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I exercise, quote-unquote, because I only walk ten minutes a day to go to work.", "tl": "Je fais du sport, entre guillemets, car je marche seulement dix minutes par jour pour aller au travail."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He is the \"boss\", so to speak, but in reality it's his assistant who makes all the decisions.", "tl": "C'est lui le chef, entre guillemets, mais c'est en réalité son assistante qui prend toutes les décisions."}]}, {"idiom_id": 382, "expression_id": 403, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "prend la parole", "english_gloss": "takes the floor / speaks publicly", "youtube_id": "1e270tPxeas", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When the director takes the floor, everyone listens to him attentively.", "tl": "Quand le directeur prend la parole, tout le monde l'écoute attentivement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She spoke up in front of the whole class to present her project.", "tl": "Elle a pris la parole devant toute la classe pour présenter son projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The mayor is going to speak publicly tonight to explain the new rules.", "tl": "Le maire va prendre la parole ce soir pour expliquer les nouvelles règles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I wish he would speak up more often during our team meetings.", "tl": "J'aimerais qu'il prenne la parole plus souvent lors de nos réunions d'équipe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Don't be shy, speak up and give your opinion on this subject.", "tl": "Ne sois pas timide, prends la parole et donne ton avis sur ce sujet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Every time he spoke publicly, he managed to convince his audience.", "tl": "Chaque fois qu'il prenait la parole, il arrivait à convaincre son public."}]}, {"idiom_id": 381, "expression_id": 402, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "gewuppt kriegt", "english_gloss": "manages to pull off", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry, our team is strong and will surely manage to pull off the new project.", "tl": "Keine Sorge, unser Team ist stark und kriegt das neue Projekt sicher gewuppt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I have a lot to do right now, but I will manage to get it done somehow.", "tl": "Ich habe gerade sehr viel zu tun, aber ich kriege das schon irgendwie gewuppt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We really have to study a lot this week if we want to pull off the difficult exam.", "tl": "Wir müssen diese Woche echt viel lernen, wenn wir die schwere Prüfung gewuppt kriegen wollen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The party was a complete success; I'm glad we managed to pull everything off so well.", "tl": "Die Party war ein voller Erfolg; ich bin froh, dass wir alles so gut gewuppt gekriegt haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Do you need help with the move, or can you manage to handle it on your own?", "tl": "Brauchst du Hilfe beim Umzug oder kriegst du das alleine gewuppt?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Without your financial support, we would have never managed to pull off the renovation of the apartment.", "tl": "Ohne deine finanzielle Unterstützung hätten wir die Renovierung der Wohnung nie gewuppt gekriegt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 380, "expression_id": 401, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "salonfähig machen", "english_gloss": "to make socially acceptable", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new party is trying to make extreme political ideas socially acceptable again.", "tl": "Die neue Partei versucht, extreme politische Ideen wieder salonfähig zu machen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "People used to wear sweatpants only at home, but fashion brands have made them socially acceptable.", "tl": "Früher trug man Jogginghosen nur zu Hause, aber Modemarken haben sie salonfähig gemacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The internet has made working from home socially acceptable.", "tl": "Das Internet hat das Arbeiten von zu Hause aus salonfähig gemacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This word used to be impolite, but television has made it socially acceptable.", "tl": "Dieses Wort war früher unhöflich, aber das Fernsehen hat es salonfähig gemacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is important that we make open conversations about mental health issues socially acceptable.", "tl": "Es ist wichtig, dass wir offene Gespräche über psychische Probleme salonfähig machen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Modern chefs have made simple street food acceptable in fancy restaurants too.", "tl": "Moderne Köche haben einfaches Streetfood auch in schicken Restaurants salonfähig gemacht."}]}, {"idiom_id": 379, "expression_id": 400, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "kaltstellen", "english_gloss": "to sideline / freeze out", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new department manager is trying to sideline her competitors.", "tl": "Die neue Abteilungsleiterin versucht, ihre Konkurrenten kaltzustellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Because he asked too many questions, the journalist was politically sidelined.", "tl": "Weil er zu viel gefragt hat, wurde der Journalist politisch kaltgestellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They simply froze me out and stopped inviting me to the important meetings.", "tl": "Sie haben mich einfach kaltgestellt und mich nicht mehr zu den wichtigen Treffen eingeladen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you state your opinion too loudly, you risk being sidelined in the project.", "tl": "Wenn du deine Meinung zu laut sagst, riskierst du, im Projekt kaltgestellt zu werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The board sidelined the troublesome employee by taking away all his tasks.", "tl": "Der Vorstand stellte den unbequemen Mitarbeiter kalt, indem er ihm alle Aufgaben wegnahm."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Watch out that they don't freeze you out of the party just because you have new ideas.", "tl": "Pass auf, dass sie dich in der Partei nicht kaltstellen, nur weil du neue Ideen hast."}]}, {"idiom_id": 378, "expression_id": 399, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "politisch ausschlachten", "english_gloss": "to exploit politically", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The opposition is trying to politically exploit the government's latest scandal.", "tl": "Die Opposition versucht, den jüngsten Skandal der Regierung politisch auszuschlachten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The accident was immediately exploited politically by some parties.", "tl": "Das Unglück wurde von einigen Parteien sofort politisch ausgeschlachtet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't think it's right to politically exploit people's fears.", "tl": "Ich finde es nicht gut, wenn man die Ängste der Menschen politisch ausschlachtet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The media has politically exploited this issue over the last few weeks.", "tl": "Die Medien haben dieses Thema in den letzten Wochen politisch ausgeschlachtet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The mayor is politically exploiting the crisis for his election campaign.", "tl": "Der Bürgermeister schlachtet die Krise für seinen Wahlkampf politisch aus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is sad to see how people are trying to politically exploit this tragedy.", "tl": "Es ist traurig zu sehen, wie versucht wird, diese Tragödie politisch auszuschlachten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 377, "expression_id": 398, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "bei guter Führung", "english_gloss": "for good behavior", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For good behavior, the prisoner can be released after just two years.", "tl": "Bei guter Führung kann der Gefangene schon nach zwei Jahren entlassen werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My lawyer says that for good behavior, I only have to serve half of the sentence.", "tl": "Mein Anwalt sagt, dass ich bei guter Führung nur die Hälfte der Strafe absitzen muss."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The judge emphasized that early release is only possible for good behavior.", "tl": "Der Richter betonte, dass eine vorzeitige Entlassung nur bei guter Führung möglich ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My parents said that for good behavior, I can go to the party on the weekend after all.", "tl": "Meine Eltern haben gesagt, dass ich bei guter Führung am Wochenende doch auf die Party darf."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In many countries, the prison sentence is automatically shortened for good behavior.", "tl": "In vielen Ländern wird die Haftstrafe bei guter Führung automatisch verkürzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The social worker explained to him what advantages he has in prison for good behavior.", "tl": "Der Sozialarbeiter erklärte ihm, welche Vorteile er bei guter Führung im Gefängnis hat."}]}, {"idiom_id": 376, "expression_id": 397, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "im Geschäft ist", "english_gloss": "has been in the business", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Since he has been in the business for ten years, he knows almost all the important people.", "tl": "Da er schon seit zehn Jahren im Geschäft ist, kennt er fast alle wichtigen Leute."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our company is new to the market, but our boss has been in the business for a long time.", "tl": "Unsere Firma ist neu auf dem Markt, aber unsere Chefin ist schon lange im Geschäft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When you have been in the business as long as she has, you don't lose your cool so easily.", "tl": "Wenn man so lange wie sie im Geschäft ist, verliert man nicht so schnell die Ruhe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My uncle, who has been in the business for over thirty years, often gives me good advice.", "tl": "Mein Onkel, der seit über dreißig Jahren im Geschäft ist, gibt mir oft gute Ratschläge."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is hard to believe that this young actor has been in the business since his childhood.", "tl": "Es ist schwer zu glauben, dass dieser junge Schauspieler schon seit seiner Kindheit im Geschäft ist."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She has only been in the business for a year, but she already works very professionally.", "tl": "Sie ist erst seit einem Jahr im Geschäft, aber sie arbeitet bereits sehr professionell."}]}, {"idiom_id": 375, "expression_id": 396, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "im großen Stil", "english_gloss": "on a large scale", "youtube_id": "7RE3yzy2ar8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The company plans to export its products abroad on a large scale.", "tl": "Das Unternehmen plant, seine Produkte im großen Stil ins Ausland zu exportieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They celebrated their wedding anniversary on a grand scale with over a hundred guests.", "tl": "Sie feierten ihren Hochzeitstag im großen Stil mit über hundert Gästen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The police are investigating fraud on a large scale in this case.", "tl": "Die Polizei ermittelt in diesem Fall wegen Betrugs im großen Stil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Vegetables are grown on a large scale in this region.", "tl": "In dieser Region wird Gemüse im großen Stil angebaut."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Only a few years ago did companies begin to introduce working from home on a large scale.", "tl": "Erst vor wenigen Jahren begannen Firmen, Homeoffice im großen Stil einzuführen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The city wants to modernize the old train stations on a large scale.", "tl": "Die Stadt will die alten Bahnhöfe im großen Stil modernisieren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 374, "expression_id": 395, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "jemanden bei Laune halten", "english_gloss": "to keep happy / in good spirits", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We need to keep the boss in good spirits with good coffee while we work on the project.", "tl": "Wir müssen den Chef mit gutem Kaffee bei Laune halten, während wir an dem Projekt arbeiten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "On long car rides, you have to keep the children happy with games and snacks.", "tl": "Auf langen Autofahrten muss man die Kinder mit Spielen und Snacks bei Laune halten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The waiter tried to keep the waiting guests in good spirits with free drinks.", "tl": "Der Kellner versuchte, die wartenden Gäste mit kostenlosen Getränken bei Laune zu halten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you want your friends to help you move, you have to keep them happy with pizza.", "tl": "Wenn du willst, dass deine Freunde dir beim Umzug helfen, musst du sie mit Pizza bei Laune halten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When learning German, I keep myself motivated with small rewards.", "tl": "Beim Deutschlernen halte ich mich selbst mit kleinen Belohnungen bei Laune."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The DJ played great music to keep the crowd in a good mood all evening.", "tl": "Der DJ spielte tolle Musik, um das Publikum den ganzen Abend bei Laune zu halten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 373, "expression_id": 394, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "das letzte Wort ist noch nicht gesprochen", "english_gloss": "the final word has not yet been spoken", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Although we lost the first game, the final word has not yet been spoken.", "tl": "Obwohl wir das erste Spiel verloren haben, ist das letzte Wort noch nicht gesprochen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss may have rejected the project, but the final word has not yet been spoken here.", "tl": "Der Chef hat das Projekt zwar abgelehnt, aber hier ist das letzte Wort noch nicht gesprochen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They want to break up, but I think the final word has not yet been spoken there.", "tl": "Sie wollen sich trennen, aber ich glaube, da ist das letzte Wort noch nicht gesprochen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The city wants to increase parking fees, but the final word has not yet been spoken.", "tl": "Die Stadt will die Parkgebühren erhöhen, aber das letzte Wort ist noch nicht gesprochen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My grade in math is bad, but the final word has not yet been spoken; there is still one exam left.", "tl": "Meine Note in Mathe ist schlecht, aber das letzte Wort ist noch nicht gesprochen; es gibt noch eine Prüfung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They sent me a rejection, but I am not giving up – the final word has not yet been spoken there.", "tl": "Sie haben mir eine Absage geschickt, aber ich gebe nicht auf – da ist das letzte Wort noch nicht gesprochen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 372, "expression_id": 393, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "nach gut Dünken", "english_gloss": "as one sees fit / at will", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You can add the spices as you see fit.", "tl": "Du kannst die Gewürze nach gut Dünken hinzufügen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In this project, employees are allowed to organize their working hours as they see fit.", "tl": "In diesem Projekt dürfen die Mitarbeiter ihre Arbeitszeit nach gut Dünken einteilen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You can decorate your room as you see fit.", "tl": "Du kannst dein Zimmer nach gut Dünken dekorieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The boss decides at his own discretion who gets the promotion.", "tl": "Der Chef entscheidet nach gut Dünken, wer die Beförderung bekommt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the vacation, we planned each day as we pleased.", "tl": "Während des Urlaubs haben wir jeden Tag nach gut Dünken geplant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You can shorten or expand the text as you see fit.", "tl": "Sie können den Text nach gut Dünken kürzen oder erweitern."}]}, {"idiom_id": 371, "expression_id": 392, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Groll hegen", "english_gloss": "to harbor a grudge", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He still harbors a grudge against his old boss because he wasn't promoted.", "tl": "Er hegt immer noch Groll gegen seinen alten Chef, weil er nicht befördert wurde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "There is no point in harboring a grudge for years; it only makes you unhappy.", "tl": "Es bringt nichts, jahrelang Groll zu hegen; das macht nur unglücklich."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Although they had a big fight, she doesn't hold any grudge against him.", "tl": "Obwohl sie sich heftig gestritten haben, hegt sie keinen Groll gegen ihn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Are you still holding a grudge over what happened last week?", "tl": "Hegst du immer noch Groll wegen der Sache von letzter Woche?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We shouldn't harbor a grudge, but rather talk openly about it.", "tl": "Wir sollten keinen Groll hegen, sondern lieber offen darüber sprechen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I never held a grudge against my parents, even if they were very strict.", "tl": "Ich habe nie Groll gegen meine Eltern gehegt, auch wenn sie sehr streng waren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 370, "expression_id": 391, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "den Gipfel überschatten", "english_gloss": "to overshadow the summit", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Dark clouds overshadow the summit, which is why the hikers had to turn back.", "tl": "Dunkle Wolken überschatten den Gipfel, weshalb die Wanderer umkehren mussten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "A serious dispute between the countries could overshadow the summit.", "tl": "Ein schwerer Streit zwischen den Ländern könnte den Gipfel überschatten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Large protests overshadowed the politicians' summit.", "tl": "Große Proteste überschatteten den Gipfel der Politiker."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Fog and heavy rain overshadowed the mountain's summit all day.", "tl": "Nebel und starker Regen überschatteten den Gipfel des Berges den ganzen Tag."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "New political conflicts overshadow the summit that begins today.", "tl": "Neue politische Konflikte überschatten den Gipfel, der heute beginnt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Nobody wanted these problems to overshadow the summit.", "tl": "Niemand wollte, dass diese Probleme den Gipfel überschatten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 369, "expression_id": 390, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich auswachsen", "english_gloss": "to develop/grow into", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry, this mild allergy will usually resolve itself as the children grow up.", "tl": "Keine Sorge, diese leichte Allergie wird sich bei Kindern meistens auswachsen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The minor argument between the neighbors quickly developed into a real war.", "tl": "Der kleine Streit zwischen den Nachbarn wuchs sich schnell zu einem echten Krieg aus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The small error in the system has grown into a huge problem.", "tl": "Der kleine Fehler im System hat sich zu einem riesigen Problem ausgewachsen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The doctor says that his bad posture will correct itself over time.", "tl": "Der Arzt sagt, dass sich seine krumme Haltung mit der Zeit auswachsen wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Over the years, the small workshop has grown into a successful company.", "tl": "Die kleine Werkstatt hat sich im Laufe der Jahre zu einem erfolgreichen Unternehmen ausgewachsen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "What started as a simple hobby is slowly growing into a full-time job.", "tl": "Was als einfaches Hobby begann, wächst sich langsam zu einem Vollzeitjob aus."}]}, {"idiom_id": 368, "expression_id": 389, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "unter Druck setzen", "english_gloss": "to put under pressure", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My boss is constantly putting me under pressure to finish the work faster.", "tl": "Mein Chef setzt mich ständig unter Druck, damit ich die Arbeit schneller fertigstelle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Parents shouldn't put their children under so much pressure because of their grades.", "tl": "Eltern sollten ihre Kinder wegen der Noten nicht so sehr unter Druck setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Please don't put me under pressure, I need some time for this decision.", "tl": "Bitte setz mich nicht unter Druck, ich brauche etwas Zeit für diese Entscheidung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The salesman tried to put us under pressure when we were buying the car.", "tl": "Der Verkäufer hat versucht, uns beim Autokauf unter Druck zu setzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The journalists put the politician under a lot of pressure with their questions.", "tl": "Die Journalisten setzten den Politiker mit ihren Fragen stark unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't want to put myself under pressure, but I have to pass this exam.", "tl": "Ich will mich nicht selbst unter Druck setzen, aber ich muss diese Prüfung bestehen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 367, "expression_id": 388, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Hin und Her", "english_gloss": "back and forth / constant vacillation", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After a lot of back and forth, we finally decided on the smaller apartment.", "tl": "Nach langem Hin und Her haben wir uns schließlich für die kleinere Wohnung entschieden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Because he was so nervous, he kept walking back and forth in the hallway.", "tl": "Weil er so nervös war, lief er im Flur ständig hin und her."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The daily back-and-forth between my apartment and work costs me a lot of time.", "tl": "Das tägliche Hin und Her zwischen meiner Wohnung und der Arbeit kostet mich viel Zeit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The constant back-and-forth with the appointments via email is really exhausting.", "tl": "Das ewige Hin und Her mit den Terminen per E-Mail ist wirklich anstrengend."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Put an end to the back-and-forth and just tell me if you want to come along or not.", "tl": "Mach dem Hin und Her ein Ende und sag mir einfach, ob du mitkommen willst oder nicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After a short back-and-forth, they agreed to split the costs.", "tl": "Nach einem kurzen Hin und Her haben sie sich darauf geeinigt, die Kosten zu teilen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 366, "expression_id": 387, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "am Rande des", "english_gloss": "on the sidelines of", "youtube_id": "7wp-pYwxgZ0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The two politicians spoke briefly with each other on the sidelines of the summit.", "tl": "Die beiden Politiker sprachen am Rande des Gipfels kurz miteinander."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The coach stood on the sidelines of the playing field during the entire game.", "tl": "Der Trainer stand während des ganzen Spiels am Rande des Spielfelds."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "On the fringes of the city festival, there were many small stalls.", "tl": "Am Rande des Stadtfests gab es viele kleine Verkaufsstände."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "On the sidelines of the meeting, important decisions were made.", "tl": "Am Rande des Treffens wurden wichtige Entscheidungen getroffen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The company was on the brink of ruin because of the crisis.", "tl": "Das Unternehmen stand wegen der Krise am Rande des Ruins."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This topic was only briefly mentioned on the sidelines of the seminar.", "tl": "Dieses Thema wurde am Rande des Seminars nur kurz erwähnt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 365, "expression_id": 386, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "einer Bitte nachgekommen", "english_gloss": "complied with a request", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Customer service quickly complied with our request and refunded the money.", "tl": "Der Kundenservice ist unserer Bitte schnell nachgekommen und hat das Geld erstattet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I would gladly comply with your request, but unfortunately I don't have the time for it.", "tl": "Ich würde Ihrer Bitte gerne nachkommen, aber mir fehlt leider die Zeit dafür."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My colleague complied with my request and closed the window.", "tl": "Mein Kollege ist meiner Bitte nachgekommen und hat das Fenster geschlossen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The city administration complied with the citizens' request to keep the park cleaner.", "tl": "Die Stadtverwaltung ist der Bitte der Bürger nachgekommen, den Park sauberer zu halten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you fill out the form, we will comply with your request immediately.", "tl": "Wenn Sie das Formular ausfüllen, werden wir Ihrer Bitte umgehend nachkommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Unfortunately, the boss did not comply with my request for a salary increase.", "tl": "Der Chef ist meiner Bitte nach einer Gehaltserhöhung leider nicht nachgekommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 364, "expression_id": 385, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "zur Disposition steht", "english_gloss": "is up for discussion / at risk of being eliminated", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our jobs are not up for discussion, the boss promised that.", "tl": "Unsere Arbeitsplätze stehen nicht zur Disposition, das hat der Chef versprochen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Because of the crisis, the budget for the new project is up for discussion.", "tl": "Wegen der Krise steht das Budget für das neue Projekt zur Disposition."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we don't find accommodation soon, our entire vacation is at risk.", "tl": "Wenn wir nicht bald eine Unterkunft finden, steht unser ganzer Urlaub zur Disposition."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Since too few students have signed up, the class trip is up for debate.", "tl": "Da sich zu wenige Schüler angemeldet haben, steht die Klassenfahrt zur Disposition."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Sunday shopping hours in this city are up for discussion.", "tl": "Die Sonntagsöffnung der Geschäfte steht in dieser Stadt zur Disposition."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Whether we are moving next year is not up for discussion at the moment.", "tl": "Ob wir nächstes Jahr umziehen, steht im Moment nicht zur Disposition."}]}, {"idiom_id": 363, "expression_id": 384, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "euch querstellt", "english_gloss": "dig your heels in / oppose / stonewall", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you dig your heels in on this project, we won't be able to meet the deadline.", "tl": "Wenn ihr euch bei diesem Projekt querstellt, werden wir den Termin nicht einhalten können."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Please don't dig your heels in, we all need to work together now.", "tl": "Bitte stellt euch nicht quer, wir müssen jetzt alle zusammenarbeiten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Why are you opposing the new working hours?", "tl": "Warum stellt ihr euch quer, wenn es um die neuen Arbeitszeiten geht?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "There is no point in digging your heels in; the decision has already been made.", "tl": "Es bringt nichts, euch querzustellen; die Entscheidung ist bereits getroffen worden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't understand why you dug your heels in so much during the meeting yesterday.", "tl": "Ich verstehe nicht, warum ihr euch gestern bei der Besprechung so quergestellt habt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You don't always have to dig your heels in as soon as someone makes a new suggestion.", "tl": "Ihr müsst euch nicht immer querstellen, sobald jemand einen neuen Vorschlag macht."}]}, {"idiom_id": 362, "expression_id": 383, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in Frage stellt", "english_gloss": "calls into question / challenges", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My boss often calls my decision into question.", "tl": "Mein Chef stellt meine Entscheidung oft in Frage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "There is no one in the company who challenges the new rules.", "tl": "Es gibt niemanden in der Firma, der die neuen Regeln in Frage stellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new study has completely called the old results into question.", "tl": "Die neue Studie hat die alten Ergebnisse komplett in Frage gestellt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is important not to always call everything into question immediately.", "tl": "Es ist wichtig, nicht immer alles sofort in Frage zu stellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We shouldn't question his honesty.", "tl": "Wir sollten seine Ehrlichkeit nicht in Frage stellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This crisis calls our entire future into question.", "tl": "Diese Krise stellt unsere ganze Zukunft in Frage."}]}, {"idiom_id": 361, "expression_id": 382, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "um die Ecke kommen", "english_gloss": "to suddenly come up with / present unexpectedly", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Now that the project is almost finished, he suddenly comes up with new requirements.", "tl": "Jetzt, wo das Projekt fast fertig ist, kommt er plötzlich mit neuen Anforderungen um die Ecke."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My sister always comes up with a better idea at the last moment.", "tl": "Meine Schwester kommt immer im letzten Moment mit einer besseren Idee um die Ecke."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You don't need to come up with a cheap excuse yet again.", "tl": "Du musst nicht schon wieder mit einer billigen Ausrede um die Ecke kommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The competition suddenly came up with a much cheaper offer.", "tl": "Die Konkurrenz ist plötzlich mit einem viel günstigeren Angebot um die Ecke gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Every time we plan a vacation, he suddenly comes up with a new problem.", "tl": "Jedes Mal, wenn wir einen Urlaub planen, kommt er mit einem neuen Problem um die Ecke."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After hours of thinking, our boss finally came up with the perfect solution.", "tl": "Nach stundenlangem Nachdenken kam unsere Chefin endlich mit der perfekten Lösung um die Ecke."}]}, {"idiom_id": 360, "expression_id": 381, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt", "english_gloss": "agreed on a compromise", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After a long discussion, the two parties finally agreed on a compromise.", "tl": "Nach einer langen Diskussion haben sich die beiden Parteien endlich auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We couldn't agree on the price at first, but in the end we agreed on a compromise.", "tl": "Wir konnten uns beim Preis zuerst nicht einigen, aber am Ende haben wir uns auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Have you already agreed on a compromise in the team?", "tl": "Habt ihr euch im Team schon auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The union and the employers agreed on a compromise yesterday.", "tl": "Die Gewerkschaft und die Arbeitgeber haben sich gestern auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It wasn't easy, but my parents finally agreed on a compromise.", "tl": "Es war nicht leicht, aber meine Eltern haben sich schließlich auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Fortunately, we quickly agreed on a compromise, so we can start right away.", "tl": "Glücklicherweise haben wir uns schnell auf einen Kompromiss geeinigt, sodass wir direkt anfangen können."}]}, {"idiom_id": 359, "expression_id": 380, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "das Ruder herumzureißen", "english_gloss": "to turn things around / steer a different course", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The company was on the verge of bankruptcy, but the new boss managed to turn things around.", "tl": "Die Firma stand kurz vor der Pleite, aber der neue Chef konnte das Ruder noch herumreißen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After the bad grades in the first half of the year, she tried to turn things around.", "tl": "Nach den schlechten Noten im ersten Halbjahr versuchte sie, das Ruder herumzureißen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our team was behind, but in the second half we turned things around and won the game.", "tl": "Unsere Mannschaft lag zurück, aber in der zweiten Halbzeit rissen wir das Ruder herum und gewannen das Spiel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is never too late to turn things around and start a healthier life.", "tl": "Es ist nie zu spät, das Ruder herumzureißen und ein gesünderes Leben zu beginnen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The project is not going well, we need to turn things around quickly now.", "tl": "Das Projekt läuft nicht gut, wir müssen jetzt schnell das Ruder herumreißen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In order to stop climate change, we urgently need to turn things around.", "tl": "Um den Klimawandel zu stoppen, müssen wir dringend das Ruder herumreißen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 358, "expression_id": 379, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Stellen gestrichen", "english_gloss": "jobs cut / positions eliminated", "youtube_id": "nl6ejwZACbI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Because of the crisis, many jobs were cut at the bank.", "tl": "Wegen der Krise wurden bei der Bank viele Stellen gestrichen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The company needs to save money and wants to cut a hundred jobs next year.", "tl": "Die Firma muss sparen und will nächstes Jahr hundert Stellen streichen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I heard that no jobs are being cut in our department.", "tl": "Ich habe gehört, dass in unserer Abteilung keine Stellen gestrichen werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Unfortunately, many positions were cut after the merger.", "tl": "Nach der Fusion sind leider viele Stellen gestrichen worden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If even more jobs are cut, we won't be able to get the work done.", "tl": "Wenn noch mehr Stellen gestrichen werden, können wir die Arbeit nicht mehr schaffen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The trade union is protesting against the plan to cut so many jobs.", "tl": "Die Gewerkschaft protestiert dagegen, dass so viele Stellen gestrichen werden sollen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 357, "expression_id": 378, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "rispetto al", "english_gloss": "compared to / in comparison with", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This year rent prices have increased a lot compared to last year.", "tl": "Quest'anno i prezzi degli affitti sono aumentati molto rispetto all'anno scorso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Today it is much colder compared to usual.", "tl": "Oggi fa molto più freddo rispetto al solito."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new software is much faster compared to the old program.", "tl": "Il nuovo software è molto più veloce rispetto al vecchio programma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My Italian level has improved a lot compared to last month.", "tl": "Il mio livello di italiano è migliorato molto rispetto al mese scorso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The current situation is very different compared to the past.", "tl": "La situazione attuale è molto diversa rispetto al passato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Compared to his brother, Marco does much more sport.", "tl": "Rispetto al fratello, Marco fa molto più sport."}]}, {"idiom_id": 356, "expression_id": 377, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "bastare perché", "english_gloss": "to take only... for / to be enough to", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It only takes a look for him to understand everything.", "tl": "Basta uno sguardo perché lui capisca tutto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It only took a small mistake for the computer to turn off.", "tl": "È bastato un piccolo errore perché il computer si spegnesse."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It will only take a phone call from you for me to run to help you.", "tl": "Basterà una tua telefonata perché io corra ad aiutarti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It only took one sunny day for the flowers to bloom.", "tl": "È bastata una giornata di sole perché i fiori sbocciassero."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It only takes a silly thing for them to start arguing.", "tl": "Basta una sciocchezza perché loro inizino a litigare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It would only take a bit of goodwill for the project to work.", "tl": "Basterebbe un po' di buona volontà perché il progetto funzionasse."}]}, {"idiom_id": 355, "expression_id": 376, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "un paio di", "english_gloss": "a couple of", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I bought a pair of new shoes for my brother's wedding.", "tl": "Ho comprato un paio di scarpe nuove per il matrimonio di mio fratello."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I need a couple of days to finish this project.", "tl": "Ho bisogno di un paio di giorni per finire questo progetto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Add a couple of garlic cloves to the sauce to give it more flavor.", "tl": "Aggiungi un paio di spicchi d'aglio alla salsa per dare più sapore."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Can I ask you a couple of questions about your new job?", "tl": "Posso farti un paio di domande sul tuo nuovo lavoro?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We will spend a couple of weeks in Tuscany this summer.", "tl": "Passeremo un paio di settimane in Toscana quest'estate."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't forget to bring a couple of warm sweaters, it gets cold in the mountains in the evening.", "tl": "Non dimenticare di portare un paio di maglioni pesanti, la sera fa freddo in montagna."}]}, {"idiom_id": 354, "expression_id": 375, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "negli ultimi tempi", "english_gloss": "lately / in recent times", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Lately I've been working too much and I feel very tired.", "tl": "Negli ultimi tempi ho lavorato troppo e mi sento molto stanco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The weather has been really strange lately, it's warm even in winter.", "tl": "Il tempo è stato davvero strano negli ultimi tempi, fa caldo anche d'inverno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In recent times I have started doing yoga to relax.", "tl": "Negli ultimi tempi ho iniziato a fare yoga per rilassarmi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I've noticed that Marco has been very quiet lately, I hope he's doing well.", "tl": "Ho notato che Marco è molto silenzioso negli ultimi tempi, spero stia bene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Prices in supermarkets have increased quite a bit in recent times.", "tl": "I prezzi nei supermercati sono aumentati parecchio negli ultimi tempi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Lately I prefer watching TV series instead of movies.", "tl": "Negli ultimi tempi preferisco guardare le serie TV invece dei film."}]}, {"idiom_id": 353, "expression_id": 374, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "andare bene", "english_gloss": "to go well / be successful", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry, I am sure everything will go well.", "tl": "Non ti preoccupare, sono sicuro che tutto andrà bene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "How did yesterday's exam go? It went well, thank you!", "tl": "Com'è andato l'esame di ieri? È andato bene, grazie!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Shall we meet at five in front of the cinema? Does that work for you?", "tl": "Ci incontriamo alle cinque davanti al cinema? Ti va bene?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I really hope your job interview goes well.", "tl": "Spero davvero che il tuo colloquio di lavoro vada bene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It would also be fine with me to have dinner at home tonight, if you are tired.", "tl": "Per me andrebbe bene anche cenare a casa stasera, se sei stanco."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Things didn't go well at the beginning, but then the situation improved.", "tl": "Le cose non sono andate bene all'inizio, ma poi la situazione è migliorata."}]}, {"idiom_id": 352, "expression_id": 373, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "dare lavoro a", "english_gloss": "to provide jobs for / employ", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new factory on the outskirts will provide jobs for more than a hundred people.", "tl": "La nuova fabbrica in periferia darà lavoro a più di cento persone."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Summer tourism provides jobs for many university students.", "tl": "Il turismo estivo dà lavoro a molti studenti universitari."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In the eighties, that big company provided jobs for the entire province.", "tl": "Negli anni Ottanta, quella grande azienda dava lavoro a tutta la provincia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We hope this project can provide jobs for many young people in the area.", "tl": "Speriamo che questo progetto possa dare lavoro a molti giovani della zona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The municipality decided to fund a cooperative that has provided jobs for ten unemployed people.", "tl": "Il comune ha deciso di finanziare una cooperativa che ha dato lavoro a dieci disoccupati."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Opening a new supermarket in the neighborhood could provide jobs for several families.", "tl": "Aprire un nuovo supermercato nel quartiere potrebbe dare lavoro a diverse famiglie."}]}, {"idiom_id": 351, "expression_id": 372, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "sul campo", "english_gloss": "in the field / hands-on", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I learned much more working in the field than reading textbooks.", "tl": "Ho imparato molto di più lavorando sul campo che leggendo i libri di testo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The journalist preferred to go on the ground to verify the news in person.", "tl": "Il giornalista ha preferito andare sul campo per verificare la notizia di persona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Archeologists spend many months a year doing field research.", "tl": "Gli archeologi passano molti mesi all'anno a fare ricerche sul campo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It doesn't matter what the statistics say, the match is always decided on the pitch.", "tl": "Non importa cosa dicono le statistiche, la partita si decide sempre sul campo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our company offers practical training directly in the field.", "tl": "La nostra azienda offre una formazione pratica direttamente sul campo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The Red Cross volunteers are already working on the ground to help the residents.", "tl": "I volontari della Croce Rossa stanno già lavorando sul campo per aiutare i residenti."}]}, {"idiom_id": 350, "expression_id": 371, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "provarci", "english_gloss": "to try (to do something)", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I know the exam is difficult, but I still want to try.", "tl": "So che l'esame è difficile, ma voglio comunque provarci."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I tried to fix the tap, but I didn't succeed. At least I tried!", "tl": "Ho provato a riparare il rubinetto, ma non ci sono riuscito. Almeno ci ho provato!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Come on, give it a shot! You have nothing to lose.", "tl": "Dai, provaci! Non hai nulla da perdere."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If they offered you that job abroad, would you go for it?", "tl": "Se ti offrissero quel lavoro all'estero, ci proveresti?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We know it's a complicated project, but we are giving it our best shot.", "tl": "Sappiamo che è un progetto complicato, ma ci proviamo con tutto l'impegno possibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It's not easy to change habits, but it's worth trying.", "tl": "Non è facile cambiare abitudini, ma vale la pena provarci."}]}, {"idiom_id": 349, "expression_id": 370, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "tenere in piedi", "english_gloss": "to keep going / sustain", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is difficult to keep a business going with these taxes.", "tl": "È difficile tenere in piedi un'attività commerciale con queste tasse."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Only the love for their children keeps their marriage going.", "tl": "Solo l'amore per i figli tiene in piedi il loro matrimonio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I need a strong coffee; it's the only thing keeping me going today.", "tl": "Ho bisogno di un caffè forte, è l'unica cosa che mi tiene in piedi oggi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't know how they manage to keep this project going without funds.", "tl": "Non so come facciano a tenere in piedi questo progetto senza fondi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Despite the flu, he took some medicine that kept him on his feet all evening.", "tl": "Nonostante l'influenza, ha preso una medicina che lo ha tenuto in piedi tutta la sera."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We are the ones who keep the entire association going with our work.", "tl": "Siamo noi con il nostro lavoro che teniamo in piedi l'intera associazione."}]}, {"idiom_id": 348, "expression_id": 369, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "nel giro di", "english_gloss": "within / in the space of", "youtube_id": "Vre4AjCfxl8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The weather will change within a few hours, so I advise you to bring an umbrella.", "tl": "Il tempo cambierà nel giro di poche ore, quindi ti consiglio di portare l'ombrello."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I hope to solve this work issue within a week.", "tl": "Spero di risolvere questo problema di lavoro nel giro di una settimana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The police arrived on the scene within ten minutes of the call.", "tl": "La polizia è arrivata sul posto nel giro di dieci minuti dalla chiamata."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This neighborhood has changed a lot in the space of a few years.", "tl": "Questo quartiere è cambiato moltissimo nel giro di pochi anni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He spent all his savings in a matter of just a few days.", "tl": "Ha speso tutti i suoi risparmi nel giro di pochissimi giorni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We will receive the test results within a month.", "tl": "Riceveremo i risultati del test nel giro di un mese."}]}, {"idiom_id": 347, "expression_id": 368, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "tutto sommato", "english_gloss": "all things considered / all in all", "youtube_id": "O8WJ8QvH8AI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The weather wasn't great, but all in all it was a nice holiday.", "tl": "Il tempo non è stato bellissimo, ma tutto sommato è stata una bella vacanza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I didn't study much, so all things considered, I'm happy with this grade.", "tl": "Non ho studiato molto, quindi tutto sommato questo voto mi va bene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new job is tiring, but all in all I get along well with my colleagues.", "tl": "Il nuovo lavoro è faticoso, ma tutto sommato mi trovo bene con i colleghi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This restaurant is a bit expensive, but all things considered, the food is very good.", "tl": "Questo ristorante è un po' caro, ma tutto sommato si mangia molto bene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Living in the suburbs has its disadvantages, but all in all I prefer the peace and quiet.", "tl": "Vivere in periferia ha i suoi svantaggi, ma tutto sommato preferisco la tranquillità."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I still have a bit of a fever, but all things considered, I feel better today.", "tl": "Ho ancora un po' di febbre, ma tutto sommato oggi mi sento meglio."}]}, {"idiom_id": 346, "expression_id": 367, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "gioco delle parti", "english_gloss": "role-play / theatrical behavior", "youtube_id": "O8WJ8QvH8AI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In business negotiations, arguing over the price is just part of the game of roles.", "tl": "Nelle trattative di lavoro, discutere sul prezzo fa parte del gioco delle parti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The debate between the two politicians was just a role-play; behind the scenes they get along.", "tl": "Il dibattito tra i due politici era solo un gioco delle parti: dietro le quinte vanno d'accordo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Playing good cop and bad cop with the kids is the classic game of roles.", "tl": "Fare il poliziotto buono e quello cattivo con i figli è il classico gioco delle parti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't want to get into this game of roles; I would just like an honest answer.", "tl": "Non voglio entrare in questo gioco delle parti, vorrei solo una risposta sincera."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "At the beginning of a relationship, there is always a bit of role-playing to make a good impression.", "tl": "All'inizio di una relazione c'è sempre un po' di gioco delle parti per fare buona impressione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In court, the clash between prosecution and defense is part of a precise game of roles.", "tl": "In tribunale, lo scontro tra accusa e difesa fa parte di un preciso gioco delle parti."}]}, {"idiom_id": 345, "expression_id": 366, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "lasciare il tempo che trova", "english_gloss": "to be of little consequence / not matter much", "youtube_id": "O8WJ8QvH8AI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "His criticisms are of little consequence, you shouldn't worry about them.", "tl": "Le sue critiche lasciano il tempo che trovano, non dovresti preoccupartene."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Long-term weather forecasts are often of little consequence.", "tl": "Le previsioni del tempo a lungo termine spesso lasciano il tempo che trovano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Unfortunately, promises made during an election campaign don't mean much.", "tl": "Le promesse fatte in campagna elettorale purtroppo lasciano il tempo che trovano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His advice is of little consequence, given that he has no experience in this field.", "tl": "Il suo consiglio lascia il tempo che trova, visto che non ha esperienza in questo campo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This new rule without enforcement doesn't mean much.", "tl": "Questa nuova regola senza controlli lascia il tempo che trova."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "His apologies don't mean much by now.", "tl": "Le sue scuse ormai lasciano il tempo che trovano."}]}, {"idiom_id": 344, "expression_id": 365, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "andare fino in fondo", "english_gloss": "to go all the way / see something through", "youtube_id": "O8WJ8QvH8AI", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We have started this project now and we have to see it through to the end.", "tl": "Ormai abbiamo iniziato questo progetto e dobbiamo andare fino in fondo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I want to find out who lost those keys, I will get to the bottom of this story.", "tl": "Voglio scoprire chi ha perso quelle chiavi, andrò fino in fondo a questa storia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you decide to enroll in university, you have to be ready to go all the way.", "tl": "Se decidi di iscriverti all'università, devi essere pronto ad andare fino in fondo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They weren't convinced about selling the house, but in the end, they went through with it.", "tl": "Non erano convinti di vendere la casa, ma alla fine sono andati fino in fondo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I can't give up right now, I want to see this through to the end.", "tl": "Non posso arrendermi proprio adesso, voglio andare fino in fondo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Do you really think they will go all the way with their protest?", "tl": "Pensi davvero che andranno fino in fondo con la loro protesta?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 343, "expression_id": 364, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "sono il frutto di", "english_gloss": "are the result of", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "His professional successes are the result of years of sacrifice.", "tl": "I suoi successi lavorativi sono il frutto di anni di sacrifici."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "These excellent grades are the result of constant commitment to studying.", "tl": "Questi ottimi voti sono il frutto di un costante impegno nello studio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company's new ideas are the result of close collaboration between departments.", "tl": "Le nuove idee dell'azienda sono il frutto di una stretta collaborazione tra i reparti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Her physical progress is the result of a healthy diet and a lot of exercise.", "tl": "I suoi progressi fisici sono il frutto di una dieta sana e di tanto sport."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This artist's works are the result of a long personal exploration.", "tl": "Le opere di questo artista sono il frutto di una lunga ricerca personale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The city's current problems are the result of decisions made many years ago.", "tl": "I problemi attuali della città sono il frutto di decisioni prese molti anni fa."}]}, {"idiom_id": 342, "expression_id": 363, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "coni d'ombra", "english_gloss": "shadow zones / blind spots", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The car's rearview mirrors help reduce blind spots while driving.", "tl": "Gli specchietti retrovisori della macchina aiutano a ridurre i coni d'ombra durante la guida."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Despite the police investigation, there are still many shadow zones in this story.", "tl": "Nonostante le indagini della polizia, ci sono ancora molti coni d'ombra in questa storia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new privacy law leaves some grey areas that need to be cleared up as soon as possible.", "tl": "La nuova legge sulla privacy lascia alcuni coni d'ombra che vanno chiariti al più presto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We all have blind spots in our character that we prefer not to show to others.", "tl": "Tutti noi abbiamo dei coni d'ombra nel nostro carattere che preferiamo non mostrare agli altri."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new router has improved the connection, eliminating the dead zones in the house.", "tl": "Il nuovo router ha migliorato la connessione, eliminando i coni d'ombra in casa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The photographer used special lights to avoid shadow zones on the model's face.", "tl": "Il fotografo ha usato delle luci speciali per evitare i coni d'ombra sul viso della modella."}]}, {"idiom_id": 341, "expression_id": 362, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "un vero groviglio", "english_gloss": "a real tangle", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After a windy day at the beach, my hair was a real tangle.", "tl": "Dopo una giornata di vento al mare, i miei capelli erano un vero groviglio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Behind the television, there is a real tangle of cables that I absolutely need to organize.", "tl": "Dietro alla televisione c'è un vero groviglio di cavi che devo assolutamente sistemare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Trying to get that document is a real bureaucratic tangle.", "tl": "Cercare di ottenere quel documento è un vero groviglio burocratico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The streets of this old town are a real tangle in which it is easy to get lost.", "tl": "Le strade di questa città vecchia sono un vero groviglio in cui è facile perdersi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "At the moment my head is a real tangle of thoughts and worries.", "tl": "In questo momento la mia testa è un vero groviglio di pensieri e preoccupazioni."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The plot of that mystery movie is a real tangle, I wasn't able to understand the ending.", "tl": "La trama di quel film giallo è un vero groviglio, non sono riuscito a capire il finale."}]}, {"idiom_id": 340, "expression_id": 361, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "calarsi dentro", "english_gloss": "to immerse oneself in", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To play this character, the actor must immerse himself in his complex psychology.", "tl": "Per interpretare questo personaggio, l'attore deve calarsi dentro la sua complessa psicologia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I immersed myself in the story from the very first pages of the novel.", "tl": "Mi sono calato dentro la storia fin dalle prime pagine del romanzo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When you travel, you should immerse yourself in the local culture to truly understand the country.", "tl": "Quando viaggi, dovresti calarti dentro la cultura locale per capire davvero il paese."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To understand the employees' problems, the boss must immerse himself in their daily routine.", "tl": "Per capire i problemi dei dipendenti, il capo deve calarsi dentro la loro routine quotidiana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This multimedia museum allows you to immerse yourself in the atmosphere of the Middle Ages.", "tl": "Questo museo multimediale ti permette di calarti dentro l'atmosfera del Medioevo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Before starting the project, we need to immerse ourselves in our clients' mindset.", "tl": "Prima di iniziare il progetto, dobbiamo calarci dentro la mentalità dei nostri clienti."}]}, {"idiom_id": 339, "expression_id": 360, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "al contrario di quanto", "english_gloss": "contrary to what", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Contrary to what the weather forecast said, today it is very sunny.", "tl": "Al contrario di quanto dicevano le previsioni, oggi c'è un bellissimo sole."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Contrary to what you think, I really like spending time with my family.", "tl": "Al contrario di quanto pensi, mi piace molto passare il tempo con la mia famiglia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The project was easy to complete, contrary to what we feared.", "tl": "Il progetto è stato facile da completare, al contrario di quanto temevamo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Contrary to what many believe, skipping breakfast is not always bad for you.", "tl": "Al contrario di quanto molti credono, saltare la colazione non fa sempre male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Contrary to what was written in the newspapers, the shop will not close.", "tl": "Al contrario di quanto è stato scritto sui giornali, il negozio non chiuderà."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Contrary to what I expected, the train journey was very comfortable.", "tl": "Al contrario di quanto mi aspettavo, il viaggio in treno è stato molto comodo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 338, "expression_id": 359, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "in gran parte", "english_gloss": "largely", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The success of the project largely depends on teamwork.", "tl": "Il successo del progetto dipende in gran parte dal lavoro di squadra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The holidays were largely ruined by the continuous rain.", "tl": "Le vacanze sono state rovinate in gran parte dalla pioggia continua."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I largely agree with what you said during the meeting.", "tl": "Concordo in gran parte con quello che hai detto durante la riunione."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The travel expenses were largely covered by the company.", "tl": "Le spese di viaggio sono state in gran parte coperte dall'azienda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The city's population is largely made up of young students.", "tl": "La popolazione della città è composta in gran parte da giovani studenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "His recovery is largely due to his positive attitude.", "tl": "Il suo recupero è dovuto in gran parte al suo atteggiamento positivo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 337, "expression_id": 358, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "dal punto di vista", "english_gloss": "from the point of view", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "From my point of view, this is the best solution for everyone.", "tl": "Dal mio punto di vista, questa è la soluzione migliore per tutti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "From an economic point of view, the project is not very cost-effective.", "tl": "Dal punto di vista economico, il progetto non è molto conveniente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We must also consider the situation from the customers' point of view.", "tl": "Dobbiamo considerare la situazione anche dal punto di vista dei clienti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "From a health standpoint, doing sports every day is very good for you.", "tl": "Dal punto di vista della salute, fare sport ogni giorno fa benissimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I understand your opinion, but from my point of view things are different.", "tl": "Capisco la tua opinione, ma dal mio punto di vista le cose stanno diversamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The movie is very beautiful from a visual point of view, but the plot is weak.", "tl": "Il film è molto bello dal punto di vista visivo, ma la trama è debole."}]}, {"idiom_id": 336, "expression_id": 357, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "in larga maggioranza", "english_gloss": "by a large majority", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The citizens voted by a large majority in favor of the new public park.", "tl": "I cittadini hanno votato in larga maggioranza a favore del nuovo parco pubblico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The school's students are, by a large majority, against the school uniform.", "tl": "Gli studenti della scuola sono, in larga maggioranza, contrari alla divisa scolastica."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company's employees chose by a large majority to continue working from home.", "tl": "I dipendenti dell'azienda hanno scelto in larga maggioranza di continuare a lavorare da casa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "According to the latest survey, young people are by a large majority optimistic about the future.", "tl": "Secondo l'ultimo sondaggio, i giovani sono in larga maggioranza ottimisti sul futuro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the building meeting, the residents decided by a large majority to renovate the facade.", "tl": "Durante l'assemblea di condominio, i residenti hanno deciso in larga maggioranza di ristrutturare la facciata."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In this country, consumers by a large majority prefer to buy local products.", "tl": "In questo paese, i consumatori preferiscono in larga maggioranza acquistare prodotti locali."}]}, {"idiom_id": 335, "expression_id": 356, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "punto di riferimento", "english_gloss": "point of reference", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My grandfather has always been a point of reference for the whole family.", "tl": "Mio nonno è sempre stato un punto di riferimento per tutta la famiglia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The old bell tower is the only landmark visible from afar.", "tl": "Il vecchio campanile è l'unico punto di riferimento visibile da lontano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That clinic has become a point of reference for the treatment of heart diseases.", "tl": "Quella clinica è diventata un punto di riferimento per la cura delle malattie cardiache."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In difficult times, Marco is my main point of reference.", "tl": "Nei momenti difficili, Marco è il mio punto di riferimento principale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This book represents an important point of reference for modern literature.", "tl": "Questo libro rappresenta un punto di riferimento importante per la letteratura moderna."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The company aims to become a point of reference in the technology sector.", "tl": "L'azienda punta a diventare un punto di riferimento nel settore della tecnologia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 334, "expression_id": 355, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "bottino di guerra", "english_gloss": "spoils of war", "youtube_id": "q4NaBl2X3AM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The soldiers returned home bringing with them a rich spoil of war.", "tl": "I soldati tornarono a casa portando con sé un ricco bottino di guerra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After the winter sales, my sister came home with many clothes, saying it was her spoils of war.", "tl": "Dopo i saldi invernali, mia sorella è tornata a casa con molti vestiti, dicendo che era il suo bottino di guerra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many of the paintings exhibited in this museum were originally spoils of war.", "tl": "Molti dei quadri esposti in questo museo erano originariamente un bottino di guerra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We won the school tournament and this cup is our spoils of war.", "tl": "Abbiamo vinto il torneo scolastico e questa coppa è il nostro bottino di guerra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During antiquity, conquered territories were often considered simple spoils of war.", "tl": "Durante l'antichità, i territori conquistati venivano spesso considerati un semplice bottino di guerra."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The children took all the party sweets and hid their spoils of war under the bed.", "tl": "I bambini hanno preso tutti i dolci della festa e hanno nascosto il loro bottino di guerra sotto il letto."}]}, {"idiom_id": 333, "expression_id": 354, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "d'une façon ou d'une autre", "english_gloss": "one way or another / somehow", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry, we will find a solution one way or another.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, nous allons trouver une solution d'une façon ou d'une autre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He always manages to get what he wants, one way or another.", "tl": "Il réussit toujours à obtenir ce qu'il veut, d'une façon ou d'une autre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This decision is going to affect us, one way or another.", "tl": "Cette décision va nous impacter, d'une façon ou d'une autre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I have to finish this project before tomorrow, one way or another.", "tl": "Je dois finir ce projet avant demain, d'une façon ou d'une autre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We must tell her the truth, one way or another.", "tl": "Il faut lui dire la vérité, d'une façon ou d'une autre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Somehow, she knew we were coming.", "tl": "D'une façon ou d'une autre, elle savait que nous allions venir."}]}, {"idiom_id": 332, "expression_id": 353, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire le pari", "english_gloss": "to make the bet / gamble", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We are making the bet that this new project will be a success.", "tl": "Nous faisons le pari que ce nouveau projet sera un succès."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She took the gamble of moving abroad without knowing the language.", "tl": "Elle a fait le pari de s'installer à l'étranger sans connaître la langue."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company wants to bet on solar energy for the future.", "tl": "L'entreprise veut faire le pari de l'énergie solaire pour l'avenir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you start your own business, you are choosing to bet on independence.", "tl": "Si tu lances ta propre entreprise, tu fais le pari de l'indépendance."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The government bet on education to reduce unemployment.", "tl": "Le gouvernement a fait le pari de l'éducation pour réduire le chômage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is sometimes necessary to take a gamble on change in order to progress.", "tl": "Il est parfois nécessaire de faire le pari du changement pour progresser."}]}, {"idiom_id": 331, "expression_id": 352, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "dans la continuité de", "english_gloss": "in continuity with / building on", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This new project builds on our previous work.", "tl": "Ce nouveau projet s'inscrit dans la continuité de nos travaux précédents."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new director wishes to work in continuity with his predecessor.", "tl": "Le nouveau directeur souhaite travailler dans la continuité de son prédécesseur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Her master's studies are a continuation of her bachelor's degree in languages.", "tl": "Ses études de master sont dans la continuité de sa licence de langues."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This second festival is organized following on from the success of last year.", "tl": "Ce deuxième festival est organisé dans la continuité du succès de l'année dernière."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Building on my good resolutions, I decided to exercise every morning.", "tl": "Dans la continuité de mes bonnes résolutions, j'ai décidé de faire du sport tous les matins."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Following on from our discussion yesterday, I am sending you the requested documents.", "tl": "Dans la continuité de notre discussion d'hier, je vous envoie les documents demandés."}]}, {"idiom_id": 330, "expression_id": 351, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "prendre sa part du gâteau", "english_gloss": "to get a piece of the pie", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In this new market, every company is trying to get its piece of the pie.", "tl": "Dans ce nouveau marché, chaque entreprise essaie de prendre sa part du gâteau."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When the project succeeded, everyone came to get their piece of the pie.", "tl": "Quand le projet a réussi, tout le monde est venu pour prendre sa part du gâteau."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You worked hard on this project, it's only fair that you get your piece of the pie.", "tl": "Tu as travaillé dur sur ce dossier, il est normal que tu prennes ta part du gâteau."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Foreign investors also want to get their piece of the pie in real estate.", "tl": "Les investisseurs étrangers veulent aussi prendre leur part du gâteau dans l'immobilier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Don't worry, there is enough work for everyone to get their piece of the pie.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, il y a assez de travail pour que chacun puisse prendre sa part du gâteau."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The unions are asking employees to mobilize to get their piece of the pie.", "tl": "Les syndicats demandent aux salariés de se mobiliser pour prendre leur part du gâteau."}]}, {"idiom_id": 329, "expression_id": 350, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en balayant rapidement", "english_gloss": "by quickly sweeping through", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I found the answer to the question by quickly scanning the document.", "tl": "J'ai trouvé la réponse à la question en balayant rapidement le document du regard."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You can clean the kitchen by quickly sweeping the floor before the guests arrive.", "tl": "Tu peux nettoyer la cuisine en balayant rapidement le sol avant l'arrivée des invités."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "By quickly scanning the room with her eyes, she immediately spotted her brother.", "tl": "En balayant rapidement la salle des yeux, elle a immédiatement repéré son frère."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He studied for his exam by quickly skimming through his course notes.", "tl": "Il a révisé pour son examen en balayant rapidement ses notes de cours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "By quickly sweeping away the dead leaves on the terrace, we finished before the rain.", "tl": "En balayant rapidement les feuilles mortes sur la terrasse, nous avons fini avant la pluie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The detective was able to find clues by quickly sweeping the crime scene with his flashlight.", "tl": "Le détective a pu trouver des indices en balayant rapidement la scène du crime avec sa lampe."}]}, {"idiom_id": 328, "expression_id": 349, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "dans la logique des choses", "english_gloss": "in the natural course of events", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After ten years in the company, her promotion is completely in the natural course of events.", "tl": "Après dix ans dans l'entreprise, sa promotion est tout à fait dans la logique des choses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They have been in love for a long time, so living together is in the natural course of things.", "tl": "Ils s'aiment depuis longtemps, alors habiter ensemble est dans la logique des choses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It is in the natural course of things that electric cars replace old models.", "tl": "Il est dans la logique des choses que les voitures électriques remplacent les anciens modèles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Retiring after such a long career is simply in the natural course of things.", "tl": "Prendre sa retraite après une si longue carrière, c'est simplement dans la logique des choses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If you work hard every day, your success will be in the natural course of events.", "tl": "Si tu travailles dur chaque jour, ta réussite sera dans la logique des choses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After walking for hours, being tired is in the natural course of things.", "tl": "Après avoir marché pendant des heures, être fatigué est dans la logique des choses."}]}, {"idiom_id": 327, "expression_id": 348, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se faire attendre", "english_gloss": "to be slow in coming", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This year, spring is slow in coming; it is still very cold in April.", "tl": "Cette année, le printemps se fait attendre, il fait encore très froid en avril."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The bus is keeping us waiting this morning, I hope it isn't canceled.", "tl": "Le bus se fait attendre ce matin, j'espère qu'il n'est pas annulé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I ordered a book last month, but the delivery is slow in coming.", "tl": "J'ai commandé un livre le mois dernier, mais la livraison se fait attendre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The guests are keeping us waiting, maybe we should start eating.", "tl": "Les invités se font attendre, nous devrions peut-être commencer à manger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He worked hard, but the results of his efforts are still slow in coming.", "tl": "Il a beaucoup travaillé, mais les résultats de ses efforts se font encore attendre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't keep everyone waiting, everyone is already in the car.", "tl": "Ne te fais pas attendre, tout le monde est déjà dans la voiture."}]}, {"idiom_id": 326, "expression_id": 347, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "qu'en est-il", "english_gloss": "what is the situation / what about", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Project A is almost finished, but what about project B?", "tl": "Le projet A est presque terminé, mais qu'en est-il du projet B ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You told me about your health issues, how are things today?", "tl": "Tu m'as parlé de tes problèmes de santé, qu'en est-il aujourd'hui ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Everyone agrees on the principle, but what about the budget?", "tl": "Tout le monde est d'accord sur le principe, mais qu'en est-il du budget ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We booked the hotel, but what about the train tickets?", "tl": "Nous avons réservé l'hôtel, mais qu'en est-il des billets de train ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "People are talking a lot about this new product, but what about its actual effectiveness?", "tl": "On parle beaucoup de ce nouveau produit, mais qu'en est-il réellement de son efficacité ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I gave my opinion on the matter, but what about your colleagues?", "tl": "J'ai donné mon avis sur la question, mais qu'en est-il de tes collègues ?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 325, "expression_id": 346, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "plaider en faveur de", "english_gloss": "to advocate for / plead in favor of", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The mayor decided to advocate for the creation of new bicycle lanes.", "tl": "Le maire a décidé de plaider en faveur de la création de nouvelles pistes cyclables."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Several teachers are advocating for a reduction in class hours.", "tl": "Plusieurs professeurs plaident en faveur d'une réduction des heures de cours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many scientists are pleading in favor of a rapid transition to renewable energy.", "tl": "De nombreux scientifiques plaident en faveur d'une transition rapide vers les énergies renouvelables."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My brother has always advocated for a simpler lifestyle.", "tl": "Mon frère a toujours plaidé en faveur d'un mode de vie plus simple."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The marketing director is going to advocate for an increase in the advertising budget.", "tl": "La directrice marketing va plaider en faveur d'une augmentation du budget publicitaire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This association advocates for the rights of homeless people.", "tl": "Cette association plaide en faveur des droits des personnes sans abri."}]}, {"idiom_id": 324, "expression_id": 345, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "l'horizon semble s'éclaircir", "english_gloss": "the outlook seems to be brightening", "youtube_id": "l1x3tLf3Az4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After months of financial crisis, the outlook finally seems to be brightening for our company.", "tl": "Après des mois de crise financière, l'horizon semble enfin s'éclaircir pour notre entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Since she found this new treatment, the outlook seems to be brightening for her health.", "tl": "Depuis qu'elle a trouvé ce nouveau traitement, l'horizon semble s'éclaircir pour sa santé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Negotiations are progressing well, and the outlook seems to be brightening for the project's future.", "tl": "Les négociations avancent bien et l'horizon semble s'éclaircir pour l'avenir du projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I received two positive responses to my job applications; the outlook seems to be brightening.", "tl": "J'ai reçu deux réponses positives à mes candidatures ; l'horizon semble s'éclaircir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The storm is moving away and the outlook seems to be brightening, both literally and figuratively.", "tl": "La tempête s'éloigne et l'horizon semble s'éclaircir, tant au sens propre qu'au figuré."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Now that I have passed my difficult exams, the outlook seems to be brightening for my school year.", "tl": "Maintenant que j'ai réussi mes examens difficiles, l'horizon semble s'éclaircir pour mon année scolaire."}]}, {"idiom_id": 323, "expression_id": 344, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se débarrasser de", "english_gloss": "to get rid of / to rid oneself of", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I need to get rid of these old clothes that I don't wear anymore.", "tl": "Je dois me débarrasser de ces vieux vêtements que je ne porte plus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He has been trying to get rid of this bad habit for months.", "tl": "Il essaie de se débarrasser de cette mauvaise habitude depuis des mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "How can we get rid of the ants in the kitchen?", "tl": "Comment est-ce qu'on peut se débarrasser des fourmis dans la cuisine ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She finally got rid of her old, broken-down car.", "tl": "Elle s'est enfin débarrassée de sa vieille voiture en panne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You should get rid of these useless papers to make some space.", "tl": "Tu devrais te débarrasser de ces papiers inutiles pour faire de la place."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The company wants to get rid of its old computers.", "tl": "L'entreprise veut se débarrasser de ses anciens ordinateurs."}]}, {"idiom_id": 322, "expression_id": 343, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tirage au sort", "english_gloss": "random draw / lottery", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The random draw for the World Cup will take place tonight in Paris.", "tl": "Le tirage au sort pour la Coupe du monde aura lieu ce soir à Paris."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Since there were too many candidates, the university had to do a random draw.", "tl": "Comme il y avait trop de candidats, l'université a dû faire un tirage au sort."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "To win this trip, you must sign up before Friday's random draw.", "tl": "Pour gagner ce voyage, vous devez vous inscrire avant le tirage au sort de vendredi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My uncle was selected by random draw to be part of a jury.", "tl": "Mon oncle a été sélectionné par tirage au sort pour faire partie d'un jury."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We can't decide who is going to do the dishes, let's do a random draw!", "tl": "On n'arrive pas à décider qui va faire la vaisselle, faisons un tirage au sort !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Since tickets for the concert are limited, they will be allocated by random draw.", "tl": "Les places pour le concert étant limitées, elles seront attribuées par tirage au sort."}]}, {"idiom_id": 321, "expression_id": 342, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire à l'envers", "english_gloss": "to trick / to pull a fast one", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I thought he was a friend, but he double-crossed me.", "tl": "Je croyais que c'était un ami, mais il me l'a faite à l'envers."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't pull a fast one on me, I know very well how it works.", "tl": "Ne me la fais pas à l'envers, je sais très bien comment ça fonctionne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They tried to trick us during the negotiations.", "tl": "Ils ont essayé de nous la faire à l'envers lors des négociations."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Be careful with this car dealer, he could pull a fast one on you.", "tl": "Fais attention avec ce concessionnaire, il pourrait te la faire à l'envers."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I hate people who always try to play tricks on others.", "tl": "Je déteste les gens qui essaient toujours de la faire à l'envers aux autres."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Did you really believe his promises? He pulled a fast one on you again!", "tl": "Tu as vraiment cru ses promesses ? Il te l'a encore faite à l'envers !"}]}, {"idiom_id": 320, "expression_id": 341, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se douter de", "english_gloss": "to suspect / to have a feeling", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "You passed your exam? I suspected as much, you worked so hard!", "tl": "Tu as réussi ton examen ? Je m'en doutais, tu as tellement travaillé !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She didn't suspect the surprise we were preparing for her at all.", "tl": "Elle ne se doutait absolument pas de la surprise que nous lui préparions."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I suspected what his answer would be, that's why I didn't insist.", "tl": "Je me doutais de sa réponse, c'est pour cela que je n'ai pas insisté."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Do they suspect anything, or is the secret well kept?", "tl": "Est-ce qu'ils se doutent de quelque chose ou est-ce que le secret est bien gardé ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We suspected it a little, but it is still bad news.", "tl": "On s'en doutait un peu, mais c'est quand même une mauvaise nouvelle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I didn't suspect the difficulty of this exercise before starting.", "tl": "Je ne me doutais pas de la difficulté de cet exercice avant de commencer."}]}, {"idiom_id": 319, "expression_id": 340, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire appel à", "english_gloss": "to call upon / to appeal to", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For this difficult project, we must call upon a specialist.", "tl": "Pour ce projet difficile, nous devons faire appel à un spécialiste."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The association is appealing to the public's generosity to help the homeless.", "tl": "L'association fait appel à la générosité du public pour aider les sans-abris."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you can't fix the leak, you should call a plumber.", "tl": "Si tu n'arrives pas à réparer la fuite, tu devrais faire appel à un plombier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This activity calls upon your imagination and your creativity.", "tl": "Cette activité fait appel à votre imagination et à votre créativité."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The police had to call upon witnesses to solve the investigation.", "tl": "La police a dû faire appel à des témoins pour résoudre l'enquête."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I prefer to call on my friends rather than a moving company.", "tl": "Je préfère faire appel à mes amis plutôt qu'à une entreprise de déménagement."}]}, {"idiom_id": 318, "expression_id": 339, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire plaisir à", "english_gloss": "to please / to do a favor for", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It really makes me happy to see you again after all this time.", "tl": "Ça me fait vraiment plaisir de te revoir après tout ce temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I wanted to please him by buying his favorite cake.", "tl": "Je voulais lui faire plaisir en lui achetant son gâteau préféré."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It would make her so happy if you came to her birthday party.", "tl": "Ça lui ferait tellement plaisir si tu venais à son anniversaire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Giving flowers to your mother is always a good idea to make her happy.", "tl": "Offrir des fleurs à sa mère, c'est toujours une bonne idée pour lui faire plaisir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't do this for the money, I just want to please my clients.", "tl": "Je ne fais pas ça pour l'argent, je veux juste faire plaisir à mes clients."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Thank you for your help, it really made me happy.", "tl": "Merci pour ton aide, ça m'a fait très plaisir."}]}, {"idiom_id": 317, "expression_id": 338, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "il n'y avait pas photo", "english_gloss": "there was no contest / it was obvious", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Between the world champion and his opponent, there was no contest; the match was over in ten minutes.", "tl": "Entre le champion du monde et son adversaire, il n'y avait pas photo ; le match s'est terminé en dix minutes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I compared the two computers and, for the same price, there was no comparison: the first one was much faster.", "tl": "J'ai comparé les deux ordinateurs et, pour le même prix, il n'y avait pas photo : le premier était bien plus rapide."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The recruiters chose Julie for the job, there was no contest compared to the other candidates.", "tl": "Les recruteurs ont choisi Julie pour le poste, il n'y avait pas photo par rapport aux autres candidats."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We were hesitating between Brittany and the south for our vacation, but given the weather, it was a no-brainer.", "tl": "On hésitait entre la Bretagne et le sud pour nos vacances, mais vu la météo, il n'y avait pas photo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Between the frozen pizza and the one from the Italian restaurant next door, there was really no comparison.", "tl": "Entre la pizza surgelée et celle du restaurant italien d'à côté, il n'y avait vraiment pas photo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My brother studied much more than I did for the exam, and when it came to the results, there was no contest.", "tl": "Mon frère a beaucoup plus révisé que moi pour l'examen, et sur les résultats, il n'y avait pas photo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 316, "expression_id": 337, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "le scandale de trop", "english_gloss": "one scandal too many", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For this minister, this corruption case was one scandal too many, and he had to resign.", "tl": "Pour ce ministre, cette affaire de corruption a été le scandale de trop, et il a dû démissionner."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Loyal customers decided to boycott the brand after what seemed to be one scandal too many.", "tl": "Les clients fidèles ont décidé de boycotter la marque après ce qui semblait être le scandale de trop."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "For the football team, their coach's behavior this weekend was one scandal too many.", "tl": "Pour l'équipe de football, le comportement de leur entraîneur ce week-end était le scandale de trop."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The newspapers believe that this new revelation is one scandal too many for the government.", "tl": "Les journaux estiment que cette nouvelle révélation est le scandale de trop pour le gouvernement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The television channel canceled the show because it was truly one scandal too many for the viewers.", "tl": "La chaîne de télévision a annulé l'émission, car c'était vraiment le scandale de trop pour les spectateurs."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The city's residents think that the construction of this useless project is one scandal too many.", "tl": "Les habitants de la ville pensent que la construction de ce projet inutile est le scandale de trop."}]}, {"idiom_id": 315, "expression_id": 336, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à titre exceptionnel", "english_gloss": "exceptionally / as an exceptional measure", "youtube_id": "k0sbt0uEfzc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Exceptionally, you can work from home this Friday.", "tl": "À titre exceptionnel, vous pouvez travailler depuis chez vous ce vendredi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The teacher agreed to accept my late assignment as an exceptional measure.", "tl": "Le professeur a accepté de recevoir mon devoir en retard à titre exceptionnel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The store agreed to refund me as an exceptional measure because the item was defective.", "tl": "Le magasin a accepté de me rembourser à titre exceptionnel car l'article était défectueux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Due to maintenance work, this train will exceptionally stop at this small station.", "tl": "En raison des travaux, ce train s'arrêtera à titre exceptionnel dans cette petite gare."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The town hall exceptionally extended the registration deadline.", "tl": "La mairie a prolongé la date limite d'inscription à titre exceptionnel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "As an exception, the children are allowed to watch television tonight.", "tl": "À titre exceptionnel, les enfants ont le droit de regarder la télévision ce soir."}]}, {"idiom_id": 314, "expression_id": 335, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à flux tendu", "english_gloss": "just-in-time / under tight pressure", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our factory works just-in-time to reduce storage costs.", "tl": "Notre usine travaille à flux tendu pour réduire les coûts de stockage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Since Julie's departure, the whole team has been operating under tight pressure.", "tl": "Depuis le départ de Julie, toute l'équipe fonctionne à flux tendu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Hospitals are short on beds and manage emergencies with zero margin.", "tl": "Les hôpitaux manquent de lits et gèrent les urgences à flux tendu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "With my small student budget, I'm living a bit tight this month.", "tl": "Avec mon petit budget d'étudiant, je vis un peu à flux tendu ce mois-ci."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This supermarket is supplied just-in-time, which explains the occasionally empty shelves.", "tl": "Ce supermarché est approvisionné à flux tendu, ce qui explique les rayons parfois vides."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We have to submit the project tomorrow, so we are all working under tight pressure.", "tl": "Nous devons rendre le projet demain, alors nous travaillons tous à flux tendu."}]}, {"idiom_id": 313, "expression_id": 334, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "avoir recours à", "english_gloss": "to resort to / make use of", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If the situation doesn't improve, we will have to resort to a specialist.", "tl": "Si la situation ne s'améliore pas, nous devrons avoir recours à un spécialiste."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The company had to make use of artificial intelligence to sort through all these documents.", "tl": "L'entreprise a dû avoir recours à l'intelligence artificielle pour trier tous ces documents."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Fortunately, I was able to solve the problem without resorting to my savings.", "tl": "Heureusement, j'ai pu résoudre le problème sans avoir recours à mes économies."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To pass this difficult exam, some students resort to private tutoring.", "tl": "Pour réussir cet examen difficile, certains étudiants ont recours à des cours particuliers."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In the past, it was often necessary to resort to force to make oneself heard.", "tl": "Autrefois, il fallait souvent avoir recours à la force pour se faire entendre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "More and more people are resorting to meditation to manage their daily stress.", "tl": "De plus en plus de gens ont recours à la méditation pour gérer leur stress quotidien."}]}, {"idiom_id": 312, "expression_id": 333, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se pencher sur", "english_gloss": "to look into / examine", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government needs to look into the housing issue for young people.", "tl": "Le gouvernement doit se pencher sur la question du logement pour les jeunes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Scientists are currently looking into the effects of climate change.", "tl": "Les scientifiques se penchent actuellement sur les effets du changement climatique."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We are going to look into this problem first thing tomorrow morning.", "tl": "Nous allons nous pencher sur ce problème dès demain matin."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is time to look into our holiday budget.", "tl": "Il est temps de se pencher sur notre budget pour les vacances."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In this course, we will examine the history of the French Revolution.", "tl": "Dans ce cours, nous nous pencherons sur l'histoire de la Révolution française."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The technical team looked into the bug, but they haven't found a solution yet.", "tl": "L'équipe technique s'est penchée sur le bug, mais ils n'ont pas encore trouvé de solution."}]}, {"idiom_id": 311, "expression_id": 332, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "par manque de", "english_gloss": "due to a lack of", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We weren't able to visit the museum due to a lack of time.", "tl": "Nous n'avons pas pu visiter le musée par manque de temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The project was canceled due to a lack of resources.", "tl": "Le projet a été annulé par manque de moyens."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Their relationship failed due to a lack of communication.", "tl": "Leur relation a échoué par manque de communication."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He didn't get the job due to a lack of experience.", "tl": "Il n'a pas obtenu le poste par manque d'expérience."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She made a lot of mistakes due to a lack of sleep.", "tl": "Elle a fait beaucoup d'erreurs par manque de sommeil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The class was canceled due to a lack of participants.", "tl": "Le cours a été annulé par manque de participants."}]}, {"idiom_id": 310, "expression_id": 331, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "au carrefour de", "english_gloss": "at the crossroads of", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Meet me at the intersection of Rue de la Paix and Rue de Rivoli.", "tl": "Retrouve-moi au carrefour de la rue de la Paix et de la rue de Rivoli."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At this stage of my life, I find myself at the crossroads of several career choices.", "tl": "À ce stade de ma vie, je me trouve au carrefour de plusieurs choix de carrière."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This historic region is located at the crossroads of several European cultures.", "tl": "Cette région historique se situe au carrefour de plusieurs cultures européennes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You need to turn left at the intersection of the main avenue and the boulevard.", "tl": "Tu dois tourner à gauche au carrefour de la grande avenue et du boulevard."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "His new book is at the crossroads of science and philosophy.", "tl": "Son nouveau livre se trouve au carrefour de la science et de la philosophie."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "At that time, the city was at the crossroads of tradition and modernity.", "tl": "À cette époque, la ville était au carrefour de la tradition et de la modernité."}]}, {"idiom_id": 309, "expression_id": 330, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "avoir le sentiment", "english_gloss": "to have the feeling / impression", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I have the feeling that we are making the right decision.", "tl": "J'ai le sentiment que nous prenons la bonne décision."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They had the feeling they had already seen this movie.", "tl": "Ils avaient le sentiment d'avoir déjà vu ce film."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Do you have the feeling that you passed your interview?", "tl": "Est-ce que tu as le sentiment d'avoir réussi ton entretien ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She has the feeling that something is wrong.", "tl": "Elle a le sentiment que quelque chose ne va pas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We have the feeling we are wasting our time with this project.", "tl": "Nous avons le sentiment de perdre notre temps avec ce projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After his presentation, he had the feeling he had convinced the client.", "tl": "Après sa présentation, il a eu le sentiment d'avoir convaincu le client."}]}, {"idiom_id": 308, "expression_id": 329, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "rendu public", "english_gloss": "made public / released", "youtube_id": "UV9rPAAsVOM", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The report on climate change was finally made public.", "tl": "Le rapport sur le changement climatique a enfin été rendu public."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The test results will be made public tomorrow morning.", "tl": "Les résultats du test seront rendus publics demain matin."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This information should never have been made public.", "tl": "Cette information n'aurait jamais dû être rendue publique."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why did they decide to make this secret document public?", "tl": "Pourquoi ont-ils décidé de rendre public ce document secret ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The findings of the investigation were made public by the police.", "tl": "Les conclusions de l'enquête ont été rendues publiques par la police."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Once made public, the bill was highly criticized.", "tl": "Une fois rendu public, le projet de loi a été très critiqué."}]}, {"idiom_id": 307, "expression_id": 328, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "handstreichartig", "english_gloss": "by surprise / in a sudden coup", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The company was taken over by surprise by a competitor.", "tl": "Die Firma wurde handstreichartig von einem Konkurrenten übernommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The mayor passed the new rules in a sudden coup, without asking anyone.", "tl": "Der Bürgermeister hat die neuen Regeln handstreichartig beschlossen, ohne jemanden zu fragen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The board of directors dismissed the boss in a sudden, surprise move.", "tl": "Der Vorstand hat den Chef handstreichartig entlassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The club president changed the bylaws in a sudden coup.", "tl": "Der Vereinsvorsitzende hat die Satzung handstreichartig geändert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our project was stopped by the management in a sudden, surprise move.", "tl": "Unser Projekt wurde von der Geschäftsführung handstreichartig gestoppt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The police cleared the occupied building in a sudden surprise action.", "tl": "Die Polizei hat das besetzte Haus handstreichartig geräumt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 306, "expression_id": 327, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Stichwort", "english_gloss": "keyword / speaking of", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For my presentation, I only wrote down a few important keywords.", "tl": "Für meinen Vortrag habe ich mir nur ein paar wichtige Stichworte aufgeschrieben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Speaking of environmental protection: What do you actually do for it in your daily life?", "tl": "Stichwort Umweltschutz: Was tust du eigentlich im Alltag dafür?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you are looking for the book, just enter the keyword into the search bar.", "tl": "Wenn du das Buch suchst, gib einfach das Stichwort in die Suchmaske ein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You have to give me a cue, otherwise I'll forget when I'm supposed to start speaking.", "tl": "Du musst mir ein Stichwort geben, sonst vergesse ich, wann ich anfangen soll zu reden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Speaking of finances: We urgently need to talk about our budget for next year.", "tl": "Stichwort Finanzen: Wir müssen dringend über unser Budget für das nächste Jahr sprechen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It's not enough to just mention a keyword in the test; you have to explain the whole concept.", "tl": "Es reicht nicht, im Test nur ein Stichwort zu nennen; du musst den ganzen Begriff erklären."}]}, {"idiom_id": 305, "expression_id": 326, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ein Stück weit", "english_gloss": "to some extent / to a certain degree", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I can understand your disappointment to some extent, but you also have to see his situation.", "tl": "Ich kann deine Enttäuschung ein Stück weit verstehen, aber du musst auch seine Situation sehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We have to adapt to the new working conditions to a certain degree.", "tl": "Wir müssen uns ein Stück weit an die neuen Arbeitsbedingungen anpassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Everyone is, to some extent, responsible for their own happiness.", "tl": "Jeder ist für sein eigenes Glück ein Stück weit selbst verantwortlich."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I agree with you to a certain extent there, but there is another important point.", "tl": "Da stimme ich Ihnen ein Stück weit zu, aber es gibt noch einen anderen wichtigen Punkt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is to some extent normal to be nervous before a big exam.", "tl": "Es ist ein Stück weit normal, vor einer großen Prüfung nervös zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The new measures have helped us to some extent to solve the problem.", "tl": "Die neuen Maßnahmen haben uns ein Stück weit geholfen, das Problem zu lösen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 304, "expression_id": 325, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in den Sternen stehen", "english_gloss": "to be written in the stars / highly uncertain", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Whether I get the new job is unfortunately still written in the stars.", "tl": "Ob ich die neue Stelle bekomme, steht leider noch in den Sternen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When we can go on vacation this year is still completely written in the stars.", "tl": "Wann wir dieses Jahr in den Urlaub fahren können, steht noch völlig in den Sternen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Whether the open-air concert will take place tomorrow is written in the stars because of the weather.", "tl": "Ob das Open-Air-Konzert morgen stattfindet, steht wegen des Wetters in den Sternen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "How apartment prices will develop in the future is written in the stars.", "tl": "Wie sich die Preise für Wohnungen in Zukunft entwickeln, steht in den Sternen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Whether he will successfully finish his training is still written in the stars at the moment.", "tl": "Ob er seine Ausbildung erfolgreich beendet, steht im Moment noch in den Sternen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When the new shopping mall will finally open is written in the stars.", "tl": "Wann das neue Einkaufszentrum endlich eröffnet wird, steht in den Sternen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 303, "expression_id": 324, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ins Minus rutschen", "english_gloss": "to slip into the red / go into deficit", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If I buy a new phone this month, my account will slip into the red.", "tl": "Wenn ich diesen Monat ein neues Handy kaufe, rutscht mein Konto ins Minus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Due to the high heating costs, the company went into deficit last quarter.", "tl": "Wegen der hohen Heizkosten ist die Firma im letzten Quartal ins Minus gerutscht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We have to be careful so that we don't go into the red at the end of the month.", "tl": "Wir müssen vorsichtig sein, damit wir am Ende des Monats nicht ins Minus rutschen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Due to the unexpected expenses, the city's budget slipped into the red.", "tl": "Durch die unerwarteten Ausgaben ist der Haushalt der Stadt ins Minus gerutscht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Unfortunately, my account has slipped into the red again because I had to pay the rent.", "tl": "Mein Konto ist leider schon wieder ins Minus gerutscht, weil ich die Miete bezahlen musste."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If the project takes even longer, we will go into the red financially.", "tl": "Wenn das Projekt noch länger dauert, rutschen wir finanziell ins Minus."}]}, {"idiom_id": 302, "expression_id": 323, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Abstriche geben", "english_gloss": "to be cutbacks / compromises", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to the low budget, there will unfortunately be some cutbacks on this project.", "tl": "Wegen des geringen Budgets wird es bei diesem Projekt leider einige Abstriche geben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The hotel was cheap, but there were significant compromises when it came to comfort.", "tl": "Das Hotel war zwar günstig, aber beim Komfort gab es deutliche Abstriche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we want to finish the product faster, there must be no compromises on quality.", "tl": "Wenn wir das Produkt schneller fertigstellen wollen, darf es keine Abstriche bei der Qualität geben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Unfortunately, there were a few compromises when planning the party because the venue was smaller than expected.", "tl": "Bei der Planung der Feier gab es leider ein paar Abstriche, weil die Location kleiner war als gedacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new job offers great working hours, but unfortunately there are cutbacks regarding the salary.", "tl": "Die neue Stelle bietet tolle Arbeitszeiten, aber beim Gehalt gibt es leider Abstriche."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Due to the teacher shortage, there will probably be cutbacks in lessons next school year.", "tl": "Durch den Lehrermangel wird es im nächsten Schuljahr wohl Abstriche beim Unterricht geben."}]}, {"idiom_id": 301, "expression_id": 322, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "wie Sie sich vorstellen können", "english_gloss": "as you can imagine", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As you can imagine, we are very busy at the moment.", "tl": "Wie Sie sich vorstellen können, haben wir im Moment sehr viel zu tun."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "As you can imagine, the flight was canceled because of the bad weather.", "tl": "Wie Sie sich vorstellen können, wurde der Flug wegen des schlechten Wetters abgesagt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The move to the new apartment was, as you can imagine, quite stressful.", "tl": "Der Umzug in die neue Wohnung war, wie Sie sich vorstellen können, ziemlich stressig."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "A new car is, as you can imagine, not exactly cheap.", "tl": "Ein neues Auto ist, wie Sie sich vorstellen können, nicht gerade billig."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "As you can imagine, we were very pleased with your invitation.", "tl": "Wie Sie sich vorstellen können, haben wir uns über Ihre Einladung sehr gefreut."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This decision was, as you can imagine, not easy for us.", "tl": "Diese Entscheidung war, wie Sie sich vorstellen können, nicht einfach für uns."}]}, {"idiom_id": 300, "expression_id": 321, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "von der Rede sein", "english_gloss": "to be talked about / to be rumored", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "There was talk of a strike in the news today.", "tl": "In den Nachrichten war heute von einem Streik die Rede."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "What is actually being talked about here? I don't understand the context.", "tl": "Wovon ist hier eigentlich die Rede? Ich verstehe den Zusammenhang nicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There was never any mention of a termination in the conversation.", "tl": "Von einer Kündigung war in dem Gespräch nie die Rede."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "There is talk of a big change in our company.", "tl": "Es ist die Rede von einer großen Veränderung in unserer Firma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That wasn't talked about at all during the meeting yesterday.", "tl": "Davon war gestern bei dem Treffen gar nicht die Rede."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When success is being talked about, everyone means something different.", "tl": "Wenn von Erfolg die Rede ist, meint jeder etwas anderes."}]}, {"idiom_id": 299, "expression_id": 320, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf der anderen Seite", "english_gloss": "on the other hand", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I like my job a lot, but on the other hand, I don't earn enough money there.", "tl": "Ich mag meinen Job sehr, aber auf der anderen Seite verdiene ich dort nicht genug Geld."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is great to live abroad; on the other hand, I miss my family a lot.", "tl": "Es ist toll, im Ausland zu leben; auf der anderen Seite vermisse ich meine Familie sehr."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new smartphone has many features, but on the other hand, it is very expensive.", "tl": "Das neue Smartphone hat viele Funktionen, aber auf der anderen Seite ist es sehr teuer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Doing sports is healthy, but on the other hand, you shouldn't overdo it either.", "tl": "Sport zu treiben ist gesund, aber auf der anderen Seite sollte man es auch nicht übertreiben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The apartment in the city is very central, but on the other hand, it is often noisy there at night.", "tl": "Die Wohnung in der Stadt ist sehr zentral, aber auf der anderen Seite ist es dort nachts oft laut."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I would like to go for a walk, but on the other hand, it looks like it's about to rain.", "tl": "Ich würde gerne spazieren gehen, aber auf der anderen Seite sieht es so aus, als ob es gleich regnet."}]}, {"idiom_id": 298, "expression_id": 319, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf den Punkt", "english_gloss": "to the point / spot on", "youtube_id": "RKT7efY4t8M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Can you please get straight to the point? We don't have much time.", "tl": "Kannst du das Problem bitte auf den Punkt bringen? Wir haben nicht viel Zeit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "His analysis of the economic situation was absolutely spot on.", "tl": "Seine Analyse der wirtschaftlichen Situation war absolut auf den Punkt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The presentation was short, but it got all the important arguments straight to the point.", "tl": "Die Präsentation war kurz, aber sie brachte alle wichtigen Argumente auf den Punkt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He always manages to get complex topics to the point in just a few sentences.", "tl": "Er schafft es immer, komplexe Themen in wenigen Sätzen auf den Punkt zu bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Your answer in the interview was short, clear, and to the point.", "tl": "Deine Antwort im Interview war kurz, klar und auf den Punkt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The new design hits our customers' taste spot on.", "tl": "Das neue Design trifft den Geschmack unserer Kunden auf den Punkt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 297, "expression_id": 318, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "im Einsatz sein", "english_gloss": "to be deployed / in action", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The fire department was in action all night to put out the fire.", "tl": "Die Feuerwehr war die ganze Nacht im Einsatz, um das Feuer zu löschen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "These old buses are still in use every day.", "tl": "Diese alten Busse sind immer noch täglich im Einsatz."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many police officers were on duty during the football match.", "tl": "Während des Fußballspiels waren viele Polizisten im Einsatz."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The emergency doctor is currently on a call and cannot answer the phone.", "tl": "Der Notarzt ist gerade im Einsatz und kann nicht ans Telefon gehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our organization has been deployed in this crisis region for years.", "tl": "Unsere Organisation ist seit Jahren in diesem Krisengebiet im Einsatz."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "New technologies are in use in almost every profession today.", "tl": "Neue Technologien sind heute in fast jedem Beruf im Einsatz."}]}, {"idiom_id": 296, "expression_id": 317, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "beisetzen", "english_gloss": "laid to rest / buried", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The family wants to lay the grandfather's ashes to rest in a burial forest.", "tl": "Die Familie möchte die Asche des Großvaters in einem Friedwald beisetzen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The famous writer was laid to rest yesterday in a private family circle.", "tl": "Der berühmte Schriftsteller wurde gestern im engen Kreis der Familie beigesetzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It was his last wish to be laid to rest in the old cemetery of his hometown.", "tl": "Es war sein letzter Wunsch, auf dem alten Friedhof seiner Heimatstadt beigesetzt zu werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Yesterday we laid my grandmother's urn to rest in the family grave.", "tl": "Gestern haben wir die Urne meiner Großmutter im Familiengrab beigesetzt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Where is the deceased artist to be laid to rest?", "tl": "Wo soll die verstorbene Künstlerin beigesetzt werden?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After the funeral service, the coffin will be laid to rest at the main cemetery.", "tl": "Nach der Trauerfeier wird der Sarg auf dem Hauptfriedhof beigesetzt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 295, "expression_id": 316, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "falsche Angaben machen", "english_gloss": "to make false statements", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Anyone who makes false statements in their application quickly loses the employer's trust.", "tl": "Wer bei der Bewerbung falsche Angaben macht, verliert schnell das Vertrauen des Arbeitgebers."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you make false statements to the insurance company, they will not pay for the damage.", "tl": "Wenn Sie bei der Versicherung falsche Angaben machen, zahlt diese den Schaden nicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The witness made false statements to the police yesterday.", "tl": "Der Zeuge hat gestern bei der Polizei falsche Angaben gemacht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Please make sure not to make any false statements on the visa application.", "tl": "Bitte achten Sie darauf, im Visumantrag keine falschen Angaben zu machen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Did you perhaps make false statements when registering online?", "tl": "Hast du bei der Registrierung im Internet etwa falsche Angaben gemacht?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is forbidden to make false statements to customs about the imported goods.", "tl": "Es ist verboten, beim Zoll falsche Angaben über die eingeführten Waren zu machen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 294, "expression_id": 315, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die Kandidatur absagen", "english_gloss": "to withdraw one's candidacy", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to health problems, the mayor had to withdraw his candidacy.", "tl": "Wegen gesundheitlicher Probleme musste der Bürgermeister seine Kandidatur absagen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If I get the new job, I will withdraw my candidacy for the works council.", "tl": "Wenn ich die neue Stelle bekomme, werde ich meine Kandidatur für den Betriebsrat absagen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The politician surprisingly withdrew his candidacy to protect his family.", "tl": "Der Politiker hat seine Kandidatur überraschend abgesagt, um seine Familie zu schützen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why did you withdraw your candidacy for the club presidency on such short notice?", "tl": "Warum hast du deine Kandidatur für den Vereinsvorsitz so kurzfristig abgesagt?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is rumored that she wants to withdraw her candidacy because she has no support.", "tl": "Es wird gemunkelt, dass sie ihre Kandidatur absagen will, weil sie keine Unterstützung hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It was a difficult decision to withdraw my candidacy at the last moment.", "tl": "Es war eine schwere Entscheidung, meine Kandidatur im letzten Moment abzusagen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 293, "expression_id": 314, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Lieber eine Kiste mehr", "english_gloss": "Better one box too many", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We have so many books; better take one extra box with you.", "tl": "Wir haben so viele Bücher; nimm lieber eine Kiste mehr mit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For the party tonight, we'd better buy one extra box, otherwise we won't have enough drinks.", "tl": "Für die Party heute Abend kaufen wir lieber eine Kiste mehr, sonst haben wir nicht genug Getränke."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When we harvest the apples in the garden, you'd better bring one extra box.", "tl": "Wenn wir die Äpfel im Garten ernten, bring lieber eine Kiste mehr mit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't know how much material we need, so we'd better order one extra box.", "tl": "Ich weiß nicht, wie viel Material wir brauchen, also bestellen wir lieber eine Kiste mehr."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Are we bringing the old things to the basement? Better take one extra box, just in case something is left over.", "tl": "Bringen wir die alten Sachen in den Keller? Lieber eine Kiste mehr mitnehmen, falls noch etwas übrig bleibt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The wine tastes fantastic, let's buy one extra box.", "tl": "Der Wein schmeckt fantastisch, lass uns lieber eine Kiste mehr kaufen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 292, "expression_id": 313, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sanieren", "english_gloss": "to renovate / refurbish / redevelop", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We bought an old house and want to completely renovate it next year.", "tl": "Wir haben ein altes Haus gekauft und wollen es nächstes Jahr komplett sanieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The city has decided to finally refurbish the old primary school.", "tl": "Die Stadt hat beschlossen, die alte Grundschule endlich zu sanieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the crisis, the company urgently needs to be restructured.", "tl": "Nach der Krise muss das Unternehmen dringend saniert werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our landlord has announced that he will soon have the bathroom renovated.", "tl": "Unser Vermieter hat angekündigt, dass er bald das Badezimmer sanieren lässt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is often very expensive to professionally renovate historical buildings.", "tl": "Es ist oft sehr teuer, historische Gebäude fachgerecht zu sanieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The bridge is closed to cars because it needs to be renovated.", "tl": "Die Brücke ist für Autos gesperrt, weil sie saniert werden muss."}]}, {"idiom_id": 291, "expression_id": 312, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "entlastet werden", "english_gloss": "to be relieved / unburdened", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Thanks to the new colleague, the entire team in the office is being relieved.", "tl": "Durch die neue Kollegin wird das ganze Team im Büro entlastet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Families are to be financially relieved starting next year.", "tl": "Familien sollen ab nächstem Jahr finanziell entlastet werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If more people use the bus, the traffic in the city will be eased.", "tl": "Wenn mehr Menschen den Bus nutzen, wird der Verkehr in der Stadt entlastet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I hope that I will finally be relieved a bit after the project.", "tl": "Ich hoffe, dass ich nach dem Projekt endlich etwas entlastet werde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The nurses in the hospital urgently need to be relieved by having more staff.", "tl": "Die Pfleger im Krankenhaus müssen dringend durch mehr Personal entlastet werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The suspect was completely exonerated by a new video evidence.", "tl": "Der Verdächtige konnte durch ein neues Beweisvideo vollständig entlastet werden."}]}, {"idiom_id": 290, "expression_id": 311, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "eine Reform beschließen", "english_gloss": "to pass/decide on a reform", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government wants to pass an important reform before the end of this year.", "tl": "Die Regierung will noch in diesem Jahr eine wichtige Reform beschließen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Yesterday, parliament passed a reform of the healthcare system.", "tl": "Das Parlament hat gestern eine Reform des Gesundheitssystems beschlossen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After long discussions, the city council finally decided on a reform of the schools.", "tl": "Nach langen Diskussionen beschloss der Stadtrat schließlich eine Reform der Schulen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is important that we pass a reform of the tax system to relieve the citizens.", "tl": "Es ist wichtig, dass wir eine Reform des Steuersystems beschließen, um die Bürger zu entlasten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "A new reform of pensions is to be passed next week.", "tl": "Nächste Woche soll eine neue Reform der Renten beschlossen werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is not easy to pass such a reform quickly.", "tl": "Es ist nicht einfach, eine solche Reform schnell zu beschließen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 289, "expression_id": 310, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in einfacher Sprache", "english_gloss": "in simple language", "youtube_id": "y_t2SIaPAs8", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "On this website, all important information is also available in simple language.", "tl": "Auf dieser Website gibt es alle wichtigen Informationen auch in einfacher Sprache."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Could you please explain that to me in simple language? I am still learning German.", "tl": "Können Sie mir das bitte in einfacher Sprache erklären? Ich lerne noch Deutsch."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There are special news programs for people who prefer texts in simple language.", "tl": "Es gibt spezielle Nachrichten für Menschen, die Texte in einfacher Sprache bevorzugen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The museum offers brochures in simple language for children and foreign guests.", "tl": "Das Museum bietet Broschüren in einfacher Sprache für Kinder und ausländische Gäste an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Contracts should always be written in simple language so that everyone understands them.", "tl": "Verträge sollten immer in einfacher Sprache verfasst sein, damit jeder sie versteht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In summary, the problem can be described in simple language like this.", "tl": "Zusammenfassend lässt sich das Problem in einfacher Sprache so beschreiben."}]}, {"idiom_id": 288, "expression_id": 309, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in den Fokus geraten", "english_gloss": "to come into focus / become a target", "youtube_id": "E3VXJMWzfiE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Due to the new scandal, the company quickly came into the focus of the media.", "tl": "Durch den neuen Skandal ist die Firma schnell in den Fokus der Medien geraten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After the success of the project, the small team also came into the focus of the management.", "tl": "Nach dem Erfolg des Projekts geriet auch das kleine Team in den Fokus der Geschäftsleitung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The topic of environmental protection has come more and more into focus in recent years.", "tl": "Das Thema Umweltschutz ist in den letzten Jahren immer mehr in den Fokus geraten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "A suspect came into the focus of the police yesterday.", "tl": "Ein Verdächtiger ist gestern in den Fokus der Polizei geraten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the exam, the grammar rules in particular come into focus.", "tl": "Bei der Prüfung geraten vor allem die Grammatikregeln in den Fokus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Because of the crisis, the health of the employees has come into focus again.", "tl": "Wegen der Krise ist die Gesundheit der Mitarbeiter wieder in den Fokus geraten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 287, "expression_id": 308, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "den Anspruch erheben", "english_gloss": "to lay claim / claim", "youtube_id": "E3VXJMWzfiE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He claims to be the best player on the team.", "tl": "Er erhebt den Anspruch, der beste Spieler im Team zu sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After the artist's death, many relatives laid claim to his paintings.", "tl": "Nach dem Tod des Künstlers erhoben viele Verwandte den Anspruch auf seine Bilder."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our boss does not claim to know everything better than we do.", "tl": "Unser Chef erhebt nicht den Anspruch, alles besser zu wissen als wir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The new company claims to manufacture the most environmentally friendly products.", "tl": "Die neue Firma erhebt den Anspruch, die umweltfreundlichsten Produkte herzustellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Both countries lay claim to this small island.", "tl": "Beide Länder erheben den Anspruch auf diese kleine Insel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't claim to speak perfect German at all, but I want to be able to have a good conversation.", "tl": "Ich erhebe gar nicht den Anspruch, perfekt Deutsch zu sprechen, aber ich möchte mich gut unterhalten können."}]}, {"idiom_id": 286, "expression_id": 307, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Schritte einleiten", "english_gloss": "to initiate steps / take action", "youtube_id": "E3VXJMWzfiE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We must take steps immediately to solve this problem.", "tl": "Wir müssen sofort Schritte einleiten, um dieses Problem zu lösen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The police have already taken steps to find the thief.", "tl": "Die Polizei hat bereits Schritte eingeleitet, um den Dieb zu finden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If the tenant doesn't pay, we must take legal action.", "tl": "Wenn der Mieter nicht bezahlt, müssen wir rechtliche Schritte einleiten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The school administration is taking steps to stop the bullying at the school.", "tl": "Die Schulleitung leitet Schritte ein, um das Mobbing an der Schule zu stoppen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The doctor initiated all the necessary steps for the treatment.", "tl": "Der Arzt hat alle notwendigen Schritte für die Behandlung eingeleitet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Steps have already been taken to secure the building.", "tl": "Es wurden bereits Schritte eingeleitet, um das Gebäude zu sichern."}]}, {"idiom_id": 285, "expression_id": 306, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Fristen einhalten", "english_gloss": "to meet deadlines", "youtube_id": "E3VXJMWzfiE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is very important that we meet all deadlines in the project.", "tl": "Es ist sehr wichtig, dass wir im Projekt alle Fristen einhalten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "As a student, you have to learn to meet important deadlines.", "tl": "Als Student muss man lernen, wichtige Fristen einzuhalten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our team is working hard to meet the deadlines for the customer.", "tl": "Unser Team arbeitet hart, um die Fristen für den Kunden einzuhalten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we don't meet the deadlines, we have to pay a penalty.", "tl": "Wenn wir die Fristen nicht einhalten, müssen wir eine Strafe zahlen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Mrs. Müller always strictly makes sure that all deadlines are met.", "tl": "Frau Müller achtet immer streng darauf, dass alle Fristen eingehalten werden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Do you think we can meet these short deadlines?", "tl": "Glaubst du, dass wir diese kurzen Fristen einhalten können?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 284, "expression_id": 305, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "keine Rolle spielen", "english_gloss": "to play no role / be irrelevant", "youtube_id": "E3VXJMWzfiE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For this job, age plays no role; only experience counts.", "tl": "Für diese Arbeit spielt das Alter keine Rolle, nur die Erfahrung zählt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Since we are celebrating indoors, the weather plays no role for us.", "tl": "Da wir drinnen feiern, spielt das Wetter für uns keine Rolle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you want to get healthy, money shouldn't play a role.", "tl": "Wenn man gesund werden will, sollte Geld keine Rolle spielen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It doesn't matter what other people think of you.", "tl": "Es spielt keine Rolle, was die anderen Leute über dich denken."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In our decision, the origin of the applicants played no role.", "tl": "In unserer Entscheidung hat die Herkunft der Bewerber keine Rolle gespielt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Whether we win or lose plays no role at the moment; the main thing is that we have fun.", "tl": "Ob wir gewinnen oder verlieren, spielt im Moment keine Rolle; Hauptsache, wir haben Spaß."}]}, {"idiom_id": 283, "expression_id": 304, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "nach unserer Kenntnis", "english_gloss": "to our knowledge", "youtube_id": "E3VXJMWzfiE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To our knowledge, the project has already been completed.", "tl": "Nach unserer Kenntnis ist das Projekt bereits abgeschlossen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "To our knowledge, the package was sent yesterday.", "tl": "Nach unserer Kenntnis wurde das Paket gestern verschickt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "To our knowledge, there are no further problems with the software.", "tl": "Es gibt nach unserer Kenntnis keine weiteren Probleme mit der Software."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To our knowledge, the conference is taking place in the main building.", "tl": "Nach unserer Kenntnis findet die Konferenz im Hauptgebäude statt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "To our knowledge, these rules apply to all employees.", "tl": "Nach unserer Kenntnis gelten diese Regeln für alle Mitarbeiter."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "To our knowledge, the hotel is completely booked out.", "tl": "Das Hotel ist nach unserer Kenntnis komplett ausgebucht."}]}, {"idiom_id": 282, "expression_id": 303, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "vor einer Bewährungsprobe stehen", "english_gloss": "to face a crucial test", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After moving to a new city, our relationship is facing a tough test.", "tl": "Nach dem Umzug in eine neue Stadt steht unsere Beziehung vor einer harten Bewährungsprobe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Due to the economic crisis, the small company is now facing a difficult test.", "tl": "Wegen der Wirtschaftskrise steht die kleine Firma jetzt vor einer schweren Bewährungsprobe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Already in its first weeks, the new government is facing a real test.", "tl": "Die neue Regierung steht schon in den ersten Wochen vor einer echten Bewährungsprobe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Before the important game on Saturday, the team is facing a major test.", "tl": "Vor dem wichtigen Spiel am Samstag steht die Mannschaft vor einer großen Bewährungsprobe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our friendship faced a test when we applied for the same job.", "tl": "Unsere Freundschaft stand vor einer Bewährungsprobe, als wir uns um denselben Job beworben haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Due to the sudden onset of winter, the power grid is facing a test.", "tl": "Durch den plötzlichen Wintereinbruch steht das Stromnetz vor einer Bewährungsprobe."}]}, {"idiom_id": 281, "expression_id": 302, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "anrollen", "english_gloss": "to approach / roll in", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "On the horizon, you can see a heavy thunderstorm rolling in.", "tl": "Am Horizont sieht man ein schweres Gewitter anrollen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The next wave of tourists is rolling in this weekend.", "tl": "Die nächste Welle von Touristen rollt am Wochenende an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The ball came rolling slowly towards the little child.", "tl": "Der Ball kam langsam auf das kleine Kind angerollt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In winter, a severe wave of flu usually rolls in.", "tl": "Im Winter rollt meistens eine schwere Grippewelle an."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I can already see our bus rolling up over there.", "tl": "Da vorne sehe ich schon unseren Bus anrollen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After the quiet summer days, work is now starting to roll in again.", "tl": "Nach den ruhigen Sommertagen rollt jetzt die Arbeit wieder an."}]}, {"idiom_id": 280, "expression_id": 301, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die Folgen abfedern", "english_gloss": "to cushion the consequences", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government is planning new measures to cushion the consequences of the crisis.", "tl": "Die Regierung plant neue Maßnahmen, um die Folgen der Krise abzufedern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We have saved some money to cushion the financial consequences if someone loses their job.", "tl": "Wir haben etwas Geld gespart, um die finanziellen Folgen abzufedern, falls jemand seinen Job verliert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Through flexible working hours, we were able to cushion the negative consequences of the pandemic.", "tl": "Durch flexible Arbeitszeiten konnten wir die negativen Folgen der Pandemie abfedern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "New trees in the city are supposed to cushion the consequences of climate change.", "tl": "Neue Bäume in der Stadt sollen die Folgen des Klimawandels abfedern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The school offers tutoring to cushion the consequences of the cancelled classes.", "tl": "Die Schule bietet Nachhilfe an, um die Folgen des Unterrichtsausfalls abzufedern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The support of friends helped her to cushion the emotional consequences of the breakup.", "tl": "Die Unterstützung von Freunden half ihr, die emotionalen Folgen der Trennung abzufedern."}]}, {"idiom_id": 279, "expression_id": 300, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "aus dem Gleichgewicht bringen", "english_gloss": "to throw off balance", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "A strong gust of wind threw the cyclist off balance.", "tl": "Ein starker Windstoß brachte den Radfahrer aus dem Gleichgewicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The bad news completely threw her off balance.", "tl": "Die schlechte Nachricht hat sie völlig aus dem Gleichgewicht gebracht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Unexpected expenses can quickly throw the monthly budget off balance.", "tl": "Unerwartete Ausgaben können das monatliche Budget schnell aus dem Gleichgewicht bringen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "A small stumble briefly threw the runner off balance.", "tl": "Ein kleiner Stolperer brachte den Läufer kurz aus dem Gleichgewicht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The short-term change to the schedule threw us all off balance.", "tl": "Die kurzfristige Änderung des Zeitplans hat uns alle aus dem Gleichgewicht gebracht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Don't let his unfriendly words throw you off balance.", "tl": "Lass dich von seinen unfreundlichen Worten nicht aus dem Gleichgewicht bringen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 278, "expression_id": 299, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "ins Gespräch kommen", "english_gloss": "to strike up a conversation", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "At parties, I sometimes find it difficult to strike up a conversation with strangers.", "tl": "Auf Partys fällt es mir manchmal schwer, mit fremden Leuten ins Gespräch zu kommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Yesterday at the trade fair, we got into conversation with many potential customers.", "tl": "Gestern auf der Messe sind wir mit vielen potenziellen Kunden ins Gespräch gekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "On the train, it is very easy to strike up a conversation with other travelers.", "tl": "Im Zug kann man sehr leicht mit anderen Reisenden ins Gespräch kommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I like my new neighbor because we immediately struck up a conversation.", "tl": "Ich mag meinen neuen Nachbarn, weil wir sofort ins Gespräch gekommen sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Just go over to her and try to strike up a conversation with her.", "tl": "Geh einfach zu ihr rüber und versuche, mit ihr ins Gespräch zu kommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The event is a good opportunity to strike up a conversation with the citizens.", "tl": "Die Veranstaltung ist eine gute Gelegenheit, um mit den Bürgern ins Gespräch zu kommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 277, "expression_id": 298, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich neu aufstellen", "english_gloss": "to reposition/reorganize oneself", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After the crisis, our company has to reorganize itself.", "tl": "Nach der Krise muss sich unser Unternehmen neu aufstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He has decided to completely reposition himself professionally.", "tl": "Er hat beschlossen, sich beruflich komplett neu aufzustellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the bad season, the team has to reorganize itself.", "tl": "Nach der schlechten Saison muss sich das Team neu aufstellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I need a break to reorganize my personal life.", "tl": "Ich brauche eine Pause, um mich privat neu aufzustellen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We need to reposition ourselves in the market to remain competitive.", "tl": "Wir müssen uns auf dem Markt neu aufstellen, um konkurrenzfähig zu bleiben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The association has reorganized itself to attract more members.", "tl": "Der Verein hat sich neu aufgestellt, um mehr Mitglieder zu gewinnen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 276, "expression_id": 297, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "jemanden veräppeln", "english_gloss": "to pull someone's leg", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Are you pulling my leg? You can't be serious!", "tl": "Willst du mich veräppeln? Das kann doch nicht dein Ernst sein!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He pulled our leg all day, and we believed his every word.", "tl": "Er hat uns den ganzen Tag veräppelt, und wir haben ihm jedes Wort geglaubt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It's not nice to tease the new colleagues.", "tl": "Es ist nicht nett, die neuen Kollegen zu veräppeln."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When I saw the price, I felt totally taken for a ride.", "tl": "Als ich den Preis sah, fühlte ich mich total veräppelt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Don't believe a word he says, he's just pulling your leg!", "tl": "Glaub ihm kein Wort, er veräppelt dich nur!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We wanted to play a joke on our teacher, but she noticed our prank immediately.", "tl": "Wir wollten unsere Lehrerin veräppeln, aber sie hat unseren Scherz sofort bemerkt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 275, "expression_id": 296, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "noch ausstehen", "english_gloss": "to still be pending", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I applied last week, but the answer is still pending.", "tl": "Ich habe mich letzte Woche beworben, aber die Antwort steht noch aus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The payment for the last invoice is unfortunately still outstanding.", "tl": "Die Zahlung für die letzte Rechnung steht leider immer noch aus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The doctor examined me, but the test results are still pending.", "tl": "Der Arzt hat mich untersucht, aber die Testergebnisse stehen noch aus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We cannot book the vacation yet because the approval from my boss is still pending.", "tl": "Wir können den Urlaub noch nicht buchen, weil die Zusage von meinem Chef noch aussteht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The delivery of the new furniture is still outstanding, but they should arrive this week.", "tl": "Die Lieferung der neuen Möbel steht noch aus, sie sollten aber diese Woche kommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The feedback from the customers about our new product is still pending.", "tl": "Das Feedback der Kunden zu unserem neuen Produkt steht noch aus."}]}, {"idiom_id": 274, "expression_id": 295, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "auf eine härtere Linie drängen", "english_gloss": "to push for a tougher stance", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Some opposition politicians are pushing for a tougher stance on migration policy.", "tl": "Einige Politiker in der Opposition drängen auf eine härtere Linie in der Migrationspolitik."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "During the last meeting, the boss pushed for a tougher stance against unpunctual employees.", "tl": "Der Chef hat bei der letzten Besprechung auf eine härtere Linie gegenüber unpünktlichen Mitarbeitern gedrängt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Environmentalists say that the government must push for a tougher stance on climate protection.", "tl": "Umweltschützer sagen, dass die Regierung auf eine härtere Linie beim Klimaschutz drängen muss."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Many parents pushed for a tougher stance against bullying at the school.", "tl": "Viele Eltern drängten auf eine härtere Linie gegen Mobbing an der Schule."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our lawyers are pushing for a tougher line in the contract negotiations.", "tl": "Unsere Anwälte drängen auf eine härtere Linie bei den Vertragsverhandlungen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I don't understand why the board is suddenly pushing for a tougher stance on the austerity measures.", "tl": "Ich verstehe nicht, warum der Vorstand plötzlich auf eine härtere Linie bei den Sparmaßnahmen drängt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 273, "expression_id": 294, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "einen Sieg einfahren", "english_gloss": "to achieve a victory", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our team absolutely has to secure a victory today in order to stay in the league.", "tl": "Unsere Mannschaft muss heute unbedingt einen Sieg einfahren, um in der Liga zu bleiben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After a tough election campaign, the candidate was finally able to achieve a clear victory.", "tl": "Nach einem harten Wahlkampf konnte die Kandidatin schließlich einen klaren Sieg einfahren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we complete this project successfully, we will achieve a great victory.", "tl": "Wenn wir dieses Projekt erfolgreich abschließen, werden wir einen großen Sieg einfahren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Yesterday, the tennis player surprisingly achieved a victory against the favorite.", "tl": "Der Tennisspieler hat gestern überraschend einen Sieg gegen den Favoriten eingefahren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Despite the difficult conditions, the team achieved a well-deserved victory in the end.", "tl": "Trotz der schwierigen Bedingungen fuhr das Team am Ende einen verdienten Sieg ein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It won't be easy to achieve a victory against this strong opponent.", "tl": "Es wird nicht einfach sein, gegen diesen starken Gegner einen Sieg einzufahren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 272, "expression_id": 293, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in den Tag starten", "english_gloss": "to start the day", "youtube_id": "zrdQERrNqxk", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I always drink a coffee in the morning to start the day off well.", "tl": "Ich trinke morgens immer einen Kaffee, um gut in den Tag zu starten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "How do you prefer to start the day?", "tl": "Wie startest du am liebsten in den Tag?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Tomorrow we want to start the day very early because we have a lot planned.", "tl": "Morgen wollen wir ganz früh in den Tag starten, weil wir viel vorhaben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Unfortunately, I started the day very stressfully today.", "tl": "Heute bin ich leider sehr stressig in den Tag gestartet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "With a little yoga, you can start the day relaxed.", "tl": "Mit ein bisschen Yoga kann man entspannt in den Tag starten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Before we start the day, we should briefly discuss the tasks.", "tl": "Bevor wir in den Tag starten, sollten wir kurz die Aufgaben besprechen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 271, "expression_id": 292, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "ir para as ruas", "english_gloss": "to take to the streets", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The teachers decided to take to the streets to demand better working conditions.", "tl": "Os professores decidiram ir para as ruas para pedir melhores condições de trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If the situation doesn't improve soon, the people will take to the streets to protest.", "tl": "Se a situação não melhorar logo, o povo vai para as ruas protestar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the final game, thousands of fans took to the streets to celebrate the victory.", "tl": "Depois do jogo final, milhares de torcedores foram para as ruas comemorar a vitória."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It's not enough to criticize on social media, sometimes it is necessary to take to the streets and act.", "tl": "Não basta criticar nas redes sociais, às vezes é preciso ir para as ruas e agir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Next Saturday, we are going to take to the streets to defend the protection of the environment.", "tl": "No próximo sábado, nós vamos para as ruas defender a proteção do meio ambiente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "At that time, students used to take to the streets almost every week.", "tl": "Naquela época, os estudantes iam para as ruas quase todas as semanas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 270, "expression_id": 291, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "ficarem na deles", "english_gloss": "to mind their own business", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It's better for them to mind their own business and not get involved in our conversation.", "tl": "É melhor eles ficarem na deles e não se meterem na nossa conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I decided to keep to myself to avoid any kind of argument.", "tl": "Eu decidi ficar na minha para evitar qualquer tipo de discussão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Pedro prefers to mind his own business during work meetings.", "tl": "O Pedro prefere ficar na dele durante as reuniões de trabalho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I think we should mind our own business and let them solve the problem.", "tl": "Acho que nós devíamos ficar na nossa e deixar que eles resolvam o problema."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I asked my neighbors to mind their own business and stop asking questions.", "tl": "Pedi aos meus vizinhos para ficarem na deles e pararem de fazer perguntas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She is very reserved and always prefers to keep to herself.", "tl": "Ela é muito reservada e prefere sempre ficar na dela."}]}, {"idiom_id": 269, "expression_id": 290, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "pra valer", "english_gloss": "for real / seriously", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After the vacation, I'm going to start studying Spanish for real.", "tl": "Depois das férias, eu vou começar a estudar espanhol pra valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It looks like it's going to rain for real now, we'd better get the umbrella.", "tl": "Parece que agora vai chover pra valer, melhor pegarmos o guarda-chuva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In the beginning it was just a joke, but now I think I'm in love for real.", "tl": "No começo era só uma brincadeira, mas agora eu acho que estou apaixonado pra valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we want to open this company, we need to dedicate ourselves for real.", "tl": "Se nós quisermos abrir essa empresa, precisamos nos dedicar pra valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Yesterday's game was just a practice, but tomorrow's is for real.", "tl": "O jogo de ontem foi só um treino, mas o de amanhã é pra valer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She decided to change her life and started working out at the gym for real.", "tl": "Ela decidiu mudar de vida e começou a treinar na academia pra valer."}]}, {"idiom_id": 268, "expression_id": 289, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "outra conversa", "english_gloss": "a whole different story", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Planning the trip was easy, but saving money for it is a whole different story.", "tl": "Planear a viagem foi fácil, mas poupar dinheiro para ela já é outra conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I don't mind helping, but doing all the work by myself is a whole different story.", "tl": "Eu não me importo de ajudar, mas fazer todo o trabalho sozinho já é outra conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you go with him, then that's a whole different story and I'll be more relieved.", "tl": "Se fores com ele, aí já é outra conversa e fico mais descansado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Buying an old house is cheap, but doing the necessary renovations is a whole different story.", "tl": "Comprar uma casa antiga é barato, mas fazer as obras necessárias é outra conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She is very nice over messages, but in person it's a whole different story.", "tl": "Ela é muito simpática por mensagens, mas pessoalmente é outra conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Passing the written test is simple, but the driving exam is a whole different story.", "tl": "Passar no teste escrito é simples, mas o exame de condução já é outra conversa."}]}, {"idiom_id": 267, "expression_id": 288, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "mais cedo ou mais tarde", "english_gloss": "sooner or later", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sooner or later, he will have to talk to the boss about the raise.", "tl": "Mais cedo ou mais tarde, ele vai ter que falar com o chefe sobre o aumento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "There's no use lying, because the truth always comes out sooner or later.", "tl": "Não adianta mentir, porque a verdade sempre aparece mais cedo ou mais tarde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you don't take care of your health, sooner or later you will have problems.", "tl": "Se você não cuidar da saúde, mais cedo ou mais tarde vai ter problemas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Sooner or later, all companies will use artificial intelligence.", "tl": "Mais cedo ou mais tarde, todas as empresas vão usar inteligência artificial."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You need to make a decision; sooner or later you will have to choose a path.", "tl": "Você precisa tomar uma decisão; mais cedo ou mais tarde terá que escolher um caminho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you keep practicing every day, sooner or later you will speak fluently.", "tl": "Se você continuar praticando todos os dias, mais cedo ou mais tarde vai falar fluentemente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 266, "expression_id": 287, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "bobeou", "english_gloss": "if you let your guard down", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you let your guard down on defense, the opponent scores.", "tl": "Bobeou na defesa, o adversário faz o gol."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This sale is really fast; if you hesitate for a second, it will be out of stock.", "tl": "Essa promoção é muito rápida; bobeou, o estoque acaba."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Don't leave your phone on the table; if you let your guard down, someone will take it.", "tl": "Não deixe o celular em cima da mesa; bobeou, alguém leva."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "At that company the pace is fast; if you slip up, someone else takes your job.", "tl": "Naquela empresa o ritmo é forte; bobeou, outro pega a sua vaga."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Pay attention to the oven; if you lose focus for a second, the cake burns.", "tl": "Preste atenção no forno; bobeou, o bolo queima."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The chess game was balanced, but he let his guard down and lost his queen.", "tl": "O jogo de xadrez estava equilibrado, mas ele bobeou e perdeu a rainha."}]}, {"idiom_id": 265, "expression_id": 286, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de forma acachapante", "english_gloss": "overwhelmingly / in a crushing manner", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The home team won the derby overwhelmingly by five to zero.", "tl": "O time da casa venceu o clássico de forma acachapante por cinco a zero."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She won the mayoral election overwhelmingly, with more than 70% of the votes.", "tl": "Ela ganhou as eleições para prefeita de forma acachapante, com mais de 70% dos votos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The lawyer proved his client's innocence in a crushing manner during the trial.", "tl": "O advogado provou a inocência do seu cliente de forma acachapante durante o julgamento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The new cell phone brand overwhelmingly outperformed the competition in just a few months.", "tl": "A nova marca de celulares superou a concorrência de forma acachapante em poucos meses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The presented data overwhelmingly shows the impact of global warming.", "tl": "Os dados apresentados mostram de forma acachapante o impacto do aquecimento global."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The young pianist overwhelmingly defeated the other contestants at the music festival.", "tl": "O jovem pianista derrotou os outros concorrentes de forma acachapante no festival de música."}]}, {"idiom_id": 264, "expression_id": 285, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "ganhar tempo", "english_gloss": "to buy time / to stall", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I need to make up an excuse to buy time before the meeting.", "tl": "Eu preciso inventar uma desculpa para ganhar tempo antes da reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We tried to buy time while the boss hadn't arrived yet.", "tl": "Nós tentamos ganhar tempo enquanto o chefe não chegava."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If we postpone the delivery, we will buy time to correct the mistakes.", "tl": "Se nós adiarmos a entrega, vamos ganhar tempo para corrigir os erros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He is just stalling because he hasn't made a decision yet.", "tl": "Ele está apenas ganhando tempo porque ainda não tomou uma decisão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Speak slowly so that we can buy time and think of a solution.", "tl": "Fale devagar para que possamos ganhar tempo e pensar em uma solução."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "With that vague answer, the politician bought time to prepare himself better.", "tl": "Com aquela resposta vaga, o político ganhou tempo para se preparar melhor."}]}, {"idiom_id": 263, "expression_id": 284, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "na lona", "english_gloss": "on the ropes / down for the count", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After running the marathon, I was completely exhausted.", "tl": "Depois de correr a maratona, eu estava completamente na lona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "With the economic crisis, his small company was on the ropes.", "tl": "Com a crise econômica, a pequena empresa dele ficou na lona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This bad flu left me down for the count the whole week.", "tl": "Essa gripe forte me deixou na lona a semana inteira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After the breakup, he felt down in the dumps for a few months.", "tl": "Depois do fim do namoro, ele se sentiu na lona por alguns meses."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I spent all my money on the trip and now I'm broke.", "tl": "Gastei todo o meu dinheiro na viagem e agora estou na lona."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I worked twelve hours today and got home completely exhausted.", "tl": "Trabalhei doze horas hoje e cheguei em casa na lona."}]}, {"idiom_id": 262, "expression_id": 283, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "correlação de forças", "english_gloss": "balance of power", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With the opposition's victory, the balance of power in parliament changed completely.", "tl": "Com a vitória da oposição, a correlação de forças no parlamento mudou completamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "At the negotiation table, the balance of power was favorable to the workers.", "tl": "Na mesa de negociação, a correlação de forças era favorável aos trabalhadores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The creation of the new military alliance altered the balance of power in the region.", "tl": "A criação da nova aliança militar alterou a correlação de forças na região."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The merger of the two large companies will change the balance of power in the technology market.", "tl": "A fusão das duas grandes empresas vai mudar a correlação de forças no mercado de tecnologia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Before making a decision, the coach analyzed the balance of power between the two teams.", "tl": "Antes de tomar uma decisão, o treinador analisou a correlação de forças entre os dois times."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The street protests helped to balance the balance of power between the government and society.", "tl": "Os protestos de rua ajudaram a equilibrar a correlação de forças entre o governo e a sociedade."}]}, {"idiom_id": 261, "expression_id": 282, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "acabou a conversa", "english_gloss": "end of story / that's it", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I already told you that you are going to bed now, and that's it!", "tl": "Já te disse que vais para a cama agora e acabou a conversa!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We don't have money to buy a new car this year, so end of story.", "tl": "Não temos dinheiro para comprar um carro novo este ano, por isso acabou a conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The deadline is tomorrow at nine in the morning, and that's final.", "tl": "O prazo limite é amanhã às nove da manhã e acabou a conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I am not going to argue with you about this subject anymore, end of story.", "tl": "Eu não vou discutir mais contigo sobre este assunto, acabou a conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Today there are no sweets for anyone, and that's that.", "tl": "Hoje não há doces para ninguém e acabou a conversa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I decided that I am not going to that party, and that's it.", "tl": "Decidi que não vou àquela festa e acabou a conversa."}]}, {"idiom_id": 260, "expression_id": 281, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "caso fique evidente", "english_gloss": "should it become evident", "youtube_id": "HbjXm7E9b5M", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Should it become evident that the project will be delayed, we need to notify the client immediately.", "tl": "Caso fique evidente que o projeto vai atrasar, precisamos avisar o cliente imediatamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Should it become evident that the situation is worsening, we should go to the hospital.", "tl": "Caso fique evidente que a situação está piorando, devemos ir ao hospital."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Should it become evident that the students did not understand the material, the teacher will repeat the explanation.", "tl": "Caso fique evidente que os alunos não compreenderam a matéria, o professor vai repetir a explicação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Should it become evident that the company is making a loss, we will have to cut expenses.", "tl": "Caso fique evidente que a empresa está tendo prejuízo, teremos de cortar despesas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Should it become evident that the app has a security flaw, the team will release an update immediately.", "tl": "Caso fique evidente que o aplicativo tem uma falha de segurança, a equipe lançará uma atualização imediatamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Should it become evident that it is going to rain, it is better for us to cancel the picnic in the park.", "tl": "Caso fique evidente que vai chover, é melhor cancelarmos o piquenique no parque."}]}, {"idiom_id": 259, "expression_id": 280, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "Até as pedras sabem", "english_gloss": "everyone knows, it is common knowledge", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That they are dating in secret? Everyone already knows!", "tl": "Que eles estão namorando em segredo? Até as pedras já sabem!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Everyone knows that the mayor is going to run for office again.", "tl": "Até as pedras sabem que o prefeito vai se candidatar novamente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "There's no use trying to hide the mistake, everyone already knows what happened.", "tl": "Não adianta tentar esconder o erro, até as pedras já sabem o que aconteceu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She pretended to be surprised, but everyone knew about the party.", "tl": "Ela fingiu ficar surpresa, mas até as pedras sabiam da festa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Everyone knows that fuel prices are going to go up next week.", "tl": "Até as pedras sabem que os preços dos combustíveis vão subir na próxima semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Who is going to win the championship? Everyone knows it will be our team.", "tl": "Quem vai ganhar o campeonato? Até as pedras sabem que será o nosso time."}]}, {"idiom_id": 258, "expression_id": 279, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "acerta a mão", "english_gloss": "to hit the mark, get it right", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After trying several times, I finally got the cake recipe right.", "tl": "Depois de tentar várias vezes, finalmente acertei a mão na receita de bolo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In the beginning it's hard to use this tool, but soon you'll get the hang of it.", "tl": "No começo é difícil usar essa ferramenta, mas logo você acerta a mão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The painter hasn't yet got the right shade of blue that the client asked for.", "tl": "O pintor ainda não acertou a mão no tom de azul que o cliente pediu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It's hard to get the right amount of water for these plants.", "tl": "É difícil acertar a mão na quantidade de água para essas plantas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It took the company a while to hit the mark with the marketing campaign, but now sales have gone up.", "tl": "A empresa demorou para acertar a mão na campanha de marketing, mas agora as vendas subiram."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She practiced a lot and finally got the rhythm of the song right.", "tl": "Ela treinou bastante e finalmente acertou a mão no ritmo da música."}]}, {"idiom_id": 257, "expression_id": 278, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "terreno movediço", "english_gloss": "unstable ground, risky situation", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Talking about politics at the dinner table is always entering risky territory.", "tl": "Falar sobre política na mesa de jantar é sempre entrar em terreno movediço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Investing all your money in this new company is stepping on unstable ground.", "tl": "Investir todo o teu dinheiro nesta nova empresa é pisar em terreno movediço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When the boss started asking questions about the project, I realized I was on shaky ground.", "tl": "Quando o chefe começou a fazer perguntas sobre o projeto, percebi que estava em terreno movediço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Without a signed contract, our partnership is on unstable ground.", "tl": "Sem um contrato assinado, a nossa parceria está num terreno movediço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I prefer not to give advice on other people's marriages; it's very risky territory.", "tl": "Eu prefiro não dar conselhos sobre casamentos alheios, é um terreno muito movediço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Changing the rules of the game halfway through the championship puts the organization on shaky ground.", "tl": "Mudar as regras do jogo a meio do campeonato coloca a organização num terreno movediço."}]}, {"idiom_id": 256, "expression_id": 277, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "abrir garrafas de champanhe", "english_gloss": "to celebrate prematurely, pop champagne", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't celebrate before the final whistle; it's still too early to celebrate prematurely.", "tl": "Não comemore antes do apito final; ainda é cedo para abrir garrafas de champanhe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They thought the contract was guaranteed and were already celebrating prematurely, but the client changed their mind.", "tl": "Eles achavam que o contrato estava garantido e já estavam abrindo garrafas de champanhe, mas o cliente mudou de ideia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The candidate started celebrating prematurely before all the votes were counted and ended up losing.", "tl": "O candidato começou a abrir garrafas de champanhe antes de apurar todos os votos e acabou perdendo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Just because the exam went well, don't start celebrating prematurely; we still need to know the grade.", "tl": "Só porque a prova correu bem, não comece já a abrir garrafas de champanhe; ainda falta saber a nota."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We haven't signed the agreement yet, so it's better not to celebrate prematurely.", "tl": "Nós ainda não assinamos o acordo, por isso é melhor não abrir garrafas de champanhe antes do tempo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The investor was already celebrating prematurely with the rise of the shares, but the next day the market fell.", "tl": "O investidor já estava abrindo garrafas de champanhe com a subida das ações, mas no dia seguinte o mercado caiu."}]}, {"idiom_id": 255, "expression_id": 276, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "jogo combinado", "english_gloss": "pre-arranged setup, collusion", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I thought the job interview was a pre-arranged setup to hire the director's cousin.", "tl": "Eu achei que a entrevista de emprego foi um jogo combinado para contratar o primo do diretor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "That television debate seemed like a pre-arranged setup between the two candidates.", "tl": "Aquele debate na televisão parecia um jogo combinado entre os dois candidatos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I'm not going to participate in this auction because I'm sure it's a rigged setup.", "tl": "Não vou participar desse leilão porque tenho certeza de que é jogo combinado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The police are investigating the championship result due to suspicion of a fixed match.", "tl": "A polícia está investigando o resultado do campeonato por suspeita de jogo combinado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We lost the board game because they made a secret pre-arranged deal.", "tl": "Nós perdemos o jogo de tabuleiro porque eles fizeram um jogo combinado em segredo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "There's no point in competing for this prize, everyone knows it's a setup.", "tl": "Não adianta concorrer a esse prêmio, todo mundo sabe que isso é jogo combinado."}]}, {"idiom_id": 254, "expression_id": 275, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "cria ruídos", "english_gloss": "to cause friction, create complications", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The lack of clear communication between departments always creates unnecessary friction.", "tl": "A falta de comunicação clara entre os departamentos sempre cria ruídos desnecessários."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Talking about money during dinner usually causes friction in the family.", "tl": "Falar sobre dinheiro durante o jantar costuma criar ruídos na família."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The management's new decision caused friction among the employees.", "tl": "A nova decisão da gerência criou ruídos entre os funcionários."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "That post on social media ended up causing friction in their relationship.", "tl": "Aquela publicação nas redes sociais acabou por criar ruídos na relação deles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Changing the project rules halfway through will only create friction in the group.", "tl": "Mudar as regras do projeto a meio do caminho só vai criar ruídos no grupo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I prefer to be direct to avoid any misunderstanding that might cause friction between us.", "tl": "Eu prefiro ser direto para evitar qualquer mal-entendido que crie ruídos entre nós."}]}, {"idiom_id": 253, "expression_id": 274, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "marchando com", "english_gloss": "to align with, support, be in step with", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our team is aligning with the board's new decisions.", "tl": "Nossa equipe está marchando com as novas decisões da diretoria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The representative guaranteed that he is in step with the population's wishes.", "tl": "O deputado garantiu que está marchando com os desejos da população."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I feel that I am finally aligning with my own values and not with those of others.", "tl": "Sinto que finalmente estou marchando com os meus próprios valores e não com os dos outros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If we don't keep in step with current technology, we are going to lose many customers.", "tl": "Se não marcharmos com a tecnologia atual, vamos perder muitos clientes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The teachers are supporting the school's new pedagogical project.", "tl": "Os professores estão marchando com o novo projeto pedagógico da escola."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The whole family ended up going along with the decision to sell the old house.", "tl": "Toda a família acabou marchando com a decisão de vender a casa antiga."}]}, {"idiom_id": 252, "expression_id": 273, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "fazem um jogo", "english_gloss": "to play a game, act strategically", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "They never say what they really think; they always play a game to get what they want.", "tl": "Eles nunca dizem o que realmente pensam; fazem sempre um jogo para conseguir o que querem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If the weather is good on Saturday, we will play a game of football with friends.", "tl": "Se o tempo estiver bom no sábado, fazemos um jogo de futebol com os amigos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In that company, people play a very complicated political game to get promoted.", "tl": "Naquela empresa, as pessoas fazem um jogo político muito complicado para subir de cargo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I think she is not being sincere with you; she is just playing a game to see your reaction.", "tl": "Acho que ela não está a ser sincera contigo, ela só faz um jogo para ver a tua reação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Every Friday night, we play a card game as a family.", "tl": "Todas as sextas-feiras à noite, nós fazemos um jogo de cartas em família."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The two directors are playing a power game to see who makes the final decision.", "tl": "Os dois diretores fazem um jogo de poder para ver quem toma a decisão final."}]}, {"idiom_id": 251, "expression_id": 272, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "desviar do assunto", "english_gloss": "to change the subject, get off track", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Whenever I ask about his plans, he tries to change the subject.", "tl": "Sempre que pergunto sobre os planos dele, ele tenta desviar do assunto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Let's not get off track; we need to decide this today.", "tl": "Não vamos desviar do assunto; precisamos decidir isso hoje."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She noticed that he changed the subject when she mentioned the money.", "tl": "Ela percebeu que ele desviou do assunto quando ela mencionou o dinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why are you changing the subject? Are you hiding something?", "tl": "Por que você está desviando do assunto? Está escondendo alguma coisa?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The politician tried to dodge the question during the interview, but the journalist insisted.", "tl": "O político tentou desviar do assunto durante a entrevista, mas o jornalista insistiu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you change the subject now, they will think you are guilty.", "tl": "Se você desviar do assunto agora, eles vão achar que você é culpado."}]}, {"idiom_id": 250, "expression_id": 271, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "deita e rola", "english_gloss": "to do as one pleases, have a field day", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Since the boss is very calm, the team does whatever they want and nobody works seriously.", "tl": "Como o chefe é muito calmo, a equipe deita e rola e ninguém trabalha sério."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The striker had a field day in yesterday's game because the opposing defense was very weak.", "tl": "O atacante deitou e rolou no jogo de ontem porque a defesa adversária estava muito fraca."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you leave the kids alone in the kitchen, they will have a field day with the sweets.", "tl": "Se você deixar as crianças sozinhas na cozinha, elas vão deitar e rolar com os doces."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The competition is having a field day because our company stopped investing in advertising.", "tl": "A concorrência está deitando e rolando porque a nossa empresa parou de investir em propaganda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The guests had a field day at the party, since the food and drinks were free.", "tl": "Os convidados deitaram e rolaram na festa, já que a comida e a bebida eram de graça."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You need to set boundaries, otherwise people will walk all over you.", "tl": "Você precisa impor limites, senão as pessoas deitam e rolam em cima de você."}]}, {"idiom_id": 249, "expression_id": 270, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "manda-chuva", "english_gloss": "big boss, head honcho", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you want a raise, you need to speak directly with the big boss of the company.", "tl": "Se você quer um aumento, precisa falar diretamente com o manda-chuva da empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Who is the head honcho around here? I need authorization to park the car.", "tl": "Quem é o manda-chuva por aqui? Preciso de autorização para estacionar o carro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She is the new big boss of the marketing department, so all decisions go through her.", "tl": "Ela é a nova manda-chuva do departamento de marketing, então todas as decisões passam por ela."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Even though he thinks he's in charge of everything, the real head honcho is the financial director.", "tl": "Apesar de ele achar que manda em tudo, o verdadeiro manda-chuva é o diretor financeiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It's no use complaining to the employees, you have to talk to the big bosses.", "tl": "Não adianta reclamar com os funcionários, você tem que falar com os manda-chuvas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She started as an intern and today she is the head honcho of the whole organization.", "tl": "Ela começou como estagiária e hoje é a manda-chuva de toda a organização."}]}, {"idiom_id": 248, "expression_id": 269, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "baita", "english_gloss": "huge, great (colloquial intensifier)", "youtube_id": "ZtnNbuOAtc4", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Yesterday I got a huge surprise when I arrived home.", "tl": "Ontem recebi uma baita surpresa quando cheguei em casa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "That doctor is a great professional, he helped my family a lot.", "tl": "Aquele médico é um baita profissional, ele ajudou muito a minha família."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We got stuck in a huge traffic jam on the highway because of the accident.", "tl": "Pegamos um baita trânsito na estrada por causa do acidente."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Last night there was a huge rainstorm and the power went out.", "tl": "Ontem à noite caiu uma baita chuva e acabou a energia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This job opening is a great opportunity for your career.", "tl": "Essa vaga de emprego é uma baita oportunidade para a sua carreira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "What a scare! You gave me a huge fright appearing out of nowhere.", "tl": "Que susto! Você me deu um baita susto aparecendo do nada."}]}, {"idiom_id": 201, "expression_id": 222, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se mettre en tête de", "english_gloss": "to set one's mind to", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He got it into his head to learn Japanese in six months.", "tl": "Il s'est mis en tête d'apprendre le japonais en six mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She has set her mind on starting her own business.", "tl": "Elle s'est mise en tête de créer sa propre entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They set their minds on renovating this old country house.", "tl": "Ils se sont mis en tête de rénover cette vieille maison de campagne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I got it into my head to run a marathon before the end of the year.", "tl": "Je me suis mis en tête de courir un marathon avant la fin de l'année."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why did you get it into your head to repaint the living room this weekend?", "tl": "Pourquoi tu t'es mis en tête de repeindre le salon ce week-end ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My brother has set his mind on becoming a great chef.", "tl": "Mon frère s'est mis en tête de devenir un grand chef cuisinier."}]}, {"idiom_id": 200, "expression_id": 221, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en cavale", "english_gloss": "on the run", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After escaping from prison, the prisoner remained on the run for three months.", "tl": "Après s'être évadé de prison, le prisonnier est resté en cavale pendant trois mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The police are actively searching for two suspects currently on the run.", "tl": "La police recherche activement deux suspects actuellement en cavale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In this movie, an innocent man is on the run to prove his innocence.", "tl": "Dans ce film, un homme innocent est en cavale pour prouver son innocence."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Did you see the news? The bank robber is still on the run.", "tl": "Tu as vu les infos ? Le braqueur de la banque est toujours en cavale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "They decided to abandon everything and go on the run abroad.", "tl": "Ils ont décidé de tout abandonner et de partir en cavale à l'étranger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Life on the run is difficult; you have to constantly hide and change your identity.", "tl": "La vie en cavale est difficile, il faut constamment se cacher et changer d'identité."}]}, {"idiom_id": 199, "expression_id": 220, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "prendre la fuite", "english_gloss": "to flee / run away", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As soon as the alarm started ringing, the thief fled.", "tl": "Dès que l'alarme a commencé à sonner, le voleur a pris la fuite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Faced with danger, some prefer to stand and fight, while others decide to run away.", "tl": "Face au danger, certains préfèrent faire face, tandis que d'autres décident de prendre la fuite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The driver responsible for the accident fled before the police arrived.", "tl": "Le conducteur responsable de l'accident a pris la fuite avant l'arrivée de la police."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When they saw the bear approaching the tent, they immediately fled.", "tl": "Quand ils ont vu l'ours s'approcher de la tente, ils ont immédiatement pris la fuite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If the situation gets too stressful at work, I sometimes feel like running away.", "tl": "Si la situation devient trop stressante au travail, j'ai parfois envie de prendre la fuite."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The suspects fled through the small streets of the city center.", "tl": "Les suspects ont pris la fuite à travers les petites rues du centre-ville."}]}, {"idiom_id": 198, "expression_id": 219, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "bouée de sauvetage", "english_gloss": "lifeline / safety net", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The government's financial aid was a real lifeline for our small business.", "tl": "L'aide financière de l'État a été une véritable bouée de sauvetage pour notre petite entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When I went through that difficult time, my friends' support was my lifeline.", "tl": "Quand j'ai traversé cette période difficile, le soutien de mes amis a été ma bouée de sauvetage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Before the boat departed, the captain showed us where the lifebuoys were.", "tl": "Avant le départ du bateau, le capitaine nous a montré où se trouvaient les bouées de sauvetage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I put some money aside in a locked account; it's my safety net in case of hard times.", "tl": "J'ai mis de l'argent de côté sur un compte bloqué, c'est ma bouée de sauvetage en cas de coup dur."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The private tutoring sessions were a lifeline for this struggling student.", "tl": "Les cours de soutien particuliers ont été une bouée de sauvetage pour cet élève en difficulté."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Luckily I had an external backup; it was my safety net when my computer crashed.", "tl": "Heureusement que j'avais une sauvegarde externe, cela a été ma bouée de sauvetage quand mon ordinateur a planté."}]}, {"idiom_id": 197, "expression_id": 218, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en dernier recours", "english_gloss": "as a last resort", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We will only call the on-duty doctor as a last resort.", "tl": "Nous n'appellerons le médecin de garde qu'en dernier recours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She decided to sell her car as a last resort to pay her debts.", "tl": "Elle a décidé de vendre sa voiture en dernier recours pour payer ses dettes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Canceling our trip should only be considered as a last resort.", "tl": "Annuler notre voyage ne doit être envisagé qu'en dernier recours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I will ask my parents for money as a last resort.", "tl": "Je demanderai de l'argent à mes parents en dernier recours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The doctor advised me to only take these sleeping pills as a last resort.", "tl": "Le médecin m'a conseillé de ne prendre ces somnifères qu'en dernier recours."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You should reset your phone only as a last resort.", "tl": "Tu devrais réinitialiser ton téléphone uniquement en dernier recours."}]}, {"idiom_id": 196, "expression_id": 217, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "il y en a pour", "english_gloss": "it amounts to / there is", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Don't worry, it will only take five minutes.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, il y en a pour seulement cinq minutes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I bought some fruits and vegetables, it comes to twenty euros.", "tl": "J'ai acheté des fruits et des légumes, il y en a pour vingt euros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Don't rush, help yourselves, there is enough for everyone.", "tl": "Ne vous pressez pas, servez-vous, il y en a pour tout le monde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Wait for me there, it will take ten minutes maximum.", "tl": "Attends-moi là, il y en aura pour dix minutes maximum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We had the car repaired and it cost a lot.", "tl": "On a fait réparer la voiture et il y en a eu pour cher."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "With all this washing up to do, it's going to take at least an hour.", "tl": "Avec toute cette vaisselle à faire, il y en a pour au moins une heure."}]}, {"idiom_id": 195, "expression_id": 216, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "remettre les pieds", "english_gloss": "to set foot again", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I will never set foot in this restaurant again, the service was horrible.", "tl": "Je ne remettrai plus jamais les pieds dans ce restaurant, le service était horrible."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After a ten-year absence, they finally set foot again in their hometown.", "tl": "Après dix ans d'absence, ils ont enfin remis les pieds dans leur ville natale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We promised never to set foot there again.", "tl": "Nous avons promis de ne plus jamais y remettre les pieds."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If I were you, I wouldn't set foot there again after what happened.", "tl": "Si j'étais toi, je ne remettrais pas les pieds là-bas après ce qui s'est passé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't want him to set foot in my house again after our argument.", "tl": "Je ne veux plus qu'il remette les pieds chez moi après notre dispute."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Do you plan on setting foot in this region again one day?", "tl": "Est-ce que vous comptez remettre les pieds dans cette région un jour ?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 194, "expression_id": 215, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "le gîte et le couvert", "english_gloss": "room and board", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In exchange for a few hours of work on the farm, they offer us room and board.", "tl": "En échange de quelques heures de travail à la ferme, ils nous offrent le gîte et le couvert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "During my studies in Paris, my uncle offered me room and board to help me save money.", "tl": "Pendant mes études à Paris, mon oncle m'a proposé le gîte et le couvert pour m'aider à économiser."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This small mountain inn offers room and board for only fifty euros per night.", "tl": "Cette petite auberge de montagne propose le gîte et le couvert pour seulement cinquante euros par nuit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Even though I have a job now, my parents continue to provide me with room and board for free.", "tl": "Même si j'ai un travail maintenant, mes parents continuent de m'assurer le gîte et le couvert gratuitement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The association is looking for volunteers and promises to provide them with room and board during the whole festival.", "tl": "L'association recherche des bénévoles et s'engage à leur fournir le gîte et le couvert durant tout le festival."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When I went to Canada, family friends warmly offered me room and board.", "tl": "Quand je suis allé au Canada, des amis de la famille m'ont chaleureusement offert le gîte et le couvert."}]}, {"idiom_id": 193, "expression_id": 214, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "au premier abord", "english_gloss": "at first glance", "youtube_id": "8yu0tgpPE00", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "At first glance, he seems a bit cold, but in reality he is very nice.", "tl": "Au premier abord, il a l'air un peu froid, mais en réalité il est très sympa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This problem seemed difficult at first glance, but we found a solution quickly.", "tl": "Ce problème semblait difficile au premier abord, mais nous avons trouvé une solution rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "At first glance, the city may seem noisy, but it has a lot of charm.", "tl": "Au premier abord, la ville peut sembler bruyante, mais elle a beaucoup de charme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "His project is interesting at first glance, but it still lacks details.", "tl": "Son projet est intéressant au premier abord, mais il manque encore de détails."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "At first glance, this book didn't appeal to me at all, and yet I loved it.", "tl": "Au premier abord, ce livre ne m'attirait pas du tout, et pourtant je l'ai adoré."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The job offer seemed perfect at first glance, but the salary was too low.", "tl": "L'offre d'emploi paraissait parfaite au premier abord, mais le salaire était trop bas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 192, "expression_id": 213, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "macht ja die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brutal Jagd auf Migranten", "english_gloss": "is still brutally hunting down migrants", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Even though the new government promised tolerance, the immigration authority ICE is still brutally hunting down migrants", "tl": "Obwohl die neue Regierung Toleranz versprochen hat, macht ja die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brutal Jagd auf Mig"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The news yesterday said that at the border, the immigration authority ICE is still brutally hunting down migrants.", "tl": "In den Nachrichten hieß es gestern, an der Grenze macht ja die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brutal Jagd auf Migra"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many people are protesting in the streets because in many cities, the immigration authority ICE is still brutally huntin", "tl": "Viele Menschen protestieren auf der Straße, denn in vielen Städten macht ja die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brut"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I don't understand why the immigration authority ICE is still brutally hunting down migrants, even though they need work", "tl": "Ich verstehe nicht, warum die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brutal Jagd auf Migranten macht, obwohl sie Arbeitskrä"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Despite all the criticism from abroad, the immigration authority ICE is still brutally hunting down migrants.", "tl": "Trotz aller Kritik aus dem Ausland macht ja die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brutal Jagd auf Migranten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Unfortunately, nothing has changed: In this country, the immigration authority ICE is still brutally hunting down migran", "tl": "Es hat sich leider nichts geändert: In diesem Land macht ja die Einwanderungsbehörde ICE immer noch brutal Jagd auf Migr"}]}, {"idiom_id": 191, "expression_id": 212, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "zum Hohn wird", "english_gloss": "becomes a mockery", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The promised help becomes a mockery if it only arrives in a year.", "tl": "Die versprochene Hilfe wird zum Hohn, wenn sie erst in einem Jahr ankommt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For the victims, this mild court verdict becomes a mockery.", "tl": "Für die Opfer wird dieses milde Urteil vor Gericht zum Hohn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our hard work becomes a mockery if the project is simply stopped now.", "tl": "Unsere harte Arbeit wird zum Hohn, wenn das Projekt jetzt einfach gestoppt wird."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Environmental protection becomes a mockery if we continue to throw away so much plastic.", "tl": "Der Umweltschutz wird zum Hohn, wenn wir weiterhin so viel Plastik wegwerfen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The small wage increase becomes a mockery in view of the rising prices.", "tl": "Die kleine Lohnerhöhung wird angesichts der steigenden Preise zum Hohn."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The new safety rules become a mockery because nobody monitors them.", "tl": "Die neuen Sicherheitsregeln werden zum Hohn, weil sie niemand kontrolliert."}]}, {"idiom_id": 190, "expression_id": 211, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "wenn ich das so sagen darf", "english_gloss": "if I may say so", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Your soup tastes excellent, if I may say so.", "tl": "Deine Suppe schmeckt hervorragend, wenn ich das so sagen darf."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new design is a big step forward, if I may say so.", "tl": "Das neue Design ist ein großer Fortschritt, wenn ich das so sagen darf."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That dress really suits you beautifully, if I may say so.", "tl": "Das Kleid steht dir wirklich ausgezeichnet, wenn ich das so sagen darf."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If I may say so, I think this plan is a bit risky.", "tl": "Wenn ich das so sagen darf, halte ich diesen Plan für etwas riskant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You already speak German very well, if I may say so.", "tl": "Sie sprechen bereits sehr gut Deutsch, wenn ich das so sagen darf."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If I may say so, the other option might be better for us.", "tl": "Wenn ich das so sagen darf, wäre die andere Option vielleicht besser für uns."}]}, {"idiom_id": 189, "expression_id": 210, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "das ist ein Unding", "english_gloss": "that is an absurdity", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is absurd that we have to work unpaid overtime every day.", "tl": "Es ist ein Unding, dass wir jeden Tag unbezahlte Überstunden machen müssen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The fact that the train is delayed by an hour again is really unacceptable!", "tl": "Dass der Zug schon wieder eine Stunde Verspätung hat, das ist wirklich ein Unding!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Giving homework over the holidays is an absurdity for many students.", "tl": "Hausaufgaben über die Ferien aufzugeben, ist für viele Schüler ein Unding."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To charge so much money for such poor service is outrageous.", "tl": "Für so einen schlechten Service so viel Geld zu verlangen, das ist ein Unding."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Having to wait three months for a doctor's appointment is simply unacceptable.", "tl": "Drei Monate auf einen Arzttermin warten zu müssen, ist einfach ein Unding."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Simply throwing plastic waste away in the forest is absolutely unacceptable.", "tl": "Plastikmüll einfach im Wald wegzuwerfen, ist ein absolutes Unding."}]}, {"idiom_id": 188, "expression_id": 209, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "als Witz verbucht", "english_gloss": "chalked up as a joke", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "At first I was angry, but in the end, I simply chalked his remark up as a joke.", "tl": "Zuerst war ich sauer, aber am Ende habe ich seine Bemerkung einfach als Witz verbucht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The strange email from the boss was chalked up as a joke by all the employees.", "tl": "Die seltsame E-Mail vom Chef wurde von allen Mitarbeitern als Witz verbucht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You shouldn't just chalk his threat up as a joke; he is serious.", "tl": "Du solltest seine Drohung nicht einfach als Witz verbuchen, er meint das ernst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When he ran off without paying, we chalked it up as a joke at first.", "tl": "Als er ohne zu bezahlen weglief, haben wir das zuerst als Witz verbucht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Nobody laughed, but she quickly chalked the awkward situation up as a joke.", "tl": "Niemand hat gelacht, aber sie hat die peinliche Situation schnell als Witz verbucht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "His unusual idea was initially only chalked up as a joke in the media.", "tl": "Seine ungewöhnliche Idee wurde in den Medien anfangs nur als Witz verbucht."}]}, {"idiom_id": 187, "expression_id": 208, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert", "english_gloss": "At times it was discussed", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "At times it was indeed discussed whether all employees could stay in the home office permanently.", "tl": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert, ob alle Mitarbeiter dauerhaft im Homeoffice bleiben können."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For a while, there was indeed discussion about starting school classes only at nine o'clock.", "tl": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert, den Unterricht an Schulen erst um neun Uhr beginnen zu lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "At times it was discussed to close the city center completely to cars.", "tl": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert, die Innenstadt komplett für Autos zu sperren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For a time, it was discussed to introduce a four-day work week with full wage compensation.", "tl": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert, eine Vier-Tage-Woche bei vollem Lohnausgleich einzuführen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "At times it was indeed discussed whether public transport should be free for all citizens.", "tl": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert, ob der öffentliche Nahverkehr für alle Bürger kostenlos sein sollte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "For a while, there was discussion about stopping the expensive construction project completely due to the high costs.", "tl": "Zeitweise wurde ja diskutiert, das teure Bauprojekt wegen der hohen Kosten komplett zu stoppen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 186, "expression_id": 207, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "im letzten Moment", "english_gloss": "at the last moment", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I caught the train at the last moment because I had overslept.", "tl": "Ich habe den Zug im letzten Moment erwischt, weil ich verschlafen hatte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She changed her mind at the last moment and didn't come along after all.", "tl": "Sie hat ihre Meinung im letzten Moment geändert und ist doch nicht mitgekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We were able to submit the project at the last moment before the deadline expired.", "tl": "Wir konnten das Projekt im letzten Moment abgeben, bevor die Frist ablief."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The driver was able to brake at the last moment to prevent an accident.", "tl": "Der Autofahrer konnte im letzten Moment bremsen, um einen Unfall zu verhindern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Fortunately, we got two tickets for the concert at the last moment.", "tl": "Zum Glück haben wir im letzten Moment noch zwei Tickets für das Konzert bekommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My colleague helped me at the last moment to finish the presentation.", "tl": "Mein Kollege hat mir im letzten Moment geholfen, die Präsentation fertigzustellen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 185, "expression_id": 206, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt", "english_gloss": "relocated their World Cup base", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I heard the Swedish team has indeed relocated its World Cup base to Mexico.", "tl": "Ich habe gehört, das schwedische Team hat sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The team has, as you know, relocated its World Cup base to Mexico to get better used to the hot climate.", "tl": "Das Team hat sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt, um sich besser an das heiße Klima zu gewöhnen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Spain has, as you know, relocated its World Cup base to Mexico because there are more modern training pitches there.", "tl": "Spanien hat sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt, weil es dort modernere Trainingsplätze gibt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The defending champion has indeed relocated its World Cup base to Mexico to escape the heavy pressure from the domestic ", "tl": "Der Titelverteidiger hat sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt, um dem großen Druck der heimischen Medien zu entkommen"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our football association has, as you know, relocated its World Cup base to Mexico so that the players can fully concentr", "tl": "Unser Fußballverband hat sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt, damit die Spieler sich ganz auf das Turnier konzentrie"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Did you already know? The national team has indeed relocated its World Cup base to Mexico and is already training there.", "tl": "Wusstest du schon? Das Nationalteam hat sein WM-Quartier ja nach Mexiko verlegt und trainiert bereits dort."}]}, {"idiom_id": 184, "expression_id": 205, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür gerühmt hat", "english_gloss": "boasted about it himself", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It's funny that he is complaining about the project now, even though he boasted about it himself just half a year ago.", "tl": "Es ist lustig, dass er sich jetzt über das Projekt beschwert, obwohl er sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür ger"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I can't believe that this is the colleague who boasted about it herself just half a year ago.", "tl": "Ich kann nicht glauben, dass das die Kollegin ist, die sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür gerühmt hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My boss is acting now as if the idea were bad, even though he boasted about it himself just half a year ago.", "tl": "Mein Chef tut jetzt so, als wäre die Idee schlecht, obwohl er sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür gerühmt hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The politician wants to know nothing more about the law, even though he boasted about it himself just half a year ago.", "tl": "Der Politiker will nichts mehr von dem Gesetz wissen, obwohl er sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür gerühmt hat"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Now he is ashamed of the result, but he boasted about it himself just half a year ago.", "tl": "Jetzt schämt er sich für das Ergebnis, aber er hat sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür gerühmt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It is hard to believe that he boasted about it himself just half a year ago.", "tl": "Es ist kaum zu glauben, dass er sich vor einem halben Jahr noch selbst dafür gerühmt hat."}]}, {"idiom_id": 183, "expression_id": 204, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Fremdscham auslöst", "english_gloss": "triggers secondhand embarrassment", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I can't watch this reality show because it simply triggers secondhand embarrassment in me.", "tl": "Ich kann diese Reality-Show nicht sehen, weil sie bei mir einfach nur Fremdscham auslöst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss's bad joke often triggers secondhand embarrassment among the employees.", "tl": "Der schlechte Witz des Chefs löst bei den Mitarbeitern oft Fremdscham aus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "His speech at the wedding was so embarrassing that it triggered secondhand embarrassment in all the guests.", "tl": "Seine Rede auf der Hochzeit war so peinlich, dass sie bei allen Gästen Fremdscham ausgelöst hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He always tries to be cool without realizing that he only triggers secondhand embarrassment by doing so.", "tl": "Er versucht immer cool zu sein, ohne zu merken, dass er damit nur Fremdscham auslöst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Some videos on the internet can trigger real secondhand embarrassment.", "tl": "Manche Videos im Internet können echte Fremdscham auslösen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "That is behavior that triggers secondhand embarrassment in many people.", "tl": "Das ist ein Verhalten, das bei vielen Menschen Fremdscham auslöst."}]}, {"idiom_id": 182, "expression_id": 203, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "In seinem vorherigen Leben", "english_gloss": "In his previous life", "youtube_id": "BRUXS4l2J70", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In his previous life, he must have been a cat because he sleeps so much.", "tl": "In seinem vorherigen Leben war er bestimmt eine Katze, weil er so viel schläft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He talks about his time in Paris as if it had been in his previous life.", "tl": "Er spricht über seine Zeit in Paris, als wäre es in seinem vorherigen Leben gewesen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My grandfather always says that he was a sailor in his previous life.", "tl": "Mein Großvater sagt immer, dass er in seinem vorherigen Leben ein Seefahrer war."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He firmly believes that he was a famous musician in his previous life.", "tl": "Er glaubt fest daran, dass er in seinem vorherigen Leben ein berühmter Musiker war."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In his previous life, he must have lived by the sea, as he loves the water so much.", "tl": "In seinem vorherigen Leben muss er am Meer gelebt haben, da er das Wasser so sehr liebt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Before he became a teacher, he worked in a bank – that was like in his previous life.", "tl": "Bevor er Lehrer wurde, arbeitete er in einer Bank – das war wie in seinem vorherigen Leben."}]}, {"idiom_id": 181, "expression_id": 202, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "unter Druck stehen", "english_gloss": "to be under pressure", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Because of the new project, the whole team is currently under a lot of pressure.", "tl": "Wegen des neuen Projekts steht das ganze Team momentan stark unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Before the exams, many students are under pressure.", "tl": "Vor den Prüfungen stehen viele Studenten unter Druck."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He is under financial pressure because he has to pay his rent.", "tl": "Er steht finanziell unter Druck, weil er seine Miete bezahlen muss."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My boss is also under pressure, that's why he is so stressed today.", "tl": "Mein Chef steht auch unter Druck, deshalb ist er heute so gestresst."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't want to make a decision right now when I'm under so much pressure.", "tl": "Ich möchte jetzt keine Entscheidung treffen, wenn ich so unter Druck stehe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The team has to win the next game, so they are under great pressure.", "tl": "Die Mannschaft muss das nächste Spiel gewinnen, sie steht also unter großem Druck."}]}, {"idiom_id": 180, "expression_id": 201, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "schlägt große Wellen", "english_gloss": "causes a big stir", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The boss's decision to abolish working from home is causing a big stir in the company.", "tl": "Die Entscheidung des Chefs, das Homeoffice abzuschaffen, schlägt große Wellen in der Firma."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new scandal surrounding the politician is making big waves in the media.", "tl": "Der neue Skandal um den Politiker schlägt große Wellen in den Medien."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The new mobile phone ban at our school is causing a big stir among the students.", "tl": "Das neue Handyverbot an unserer Schule schlägt große Wellen unter den Schülern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The rumor about a new smartphone model is already making big waves on the internet.", "tl": "Das Gerücht über ein neues Smartphone-Modell schlägt bereits große Wellen im Internet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "His critical remark in the interview caused a big stir yesterday.", "tl": "Seine kritische Äußerung im Interview hat gestern große Wellen geschlagen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The plan to build a new parking lot in the city center is causing a big stir among the citizens.", "tl": "Der Plan, einen neuen Parkplatz im Stadtzentrum zu bauen, schlägt große Wellen bei den Bürgern."}]}, {"idiom_id": 179, "expression_id": 200, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "die nächste Frage vorweggenommen", "english_gloss": "preempted the next question", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With his answer, the politician preempted the journalist's next question.", "tl": "Der Politiker hat mit seiner Antwort die nächste Frage des Journalisten vorweggenommen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You have actually already preempted my next question with that, thank you!", "tl": "Sie haben damit eigentlich schon meine nächste Frage vorweggenommen, danke!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The professor explained the formula and thereby preempted the students' next question.", "tl": "Der Professor erklärte die Formel und nahm damit die nächste Frage der Studenten vorweg."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To preempt the next question: Yes, delivery is completely free of charge for you.", "tl": "Um die nächste Frage vorwegzunehmen: Ja, die Lieferung ist für Sie völlig kostenlos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You just preempted my next question, because I wanted to know exactly the same thing.", "tl": "Du hast gerade meine nächste Frage vorweggenommen, ich wollte nämlich genau das Gleiche wissen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "With this new graphic, we have already preempted the customers' next question.", "tl": "Mit dieser neuen Grafik haben wir die nächste Frage der Kunden bereits vorweggenommen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 178, "expression_id": 199, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "unter Spannung stehen", "english_gloss": "to be under tension", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Watch out! This electrical wire is still live.", "tl": "Achtung! Diese elektrische Leitung steht immer noch unter Spannung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Before the important job interview, he was tense all morning.", "tl": "Vor dem wichtigen Vorstellungsgespräch stand er den ganzen Morgen unter Spannung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The atmosphere in the office was tense because of the sudden layoffs.", "tl": "Die Atmosphäre im Büro stand wegen der plötzlichen Kündigungen unter Spannung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "During your workout, make sure your muscles are always under slight tension.", "tl": "Achte beim Training darauf, dass deine Muskeln immer leicht unter Spannung stehen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Since the big argument, the relationship between the two siblings has been strained.", "tl": "Seit dem großen Streit steht die Beziehung der beiden Geschwister unter Spannung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I just can't relax today; I'm somehow completely tense.", "tl": "Ich kann mich heute einfach nicht entspannen, ich stehe irgendwie völlig unter Spannung."}]}, {"idiom_id": 177, "expression_id": 198, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "hinter sich gelassen", "english_gloss": "left behind", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We have finally left the difficult times behind us.", "tl": "Wir haben die schwierige Zeit endlich hinter uns gelassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He left his hometown behind to study in Berlin.", "tl": "Er hat seine Heimatstadt hinter sich gelassen, um in Berlin zu studieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After years of work, I have left the competition behind.", "tl": "Nach jahrelanger Arbeit habe ich die Konkurrenz hinter mir gelassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "On vacation, they completely left the stress of everyday life behind.", "tl": "Im Urlaub haben sie den Alltagsstress komplett hinter sich gelassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You should leave your past mistakes behind you.", "tl": "Du solltest deine Fehler aus der Vergangenheit hinter dir lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She left all the other runners behind and won the race.", "tl": "Sie hat alle anderen Läuferinnen hinter sich gelassen und das Rennen gewonnen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 176, "expression_id": 197, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "an der Tagesordnung", "english_gloss": "the order of the day", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Unfortunately, overtime is the order of the day in this department.", "tl": "In dieser Abteilung sind Überstunden leider an der Tagesordnung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In autumn, rain and strong winds are a daily occurrence here.", "tl": "Im Herbst sind Regen und starker Wind hier an der Tagesordnung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Technical problems were commonplace at the beginning of this project.", "tl": "Technische Probleme waren am Anfang bei diesem Projekt an der Tagesordnung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In school, minor arguments in the schoolyard were a daily occurrence.", "tl": "In der Schule waren kleine Streitereien auf dem Pausenhof an der Tagesordnung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Train delays have now become a daily occurrence for commuters.", "tl": "Verspätungen bei der Bahn sind für Pendler mittlerweile an der Tagesordnung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Misunderstandings are often commonplace at the beginning of a new relationship.", "tl": "Missverständnisse sind in einer neuen Beziehung am Anfang oft an der Tagesordnung."}]}, {"idiom_id": 175, "expression_id": 196, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in der Nacht auf Mittwoch", "english_gloss": "in the night leading to Wednesday", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the night leading to Wednesday, there was a heavy thunderstorm in our region.", "tl": "In der Nacht auf Mittwoch gab es ein schweres Gewitter in unserer Region."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The highway will be closed in the night leading to Wednesday due to construction work.", "tl": "Die Autobahn wird in der Nacht auf Mittwoch wegen Bauarbeiten gesperrt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I could hardly sleep in the night leading to Wednesday because it was so hot.", "tl": "Ich konnte in der Nacht auf Mittwoch kaum schlafen, weil es so heiß war."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In the night leading to Wednesday, unknown persons stole a bicycle from our garden.", "tl": "In der Nacht auf Mittwoch haben Unbekannte ein Fahrrad aus unserem Garten gestohlen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The website will not be accessible for a few hours in the night leading to Wednesday.", "tl": "Die Website wird in der Nacht auf Mittwoch für einige Stunden nicht erreichbar sein."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "My flight doesn't leave until the night leading to Wednesday, so I still have enough time to pack.", "tl": "Mein Flug geht erst in der Nacht auf Mittwoch, also habe ich noch genug Zeit zum Packen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 174, "expression_id": 195, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "rasend schnell", "english_gloss": "blazingly fast", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With the new fiber-optic connection, the internet loads blazingly fast.", "tl": "Mit dem neuen Glasfaseranschluss lädt das Internet rasend schnell."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Time always passes blazingly fast on vacation.", "tl": "Die Zeit vergeht im Urlaub immer rasend schnell."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The red sports car drove past us blazingly fast.", "tl": "Das rote Sportauto fuhr rasend schnell an uns vorbei."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Our new team member learns blazingly fast and already works independently.", "tl": "Unser neues Teammitglied lernt rasend schnell und arbeitet schon selbstständig."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The news of the company's closure spread blazingly fast.", "tl": "Die Nachricht von der Schließung der Firma verbreitete sich rasend schnell."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The weather changed blazingly fast today; suddenly a storm is brewing.", "tl": "Das Wetter hat sich heute rasend schnell geändert, plötzlich zieht ein Sturm auf."}]}, {"idiom_id": 173, "expression_id": 194, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "immer mal wieder", "english_gloss": "every now and then", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I go jogging every now and then to stay fit.", "tl": "Ich gehe immer mal wieder joggen, um fit zu bleiben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We meet up for a coffee every now and then to chat.", "tl": "Wir treffen uns immer mal wieder auf einen Kaffee, um zu quatschen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You should back up your data on an external hard drive every now and then.", "tl": "Man sollte seine Daten immer mal wieder auf einer externen Festplatte sichern."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In the summer it rains here every now and then, but mostly it is sunny.", "tl": "Im Sommer regnet es hier immer mal wieder, aber meistens ist es sonnig."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My boss praises me every now and then for my good work.", "tl": "Mein Chef lobt mich immer mal wieder für meine gute Arbeit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I visit my old hometown every now and then to see my family.", "tl": "Ich besuche immer mal wieder meine alte Heimatstadt, um meine Familie zu sehen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 172, "expression_id": 193, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "so zynisch das klingt", "english_gloss": "as cynical as it sounds", "youtube_id": "RohkznZfY1A", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As cynical as it sounds, the layoff was the best thing that could have happened to me.", "tl": "So zynisch das klingt, aber die Kündigung war das Beste, was mir passieren konnte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "As cynical as it sounds, the company actually benefits from the current crisis.", "tl": "So zynisch das klingt, das Unternehmen profitiert tatsächlich von der aktuellen Krise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "As cynical as it sounds, I'm glad we broke up before the vacation.", "tl": "So zynisch das klingt, ich bin froh, dass wir uns vor dem Urlaub getrennt haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "As cynical as it sounds, the accident opened his eyes and changed his life.", "tl": "So zynisch das klingt, der Unfall hat ihm die Augen geöffnet und sein Leben verändert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "As cynical as it sounds, the housing shortage is good for landlords who want to raise prices.", "tl": "So zynisch das klingt, der Wohnungsmangel ist gut für Vermieter, die die Preise erhöhen wollen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "As cynical as it sounds, the bad weather helped us save money because we stayed at home.", "tl": "So zynisch das klingt, das schlechte Wetter hat uns geholfen, Geld zu sparen, weil wir zu Hause geblieben sind."}]}, {"idiom_id": 171, "expression_id": 192, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich ... freikaufen", "english_gloss": "to buy one's way out", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He doesn't want to help with the move this weekend, so he is trying to buy his way out with a donation.", "tl": "Er will am Wochenende nicht beim Umzug helfen, also versucht er, sich mit einer Spende freizukaufen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The hostages were finally able to buy their way out after long negotiations.", "tl": "Die Entführten konnten sich nach langen Verhandlungen endlich freikaufen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The young athlete wants to buy his way out of his current contract in order to change clubs.", "tl": "Der junge Sportler möchte sich aus seinem laufenden Vertrag freikaufen, um den Verein zu wechseln."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Do you really believe you can just buy your way out of every mistake with money?", "tl": "Glaubst du wirklich, du kannst dich von jedem Fehler einfach mit Geld freikaufen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Instead of going to prison, he bought his way out with a very heavy fine.", "tl": "Statt ins Gefängnis zu gehen, hat er sich mit einer sehr hohen Geldstrafe freigekauft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Sometimes I wish I could buy my way out of all my daily duties.", "tl": "Manchmal wünsche ich mir, ich könnte mich von all meinen täglichen Pflichten freikaufen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 170, "expression_id": 191, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich gerichtlich zu wehren", "english_gloss": "to defend oneself legally", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If the landlord increases the rent illegally, you have the right to defend yourself legally.", "tl": "Wenn der Vermieter die Miete illegal erhöht, haben Sie das Recht, sich gerichtlich zu wehren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "After the unfair dismissal, he decided to take legal action against his former boss.", "tl": "Nach der ungerechten Kündigung beschloss er, sich gerichtlich gegen seinen ehemaligen Chef zu wehren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The company did not want to pay for the damage, so the customer defended herself legally.", "tl": "Die Firma wollte den Schaden nicht bezahlen, also wehrte sich die Kundin gerichtlich."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Have you ever legally defended yourselves against a decision by the authorities?", "tl": "Habt ihr euch schon mal gerichtlich gegen eine Entscheidung der Behörden gewehrt?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is expensive and exhausting to defend oneself legally, but sometimes there is no other way.", "tl": "Es ist teuer und anstrengend, sich gerichtlich zu wehren, aber manchmal gibt es keinen anderen Weg."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If they damage my reputation, I will definitely defend myself legally.", "tl": "Wenn sie meinen Ruf schädigen, werde ich mich auf jeden Fall gerichtlich wehren."}]}, {"idiom_id": 169, "expression_id": 190, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "einhergehend mit", "english_gloss": "going hand in hand with / accompanying", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Digitalization brings many advantages, but the changes associated with it make some employees feel insecure.", "tl": "Die Digitalisierung bringt viele Vorteile, aber die damit einhergehenden Veränderungen verunsichern einige Mitarbeiter."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Along with a healthy diet, one should also exercise regularly.", "tl": "Einhergehend mit einer gesunden Ernährung sollte man sich auch regelmäßig bewegen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Inflation and the accompanying increase in prices are putting a strain on many families.", "tl": "Die Inflation und die damit einhergehende Erhöhung der Preise belasten viele Familien."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The storm, accompanied by heavy rain, caused a lot of damage in the city yesterday.", "tl": "Der Sturm, einhergehend mit starkem Regen, verursachte gestern viele Schäden in der Stadt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Her new position as boss was accompanied by more responsibility.", "tl": "Ihre neue Position als Chefin ist mit mehr Verantwortung einhergegangen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The introduction of the new software was accompanied by some technical problems.", "tl": "Die Einführung der neuen Software ging mit einigen technischen Problemen einher."}]}, {"idiom_id": 168, "expression_id": 189, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in gewisser Weise", "english_gloss": "in a certain way / to some extent", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In a certain way, I can understand his decision, even if I don't agree.", "tl": "Ich kann seine Entscheidung in gewisser Weise verstehen, auch wenn ich nicht zustimme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The project was a success to some extent, although we didn't quite reach the goal.", "tl": "Das Projekt war in gewisser Weise ein Erfolg, obwohl wir das Ziel nicht ganz erreicht haben."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "New technologies make our lives easier in a certain way, but also more stressful.", "tl": "Neue Technologien machen unser Leben in gewisser Weise einfacher, aber auch stressiger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He is right, we are responsible for our own happiness to some extent.", "tl": "Er hat recht, wir sind in gewisser Weise für unser eigenes Glück verantwortlich."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Her criticism is justified to some extent, but the tone was rude.", "tl": "Ihre Kritik ist in gewisser Weise berechtigt, aber der Ton war unhöflich."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Every book is, in a certain way, a journey into another world.", "tl": "Jedes Buch ist in gewisser Weise eine Reise in eine andere Welt."}]}, {"idiom_id": 167, "expression_id": 188, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "mal angenommen", "english_gloss": "assuming that / let's assume", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Let's assume we fly to Spain in the summer: where exactly do we want to go?", "tl": "Mal angenommen, wir fliegen im Sommer nach Spanien: Wo genau wollen wir hin?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Assuming you had tomorrow off, what would you do with the day?", "tl": "Mal angenommen, du hättest morgen frei – was würdest du mit dem Tag machen?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Let's assume the project isn't finished on time, do we have a plan B then?", "tl": "Mal angenommen, das Projekt wird nicht rechtzeitig fertig, haben wir dann einen Plan B?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Assuming I help you move, will you invite me to dinner then?", "tl": "Mal angenommen, ich helfe dir beim Umzug, lädst du mich dann zum Essen ein?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Let's assume it rains on the weekend, can we celebrate the barbecue indoors too?", "tl": "Mal angenommen, es regnet am Wochenende, können wir das Grillfest auch drinnen feiern?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Assuming you win a million euros, would you quit your job immediately?", "tl": "Mal angenommen, du gewinnst eine Million Euro: Würdest du deinen Job sofort kündigen?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 166, "expression_id": 187, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Kritik sich daran auch entzündet", "english_gloss": "criticism is also sparked by it", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "There are many advantages, but criticism is also sparked by the fact that working hours are now more strictly monitored.", "tl": "Es gibt viele Vorteile, aber die Kritik entzündet sich auch daran, dass die Arbeitszeiten jetzt strenger kontrolliert we"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Although the new cycle path is safe, criticism is also sparked by the fact that many parking spaces are now being lost.", "tl": "Der neue Radweg ist zwar sicher, doch die Kritik entzündet sich auch daran, dass nun viele Parkplätze wegfallen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The tablets are useful, but criticism is also sparked by the fact that the teachers were not trained enough.", "tl": "Die Tablets sind nützlich, aber die Kritik entzündet sich auch daran, dass die Lehrer nicht genug geschult wurden."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The reform is supposed to help the environment, but criticism is also sparked by the fact that petrol prices are rising.", "tl": "Die Reform soll der Umwelt helfen, doch die Kritik entzündet sich auch daran, dass die Preise für Benzin steigen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The exhibition is very popular, although criticism is also sparked by how expensive the tickets are.", "tl": "Die Ausstellung ist sehr beliebt, obwohl sich die Kritik auch daran entzündet, wie teuer die Eintrittskarten sind."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The design of the app is modern, but criticism is also sparked by the fact that some functions are now more complicated.", "tl": "Das Design der App ist modern, aber die Kritik entzündet sich auch daran, dass einige Funktionen jetzt komplizierter sin"}]}, {"idiom_id": 165, "expression_id": 186, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "voll des Lobes ist", "english_gloss": "is full of praise", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The boss is full of praise for our team's new project.", "tl": "Der Chef ist voll des Lobes für das neue Projekt unseres Teams."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The teacher was full of praise for the students' homework.", "tl": "Die Lehrerin war voll des Lobes über die Hausaufgaben der Schüler."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "My mother is full of praise for the food in this restaurant.", "tl": "Meine Mutter ist voll des Lobes über das Essen in diesem Restaurant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The customers are full of praise for our fast customer service.", "tl": "Die Kunden sind voll des Lobes für unseren schnellen Kundenservice."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "After the game, the coach was full of praise for the team.", "tl": "Der Trainer war nach dem Spiel voll des Lobes für die Mannschaft."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The press is full of praise for the director's new film.", "tl": "Die Presse ist voll des Lobes für den neuen Film des Regisseurs."}]}, {"idiom_id": 164, "expression_id": 185, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "in Kraft getreten", "english_gloss": "came into force / took effect", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new law came into force on the first of January.", "tl": "Das neue Gesetz ist am ersten Januar in Kraft getreten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new safety rules for the factory took effect yesterday.", "tl": "Die neuen Sicherheitsregeln für die Fabrik sind gestern in Kraft getreten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The travel warning officially came into force starting today.", "tl": "Die Reisewarnung ist ab heute offiziell in Kraft getreten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The rental agreement only took effect after the landlord's signature.", "tl": "Der Mietvertrag ist erst nach der Unterschrift des Vermieters in Kraft getreten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new exam regulations have come into force for all students.", "tl": "Die neue Prüfungsordnung ist für alle Studenten in Kraft getreten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The driving ban for older cars has taken effect in the city center.", "tl": "Das Fahrverbot für ältere Autos ist in der Innenstadt in Kraft getreten."}]}, {"idiom_id": 163, "expression_id": 184, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "sich gegen Geflüchtete abschotten", "english_gloss": "to seal/shield oneself off from refugees", "youtube_id": "3yeyV4Q2RS0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Some European countries want to shield themselves more and more from refugees.", "tl": "Einige europäische Länder wollen sich immer mehr gegen Geflüchtete abschotten."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It is not a solution to simply seal oneself off from refugees and close the borders.", "tl": "Es ist keine Lösung, sich einfach gegen Geflüchtete abzuschotten und die Grenzen zu schließen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The rich region shields itself from refugees instead of helping them.", "tl": "Die reiche Region schottet sich gegen Geflüchtete ab, anstatt ihnen zu helfen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why is the government sealing itself off so strongly from refugees?", "tl": "Warum schottet sich die Regierung so stark gegen Geflüchtete ab?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If we shield ourselves from refugees, we lose our humanity.", "tl": "Wenn wir uns gegen Geflüchtete abschotten, verlieren wir unsere Menschlichkeit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Many citizens criticize the fact that the European Union is sealing itself off from refugees.", "tl": "Viele Bürger kritisieren, dass sich die Europäische Union gegen Geflüchtete abschottet."}]}, {"idiom_id": 162, "expression_id": 140, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vem de dentro", "english_gloss": "to come from within", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "True happiness comes from within, not from the things we buy.", "tl": "A verdadeira felicidade vem de dentro, não das coisas que compramos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In the most difficult times, the strength to keep going comes from within.", "tl": "Nas horas mais difíceis, a força para continuar vem de dentro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "True beauty comes from within, through our actions and kindness.", "tl": "A verdadeira beleza vem de dentro, através das nossas ações e bondade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is not possible to force someone to change; that desire has to come from within.", "tl": "Não é possível forçar alguém a mudar; essa vontade tem de vir de dentro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The inspiration to write this book came from within, from my own memories.", "tl": "A inspiração para escrever este livro veio de dentro, das minhas próprias memórias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I feel a deep peace that comes from within and helps me stay calm.", "tl": "Sinto uma paz profunda que vem de dentro e me ajuda a manter a calma."}]}, {"idiom_id": 161, "expression_id": 139, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "fazer por obrigação", "english_gloss": "to do out of obligation", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I don't like cleaning the house on Saturdays, but I do it out of obligation.", "tl": "Eu não gosto de limpar a casa ao sábado, mas faço-o por obrigação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He makes these family visits only out of obligation, not because he really wants to.", "tl": "Ele faz estas visitas de família apenas por obrigação, não porque realmente queira."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You shouldn't do favors for your friends just out of obligation.", "tl": "Não deves fazer favores aos teus amigos apenas por obrigação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She does that job out of obligation, as she needs to pay the bills at the end of the month.", "tl": "Ela faz aquele trabalho por obrigação, pois precisa de pagar as contas ao fim do mês."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We did that out of obligation, but the truth is we didn't want to go.", "tl": "Nós fizemos aquilo por obrigação, mas a verdade é que não queríamos ir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you do things only out of obligation, the result will never be very good.", "tl": "Se fizeres as coisas apenas por obrigação, o resultado nunca será muito bom."}]}, {"idiom_id": 160, "expression_id": 138, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "Para começo de conversa", "english_gloss": "for starters / to begin with", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "To begin with, we need to buy all the ingredients for the recipe.", "tl": "Para começo de conversa, nós precisamos comprar todos os ingredientes da receita."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For starters, the project hasn't been approved by the director yet.", "tl": "Para começo de conversa, o projeto ainda não foi aprovado pelo diretor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I didn't go to the party because, to begin with, I wasn't even invited.", "tl": "Eu não fui à festa porque, para começo de conversa, eu nem fui convidado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For starters, traveling in the summer is much more expensive than in the winter.", "tl": "Para começo de conversa, viajar no verão é muito mais caro do que no inverno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "To begin with, you should practice your pronunciation every day.", "tl": "Para começo de conversa, você deve praticar a pronúncia todos os dias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We can't buy this house; for starters, we don't have enough money.", "tl": "Nós não podemos comprar essa casa; para começo de conversa, não temos dinheiro suficiente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 159, "expression_id": 137, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "é outra coisa", "english_gloss": "it's a completely different story", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Eating fresh fruit directly from the tree is a completely different story.", "tl": "Comer fruta fresca diretamente da árvore é outra coisa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Traveling by train is good, but going by car is a whole different story because we have more freedom.", "tl": "Viajar de comboio é bom, mas ir de carro é outra coisa porque temos mais liberdade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Working from home is comfortable, but being in the office with the team is a completely different thing.", "tl": "Trabalhar em casa é confortável, mas estar no escritório com a equipa é outra coisa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Studying grammar helps, but speaking with natives every day is a whole different story.", "tl": "Estudar gramática ajuda, mas falar com nativos todos os dias é outra coisa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "That cheap coffee is acceptable, but this artisanal coffee is on a completely different level.", "tl": "Aquele café barato é aceitável, mas este café artesanal é outra coisa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Watching the game on television is good, but going to the stadium is a completely different story.", "tl": "Ver o jogo na televisão é bom, mas ir ao estádio é outra coisa."}]}, {"idiom_id": 158, "expression_id": 136, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "não consigo me achar", "english_gloss": "to not be able to find one's way", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I'm downtown without internet and I can't find my way.", "tl": "Estou no centro da cidade sem internet e não consigo me achar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They just arrived at college and still can't find their way around campus.", "tl": "Eles acabaram de chegar na faculdade e ainda não conseguem se achar no campus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The airport is giant; I can't find my way without looking at the map.", "tl": "O aeroporto é gigante; eu não consigo me achar sem olhar o mapa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Whenever I come to this new neighborhood, I can't find my way.", "tl": "Sempre que venho a este bairro novo, eu não consigo me achar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Are you walking in circles? Can't you find your way?", "tl": "Você está andando em círculos? Não consegue se achar?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We entered through that door and now we can't find our way in this building.", "tl": "Nós entramos por aquela porta e agora não conseguimos nos achar neste prédio."}]}, {"idiom_id": 157, "expression_id": 135, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "vale-tudo", "english_gloss": "free-for-all / anything goes", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the election campaign, it seems to have become a free-for-all to get votes.", "tl": "Na campanha eleitoral, parece que virou um vale-tudo para conseguir votos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Couples' arguments shouldn't be a free-for-all where you say anything just to hurt.", "tl": "Discussões de casal não deviam ser um vale-tudo onde se diz qualquer coisa para magoar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The technology market is a real free-for-all; companies do everything to beat the competition.", "tl": "O mercado de tecnologia é um verdadeiro vale-tudo; as empresas fazem de tudo para vencer a concorrência."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The store opened at six in the morning and Black Friday shopping turned into a free-for-all.", "tl": "A loja abriu às seis da manhã e as compras de Black Friday viraram um vale-tudo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We wanted to play a friendly game of soccer, but the game ended up turning into a free-for-all.", "tl": "Nós queríamos jogar futebol de forma amigável, mas o jogo acabou virando um vale-tudo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In that company, the fight for promotions is a free-for-all with no clear rules.", "tl": "Naquela empresa, a disputa pelas promoções é um vale-tudo sem regras claras."}]}, {"idiom_id": 156, "expression_id": 134, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "fora de sintonia", "english_gloss": "out of sync / out of touch", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I feel that our department is a bit out of sync with the company's management.", "tl": "Sinto que o nosso departamento está um pouco fora de sintonia com a direção da empresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We used to agree on everything, but lately we seem out of sync.", "tl": "Nós costumávamos concordar em tudo, mas ultimamente parecemos fora de sintonia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The audio and video of this movie are completely out of sync.", "tl": "O áudio e o vídeo deste filme estão completamente fora de sintonia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Some politicians seem totally out of touch with the country's reality.", "tl": "Alguns políticos parecem totalmente fora de sintonia com a realidade do país."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The dancers got out of sync during the performance.", "tl": "Os dançarinos ficaram fora de sintonia durante a apresentação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After so many years living apart, they met again but were out of sync.", "tl": "Depois de tantos anos a viver longe, eles voltaram a encontrar-se mas estavam fora de sintonia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 155, "expression_id": 133, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "fazer tudo de novo", "english_gloss": "to do it all over again", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If the computer freezes now, I'll have to do it all over again.", "tl": "Se o computador travar agora, vou ter que fazer tudo de novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If I could go back in time, I would do it all over again.", "tl": "Se eu pudesse voltar no tempo, eu faria tudo de novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The teacher didn't like our project and asked us to do it all over again.", "tl": "O professor não gostou do nosso trabalho e pediu para fazermos tudo de novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The recipe went wrong, so I had to throw it away and do it all over again.", "tl": "A receita deu errado, então tive que jogar fora e fazer tudo de novo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I lost the documents and now I'll need to do it all over again to get a duplicate.", "tl": "Perdi os documentos e agora vou precisar fazer tudo de novo para conseguir a segunda via."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He made a silly mistake at the beginning of the report and had to do it all over again.", "tl": "Ele cometeu um erro bobo no início do relatório e teve que fazer tudo de novo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 154, "expression_id": 132, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "não tem a menor ideia", "english_gloss": "to not have the slightest idea", "youtube_id": "bsZb64m3WsY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I don't have the slightest idea where I left my house keys.", "tl": "Eu não tenho a menor ideia de onde deixei as minhas chaves de casa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My boss doesn't have the slightest idea how to solve this problem.", "tl": "O meu chefe não tem a menor ideia de como resolver este problema."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We didn't have the slightest idea that the party was a surprise.", "tl": "Nós não tínhamos a menor ideia de que a festa era uma surpresa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "They don't have the slightest idea of what is going to happen tomorrow at the meeting.", "tl": "Eles não têm a menor ideia do que vai acontecer amanhã na reunião."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She didn't have the slightest idea how to answer that difficult question.", "tl": "Ela não teve a menor ideia de como responder àquela pergunta difícil."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You don't have the slightest idea how difficult it is to live alone in a new city.", "tl": "Tu não tens a menor ideia de como é difícil morar sozinho numa cidade nova."}]}, {"idiom_id": 153, "expression_id": 131, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "abriu mão de", "english_gloss": "to give up / waive / forgo", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "She gave up a big promotion to spend more time with her children.", "tl": "Ela abriu mão de uma grande promoção para passar mais tempo com os filhos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I don't mind giving up my weekend to help you with the move.", "tl": "Eu não me importo de abrir mão do meu fim de semana para ajudar você com a mudança."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They gave up their inheritance rights to avoid fights in the family.", "tl": "Eles abriram mão do direito de herança para evitar brigas na família."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To lose weight, he had to give up sweets and sodas.", "tl": "Para emagrecer, ele teve que abrir mão de doces e refrigerantes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I never give up my principles, no matter the situation.", "tl": "Eu nunca abro mão dos meus princípios, não importa a situação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We had to give up our vacation trip because the car broke down.", "tl": "Nós tivemos que abrir mão da viagem de férias porque o carro quebrou."}]}, {"idiom_id": 152, "expression_id": 130, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "chuva de dinheiro", "english_gloss": "shower of money / windfall", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After receiving the unexpected inheritance, she felt like she was under a real shower of money.", "tl": "Depois de receber a herança inesperada, ela sentiu que estava sob uma verdadeira chuva de dinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new tech startup attracted investors and is now receiving a windfall of money.", "tl": "A nova startup de tecnologia atraiu investidores e agora está recebendo uma chuva de dinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Many thought the new government project would be a windfall of money for the region.", "tl": "Muitos pensavam que o novo projeto do governo seria uma chuva de dinheiro para a região."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't spend it all now; this windfall won't last forever.", "tl": "Não gaste tudo agora; essa chuva de dinheiro não vai durar para sempre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "With the new sponsorship contract, the young athlete saw a shower of money enter his account.", "tl": "Com o novo contrato de patrocínio, o jovem atleta viu uma chuva de dinheiro entrar na sua conta."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I wish a shower of money would fall from the sky to pay off all my debts!", "tl": "Quem dera que caísse uma chuva de dinheiro do céu para pagar todas as minhas dívidas!"}]}, {"idiom_id": 151, "expression_id": 129, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "é escrachado", "english_gloss": "it is blatant / shameless", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That lie he told was so blatant that nobody believed it.", "tl": "Aquela mentira que ele contou foi tão escrachada que ninguém acreditou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The design of this new phone is a blatant copy of last year's model.", "tl": "O design desse novo celular é uma cópia escrachada do modelo do ano passado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I like his humor; it's very crude and unfiltered.", "tl": "Eu gosto do humor dele; é bem escrachado e sem filtros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The boss's favoritism toward his son is blatant; everyone in the office notices.", "tl": "O favoritismo do chefe com o filho é escrachado, todo mundo no escritório percebe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She gave a shameless excuse for not going to yesterday's meeting.", "tl": "Ela deu uma desculpa escrachada para não ir à reunião de ontem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The ad in the middle of the video was so blatant that I closed the page.", "tl": "A propaganda no meio do vídeo foi tão escrachada que eu fechei a página."}]}, {"idiom_id": 150, "expression_id": 128, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "moeda de troca", "english_gloss": "bargaining chip", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "They used the accumulated overtime as a bargaining chip to get more days off.", "tl": "Eles usaram as horas extras acumuladas como moeda de troca para conseguir mais dias de folga."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The government tried to use the new bill as a bargaining chip in negotiations with the opposition.", "tl": "O governo tentou usar o novo projeto de lei como moeda de troca nas negociações com a oposição."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't want our friendship to be used as a bargaining chip for you to get what you want.", "tl": "Não quero que a nossa amizade seja usada como moeda de troca para você conseguir o que quer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you have another job offer, you can use that as an excellent bargaining chip with your boss.", "tl": "Se você tem outra proposta de emprego, pode usar isso como uma excelente moeda de troca com o seu chefe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Parents should not use time with their children as a bargaining chip during a divorce.", "tl": "Os pais não devem usar o tempo com os filhos como moeda de troca durante o divórcio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The neighboring country used the gas supply as a bargaining chip to avoid economic sanctions.", "tl": "O país vizinho usou o fornecimento de gás como moeda de troca para evitar as sanções econômicas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 149, "expression_id": 127, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "na prática", "english_gloss": "in practice / in reality", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The plan seemed perfect on paper, but in practice many problems arose.", "tl": "O plano parecia perfeito no papel, mas na prática surgiram muitos problemas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I know all the grammar theory, but in practice I still make some mistakes when speaking.", "tl": "Eu sei toda a teoria da gramática, mas na prática ainda cometo alguns erros ao falar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The law says everyone has the same rights, but in reality things are different.", "tl": "A lei diz que todos têm os mesmos direitos, mas na prática as coisas são diferentes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This app promises to save time, but in practice it is very difficult to use.", "tl": "Este aplicativo promete economizar tempo, mas na prática ele é muito difícil de usar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The course teaches a lot of theory, but we need to see how this works in practice.", "tl": "O curso ensina muita teoria, mas precisamos ver como isso funciona na prática."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We try to save money, but in practice it is difficult to avoid extra expenses.", "tl": "Nós tentamos economizar dinheiro, mas na prática é difícil evitar gastos extras."}]}, {"idiom_id": 148, "expression_id": 126, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "ficava na fila", "english_gloss": "to wait in line / stand in line", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When I was a child, I always used to stand in the cinema line with my father.", "tl": "Quando eu era criança, eu sempre ficava na fila do cinema com o meu pai."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She used to wait in the supermarket line while her husband chose the fruits.", "tl": "Ela ficava na fila do supermercado enquanto o marido escolhia as frutas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In the past, we used to stand in line for hours to buy concert tickets.", "tl": "Antigamente, a gente ficava na fila por horas para comprar ingressos de shows."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He used to stand in line reading a book to make the time go by faster.", "tl": "Ele ficava na fila lendo um livro para o tempo passar mais rápido."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In your old school, who used to stand in the cafeteria line during recess?", "tl": "Na sua antiga escola, quem ficava na fila da cantina na hora do recreio?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Did you always use to wait in line at the bank before the app existed?", "tl": "Você sempre ficava na fila do banco antes de o aplicativo existir?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 147, "expression_id": 125, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "não tinha lastro", "english_gloss": "had no backing / lacked foundation", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "That new digital currency rose quickly, but the truth is it had no backing at all.", "tl": "Aquela nova moeda digital subiu rápido, mas a verdade é que não tinha lastro nenhum."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The scientist's theory was interesting, but it lacked foundation in real data.", "tl": "A teoria do cientista era interessante, mas não tinha lastro em dados reais."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The accusation against the director was serious, but they soon realized it had no foundation.", "tl": "A acusação contra o diretor era grave, mas logo perceberam que não tinha lastro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The business plan looked good on paper, but it had no financial backing to move forward.", "tl": "O plano de negócios parecia bom no papel, mas não tinha lastro financeiro para avançar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "He spoke with great authority, but his opinion had no foundation in reality.", "tl": "Ele falava com muita autoridade, mas a sua opinião não tinha lastro na realidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In the past, that national currency had no backing and quickly lost its value.", "tl": "No passado, aquela moeda nacional não tinha lastro e perdeu o valor rapidamente."}]}, {"idiom_id": 146, "expression_id": 124, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "toma lá dá cá", "english_gloss": "quid pro quo / give-and-take", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In politics, it often all comes down to a game of give-and-take.", "tl": "Na política, muitas vezes tudo se resume a um jogo de toma lá dá cá."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "A good friendship shouldn't be based on give-and-take; we should help without expecting anything in return.", "tl": "Uma boa amizade não deve ser baseada no toma lá dá cá; devemos ajudar sem esperar nada em troca."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "To close the deal, we had to accept the policy of quid pro quo with the suppliers.", "tl": "Para fechar o negócio, tivemos de aceitar a política do toma lá dá cá com os fornecedores."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I'll make dinner today and you clean the kitchen tomorrow; it works on a give-and-take basis.", "tl": "Eu faço o jantar hoje e tu limpas a cozinha amanhã; funciona na base do toma lá dá cá."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The new director wants to end the quid pro quo that existed in the company to get promotions.", "tl": "O novo diretor quer acabar com o toma lá dá cá que existia na empresa para conseguir promoções."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In marriage, there has to be a bit of give-and-take for things to work well.", "tl": "No casamento, tem de haver um pouco de toma lá dá cá para que as coisas funcionem bem."}]}, {"idiom_id": 145, "expression_id": 123, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "só para se ter uma ideia", "english_gloss": "just to give you an idea", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The rent here is very expensive; just to give you an idea, a small room costs eight hundred euros.", "tl": "O aluguel aqui é muito caro; só para se ter uma ideia, um quarto pequeno custa oitocentos euros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It was very cold yesterday. Just to give you an idea, the lake water froze.", "tl": "Estava muito frio ontem. Só para se ter uma ideia, a água do lago congelou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She works a lot. Just to give you an idea, she rarely takes a vacation in the summer.", "tl": "Ela trabalha muito. Só para se ter uma ideia, ela raramente tira férias no verão."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The trip is very long; just to give you an idea, we need to take three different flights.", "tl": "A viagem é muito longa; só para se ter uma ideia, precisamos pegar três voos diferentes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The restaurant is super popular. Just to give you an idea, you need to book a month in advance.", "tl": "O restaurante é super popular. Só para se ter uma ideia, é preciso reservar com um mês de antecedência."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The book is huge. Just to give you an idea, it has more than a thousand pages.", "tl": "O livro é enorme. Só para se ter uma ideia, ele tem mais de mil páginas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 144, "expression_id": 122, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "barganha política", "english_gloss": "political bargaining / horse-trading", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The new president promised to end political bargaining when choosing ministers.", "tl": "O novo presidente prometeu acabar com a barganha política na hora de escolher os ministros."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Many citizens are tired of the political bargaining that happens behind the scenes in congress.", "tl": "Muitos cidadãos estão cansados da barganha política que acontece nos bastidores do congresso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The approval of the new health law required a lot of political bargaining between the parties.", "tl": "A aprovação da nova lei de saúde exigiu muita barganha política entre os partidos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He got the director position not by merit, but because of political bargaining.", "tl": "Ele conseguiu o cargo de diretor não por mérito, mas por causa de uma barganha política."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "In any democracy, political bargaining is a normal tool to reach an agreement.", "tl": "Em qualquer democracia, a barganha política é uma ferramenta normal para se chegar a um acordo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Budget negotiations always involve complex political bargaining.", "tl": "As negociações do orçamento sempre envolvem barganhas políticas complexas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 143, "expression_id": 121, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "numa tacada só", "english_gloss": "in one fell swoop / in a single stroke", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I decided to clean out my inbox and replied to all the emails in one fell swoop.", "tl": "Decidi limpar a caixa de entrada e respondi a todos os e-mails numa tacada só."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She bought all the Christmas presents in one fell swoop to avoid the December rush.", "tl": "Ela comprou todos os presentes de Natal numa tacada só para evitar a confusão de dezembro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Since the bank and the supermarket are close by, I sorted everything out in a single stroke.", "tl": "Como o banco e o supermercado são perto, resolvi tudo numa tacada só."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He studied the material for the entire semester in one fell swoop the night before the exam.", "tl": "Ele estudou a matéria do semestre inteiro numa tacada só na noite anterior ao exame."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Instead of cleaning the house little by little, I prefer to do it all in one fell swoop on Saturday.", "tl": "Em vez de arrumar a casa aos poucos, prefiro fazer tudo numa tacada só no sábado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The company laid off half of the employees in one fell swoop to cut costs.", "tl": "A empresa demitiu metade dos funcionários numa tacada só para cortar custos."}]}, {"idiom_id": 142, "expression_id": 120, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "por um fio de cabelo", "english_gloss": "by a hair / very close to", "youtube_id": "r9IE_1fJXfE", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The car almost hit the post; we escaped by a hair.", "tl": "O carro quase bateu no poste; escapamos por um fio de cabelo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I passed the math exam by a hair.", "tl": "Eu passei no exame de matemática por um fio de cabelo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our team didn't win the championship by a hair.", "tl": "O nosso time não ganhou o campeonato por um fio de cabelo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She managed to catch the train by a hair, the doors were already closing.", "tl": "Ela conseguiu pegar o trem por um fio de cabelo, as portas já estavam fechando."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The project was delivered on time by a hair.", "tl": "O projeto foi entregue no prazo por um fio de cabelo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The glass vase almost fell off the table, but I caught it by a hair.", "tl": "O vaso de vidro quase caiu da mesa, mas eu o segurei por um fio de cabelo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 141, "expression_id": 149, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "acabado de sair", "english_gloss": "had just left / got out", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The warm bread, fresh out of the oven, smelled incredibly good.", "tl": "O pão quente, acabado de sair do forno, cheirava incrivelmente bem."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "As a young man just out of university, he had many doubts about the future.", "tl": "Como um jovem acabado de sair da universidade, ele tinha muitas dúvidas sobre o futuro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They were excited, having just left the cinema after watching the new movie.", "tl": "Eles estavam animados, acabados de sair do cinema depois de ver o novo filme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Sorry about the wet hair, I've just got out of the shower.", "tl": "Desculpa o cabelo molhado, estou acabado de sair do banho."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We have breaking news, fresh out of the newsroom.", "tl": "Temos uma notícia de última hora, acabada de sair da redação."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The passenger, having just got off the plane, was desperately looking for his bags.", "tl": "O passageiro, acabado de sair do avião, procurava desesperadamente pelas suas malas."}]}, {"idiom_id": 140, "expression_id": 148, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "dar a ideia", "english_gloss": "to give the idea / suggest", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Who suggested having a picnic in the park?", "tl": "Quem é que deu a ideia de fazermos um piquenique no parque?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The way she spoke gave the impression that she didn't want to go to the party.", "tl": "A forma como ela falou deu a ideia de que não queria ir à festa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I suggested changing the meeting date to next week.", "tl": "Eu dei a ideia de mudar a data da reunião para a próxima semana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Those dark colors make the room seem smaller than it actually is.", "tl": "Essas cores escuras dão a ideia de que o quarto é menor do que realmente é."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It was my brother who suggested buying this used car.", "tl": "Foi o meu irmão que deu a ideia de comprarmos este carro usado."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The silence in the house gave the impression that no one was there.", "tl": "O silêncio na casa dava a ideia de que não estava lá ninguém."}]}, {"idiom_id": 139, "expression_id": 147, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "tanto que", "english_gloss": "so much so that", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I was very tired yesterday, so much so that I fell asleep on the couch before dinner.", "tl": "Eu estava muito cansado ontem, tanto que dormi no sofá antes do jantar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She liked the cake, so much so that she ate three slices.", "tl": "Ela gostou do bolo, tanto que comeu três fatias."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "It rained a lot at night, so much so that some streets were flooded.", "tl": "Choveu muito à noite, tanto que algumas ruas ficaram inundadas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He studied hard for the exam, so much so that he got the maximum grade.", "tl": "Ele estudou bastante para o exame, tanto que tirou a nota máxima."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We get along very well, so much so that we travel together every year.", "tl": "Nós nos damos muito bem, tanto que viajamos juntos todos os anos."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The city has grown in recent years, so much so that it now has a new shopping mall.", "tl": "A cidade cresceu nos últimos anos, tanto que agora tem um novo shopping."}]}, {"idiom_id": 138, "expression_id": 146, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "de bom humor", "english_gloss": "in a good mood", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My father always wakes up in a good mood and singing.", "tl": "O meu pai acorda sempre de bom humor e a cantar."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Take the opportunity to talk to the boss now, because he seems to be in a good mood.", "tl": "Aproveita para falar com o chefe agora, porque ele parece estar de bom humor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When it's sunny, I immediately get in a good mood.", "tl": "Quando está sol, eu fico logo de bom humor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Despite the horrible traffic, she arrived at the party in a good mood.", "tl": "Apesar do trânsito horrível, ela chegou à festa de bom humor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't know what happened, but today I'm not in a good mood for jokes.", "tl": "Não sei o que aconteceu, mas hoje não estou de bom humor para brincadeiras."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Doing physical exercise helps me stay in a good mood during the day.", "tl": "Praticar exercício físico ajuda-me a manter-me de bom humor durante o dia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 137, "expression_id": 145, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "o fato é que", "english_gloss": "the fact is that", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The fact is that we need more time to finish this project.", "tl": "O fato é que nós precisamos de mais tempo para terminar este projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I like the city a lot, but the fact is that the cost of living here is very high.", "tl": "Eu gosto muito da cidade, mas o fato é que o custo de vida aqui é muito alto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The fact is that if you don't sleep well, you won't be able to concentrate tomorrow.", "tl": "O fato é que, se você não dormir bem, não vai conseguir se concentrar amanhã."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "He says he is going to save money, but the fact is that he keeps spending a lot of money.", "tl": "Ele diz que vai economizar, mas o fato é que ele continua gastando muito dinheiro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The fact is that learning a new language requires a lot of patience and daily practice.", "tl": "O fato é que aprender uma nova língua exige muita paciência e prática diária."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We wanted to travel over the weekend, but the fact is that it is going to rain every day.", "tl": "Queríamos viajar no fim de semana, mas o fato é que vai chover todos os dias."}]}, {"idiom_id": 136, "expression_id": 144, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "por conta própria", "english_gloss": "on one's own / singlehandedly", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I decided to leave the company and now I work on my own.", "tl": "Decidi sair da empresa e agora trabalho por conta própria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She learned to play the piano on her own, without any teacher's help.", "tl": "Ela aprendeu a tocar piano por conta própria, sem ajuda de nenhum professor."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "You are already eighteen years old, you need to make your decisions on your own.", "tl": "Você já tem dezoito anos, precisa tomar suas decisões por conta própria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Instead of hiring an agency, we organized the whole trip on our own.", "tl": "Em vez de contratar uma agência, nós organizamos toda a viagem por conta própria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The computer was having problems, but I managed to fix it on my own.", "tl": "O computador estava com problemas, mas eu consegui consertá-lo por conta própria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The children are already very independent and do their homework on their own.", "tl": "As crianças já são bem independentes e fazem as tarefas por conta própria."}]}, {"idiom_id": 135, "expression_id": 143, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "logo depois", "english_gloss": "right after / shortly after", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I usually have a coffee right after lunch.", "tl": "Eu costumo tomar um café logo depois do almoço."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "She sent the report right after the meeting ended.", "tl": "Ela enviou o relatório logo depois que a reunião terminou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We arrived at the hotel and, shortly after, went for a walk around the city.", "tl": "Nós chegamos ao hotel e, logo depois, fomos dar uma volta pela cidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It is important to drink water right after exercising.", "tl": "É importante beber água logo depois de fazer exercício físico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The concert ended and, shortly after, it started to rain very hard.", "tl": "O concerto acabou e, logo depois, começou a chover muito forte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "He got a good job right after graduating from university.", "tl": "Ele conseguiu um bom emprego logo depois de se formar na universidade."}]}, {"idiom_id": 134, "expression_id": 142, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "uma espécie de", "english_gloss": "a kind of / a sort of", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "He bought a kind of sofa that also serves as a bed.", "tl": "Ele comprou uma espécie de sofá que também serve de cama."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I felt a sort of relief when the exam ended.", "tl": "Senti uma espécie de alívio quando o exame terminou."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That wasn't a common dog, it looked like a kind of wolf.", "tl": "Aquilo não era um cão comum, parecia uma espécie de lobo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We made a kind of agreement to divide the household chores.", "tl": "Nós fizemos uma espécie de acordo para dividir as tarefas domésticas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She uses a kind of natural oil to moisturize her hair.", "tl": "Ela usa uma espécie de óleo natural para hidratar o cabelo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "What we found in the closet was a kind of old diary.", "tl": "O que encontramos no armário era uma espécie de diário antigo."}]}, {"idiom_id": 133, "expression_id": 141, "lang": "pt", "idiom_text": "me levou a", "english_gloss": "led me to / moved me to", "youtube_id": "OFjCDj172WY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My interest in languages led me to live abroad.", "tl": "O meu interesse por línguas me levou a morar no exterior."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The doctor's recommendation led me to change my eating habits.", "tl": "A recomendação do médico me levou a mudar meus hábitos alimentares."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Curiosity moved me to research more about the city's history.", "tl": "A curiosidade me levou a pesquisar mais sobre a história da cidade."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The lack of planning led me to make some mistakes in the project.", "tl": "A falta de planejamento me levou a cometer alguns erros no projeto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "A happy coincidence led me to meet my best friend.", "tl": "Uma feliz coincidência me levou a conhecer o meu melhor amigo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The high price of fuel led me to sell the car.", "tl": "O preço alto do combustível me levou a vender o carro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 132, "expression_id": 119, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "vanno di moda", "english_gloss": "are fashionable / in vogue", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This year, wide-leg pants are fashionable among young people.", "tl": "Quest'anno i pantaloni larghi vanno di moda tra i giovani."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Today it is very fashionable to have breakfast outdoors on weekends.", "tl": "Oggi va molto di moda fare colazione all'aperto nei fine settimana."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In the nineties, these leather jackets were very fashionable.", "tl": "Negli anni novanta, queste giacche di pelle andavano molto di moda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Do you think vinyl records will still be in vogue in the future?", "tl": "Pensi che i dischi in vinile andranno ancora di moda in futuro?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I don't want to buy that phone just because it's fashionable right now.", "tl": "Non voglio comprare quel telefono solo perché va di moda adesso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Vegetarian restaurants are very fashionable in this city.", "tl": "I ristoranti vegetariani vanno molto di moda in questa città."}]}, {"idiom_id": 131, "expression_id": 118, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "prima o poi", "english_gloss": "sooner or later", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Sooner or later you will find your dream job, you just have to be patient.", "tl": "Prima o poi troverai il lavoro dei tuoi sogni, devi solo avere pazienza."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "You cannot hide the truth forever, sooner or later it will come out.", "tl": "Non puoi nascondere la verità per sempre, prima o poi verrà fuori."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I would really like to visit Japan sooner or later.", "tl": "Mi piacerebbe molto visitare il Giappone prima o poi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I knew that sooner or later you would buy a new phone.", "tl": "Sapevo che prima o poi avresti comprato un nuovo telefono."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Stop worrying, sooner or later it will stop raining.", "tl": "Smetti di preoccuparti, prima o poi smetterà di piovere."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We need to arrange to have a coffee together sooner or later.", "tl": "Dobbiamo organizzarci per prendere un caffè insieme prima o poi."}]}, {"idiom_id": 130, "expression_id": 117, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "non può far nulla", "english_gloss": "cannot do anything / is powerless", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The doctor said that by now he cannot do anything to cure this illness.", "tl": "Il medico ha detto che ormai non può far nulla per curare questa malattia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I would really like to help you, but in this situation I can't do anything.", "tl": "Vorrei tanto aiutarti, ma in questa situazione non posso far nulla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Without the boss's authorization, the secretary can't do anything.", "tl": "Senza l'autorizzazione del capo, la segretaria non può far nulla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Don't get angry, it's the bank's decision and you can't do anything to change it.", "tl": "Non ti arrabbiare, è una decisione della banca e tu non puoi far nulla per cambiarla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If there is no internet connection, this computer cannot do anything.", "tl": "Se manca la connessione internet, questo computer non può far nulla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The flight is delayed due to bad weather and unfortunately we can't do anything.", "tl": "Il volo è in ritardo a causa del maltempo e noi purtroppo non possiamo far nulla."}]}, {"idiom_id": 129, "expression_id": 116, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "con tanta fatica", "english_gloss": "with great effort / painstakingly", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I got this promotion with great effort, and now I want to enjoy it.", "tl": "Ho ottenuto questa promozione con tanta fatica, e ora voglio godermela."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We reached the top of the mountain with great effort, but the view was incredible.", "tl": "Siamo arrivati in cima alla montagna con tanta fatica, ma la vista era incredibile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Marco passed the math exam with great effort.", "tl": "Marco ha superato l'esame di matematica con tanta fatica."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "After the argument, they rebuilt their relationship with great effort.", "tl": "Dopo il litigio, hanno ricostruito il loro rapporto con tanta fatica."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My parents bought this house with great effort.", "tl": "I miei genitori hanno comprato questa casa con tanta fatica."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She finished writing her first novel with great effort.", "tl": "Ha finito di scrivere il suo primo romanzo con tanta fatica."}]}, {"idiom_id": 128, "expression_id": 115, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "visto sfilare", "english_gloss": "seen parading / seen passing by", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "During fashion week, I saw models from all over the world parading.", "tl": "Durante la settimana della moda, ho visto sfilare modelle da tutto il mondo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "From the office window, we saw the town's marching band pass by.", "tl": "Dalla finestra dell'ufficio abbiamo visto sfilare la banda musicale del paese."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "On the festival's red carpet, we saw many famous actors parade by.", "tl": "Sul tappeto rosso del festival abbiamo visto sfilare molti attori famosi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Did you see the protesters marching through the downtown streets this morning?", "tl": "Hai visto sfilare i manifestanti per le vie del centro stamattina?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The children were happy because they saw the Carnival floats pass by.", "tl": "I bambini erano felici perché hanno visto sfilare i carri di Carnevale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We stood on the balcony and saw the cyclists of the race pass by.", "tl": "Ci siamo messi sul balcone e abbiamo visto sfilare i ciclisti della corsa."}]}, {"idiom_id": 127, "expression_id": 114, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "A proposito di questo", "english_gloss": "Speaking of this / on this note", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Speaking of this, have you finished preparing the report for the boss?", "tl": "A proposito di questo, hai finito di preparare il rapporto per il capo?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "On this note, we still need to book the train tickets.", "tl": "A proposito di questo, dobbiamo ancora prenotare i biglietti del treno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Speaking of this, do you know if Marco is coming to the party tonight?", "tl": "A proposito di questo, sai se Marco verrà alla festa stasera?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "On this note, I think we should speak directly with the director.", "tl": "A proposito di questo, penso che dovremmo parlare direttamente con il direttore."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Speaking of this, how much did we spend on yesterday's dinner?", "tl": "A proposito di questo, quanto abbiamo speso per la cena di ieri?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Speaking of this, the teacher said that the exam has been postponed.", "tl": "A proposito di questo, l'insegnante ha detto che l'esame è stato rimandato."}]}, {"idiom_id": 126, "expression_id": 113, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "quello a cui stiamo guardando", "english_gloss": "what we are looking at", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "What we are looking at is not the present, but the future of our company.", "tl": "Quello a cui stiamo guardando non è il presente, ma il futuro della nostra azienda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Perhaps what we are looking at is only a part of a much bigger problem.", "tl": "Forse quello a cui stiamo guardando è solo una parte di un problema molto più grande."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We need to understand if what we are looking at is a truly achievable goal.", "tl": "Dobbiamo capire se quello a cui stiamo guardando è un obiettivo davvero realizzabile."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This graph clearly shows what we have been looking at for months now.", "tl": "Questo grafico mostra chiaramente quello a cui stiamo guardando ormai da mesi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This is not what we are looking at to resolve the current situation.", "tl": "Non è questo quello a cui stiamo guardando per risolvere la situazione attuale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If what we are looking at is real change, then we must act immediately.", "tl": "Se quello a cui stiamo guardando è un cambiamento reale, allora dobbiamo agire subito."}]}, {"idiom_id": 125, "expression_id": 112, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "a partire da", "english_gloss": "starting from / based on", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Starting from next Monday, the office will also be open in the afternoon.", "tl": "A partire da lunedì prossimo, l'ufficio sarà aperto anche il pomeriggio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Tickets for the concert are available starting from twenty euros.", "tl": "I biglietti per il concerto sono disponibili a partire da venti euro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This movie is recommended starting from twelve years of age.", "tl": "Questo film è consigliato a partire dai dodici anni di età."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We developed the new project starting from your ideas.", "tl": "Abbiamo sviluppato il nuovo progetto a partire dalle vostre idee."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Starting tomorrow, many rules within the company will change.", "tl": "A partire da domani, cambieranno molte regole all'interno dell'azienda."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You can reconstruct your family history starting from these old documents.", "tl": "Puoi ricostruire la storia della tua famiglia a partire da questi vecchi documenti."}]}, {"idiom_id": 124, "expression_id": 111, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "rispolverate", "english_gloss": "dusted off / revived", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "For the trip to France, I dusted off my old school French.", "tl": "Per il viaggio in Francia, ho rispolverato il mio vecchio francese scolastico."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This year at Christmas, some old family traditions were dusted off.", "tl": "Quest'anno a Natale sono state rispolverate alcune vecchie tradizioni di famiglia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "If you want to pass the driving test, brush up on the highway code.", "tl": "Se volete passare l'esame di guida, rispolverate bene il codice della strada."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "During the lockdown, many people revived their passion for cooking.", "tl": "Durante il lockdown, molte persone hanno rispolverato la passione per la cucina."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The director decided to dust off an old project that he had abandoned years ago.", "tl": "Il regista ha deciso di rispolverare un vecchio progetto che aveva abbandonato anni fa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Grandma's old recipes were dusted off for tonight's dinner.", "tl": "Le vecchie ricette della nonna sono state rispolverate per la cena di stasera."}]}, {"idiom_id": 123, "expression_id": 110, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "al di là del", "english_gloss": "beyond / regardless of", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Beyond the price, this computer is really great for my work.", "tl": "Al di là del prezzo, questo computer è davvero ottimo per il mio lavoro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Beyond the hill, there is a small medieval village that is worth visiting.", "tl": "Al di là della collina c'è un piccolo paese medievale che merita di essere visitato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Beyond our expectations, the project was a great success.", "tl": "Al di là delle nostre aspettative, il progetto è stato un grande successo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Regardless of the fact that it's late, we should still call him to let him know.", "tl": "Al di là del fatto che sia tardi, dovremmo comunque chiamarlo per avvisarlo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Beyond appearances, Marco is a very sensitive and generous person.", "tl": "Al di là delle apparenze, Marco è una persona molto sensibile e generosa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Beyond the initial mistakes, the presentation went very well.", "tl": "Al di là degli errori iniziali, la presentazione è andata molto bene."}]}, {"idiom_id": 122, "expression_id": 109, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "nei luoghi che contano", "english_gloss": "in the places that matter", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "If you want to advance your career, you have to be seen in the places that matter.", "tl": "Se vuoi fare carriera, devi farti vedere nei luoghi che contano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Many important decisions are made behind closed doors, in the places that matter.", "tl": "Molte decisioni importanti vengono prese a porte chiuse, nei luoghi che contano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Marco spends all his free time in the places that matter in the city to meet influential people.", "tl": "Marco passa tutto il suo tempo libero nei luoghi che contano della città per conoscere persone influenti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For a young artist, it is essential to exhibit their work in the places that matter.", "tl": "Per un giovane artista è fondamentale esporre le proprie opere nei luoghi che contano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "As a journalist, she always has contacts in the places that matter.", "tl": "Come giornalista, lei ha sempre dei contatti nei luoghi che contano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I'm not interested in being present in the places that matter, I prefer the peace of my own home.", "tl": "Non mi interessa essere presente nei luoghi che contano, preferisco la tranquillità di casa mia."}]}, {"idiom_id": 121, "expression_id": 108, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "sotto la superficie", "english_gloss": "under the surface", "youtube_id": "LFEaVZPD1TU", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The lake water seems calm, but under the surface there are strong currents.", "tl": "L'acqua del lago sembra calma, ma sotto la superficie ci sono forti correnti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Marco always seems calm, but under the surface he hides a lot of anxiety.", "tl": "Marco sembra sempre tranquillo, ma sotto la superficie nasconde molta ansia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Under the surface of this apparent friendship, there was actually a lot of rivalry.", "tl": "Sotto la superficie di questa apparente amicizia c'era in realtà molta rivalità."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "To fully understand the situation, we must look under the surface of things.", "tl": "Per capire a fondo la situazione, dobbiamo guardare sotto la superficie delle cose."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Geologists are studying what exactly lies under the surface of the volcano.", "tl": "I geologi stanno studiando cosa si trova esattamente sotto la superficie del vulcano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Even though everything seems perfect, under the surface there are serious family problems.", "tl": "Anche se tutto sembra perfetto, sotto la superficie ci sono seri problemi familiari."}]}, {"idiom_id": 120, "expression_id": 107, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "non provò nemmeno a addolcire la notizia", "english_gloss": "he didn't even try to sugarcoat the news", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The doctor entered the room and didn't even try to sugarcoat the news: it was very serious.", "tl": "Il medico entrò nella stanza e non provò nemmeno a addolcire la notizia: era molto grave."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The boss called me into his office and didn't even try to sugarcoat the news of my dismissal.", "tl": "Il capo mi ha chiamato nel suo ufficio e non ha nemmeno provato a addolcire la notizia del mio licenziamento."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I knew he would be disappointed, so I didn't even try to sugarcoat the news.", "tl": "Sapevo che ci sarebbe rimasto male, quindi non ho nemmeno provato a addolcire la notizia."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The journalists on television didn't even try to sugarcoat the news of the train disaster.", "tl": "I giornalisti alla televisione non hanno nemmeno provato a addolcire la notizia del disastro ferroviario."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My father was a very direct man and didn't even try to sugarcoat the news when things went wrong.", "tl": "Mio padre era un uomo molto diretto e non provava nemmeno a addolcire la notizia quando le cose andavano male."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "It's useless to beat around the bush, don't even try to sugarcoat the news with them.", "tl": "È inutile girarci intorno, non provare nemmeno a addolcire la notizia con loro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 119, "expression_id": 106, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "non smise mai di crederci", "english_gloss": "never stopped believing in it", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Despite the many difficulties, the scientist never stopped believing in it and finally found the cure.", "tl": "Nonostante le molte difficoltà, lo scienziato non smise mai di crederci e alla fine trovò la cura."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Even when everyone told me to give up, I never stopped believing in it.", "tl": "Anche quando tutti mi dicevano di mollare, io non ho mai smesso di crederci."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The players were at a disadvantage, but they never stopped believing in it until the last minute.", "tl": "I giocatori erano in svantaggio, ma non smisero mai di crederci fino all'ultimo minuto."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Her project seemed like an impossible dream, but she never stopped believing in it.", "tl": "Il suo progetto sembrava un sogno impossibile, ma lei non ha mai smesso di crederci."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Even though no publisher wanted to publish his book, the writer never stopped believing in it.", "tl": "Anche se nessun editore voleva pubblicare il suo libro, lo scrittore non smise mai di crederci."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you really want to reach your goal, remember to never stop believing in it.", "tl": "Se vuoi davvero raggiungere il tuo obiettivo, ricordati di non smettere mai di crederci."}]}, {"idiom_id": 118, "expression_id": 105, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "continuavano solo a portarmi in giro", "english_gloss": "they just kept stringing me along", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I realized they didn't really want to hire me, they just kept stringing me along.", "tl": "Ho capito che non volevano davvero assumermi, continuavano solo a portarmi in giro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "They had no intention of selling me the car, they just kept stringing me along.", "tl": "Non avevano nessuna intenzione di vendermi la macchina, continuavano solo a portarmi in giro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I thought she really liked me, but she just kept stringing me along.", "tl": "Pensavo che le piacessi sul serio, ma lei continuava solo a portarmi in giro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Those clients didn't want to sign the contract, they just kept stringing me along.", "tl": "Quei clienti non volevano firmare il contratto, continuavano solo a portarmi in giro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Those real estate agents didn't have a real house to show us, they just kept stringing us along.", "tl": "Quegli agenti immobiliari non avevano una vera casa da mostrarci, continuavano solo a portarci in giro."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "In the end I resigned because the bosses just kept stringing me along.", "tl": "Alla fine ho dato le dimissioni perché i capi continuavano solo a portarmi in giro."}]}, {"idiom_id": 117, "expression_id": 104, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "quando mi presero in prova", "english_gloss": "when they took me on trial", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I still remember how happy I was when they took me on trial at that bakery.", "tl": "Ricordo ancora la felicità di quando mi presero in prova in quella pasticceria."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "When they took me on trial, I had to prove my worth every single day.", "tl": "Quando mi presero in prova, dovevo dimostrare il mio valore ogni singolo giorno."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "At the beginning I didn't know how to do anything, but when they took me on trial I did my very best.", "tl": "All'inizio non sapevo fare nulla, ma quando mi presero in prova mi impegnai al massimo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When they took me on trial as a waiter, the restaurant was always full of customers.", "tl": "Quando mi presero in prova come cameriere, il ristorante era sempre pieno di clienti."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I was very happy when they took me on trial, even though the salary was low.", "tl": "Ero felicissimo quando mi hanno preso in prova, anche se lo stipendio era basso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The manager was very strict when he took me on trial for that job at the bank.", "tl": "Il direttore era molto severo quando mi prese in prova per quel posto in banca."}]}, {"idiom_id": 116, "expression_id": 103, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "non avremmo osato nemmeno battere ciglio", "english_gloss": "we wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In front of the boss being so angry, we wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye.", "tl": "Davanti al direttore così arrabbiato, noi non avremmo osato nemmeno battere ciglio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "There was such a tense silence in the room that I wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye.", "tl": "C'era un silenzio così teso nella stanza che io non avrei osato nemmeno battere ciglio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "With such a strict father, the kids wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye without his permission.", "tl": "Con un padre così severo, i ragazzi non avrebbero osato nemmeno battere ciglio senza il suo permesso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If you had found yourselves in front of that bear, you wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye.", "tl": "Se vi foste trovati davanti a quell'orso, non avreste osato nemmeno battere ciglio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "During the oral exam with that professor, she wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye.", "tl": "Durante l'esame orale con quel professore, lei non avrebbe osato nemmeno battere ciglio."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "While the police were asking us those questions, we wouldn't have even dared to bat an eye.", "tl": "Mentre la polizia ci faceva quelle domande, noi non avremmo osato nemmeno battere ciglio."}]}, {"idiom_id": 115, "expression_id": 102, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "Facevamo una specie di colpo in banca", "english_gloss": "We pulled off a sort of bank heist", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As kids, when we played in the garden, we always pulled off a sort of bank heist.", "tl": "Da bambini, quando giocavamo in giardino, facevamo sempre una specie di colpo in banca."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Last night in the video game we pulled off a sort of bank heist with our friends.", "tl": "Ieri sera nel videogioco abbiamo fatto una specie di colpo in banca con i nostri amici."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "To organize this surprise party, it feels like we have to pull off a sort of bank heist!", "tl": "Per organizzare questa festa a sorpresa, sembra che dobbiamo fare una specie di colpo in banca!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In the new action movie, the main characters pulled off a sort of bank heist but were caught.", "tl": "Nel nuovo film d'azione, i protagonisti hanno fatto una specie di colpo in banca ma sono stati catturati."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why were you running so fast yesterday? It looked like you were pulling off a sort of bank heist.", "tl": "Perché correvi così veloce ieri? Sembrava che facessi una specie di colpo in banca."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If we really needed all that money, would we pull off a sort of bank heist?", "tl": "Se avessimo davvero bisogno di tutti quei soldi, faremmo una specie di colpo in banca?"}]}, {"idiom_id": 114, "expression_id": 101, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentato", "english_gloss": "I always pretended to have fallen asleep", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "As a child, when I heard my parents arguing in the living room, I always pretended to have fallen asleep.", "tl": "Da piccolo, quando sentivo i miei genitori litigare in salotto, facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentato."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "During long car trips with my family, I always pretended to have fallen asleep so I wouldn't have to talk.", "tl": "Durante i lunghi viaggi in macchina con la mia famiglia, facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentata per non dover parla"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When my roommate came back late at night, I always pretended to have fallen asleep to avoid arguments.", "tl": "Quando il mio compagno di stanza tornava tardi la sera, facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentato per evitare discussi"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "If my father came into the room to tell me to turn off the TV, I always pretended to have fallen asleep on the couch.", "tl": "Se mio padre entrava in camera per dirmi di spegnere la TV, facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentato sul divano."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "When my mother came to wake me up early on Sundays, I always pretended to have fallen asleep again.", "tl": "Quando mia madre veniva a svegliarmi presto la domenica, facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentata di nuovo."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If someone called me on my cell phone late, I wouldn't answer and the next day I always pretended to have fallen asleep ", "tl": "Se qualcuno mi cercava sul cellulare tardi, non rispondevo e il giorno dopo facevo sempre finta di essermi addormentato "}]}, {"idiom_id": 113, "expression_id": 100, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "non ho parole", "english_gloss": "I am speechless", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "In the face of such selfish behavior, I really have no words.", "tl": "Davanti a un comportamento così egoista, davvero non ho parole."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The beauty of this landscape leaves me breathless, I have no words to describe it.", "tl": "La bellezza di questo panorama mi lascia senza fiato, non ho parole per descriverla."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "They cancelled the train again without warning? I'm speechless!", "tl": "Hanno cancellato il treno di nuovo senza preavviso? Non ho parole!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For your incredible generosity, my wife and I have no words.", "tl": "Per la vostra incredibile generosità, io e mia moglie non abbiamo parole."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Marco is speechless about how he was treated at work today.", "tl": "Marco non ha parole per come è stato trattato al lavoro oggi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you think you can solve the problem this way, I have no words.", "tl": "Se pensi di risolvere il problema in questo modo, io non ho parole."}]}, {"idiom_id": 112, "expression_id": 99, "lang": "it", "idiom_text": "mi è capitata così per caso sotto il naso", "english_gloss": "happened to fall right under my nose by chance", "youtube_id": "QDHBOlWm-o0", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I was tidying up the closet when this old photo happened to fall right under my nose by chance.", "tl": "Stavo riordinando l'armadio quando questa vecchia foto mi è capitata così per caso sotto il naso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I wasn't looking for a new job, but this job posting just happened to fall right under my nose by chance.", "tl": "Non stavo cercando un nuovo lavoro, ma questo annuncio mi è capitato così per caso sotto il naso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I was looking for a dinner idea and these vegetarian recipes happened to fall right under my nose by chance.", "tl": "Cercavo un'idea per la cena e queste ricette vegetariane mi sono capitate così per caso sotto il naso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "While I was looking for my passport in the drawer, those old tickets happened to fall right under my nose by chance.", "tl": "Mentre cercavo il passaporto nel cassetto, quei vecchi biglietti mi sono capitati così per caso sotto il naso."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I didn't want to buy a house in the countryside, but this opportunity happened to fall right under my nose by chance and", "tl": "Non volevo comprare una casa in campagna, ma questa occasione mi è capitata così per caso sotto il naso e l'ho presa."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I was in the library without a specific idea, then this history book happened to fall right under my nose by chance.", "tl": "Ero in biblioteca senza un'idea precisa, poi questo libro di storia mi è capitato così per caso sotto il naso."}]}, {"idiom_id": 111, "expression_id": 88, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faisant appel à", "english_gloss": "appealing to / drawing upon", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is a brain teaser drawing upon your logic and patience.", "tl": "C'est un jeu de réflexion faisant appel à votre logique et à votre patience."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "For this difficult project, the company is calling upon external experts.", "tl": "Pour ce projet difficile, l'entreprise fait appel à des experts externes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She wrote an exciting novel, drawing upon her own childhood memories.", "tl": "Elle a écrit un roman passionnant, faisant appel à ses propres souvenirs d'enfance."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "We are appealing to your generosity to help families in need.", "tl": "Nous faisons appel à votre générosité pour aider les familles dans le besoin."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The teacher offers exercises drawing upon the students' imagination.", "tl": "Le professeur propose des exercices faisant appel à l'imagination des élèves."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "When my car broke down, I called upon a tow truck service.", "tl": "Quand ma voiture est tombée en panne, j'ai fait appel à un dépanneur."}]}, {"idiom_id": 110, "expression_id": 87, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "mettre la main dessus", "english_gloss": "to get one's hands on it", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I looked for my keys everywhere this morning, but I couldn't get my hands on them.", "tl": "J'ai cherché mes clés partout ce matin, mais je n'ai pas réussi à mettre la main dessus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "As soon as I get my hands on it, I will email you the document.", "tl": "Dès que je mettrai la main dessus, je t'enverrai le document par mail."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This book is very rare, but if you manage to get your hands on it, lend it to me!", "tl": "Ce livre est très rare, mais si tu arrives à mettre la main dessus, prête-le-moi !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The police had been looking for this thief for weeks, and they finally got their hands on him last night.", "tl": "La police cherchait ce voleur depuis des semaines, et ils ont enfin mis la main dessus hier soir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "If I could get my hands on it, I would buy this apartment immediately.", "tl": "Si je pouvais mettre la main dessus, j'achèterais cet appartement immédiatement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I absolutely must get my hands on it before this afternoon's meeting.", "tl": "Il faut absolument que je mette la main dessus avant la réunion de cet après-midi."}]}, {"idiom_id": 109, "expression_id": 86, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "avoir tendance à", "english_gloss": "to tend to / have a tendency to", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "She tends to go to bed late on weekends.", "tl": "Elle a tendance à se coucher tard le week-end."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "We tend to buy things we don't need.", "tl": "On a tendance à acheter des choses dont on n'a pas besoin."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "When I was young, I tended to forget my homework.", "tl": "Quand j'étais jeune, j'avais tendance à oublier mes devoirs."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In summer, temperatures tend to rise quickly.", "tl": "En été, les températures ont tendance à augmenter rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You tend to stress too much before an exam.", "tl": "Tu as tendance à trop stresser avant un examen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "People tend to spend too much time on their phones.", "tl": "Les gens ont tendance à passer trop de temps sur leur téléphone."}]}, {"idiom_id": 108, "expression_id": 85, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en vertu de", "english_gloss": "by virtue of / under", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Under this contract, you must pay the rent before the fifth of each month.", "tl": "En vertu de ce contrat, vous devez payer le loyer avant le cinq de chaque mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "By virtue of the law, all citizens have the right to the protection of their private life.", "tl": "En vertu de la loi, tous les citoyens ont droit à la protection de leur vie privée."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Under the internal regulations, smoking is prohibited in the offices.", "tl": "En vertu du règlement intérieur, il est interdit de fumer dans les bureaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The mayor made this decision by virtue of the powers granted to him.", "tl": "Le maire a pris cette décision en vertu des pouvoirs qui lui sont accordés."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Under this agreement, the two companies will collaborate on a new project.", "tl": "En vertu de cet accord, les deux entreprises vont collaborer sur un nouveau projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "By virtue of her student status, she benefits from reduced fares for public transport.", "tl": "En vertu de son statut d'étudiant, elle bénéficie de tarifs réduits pour les transports."}]}, {"idiom_id": 107, "expression_id": 84, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "au fur et à mesure", "english_gloss": "gradually / as we go along", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Add the water gradually to get the right consistency.", "tl": "Ajoutez l'eau au fur et à mesure pour obtenir la bonne consistance."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Don't worry, you will understand as you go along.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, tu vas comprendre au fur et à mesure."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I prefer to tidy my desk as I go along so I don't get overwhelmed.", "tl": "Je préfère ranger mon bureau au fur et à mesure pour ne pas être débordé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The story becomes more and more interesting as we progress through the book.", "tl": "L'histoire devient de plus en plus intéressante au fur et à mesure qu'on avance dans le livre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We will correct the mistakes as they come up.", "tl": "Nous corrigerons les erreurs au fur et à mesure qu'elles se présentent."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The landscape changed as the train moved towards the south.", "tl": "Le paysage changeait au fur et à mesure que le train avançait vers le sud."}]}, {"idiom_id": 106, "expression_id": 83, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "point de départ", "english_gloss": "starting point", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This report will be our starting point for tomorrow's meeting.", "tl": "Ce rapport sera notre point de départ pour la réunion de demain."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Lyon station is the ideal starting point for visiting the south of France.", "tl": "La gare de Lyon est le point de départ idéal pour visiter le sud de la France."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Your idea is excellent; it's a good starting point for our group project.", "tl": "Ton idée est excellente, c'est un bon point de départ pour notre projet de groupe."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This scientific discovery was the starting point of a new era.", "tl": "Cette découverte scientifique a été le point de départ d'une nouvelle ère."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My first internship in a company was the starting point of my career.", "tl": "Mon premier stage en entreprise a été le point de départ de ma carrière."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "We need to find a common starting point before beginning the negotiations.", "tl": "Nous devons trouver un point de départ commun avant de commencer les négociations."}]}, {"idiom_id": 105, "expression_id": 82, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en gros", "english_gloss": "basically / in a nutshell", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Basically, the project consists of reducing our plastic waste.", "tl": "En gros, le projet consiste à réduire nos déchets plastiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I didn't understand everything, but basically, it's the story of time travel.", "tl": "Je n'ai pas tout compris, mais en gros, c'est l'histoire d'un voyage dans le temps."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In a nutshell, they agree with us, but they want to negotiate the price.", "tl": "En gros, ils sont d'accord avec nous, mais ils veulent négocier le prix."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "It's going to cost roughly fifty euros per person.", "tl": "Ça va coûter en gros cinquante euros par personne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "My job, basically, is to manage clients and answer their questions.", "tl": "Mon travail, en gros, c'est de gérer les clients et de répondre à leurs questions."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Anyway, basically, we have to start all over again from the beginning.", "tl": "Bref, en gros, on doit tout recommencer depuis le début."}]}, {"idiom_id": 104, "expression_id": 81, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "par l'entremise de", "english_gloss": "through the mediation of / via", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I found this job through the intermediary of a childhood friend.", "tl": "J'ai trouvé ce travail par l'entremise d'un ami d'enfance."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The two countries negotiated an agreement through the mediation of the UN.", "tl": "Les deux pays ont négocié un accord par l'entremise de l'ONU."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We bought our house through a local real estate agency.", "tl": "Nous avons acheté notre maison par l'entremise d'une agence immobilière locale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I met this artist through a mutual contact.", "tl": "J'ai rencontré cet artiste par l'entremise d'un contact commun."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The documents were sent through our lawyer.", "tl": "Les documents ont été transmis par l'entremise de notre avocat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She got involved in the association through her sister.", "tl": "Elle s'est engagée dans l'association par l'entremise de sa sœur."}]}, {"idiom_id": 103, "expression_id": 80, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "par la bande", "english_gloss": "indirectly / through the back door", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I heard the news indirectly, before the official announcement.", "tl": "J'ai appris la nouvelle par la bande, avant l'annonce officielle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He didn't apply directly; he got this job through the back door thanks to a friend.", "tl": "Il n'a pas postulé directement ; il a obtenu ce poste par la bande grâce à un ami."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Instead of speaking to him directly, she tried to influence him indirectly.", "tl": "Au lieu de lui parler directement, elle a essayé de l'influencer par la bande."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "How did you get these documents? Through the back door, I suppose?", "tl": "Comment as-tu eu ces documents ? Par la bande, je suppose ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We managed to settle this problem indirectly, without going through the court.", "tl": "Nous avons réussi à régler ce problème par la bande, sans passer par le tribunal."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The information reached me in a roundabout way, but I don't know if it's true.", "tl": "L'information est arrivée jusqu'à moi par la bande, mais je ne sais pas si elle est vraie."}]}, {"idiom_id": 102, "expression_id": 79, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en dernier lieu", "english_gloss": "ultimately / in the final analysis", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "After hesitating between several options, we ultimately chose to stay at home.", "tl": "Après avoir hésité entre plusieurs options, nous avons choisi, en dernier lieu, de rester à la maison."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you can't manage to fix the computer, contact technical support as a last resort.", "tl": "Si vous n'arrivez pas à réparer l'ordinateur, contactez le service technique en dernier lieu."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We must think about the budget and, lastly, about the project's launch date.", "tl": "Nous devons penser au budget et, en dernier lieu, à la date de lancement du projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The doctor advised me to change my diet and, as a last resort, to take medication.", "tl": "Le médecin m'a conseillé de changer de régime et, en dernier lieu, de prendre des médicaments."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "For our trip, we will visit Rome, Florence and, lastly, Venice.", "tl": "Pour notre voyage, nous visiterons Rome, Florence et, en dernier lieu, Venise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Ultimately, it is the director who will make the decision.", "tl": "C'est le directeur qui prendra la décision en dernier lieu."}]}, {"idiom_id": 101, "expression_id": 78, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "m'a embarqué", "english_gloss": "swept me away / got me hooked", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This detective novel got me hooked from the very first chapter.", "tl": "Ce roman policier m'a embarqué dès le premier chapitre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The movie was a bit long, but the story completely swept me away.", "tl": "Le film était un peu long, mais l'histoire m'a complètement embarqué."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "From the very first notes, this melody swept me away to another world.", "tl": "Dès les premières notes, cette mélodie m'a embarqué dans un autre monde."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When he told me about his start-up project, his enthusiasm got me hooked right away.", "tl": "Quand il m'a parlé de son projet de start-up, son enthousiasme m'a tout de suite embarqué."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The virtual art exhibition really swept me away; it was magical.", "tl": "L'exposition d'art virtuel m'a vraiment embarqué, c'était magique."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She started telling her childhood memories, and her story swept me away.", "tl": "Elle a commencé à raconter ses souvenirs d'enfance et son récit m'a embarqué."}]}, {"idiom_id": 100, "expression_id": 77, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à toutes fins utiles", "english_gloss": "for whatever it's worth / just in case", "youtube_id": "sTf00HZ_UuY", "has_context": false, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I am sending you the summary of our meeting, just in case.", "tl": "Je vous envoie le récapitulatif de notre réunion, à toutes fins utiles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Here is my cell phone number, for whatever it's worth, in case you have any trouble this weekend.", "tl": "Voici mon numéro de portable, à toutes fins utiles, si jamais vous avez un problème ce week-end."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I printed the plane tickets just in case, even though we already have them on our phones.", "tl": "J'ai imprimé les billets d'avion à toutes fins utiles, même si nous les avons déjà sur nos téléphones."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "For what it's worth, you should know that the museum is free on the first Sunday of the month.", "tl": "À toutes fins utiles, sachez que le musée est gratuit le premier dimanche du mois."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I kept a copy of the old contract just in case.", "tl": "J'ai gardé une copie de l'ancien contrat à toutes fins utiles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "I'm leaving you the address of the nearest clinic, just in case.", "tl": "Je te laisse l'adresse de la clinique la plus proche, à toutes fins utiles."}]}, {"idiom_id": 99, "expression_id": 98, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "plus préoccupant encore", "english_gloss": "even more worrying", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The drop in grades is a problem, but even more worrying, the students lack motivation.", "tl": "La baisse des notes est un problème, mais plus préoccupant encore, les élèves manquent de motivation."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Unemployment is rising and, even more worrying, many local businesses are closing down.", "tl": "Le chômage augmente et, plus préoccupant encore, de nombreuses entreprises locales ferment leurs portes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Temperatures are rising every year, and even more worrying, water reserves are rapidly decreasing.", "tl": "Les températures augmentent chaque année, et plus préoccupant encore, les réserves d'eau diminuent rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Many people sleep poorly, and even more worrying, they never consult a doctor about it.", "tl": "Beaucoup de gens dorment mal, et plus préoccupant encore, ils ne consultent jamais de médecin pour cela."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This software has a few bugs, but even more worrying, it does not protect your personal data well.", "tl": "Ce logiciel a quelques bugs, mais plus préoccupant encore, il ne protège pas bien vos données personnelles."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The mayor canceled the park project and, even more worrying, he refuses to explain his decision to the residents.", "tl": "Le maire a annulé le projet de parc et, plus préoccupant encore, il refuse d'expliquer sa décision aux habitants."}]}, {"idiom_id": 98, "expression_id": 97, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se sentir mal dans sa peau", "english_gloss": "to feel uncomfortable in one's own skin", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Lately, I've been feeling uncomfortable in my own skin without really knowing why.", "tl": "Depuis quelque temps, je me sens mal dans ma peau sans vraiment savoir pourquoi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "If you feel uncomfortable in your own skin, you should talk to a professional about it.", "tl": "Si tu te sens mal dans ta peau, tu devrais en parler à un professionnel."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "During her teenage years, she felt very uncomfortable in her own skin because of her shyness.", "tl": "Pendant son adolescence, elle se sentait très mal dans sa peau à cause de sa timidité."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Many young people feel uncomfortable in their own skin because of social media.", "tl": "Beaucoup de jeunes se sentent mal dans leur peau à cause des réseaux sociaux."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "It is difficult to succeed in your projects when you feel uncomfortable in your own skin.", "tl": "Il est difficile de réussir ses projets quand on se sent mal dans sa peau."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "After changing jobs, he finally stopped feeling uncomfortable in his own skin.", "tl": "Après avoir changé de travail, il a enfin arrêté de se sentir mal dans sa peau."}]}, {"idiom_id": 97, "expression_id": 96, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à compter de", "english_gloss": "starting from / as of", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Starting next Monday, our working hours will change.", "tl": "À compter de lundi prochain, nos horaires de travail vont changer."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Public transport fares will increase as of April first.", "tl": "Les tarifs des transports en commun vont augmenter à compter du premier avril."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Your subscription will be active starting from the receipt of your payment.", "tl": "Votre abonnement sera actif à compter de la réception de votre paiement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Starting today, I am going to try to exercise every morning.", "tl": "À compter d'aujourd'hui, je vais essayer de faire du sport tous les matins."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Registration for the new semester will be open starting tomorrow.", "tl": "Les inscriptions pour le nouveau semestre seront ouvertes à compter de demain."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You have ten days to reply, starting from the date this letter was sent.", "tl": "Vous disposez d'un délai de dix jours pour répondre, à compter de la date d'envoi de ce courrier."}]}, {"idiom_id": 96, "expression_id": 95, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "un net rajeunissement", "english_gloss": "a marked decrease in age / rejuvenation", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "With the arrival of the new interns, we are seeing a marked rejuvenation of the marketing team.", "tl": "Avec l'arrivée des nouveaux stagiaires, on constate un net rajeunissement de l'équipe de marketing."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The latest elections have led to a marked decrease in the average age of the assembly.", "tl": "Les dernières élections ont entraîné un net rajeunissement de l'assemblée."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This classical music festival managed to attract a noticeably younger audience this year.", "tl": "Ce festival de musique classique a réussi à attirer un net rajeunissement de son public cette année."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The change of logo and colors brought a marked rejuvenation to the brand's image.", "tl": "Le changement de logo et de couleurs a apporté un net rajeunissement à l'image de la marque."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Thanks to the construction of the university, this neighborhood is experiencing a marked decrease in the average age of ", "tl": "Grâce à la construction de l'université, ce quartier connaît un net rajeunissement de sa population."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The coach decided to trust the young players, which explains the marked rejuvenation of the club.", "tl": "L'entraîneur a décidé de faire confiance aux jeunes joueurs, ce qui explique le net rajeunissement du club."}]}, {"idiom_id": 95, "expression_id": 94, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "être en mesure de", "english_gloss": "to be in a position to / be able to", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We are not in a position to accept your request at this time.", "tl": "Nous ne sommes pas en mesure d'accepter votre demande pour le moment."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Would you be in a position to help me with this project next week?", "tl": "Serais-tu en mesure de m'aider avec ce projet la semaine prochaine ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The technician was not able to repair the machine yesterday.", "tl": "Le technicien n'a pas été en mesure de réparer la machine hier."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Thanks to her savings, she is finally in a position to buy an apartment.", "tl": "Grâce à ses économies, elle est enfin en mesure d'acheter un appartement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "I doubt they are in a position to solve this problem quickly.", "tl": "Je doute qu'ils soient en mesure de résoudre ce problème rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If we had more time, we would be able to finish the report today.", "tl": "Si nous avions plus de temps, nous serions en mesure de finir le rapport aujourd'hui."}]}, {"idiom_id": 94, "expression_id": 93, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "raconter les coulisses", "english_gloss": "to tell what goes on behind the scenes", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The director likes to talk about the behind-the-scenes of the shoot in his interviews.", "tl": "Le réalisateur aime raconter les coulisses du tournage dans ses interviews."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "This political journalist is going to tell us what went on behind the scenes of the election.", "tl": "Ce journaliste politique va nous raconter les coulisses de l'élection."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the show, the actors agreed to share what went on behind the scenes of the play.", "tl": "Après le spectacle, les acteurs ont accepté de raconter les coulisses de la pièce."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "In his new book, the founder tells the behind-the-scenes story of the company's creation.", "tl": "Dans son nouveau livre, le fondateur raconte les coulisses de la création de l'entreprise."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "On her YouTube channel, she loves to share the behind-the-scenes of her travels.", "tl": "Sur sa chaîne YouTube, elle adore raconter les coulisses de ses voyages."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If you want, I can tell you what went on behind the scenes of organizing the festival.", "tl": "Si tu veux, je peux te raconter les coulisses de l'organisation du festival."}]}, {"idiom_id": 93, "expression_id": 92, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "s'emparer de", "english_gloss": "to seize / take up / tackle", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The thief grabbed her bag before running away.", "tl": "Le voleur s'est emparé de son sac avant de s'enfuir en courant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "An immense sadness took hold of her when she heard the news.", "tl": "Une immense tristesse s'est emparée d'elle quand elle a appris la nouvelle."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The media quickly seized upon this hot topic.", "tl": "Les médias se sont rapidement emparés de ce sujet brûlant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The army managed to seize the capital after several days of fighting.", "tl": "L'armée a réussi à s'emparer de la capitale après plusieurs jours de combat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She took charge of the new project with a lot of enthusiasm.", "tl": "Elle s'est emparée du nouveau projet avec beaucoup d'enthousiasme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Doubt took hold of him just before going on stage.", "tl": "Le doute s'est emparé de lui juste avant de monter sur scène."}]}, {"idiom_id": 92, "expression_id": 91, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "passer à l'acte", "english_gloss": "to take action / carry out an act", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "We've been talking about it for months, now we have to take action.", "tl": "On en parle depuis des mois, maintenant il faut passer à l'acte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He hesitated for a long time, but he finally took action.", "tl": "Il a hésité pendant longtemps, mais il est enfin passé à l'acte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Preparing a plan is important, but you also have to know when to take action.", "tl": "Préparer un plan est important, mais il faut aussi savoir passer à l'acte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I want to resign, but I'm afraid to take action.", "tl": "Je veux démissionner, mais j'ai peur de passer à l'acte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The police knew his intentions, but they didn't think he would carry out the act.", "tl": "La police connaissait ses intentions, mais elle ne pensait pas qu'il passerait à l'acte."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Many people have good ideas, but few of them actually take action.", "tl": "Beaucoup de gens ont de bonnes idées, mais peu d'entre eux passent à l'acte."}]}, {"idiom_id": 91, "expression_id": 90, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "s'en prendre à", "english_gloss": "to pick on / attack / go after", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When he is stressed, he always takes it out on his colleagues.", "tl": "Quand il est stressé, il s'en prend toujours à ses collègues."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "It's not my fault, so don't take it out on me!", "tl": "Ce n'est pas ma faute, alors ne t'en prends pas à moi !"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "After the defeat, the fans went after the referee.", "tl": "Après la défaite, les supporters s'en sont pris à l'arbitre."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You shouldn't pick on someone weaker than you.", "tl": "Tu ne devrais pas t'en prendre à plus faible que toi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Why did she take it out on her best friend?", "tl": "Pourquoi est-ce qu'elle s'en est pris à son meilleur ami ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "If the project fails, they are going to blame management.", "tl": "Si le projet échoue, ils vont s'en prendre à la direction."}]}, {"idiom_id": 90, "expression_id": 89, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "faire un carnage", "english_gloss": "to go on a rampage / commit a massacre", "youtube_id": "EXXtAZ1odSo", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The guests went to town on the buffet; there is absolutely nothing left to eat.", "tl": "Les invités ont fait un carnage dans le buffet, il ne reste plus rien à manger."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The fox got into the chicken coop last night and caused a massacre.", "tl": "Le renard est entré dans le poulailler hier soir et a fait un carnage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Our star striker went on a rampage during the match, scoring four goals.", "tl": "Notre attaquant vedette a fait un carnage lors du match en marquant quatre buts."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Last night's storm wreaked havoc in my parents' garden.", "tl": "La tempête de la nuit dernière a fait un carnage dans le jardin de mes parents."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She went wild during the sales; she came back with ten bags.", "tl": "Elle a fait un carnage pendant les soldes, elle est revenue avec dix sacs."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The last physics exam was so difficult that it caused absolute carnage among the students.", "tl": "Le dernier examen de physique était si difficile qu'il a fait un carnage chez les étudiants."}]}, {"idiom_id": 89, "expression_id": 76, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "avoir du mal à", "english_gloss": "to have difficulty doing / struggle to", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I have difficulty sleeping when it's too hot.", "tl": "J'ai du mal à dormir quand il fait trop chaud."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He struggles to understand his math teacher.", "tl": "Il a du mal à comprendre son professeur de mathématiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "We had a hard time finding the restaurant without a map.", "tl": "Nous avons eu du mal à trouver le restaurant sans plan."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "When I was a child, I had trouble reading.", "tl": "Quand j'étais enfant, j'avais du mal à lire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Do you have difficulty getting up early in the morning?", "tl": "Est-ce que vous avez du mal à vous lever tôt le matin ?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "They will have a hard time finishing this project on time.", "tl": "Ils auront du mal à finir ce projet à temps."}]}, {"idiom_id": 88, "expression_id": 75, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "à longueur de temps", "english_gloss": "all the time / constantly", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "My colleague complains about his job all the time, it's tiring.", "tl": "Mon collègue se plaint de son travail à longueur de temps, c'est fatigant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Teenagers look at their phones all the time nowadays.", "tl": "Les adolescents regardent leur téléphone à longueur de temps aujourd'hui."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "In this region, it rains constantly during autumn.", "tl": "Dans cette région, il pleut à longueur de temps pendant l'automne."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "She listens to the same song all the time, I know it by heart now.", "tl": "Elle écoute la même chanson à longueur de temps, je la connais par cœur maintenant."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Our dog barks constantly as soon as there is noise outside.", "tl": "Notre chien aboie à longueur de temps dès qu'il y a du bruit dehors."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "You can't think about work all the time, you need to relax.", "tl": "Tu ne peux pas penser au travail à longueur de temps, tu as besoin de te détendre."}]}, {"idiom_id": 87, "expression_id": 74, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "dès qu'on essaie de gratter", "english_gloss": "as soon as we try to scratch the surface", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "This bill seems perfect, but as soon as you try to scratch the surface, you discover big problems.", "tl": "Ce projet de loi semble parfait, mais dès qu'on essaie de gratter, on découvre de gros problèmes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "He seems very cold, but as soon as you try to scratch the surface a little, you discover a very sensitive person.", "tl": "Il a l'air très froid, mais dès qu'on essaie de gratter un peu, on découvre quelqu'un de très sensible."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "This job offer is too good to be true; as soon as you try to scratch the surface, you see that the salary is very low.", "tl": "Cette offre d'emploi est trop belle pour être vraie ; dès qu'on essaie de gratter, on voit que le salaire est très bas."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The history of this old house is fascinating as soon as you try to scratch the surface of the past a little.", "tl": "L'histoire de cette vieille maison est fascinante dès qu'on essaie de gratter un peu le passé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "This brand calls itself eco-friendly, but as soon as you try to scratch the surface, you realize it's just marketing.", "tl": "Cette marque se dit écologique, mais dès qu'on essaie de gratter, on se rend compte que c'est juste du marketing."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The details of this agreement are vague, and as soon as I try to scratch the surface, nobody wants to answer me.", "tl": "Les détails de cet accord sont flous, et dès que j'essaie de gratter, personne ne veut me répondre."}]}, {"idiom_id": 86, "expression_id": 73, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "en deçà", "english_gloss": "below / short of", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "His recent results are well below our expectations.", "tl": "Ses résultats récents sont bien en deçà de nos attentes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The total cost of the project remained below the initial budget.", "tl": "Le coût total du projet est resté en deçà du budget initial."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Temperatures this month are below seasonal averages.", "tl": "Les températures de ce mois-ci sont en deçà des normales de saison."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You have a lot of talent, but this work is below your capabilities.", "tl": "Tu as beaucoup de talent, mais ce travail est en deçà de tes capacités."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The pollution level in this area is finally below the legal limit.", "tl": "Le niveau de pollution dans cette zone est enfin en deçà de la limite légale."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The quality of service in this hotel was short of what was promised on their website.", "tl": "La qualité du service dans cet hôtel était en deçà de ce qui était promis sur leur site."}]}, {"idiom_id": 85, "expression_id": 72, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "pompier pyromane", "english_gloss": "arsonist firefighter (someone who creates then solves problems)", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Our boss is playing the arsonist firefighter: he creates tension in the team and then offers to resolve the conflict.", "tl": "Notre chef joue au pompier pyromane : il crée des tensions dans l'équipe et propose ensuite de résoudre le conflit."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The government is acting like an arsonist firefighter by cutting budgets before offering emergency aid.", "tl": "Le gouvernement se comporte en pompier pyromane en coupant les budgets avant de proposer des aides d'urgence."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "She loves playing the arsonist firefighter: she starts rumors and then comes to comfort you.", "tl": "Elle adore jouer au pompier pyromane : elle lance des rumeurs et vient ensuite te consoler."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "This consultant is a real arsonist firefighter; he deliberately complicates the situation so that we hire him again.", "tl": "Ce consultant est un vrai pompier pyromane ; il complique exprès la situation pour qu'on l'embauche à nouveau."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "Stop acting like an arsonist firefighter by provoking arguments only to make romantic apologies later.", "tl": "Arrête de faire le pompier pyromane en provoquant des disputes pour ensuite faire des excuses romantiques."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The media sometimes act like arsonist firefighters by creating panic and then selling solutions.", "tl": "Les médias agissent parfois comme des pompiers pyromanes en créant de la panique pour ensuite vendre des solutions."}]}, {"idiom_id": 84, "expression_id": 71, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "se mettre en place", "english_gloss": "to be set up / fall into place", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Everything is falling into place for the party tonight.", "tl": "Tout se met en place pour la fête de ce soir."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The new project was set up very quickly.", "tl": "Le nouveau projet s'est mis en place très rapidement."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Don't worry, things will eventually fall into place.", "tl": "Ne t'inquiète pas, les choses vont finir par se mettre en place."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The musicians are getting into position on the stage before the start of the concert.", "tl": "Les musiciens se mettent en place sur la scène avant le début du concert."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "New safety rules will be put in place starting Monday.", "tl": "De nouvelles règles de sécurité vont se mettre en place dès lundi."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "The new organization is gradually being set up in the company.", "tl": "La nouvelle organisation se met en place petit à petit dans l'entreprise."}]}, {"idiom_id": 83, "expression_id": 70, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "tout un tas de", "english_gloss": "a whole bunch of / a lot of", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I found a whole bunch of old books in my grandparents' attic.", "tl": "J'ai trouvé tout un tas de vieux livres dans le grenier de mes grands-parents."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "I still have a whole bunch of things to do before I can go on vacation.", "tl": "J'ai encore tout un tas de choses à faire avant de pouvoir partir en vacances."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He made up a whole bunch of excuses for not coming to my birthday party.", "tl": "Il a inventé tout un tas d'excuses pour ne pas venir à ma fête d'anniversaire."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Children always ask themselves a whole bunch of questions about the world around them.", "tl": "Les enfants se posent toujours tout un tas de questions sur le monde qui les entoure."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "You can find a whole bunch of useful tips on this travel forum.", "tl": "On peut trouver tout un tas de conseils utiles sur ce forum de voyage."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "This new update created a whole bunch of problems on my computer.", "tl": "Cette nouvelle mise à jour a créé tout un tas de problèmes sur mon ordinateur."}]}, {"idiom_id": 82, "expression_id": 69, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "distingo", "english_gloss": "distinction / subtle difference", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "It is sometimes difficult to make a distinction between professional and private life.", "tl": "Il est parfois difficile de faire le distingo entre la vie professionnelle et la vie privée."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The law makes a very clear distinction between these two types of offenses.", "tl": "La loi fait un distingo très clair entre ces deux types d'infractions."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "I don't really make a distinction between these two brands; to me, they are equal.", "tl": "Je ne fais pas vraiment de distingo entre ces deux marques, pour moi elles se valent."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why do you make a distinction between his first book and the second? They are very similar.", "tl": "Pourquoi fais-tu un distingo entre son premier livre et le deuxième ? Ils sont très similaires."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The director made a subtle distinction between short-term and long-term goals.", "tl": "Le directeur a établi un distingo subtil entre les objectifs à court terme et à long terme."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Children sometimes have trouble making the distinction between dreams and reality.", "tl": "Les enfants ont parfois du mal à faire le distingo entre le rêve et la réalité."}]}, {"idiom_id": 81, "expression_id": 68, "lang": "fr", "idiom_text": "autrement dit", "english_gloss": "in other words", "youtube_id": "mSjmEEPQ7ls", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The office will be closed on Friday; in other words, we have a long weekend.", "tl": "Le bureau sera fermé vendredi, autrement dit, nous avons un long week-end."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Our expenses exceed our income; in other words, we need to save money.", "tl": "Nos dépenses dépassent nos revenus, autrement dit, nous devons faire des économies."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "He didn't call me back; in other words, he is not interested in the project.", "tl": "Il ne m'a pas rappelé, autrement dit, il n'est pas intéressé par le projet."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "You got the best grade in the class; in other words, your hard work paid off.", "tl": "Tu as obtenu la meilleure note de la classe, autrement dit, ton travail a payé."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The train is canceled; in other words, we are going to have to take the bus.", "tl": "Le train est annulé, autrement dit, nous allons devoir prendre le bus."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "She refuses to eat meat; in other words, she is a vegetarian.", "tl": "Elle refuse de manger de la viande, autrement dit, elle est végétarienne."}]}, {"idiom_id": 80, "expression_id": 45, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Bis heute ist Berkoff ein Vorbild für viele Frauen", "english_gloss": "To this day, Berkoff is a role model for many women", "youtube_id": "g5Q2LszshRc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "Although she ended her career years ago, Berkoff is a role model for many women to this day.", "tl": "Obwohl sie ihre Karriere vor Jahren beendet hat, ist Berkoff bis heute ein Vorbild für viele Frauen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "In an interview, the director said, \"To this day, Berkoff is a role model for many women in the film industry.\"", "tl": "In einem Interview sagte die Regisseurin: „Bis heute ist Berkoff ein Vorbild für viele Frauen in der Filmindustrie.“"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Her groundbreaking work in science shows: To this day, Berkoff is a role model for many women.", "tl": "Ihre bahnbrechende Arbeit in der Wissenschaft zeigt: Bis heute ist Berkoff ein Vorbild für viele Frauen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Why do you think Berkoff is still a role model for many women to this day?", "tl": "Warum glauben Sie, dass Berkoff bis heute ein Vorbild für viele Frauen ist?"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "She never wanted to be famous, but to this day Berkoff is a role model for many women all over the world.", "tl": "Sie wollte nie berühmt werden, aber bis heute ist Berkoff ein Vorbild für viele Frauen auf der ganzen Welt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "There is no question about it: To this day, Berkoff is a role model for many women who want to go their own way.", "tl": "Es steht außer Frage: Bis heute ist Berkoff ein Vorbild für viele Frauen, die ihren eigenen Weg gehen wollen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 79, "expression_id": 44, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Das hätte ich mir nie träumen lassen.", "english_gloss": "I would never have dreamed of that.", "youtube_id": "g5Q2LszshRc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "I got the promotion! I would never have dreamed of that a year ago.", "tl": "Ich habe die Beförderung bekommen! Das hätte ich mir vor einem Jahr nie träumen lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Now I'm actually standing on the Eiffel Tower. I would never have dreamed of that as a child.", "tl": "Jetzt stehe ich tatsächlich auf dem Eiffelturm. Das hätte ich mir als Kind nie träumen lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "That we would meet again by chance on vacation after ten years – I would never have dreamed of that!", "tl": "Dass wir uns nach zehn Jahren zufällig im Urlaub wiedersehen – das hätte ich mir nie träumen lassen!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "I won the grand prize in the raffle. I would never have dreamed of that in my life!", "tl": "Ich habe den Hauptpreis bei der Tombola gewonnen. Das hätte ich mir im Leben nie träumen lassen!"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "We finally bought our own house. We would never have dreamed of that five years ago.", "tl": "Wir haben endlich unser eigenes Haus gekauft. Das hätten wir uns vor fünf Jahren nie träumen lassen."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "That the company would go bankrupt so quickly, I really would never have dreamed of that.", "tl": "Dass die Firma so schnell pleitegeht, das hätte ich mir wirklich nie träumen lassen."}]}, {"idiom_id": 78, "expression_id": 43, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Der Chef dachte, ich habe keine Ahnung von Politik.", "english_gloss": "The boss thought I had no clue about politics.", "youtube_id": "g5Q2LszshRc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The boss thought I had no clue about politics, but then I explained the new tax reform to him.", "tl": "Der Chef dachte, ich habe keine Ahnung von Politik, aber dann habe ich ihm die neue Steuerreform erklärt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "My boss probably thought I had no clue about politics, which is why he didn't invite me to the meeting with the politici", "tl": "Mein Chef dachte wohl, ich hätte keine Ahnung von Politik, weshalb er mich nicht zum Treffen mit den Politikern eingelad"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Why did the boss actually think I had no clue about politics? I read the newspaper every day, after all.", "tl": "Warum dachte der Chef eigentlich, ich habe keine Ahnung von Politik? Ich lese doch jeden Tag die Zeitung."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "Just because I rarely comment on it in the office, the boss thought I had no clue about politics.", "tl": "Nur weil ich mich im Büro selten dazu äußere, dachte der Chef, ich habe keine Ahnung von Politik."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The boss mistakenly thought I had no clue about politics and was very surprised by my analysis.", "tl": "Der Chef dachte fälschlicherweise, ich habe keine Ahnung von Politik, und war von meiner Analyse sehr überrascht."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Our boss always thought I had no clue about politics until we talked about the elections during lunch.", "tl": "Unser Chef dachte immer, ich habe keine Ahnung von Politik, bis wir uns beim Mittagessen über die Wahlen unterhalten hab"}]}, {"idiom_id": 77, "expression_id": 42, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Das war damals etwas ganz Besonderes.", "english_gloss": "That was something very special back then.", "youtube_id": "g5Q2LszshRc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "When I got my first mobile phone, that was something very special back then.", "tl": "Als ich mein erstes Handy bekam, war das damals etwas ganz Besonderes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "Once a month we went to a restaurant; that was something very special for us kids back then.", "tl": "Einmal im Monat sind wir ins Restaurant gegangen; das war damals etwas ganz Besonderes für uns Kinder."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Flying on vacation by plane – that was something very special back then.", "tl": "Mit dem Flugzeug in den Urlaub zu fliegen – das war damals etwas ganz Besonderes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "My grandparents were the first on the street to have a color TV. That was something very special back then.", "tl": "Meine Großeltern hatten als Erste in der Straße einen Farbfernseher. Das war damals etwas ganz Besonderes."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "A visit to the cinema on the weekend? That was something very special back then, which people didn't do often.", "tl": "Ein Kinobesuch am Wochenende? Das war damals etwas ganz Besonderes, das man nicht oft gemacht hat."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Finding a real letter in the mailbox – that was something very special back then.", "tl": "Einen echten Brief im Briefkasten zu finden – das war damals etwas ganz Besonderes."}]}, {"idiom_id": 76, "expression_id": 41, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwortung in der NATO übernehmen.", "english_gloss": "Therefore, European countries want to take on more responsibility in NATO.", "youtube_id": "g5Q2LszshRc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The threat situation has changed, which is why European countries now want to take on even more responsibility in NATO.", "tl": "Die Bedrohungslage hat sich verändert, deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwortung in der NATO "}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The US is demanding more commitment; therefore, European countries now want to take on even more responsibility in NATO.", "tl": "Die USA fordern mehr Engagement; deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwortung in der NATO überne"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "Security is not free, which is why European countries now want to take on even more responsibility in NATO.", "tl": "Sicherheit ist nicht kostenlos, deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwortung in der NATO überneh"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "There are new crises worldwide. Therefore, European countries now want to take on even more responsibility in NATO.", "tl": "Es gibt neue Krisen weltweit. Deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwortung in der NATO übernehme"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 5, "en": "The defense ministers are in agreement: Therefore, European countries now want to take on even more responsibility in NA", "tl": "Die Verteidigungsminister sind sich einig: Deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwortung in der N"}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 6, "en": "Peace in Europe is no longer a given, which is why European countries now want to take on even more responsibility in NA", "tl": "Frieden in Europa ist keine Selbstverständlichkeit mehr, deshalb wollen die europäischen Länder jetzt noch mehr Verantwo"}]}, {"idiom_id": 75, "expression_id": 40, "lang": "de", "idiom_text": "Bei dem Treffen geht es um die Frage", "english_gloss": "The meeting is about the question", "youtube_id": "g5Q2LszshRc", "has_context": true, "examples": [{"example_id": null, "ord": 1, "en": "The meeting is about the question of how we can finance the new project.", "tl": "Bei dem Treffen geht es um die Frage, wie wir das neue Projekt finanzieren können."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 2, "en": "The meeting is about the question of whether we are organizing a summer festival this year.", "tl": "Bei dem Treffen geht es um die Frage, ob wir dieses Jahr ein Sommerfest organisieren."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 3, "en": "The meeting was about the question of who will take responsibility for the marketing.", "tl": "Bei dem Treffen ging es um die Frage, wer die Verantwortung für das Marketing übernimmt."}, {"example_id": null, "ord": 4, "en": "The meeting is about the question of how we 